rrect about GBN protocol? ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. Only using ACK-s\nB. Using cumulative ACK-s\nC. Receiver discards all out-of-order packets\nD. It is not pipelined protocol\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 460, "output_tokens": 357, "total_tokens": 817}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_17", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following about TCP connection is not correct? ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. It is a broadcast connection\nB. It is a point-to-point connection\nC. It is a pipelined connection\nD. It is a full duplex connection\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 464, "output_tokens": 295, "total_tokens": 759}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_59", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the following four descriptions about MSS and MTU, which one is not correct? ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. The MSS is the maximum amount of application-layer data in the segment\nB. The MSS is the maximum size of the TCP segment including headers\nC. The MSS is typically set by MTU\nD. The MTU means the largest link-layer frame\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 556, "output_tokens": 338, "total_tokens": 894}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_61", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the following four descriptions about the relationship between the transport layer and the network layer, which one is not correct? ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. The transport-layer protocol provides logical communication between hosts\nB. The transport-layer protocol provides logical communication between processes\nC. The services that a transport-layer protocol can provide are often constrained by the service model of the network-layer protocol\nD. A computer network may make available multiple transport protocols\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 604, "output_tokens": 255, "total_tokens": 859}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_63", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The following four descriptions about multiplexing and de-multiplexing, which one is correct? ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. A UDP socket is identified by a two-tuples consisting of a source port number and a destination port number.\nB. If two UDP segment have different source port number, they may be directed to the same destination process.\nC. If two TCP segments with different source port number, they may be directed to the same destination process.\nD. If two TCP segments with same destination IP address and destination port number, they must be the same TCP connection.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. UDP sockets are identified by a two-tuple of destination IP address and destination port number, not source port number. However, with TCP, multiple segments from different source ports can still be directed to the same destination process if they belong to different connections, but two TCP segments with the same destination IP and port must also differ in source IP or port to be different connections.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 897, "output_tokens": 511, "total_tokens": 1408}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_66", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following about TCP is not correct? ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. It is a connectionless protocol\nB. Point-to-point protocol\nC. Reliable, in-order byte steam protocol\nD. Pipelined protocol\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 444, "output_tokens": 262, "total_tokens": 706}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_165", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the odd one from the following: ( ).\n\nOptions: \nA. Koha\nB. VTLS\nC. SLIM++\nD. SOUL\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 384, "output_tokens": 251, "total_tokens": 635}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_232", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following variables cannot be expressed in quantitative terms? ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. Socio-economic Status\nB. Marital Status\nC. Numerical Aptitude\nD. Professional Attitude\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 424, "output_tokens": 272, "total_tokens": 696}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_252", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mark the 'odd one out' ( ).\n\nOptions: \nA. Cow-Calf principle\nB. Principle of osmosis\nC. Wall picture principle\nD. Whole organ principle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The odd one out is \\boxed{B}. The Cow-Calf, Wall picture, and Whole organ principles are all related to methods in anatomical or specimen preservation, such as museum display techniques. The Principle of osmosis, however, is a biological process involving solvent movement across a membrane, which is unrelated to these preservation concepts.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 504, "output_tokens": 410, "total_tokens": 914}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_270", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is not true about e journals? ( ) \n\nOptions: \nA. They are distributed through digital methods\nB. They also have editors or editorial boards\nC. They are publications of serial nature\nD. They are always free of cost\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 468, "output_tokens": 280, "total_tokens": 748}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost