 a bank uses information to launch a personalized credit card product ( ).\n\nOptions: \nA. this reduces costs\nB. this adds value\nC. this manages risk\nD. creates opportunity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 412, "output_tokens": 223, "total_tokens": 635}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_598", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: 530.Which of the following can be used to determine the tangible value of information? ( ). \n\nOptions: \nA. Profit-cost of gathering information\nB. Labor costs-cost of gathering information\nC. Quality of information-cost of gathering information\nD. Value of information-cost of gathering information\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 504, "output_tokens": 225, "total_tokens": 729}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_631", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A KM developer is better off working with a single expert when:( ).\n\nOptions: \nA. the problem domain is complex.\nB. there must be alternative ways of generating the knowledge.\nC. there is a need to share more confidentiality with project-related information.\nD. there is a need for a synthesis of experience.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 642, "output_tokens": 902, "total_tokens": 1544}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_640", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of them is wrongly connected? ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. Socialization----the conversion of tacit knowledge to tacit knowledge\nB. Combination----the conversion of explicit knowledge to Tacit knowledge\nC. Externalization----the conversion of tacit to explicit knowledge\nD. Internalization---the conversion of explicit to tacit knowledge\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 532, "output_tokens": 283, "total_tokens": 815}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_645", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To building KM system there are a lot of challenges that includes following EXCEPT: ( ).\n\nOptions: \nA. Culture\nB. Knowledge Evaluation\nC. Knowledge Processing\nD. Knowledge filtering\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 412, "output_tokens": 281, "total_tokens": 693}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_659", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of the following is most suitable for different place, same time conditions in knowledge sharing process? ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. Face to face meeting\nB. Peer to Peer shared computer\nC. E-Mail\nD. Video conferencing\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 456, "output_tokens": 245, "total_tokens": 701}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_662", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which is the number one challenge in getting people to share their knowledge rather than hoarding it:( ).\n\nOptions: \nA. Change in culture\nB. Knowledge Evaluation\nC. Knowledge Processing\nD. Knowledge Implementation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 428, "output_tokens": 251, "total_tokens": 679}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_670", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following comes as last priority while implementing Knowledge Management? ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. Global Connectivity\nB. Distributed Expertise\nC. Rapid changes in Products & Processes\nD. Changing technologies\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}.  \n\nKnowledge Management implementation prioritizes foundational elements like connectivity, expertise distribution, and adapting to technology changes, as these enable effective knowledge sharing and use. Rapid changes in products and processes are typically a consequence or driver, not a direct priority, since KM focuses on capturing and reusing knowledge amid such changes. Thus, it comes last among the listed options.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 525, "output_tokens": 395, "total_tokens": 920}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_674", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following make Knowledge Management efforts futile? ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. Sharing of valuable knowledge\nB. Sharing Best Practices\nC. Lack of solid Business case\nD. Identification and disseminate knowledge\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 428, "output_tokens": 198, "total_tokens": 626}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_687", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: which of the following problem is reversible and certain outcome based? ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. Chess\nB. Bridge\nC. 8 puzzle\nD. Travelling salesman\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 400, "output_tokens": 346, "total_tokens": 746}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_696", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: let suppose we have a problem with 1 initial state and m goal states. The total number of possibilities in both the directions is same. Then which reasoning process should be applied in order to obtain a result. ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. Backward\nB. Forward\nC. Heuristic\nD. Can't be told\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 524, "output_tokens": 281, "total_tokens": 805}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_716", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A natural language generation program must decide: ( ).\n\nOptions: \nA. What to say\nB. When to say something\nC. Why it is being used\nD. Both A and B\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 416, "output_tokens": 338, "total_tokens": 754}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_726", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Categorize crossword puzzle in fully observable / partially observable. ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. Fully observable\nB. Partially observable\nC. All of the mentioned\nD. None of the mentioned\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 420, "output_tokens": 202, "total_tokens": 622}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_113", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Now a day's what is a most important vital resource for societal development of a country? ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. Books\nB. Knowledge\nC. Information\nD. Data\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}  \n\nKnowledge is the most vital resource because it enables the application and synthesis of information and data to drive innovation and decision-making. While information and data are raw materials, knowledge provides the understanding needed to use them effectively for societal progress. Books are a medium, but knowledge itself is the core driver of development.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 506, "output_tokens": 288, "total_tokens": 794}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_293", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Today which type of information sources is most useful? ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. Reference sources\nB. Documentary source\nC. Non-Documentary source\nD. Both the Documentary and Non-Documentary sources\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 432, "output_tokens": 286, "total_tokens": 718}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_592", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For a manager, the most important attribute of information quality is ( ).\n\nOptions: \nA. Media\nB. Presentation\nC. Relevance\nD. Manipulation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 403, "output_tokens": 242, "total_tokens": 645}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "ArcMMLU_677", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is not recommended for fostering Knowledge management? ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. Ignoring people or cultural issues\nB. Valuing and rewarding Individual's knowledge\nC. A Culture that recognizes tacit knowledge\nD. Encouraging employees to share knowledge\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 487, "output_tokens": 217, "total_tokens": 704}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "LiveCodeBench_84", "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nGiven an array of strings words and a string s, determine if s is an acronym of words.\nThe string s is considered an acronym of words if it can be formed by concatenating the first character of each string in words in order. For example, \"ab\" can be formed from [\"apple\", \"banana\"], but it can't be formed from [\"bear\", \"aardvark\"].\nReturn true if s is an acronym of words, and false otherwise. \n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: words = [\"alice\",\"bob\",\"charlie\"], s = \"abc\"\nOutput: true\nExplanation: The first character in the words \"alice\", \"bob\", and \"charlie\" are 'a', 'b', and 'c', respectively. Hence, s = \"abc\" is the acronym. \n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: words = [\"an\",\"apple\"], s = \"a\"\nOutput: false\nExplanation: The first character in the words \"an\" and \"apple\" are 'a' and 'a', respectively. \nThe acronym formed by concatenating these characters is \"aa\". \nHence, s = \"a\" is not the acronym.\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput: words = [\"never\",\"gonna\",\"give\",\"up\",\"on\",\"you\"], s = \"ngguoy\"\nOutput: true\nExplanation: By concatenating the first character of the words in the array, we get the string \"ngguoy\". \nHence, s = \"ngguoy\" is the acronym.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= words.length <= 100\n1 <= words[i].length <= 10\n1 <= s.length <= 100\nwords[i] and s consist of lowercase English letters.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "```python\ndef isAcronym(words, s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Determine if s is an acronym of words.\n    \n    Args:\n        words: List of strings\n        s: String to check if it's an acronym\n    \n    Returns:\n        Boolean indicating whether s is an acronym of words\n    \"\"\"\n    # Check if the length of s matches the number of words\n    if len(s) != len(words):\n        return False\n    \n    # Check if each character in s matches the first character of each word\n    for i in range(len(words)):\n        if not words[i] or s[i] != words[i][0]:\n            return False\n    \n    return True\n```", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1556, "output_tokens": 543, "total_tokens": 2099}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "LiveCodeBench_67", "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYour laptop keyboard is faulty, and whenever you type a character 'i' on it, it reverses the string that you have written. Typing other characters works as expected.\nYou are given a 0-indexed string s, and you type each character of s using your faulty keyboard.\nReturn the final string that will be present on your laptop screen.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: s = \"string\"\nOutput: \"rtsng\"\nExplanation: \nAfter typing first character, the text on the screen is \"s\".\nAfter the second character, the text is \"st\". \nAfter the third character, the text is \"str\".\nSince the fourth character is an 'i', the text gets reversed and becomes \"rts\".\nAfter the fifth character, the text is \"rtsn\". \nAfter the sixth character, the text is \"rtsng\". \nTherefore, we return \"rtsng\".\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: s = \"poiinter\"\nOutput: \"ponter\"\nExplanation: \nAfter the first character, the text on the screen is \"p\".\nAfter the second character, the text is \"po\". \nSince the third character you type is an 'i', the text gets reversed and becomes \"op\". \nSince the fourth character you type is an 'i', the text gets reversed and becomes \"po\".\nAfter the fifth character, the text is \"pon\".\nAfter the sixth character, the text is \"pont\". \nAfter the seventh character, the text is \"ponte\". \nAfter the eighth character, the text is \"ponter\". \nTherefore, we return \"ponter\".\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= s.length <= 100\ns consists of lowercase English letters.\ns[0] != 'i'", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "```python\ndef finalString(s):\n    result = \"\"\n    for char in s:\n        if char == 'i':\n            result = result[::-1]\n        else:\n            result += char\n    return result\n```", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1556, "output_tokens": 184, "total_tokens": 1740}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "LiveCodeBench_220", "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. The function should take stdin as input and print the output. Simply call the function after the definition. Question:\nTakahashi has decided to enjoy a wired full-course meal consisting of N courses in a restaurant.\r\nThe i-th course is:\n\n- if X_i=0, an antidotal course with a tastiness of Y_i;\n- if X_i=1, a poisonous course with a tastiness of Y_i.\n\nWhen Takahashi eats a course, his state changes as follows:  \n\n- Initially, Takahashi has a healthy stomach.\n- When he has a healthy stomach,\n- if he eats an antidotal course, his stomach remains healthy;\n- if he eats a poisonous course, he gets an upset stomach.\n\n\n- When he has an upset stomach,\n- if he eats an antidotal course, his stomach becomes healthy;\n- if he eats a poisonous course, he dies.\n\n\n\nThe meal progresses as follows.\n\n- Repeat the following process for i = 1, \\ldots, N in this order.\n- First, the i-th course is served to Takahashi.\n- Next, he chooses whether to \"eat\" or \"skip\" the course.\n- If he chooses to \"eat\" it, he eats the i-th course.  His state also changes depending on the course he eats.\n- If he chooses to \"skip\" it, he does not eat the i-th course.  This course cannot be served later or kept somehow.\n\n\n- Finally, (if his state changes, after the change) if he is not dead,\n- if i \\neq N, he proceeds to the next course.\n- if i = N, he makes it out of the restaurant alive.\n\n\n\n\n\nAn important meeting awaits him, so he must make it out of there alive.\r\nFind the maximum possible sum of tastiness of the courses that he eats (or 0 if he eats nothing) when he decides whether to \"eat\" or \"skip\" the courses under that condition.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\r\nX_1 Y_1\r\nX_2 Y_2\r\n\\vdots\r\nX_N Y_N\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the answer as an integer.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- All input values are integers.\n- 1 \\le N \\le 3 \\times 10^5\n- X_i \\in \\{{0,1\\}}\n- In other words, X_i is either 0 or 1.\n\n\n- -10^9 \\le Y_i \\le 10^9\n\nSample Input 1\n\n5\r\n1 100\r\n1 300\r\n0 -200\r\n1 500\r\n1 300\n\nSample Output 1\n\n600\r\n\nThe following choices result in a total tastiness of the courses that he eats amounting to 600, which is the maximum possible.\n\n- He skips the 1-st course.  He now has a healthy stomach.\n- He eats the 2-nd course.  He now has an upset stomach, and the total tastiness of the courses that he eats amounts to 300.\n- He eats the 3-rd course.  He now has a healthy stomach again, and the total tastiness of the courses that he eats amounts to 100.\n- He eats the 4-th course.  He now has an upset stomach, and the total tastiness of the courses that he eats amounts to 600.\n- He skips the 5-th course.  He now has an upset stomach.\n- In the end, he is not dead, so he makes it out of the restaurant alive.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n4\r\n0 -1\r\n1 -2\r\n0 -3\r\n1 -4\n\nSample Output 2\n\n0\r\n\nFor this input, it is optimal to eat nothing, in which case the answer is 0.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n15\r\n1 900000000\r\n0 600000000\r\n1 -300000000\r\n0 -700000000\r\n1 200000000\r\n1 300000000\r\n0 -600000000\r\n1 -900000000\r\n1 600000000\r\n1 -100000000\r\n1 -4000