OR, because we only do point query. And our update is on the difference array.\n\nWait: our `fenw_flip` is used to store the difference array for flip counts. But we want `total_flips[i] = diff[1]^diff[2]^...^diff[i]`\n\nBut since we are working mod 2, XOR is equivalent to sum mod 2.\n\nBut we can just use a standard Fenwick tree for sum, and take `% 2` at the end.\n\nBecause `x % 2` is the same as the LSB.\n\nSo we can use a Fenwick tree that stores integers, and `query(i) % 2` gives the flip count mod 2.\n\nBut then update: we do `+= 1` at L and R+1.\n\nBut then multiple flips: it accumulates.\n\nYes.\n\nSo let's do:\n\n### FenwSum: Fenwick tree for sum (integer)\n\n- `__init__(n)`\n- `update(i, delta)`\n- `query(i)` -> prefix sum at i\n- `range_query(l, r)` = `query(r) - query(l-1)`\n\nBut for `fenw_flip`, we only need point query: `total_flips(i) = fenw_flip.query(i)`, then mod 2.\n\nBut we are doing range update via difference array: so we do:\n- `fenw_flip.update(L, 1)`\n- `fenw_flip.update(R+1, -1)`\n\nBut wait: for difference array for additive updates, to add `v` to [L,R], we do:\n- `diff[L] += v`\n- `diff[R+1] -= v`\n\nThen `total[i] = diff[1]+...+diff[i]`\n\nSo we can use a Fenw tree that stores the `diff` array, and `query(i)` gives total additive flips at i.\n\nThen `flip_parity = query(i) % 2`\n\nPerfect.\n\nSo we'll create a FenwSum tree for `flip_diff`, size N+10.\n\nSimilarly, `fenw_bad` is a FenwSum tree for the `bad_arr`, size N+10.\n\n### Implementation:\n\nNote: all indices 1-indexed.\n\nSteps:\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\nsys.setrecursionlimit(1 << 25)\n\nclass Fenw:\n    def __init__(self, n):\n        self.n = n\n        self.tree = [0] * (n + 1)\n    \n    def update(self, i, delta):\n        while i <= self.n:\n            self.tree[i] += delta\n            i += i & -i\n    \n    def query(self, i):  # prefix sum [1, i]\n        s = 0\n        while i:\n            s += self.tree[i]\n            i -= i & -i\n        return s\n    \n    def range_query(self, l, r):\n        if l > r:\n            return 0\n        return self.query(r) - self.query(l - 1)\n\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    it = iter(data)\n    N = int(next(it)); Q = int(next(it))\n    S = next(it)\n    \n    # Fenw for flip difference array (additive)\n    fenw_flip = Fenw(N + 10)\n    # Fenw for bad array (sum of bad[i] for i in [1, N-1])\n    fenw_bad = Fenw(N + 10)\n    # bad_arr[i] for i in 1 to N-1\n    bad_arr = [0] * (N + 1)  # 1-indexed\n    \n    # Helper function to get current char at pos i (1-indexed)\n    def get_char(i):\n        orig = 1 if S[i - 1] == '1' else 0\n        total_flips = fenw_flip.query(i)  # total additive flips at i\n        return (orig + total_flips) % 2\n    \n    # Initialize bad_arr\n    for i in range(1, N):  # i from 1 to N-1\n        c1 = get_char(i)\n        c2 = get_char(i + 1)\n        if c1 == c2:\n            bad_arr[i] = 1\n            fenw_bad.update(i, 1)\n        else:\n            bad_arr[i] = 0\n    \n    out_lines = []\n    index = 0\n    for _ in range(Q):\n        t = int(next(it)); L = int(next(it)); R = int(next(it))\n        if t == 1:\n            # Flip [L, R]\n            fenw_flip.update(L, 1)\n            fenw_flip.update(R + 1, -1)\n            \n            # Update bad_arr at positions: L-1 and R (if in [1, N-1])\n            for pos in [L - 1, R]:\n                if 1 <= pos <= N - 1:\n                    old_val = bad_arr[pos]\n                    c1 = get_char(pos)\n                    c2 = get_char(pos + 1)\n                    new_val = 1 if c1 == c2 else 0\n                    if old_val != new_val:\n                        delta = new_val - old_val\n                        fenw_bad.update(pos, delta)\n                        bad_arr[pos] = new_val\n        else:  # t == 2\n            if L == R:\n                out_lines.append(\"Yes\")\n            else:\n                # Query [L, R-1] in bad_arr: an