ords.\nG. Word is the elementary data unit, Byte is a group of 8 bits, Bit is dependent on the hardware architecture.\nH. Word is a group of 1024 bits, Bit is the smallest data unit but is not used in storage, Byte is a group of 4 or 8 bits depending on the processor.\nI. Bit is a group of 2 bytes, Byte is the standard unit of data transfer, Word is the amount of data that a processor can handle at one time.\nJ. Bit is the most elementary data unit, Byte is a group of 8 bits, Word is dependent upon the hardware architecture of the computer.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1580, "output_tokens": 318, "total_tokens": 1898}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9186", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Briefly discuss the major functional unit of the Central Processing Unit (CPU).\n\nOptions: \nA. The CPU consists of six major functional units: Control Unit (CU), Arithmetic Control Unit (ALU), Internal Storage Unit (ISU), Cache Memory, Input/Output (I/O) Management, and Data Bus.\nB. The CPU consists of two major functional units: Control Unit (CU) and Arithmetic Control Unit (ALU).\nC. The CPU consists of four major functional units: Control Unit (CU), Arithmetic Control Unit (ALU), Internal Storage Unit (ISU), and Cache Memory.\nD. The CPU consists of three major functional units: Control Unit (CU), Cache Memory, and Internal Storage Unit (ISU).\nE. The CPU consists of four major functional units: Control Unit (CU), Arithmetic Control Unit (ALU), Cache Memory, and External Storage Unit (ESU).\nF. The CPU consists of one major functional unit: Control Unit (CU).\nG. The CPU consists of five major functional units: Control Unit (CU), Arithmetic Control Unit (ALU), Internal Storage Unit (ISU), Cache Memory, and Input/Output (I/O) Management.\nH. The CPU consists of seven major functional units: Control Unit (CU), Arithmetic Control Unit (ALU), Internal Storage Unit (ISU), Cache Memory, Input/Output (I/O) Management, Data Bus, and Graphics Processing Unit (GPU).\nI. The CPU consists of three major functional units: Control Unit (CU), Arithmetic Control Unit (ALU), and Internal Storage Unit (ISU).\nJ. The CPU consists of two major functional units: Arithmetic Control Unit (ALU) and Cache Memory.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1651, "output_tokens": 300, "total_tokens": 1951}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9195", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The IP protocol is primarily concerned with\n\nOptions: \nA. Reliable delivery of large (multi-packet) messages between machines that are not necessarily directly connected\nB. Providing a user interface for network management\nC. Coordinating the hardware components of the network\nD. Routing packets through the network\nE. Controlling the power consumption of network devices\nF. Reliable delivery of packets between directly connected machines\nG. Ensuring compatibility between different network technologies\nH. Monitoring