ional branch instruction is specified in an APL program.\n\nOptions: \nA. A caret (^) followed by a number or a label\nB. A forward slash (/) followed by a number or a label\nC. A left pointing arrow followed by a number or a label\nD. An exclamation mark followed by a number or a label\nE. A right pointing arrow followed by a number or a label\nF. A single colon followed by a number or a label\nG. A question mark followed by a number or a label\nH. A backslash (\\) followed by a number or a label\nI. A percentage sign (%) followed by a number or a label\nJ. A double colon followed by a number or a label\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 887, "output_tokens": 210, "total_tokens": 1097}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9420", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A user enters a Web address in a browser, and a request for a file is sent to a Web server. Which of the following best describes how the file is sent to the user?\n\nOptions: \nA. The server attempts to connect directly to the user's computer. If the connection is successful, the entire file is sent. If the connection is unsuccessful, an error message is sent to the user.\nB. The file is broken into packets for transmission. The user's browser must request each packet randomly until all packets are received.\nC. The server compresses the file into a single packet for transmission. The user's browser decompresses the packet upon receipt.\nD. The server repeatedly attempts to connect directly to the user's computer until a connection is made. Once the connection is made, the entire file is sent.\nE. The file is broken into packets for transmission. The packets must be reassembled upon receipt.\nF. The file is broken into packets for transmission. The user's browser must request each packet in order until all packets are received.\nG. The server sends each packet to the user's computer, which must confirm receipt of each packet before the next one is sent.\nH. The file is sent in separate sections, which are downloaded sequentially by the user's browser.\nI. The server sends the file in a continuous stream to the user's browser, which buffers the stream for viewing.\nJ. The server sends the entire file in one large transmission to the user's browser.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1468, "output_tokens": 242, "total_tokens": 1710}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9431", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: TCP protocol is responsible (among other things) for\n\nOptions: \nA. Ensuring secure and encrypted communication between machines\nB. Enabling communication between different network protocols\nC. Routing packets through the network\nD. Managing the energy consumption of network devices\nE. Dealing with differences among operating system architectures\nF. Reliable delivery of large (multi-packet) messages between machines that are not necessarily directly connected\nG. Managing the physical layer of networ