 and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A particular parallel program computation requires 100 seconds when executed on a single processor. If 40 percent of this computation is \"inherently sequential\" (i.e., will not benefit from additional processors), then the theoretically best possible elapsed times for this program running with 2 and 4 processors, respectively, are\n\nOptions: \nA. 100 and 50 seconds\nB. 40 and 20 seconds\nC. 60 and 30 seconds\nD. 20 and 10 seconds\nE. 80 and 40 seconds\nF. 70 and 55 seconds\nG. 30 and 15 seconds\nH. 50 and 25 seconds\nI. 110 and 55 seconds\nJ. 90 and 45 seconds\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 963, "output_tokens": 455, "total_tokens": 1418}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9235", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: At time 0, five jobs are available for execution on a single processor, with service times of 25, 15, 5, 3, and 2 time units. Which of the following is the minimum value of the average completion time of these jobs?\n\nOptions: \nA. 40\nB. 10\nC. 76/5\nD. 100/5\nE. 60\nF. 208/5\nG. 92/5\nH. 30\nI. 20\nJ. 50\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 783, "output_tokens": 433, "total_tokens": 1216}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9236", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider the Bayesian network given below. How many independent parameters are needed for this Bayesian Network H -> U <- P <- W?\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 10\nC. 2\nD. 8\nE. 14\nF. 12\nG. 16\nH. 4\nI. 5\nJ. 6\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 580, "output_tokens": 496, "total_tokens": 1076}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9246", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose that $(X, Y, Z)$ are jointly Gaussian and that $X \\rightarrow Y \\rightarrow Z$ forms a Markov chain. Let $X$ and $Y$ have correlation coefficient 0.1 and let $Y$ and $Z$ have correlation coefficient 0.9. Find $I(X;Z)$ in bits.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.45\nB. 1.2\nC. 0.1\nD. 0.9\nE. 0.00587\nF. 0.15\nG. 0.6\nH. 0.7\nI. 0.025\nJ. 0.3\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 860, "output_tokens": 799, "total_tokens": 1659}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-2