4]\nE. [7, 9, 11, 13]\nF. [6, 8, 10, 14]\nG. [6, 7, 9, 11]\nH. [8, 9, 11, 13]\nI. [3, 6, 8, 12]\nJ. [8, 10, 12, 14]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1120, "output_tokens": 1769, "total_tokens": 2889}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9320", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A TCP entity sends 6 segments across the Internet. The measured round-trip times (RTTM) for the 6 segments are 68ms, 42ms, 65ms, 80ms, 38ms, and 75ms, respectively. Assume that the smooth averaged RTT (RTTs) and Deviation (RTTD) was respectively 70ms and 10ms just before the first of these six samples. According to the Jacobson's algorithm, the retransmission timeout (RTO) is given by one RTTs plus 4 times the value of RTTD. Determine the value of RTO (in ms) after the six segments using the Jacobson's algorithm if the exponential smoothing parameters (a and B) are 0.15 and 0.2 for calculating RTTs and RTTD respectively.\n\nOptions: \nA. 140.00\nB. 97.56\nC. 114.28\nD. 138.32\nE. 150.34\nF. 130.45\nG. 120.48\nH. 110.22\nI. 105.62\nJ. 125.78\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1384, "output_tokens": 565, "total_tokens": 1949}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9322", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A train pulls out of the station at constant velocity. The received signal energy thus falls off with time as $1/i^2$. The total received signal at time $i$ is $Y_i = \\frac{{1}}{{i}}X_i + Z_i$ where $Z_1, Z_2, \\ldots$ are i.i.d. drawn from $N(0,1)$. The transmitter constraint for block length $n$ is $\\frac{{1}}{{n}}\\sum_{{i=1}}^n x_i^2(w) \\leq 2  $ for $w \\in \\{{1,2,\\ldots, 2^{{nR}}\\}}$. Use Fano's inequality to find the capacity for this channel.\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.5\nB. 2.5\nC. 1.0\nD. 0.0\nE. 0.5\nF. 0.75\nG. 3.0\nH. 1.25\nI. 0.25\nJ. 2.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1196, "output_tokens": 751, "total_tokens": 1947}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9323", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many trees are there on n (n > 1) labeled vertices with no vertices of degree 1 or 2?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2n\nB. 2^(n-1)\nC. 1\nD. 2\nE. n + 1\nF. (n-1)!\nG. n^2\nH. 0\nI. 3\nJ. n - 1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 616, "output_tokens": 489, "total_tokens": 1105}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9325", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Write a FORTRAN program segment to compute values of the POISSON distribution given by P(X) = e^-mm^x/x! Assume (1) that X and m are integer variables; (2) that X and m are small enough that no term will exceed the size permitted for a real variable in your computer; and (3) that the function FACT (n) for computing n! is available.\n\nOptions: \nA. FUNCTION P(X,M) INTEGER X Y = FLOAT(M) P = EXP(M) * M ** X / FACT(X) RETURN END\nB. FUNCTION P(X,M) INTEGER X, M P = EXP(-M) * M ** X / FACT(X) RETURN END\nC. FUNCTION P(X,M) INTEGER X, M P = EXP(-M) / (M ** X * FACT(X)) RETURN END\nD. FUNCTION P(X,M) INTEGER X Y = FLOAT (M) P = EXP(-Y) * M ** X / FACT (X) RETURN END\nE. FUNCTION P(X,M) INTEGER X Y = FLOAT (M) P = EXP(Y) * M ** X / FACT (X) RETURN END\nF. FUNCTION P(X,M) REAL X Y = FLOAT(M) P = EXP(Y) / (M ** X / FACT(X)) RETURN END\nG. FUNCTION P(X,M) REAL X Y = FLOAT(M) P = EXP(-Y) * Y ** X RETURN END\nH. FUNCTION P(X,M) INTEGER X Y = FLOAT (M) P = EXP(-Y) * M ** X * FACT (X) RETURN END\nI. FUNCTION P(X,M) INTEGER X Y = FLOAT(M) P = EXP(-Y) / (M ** X * FACT(X)) RETURN END\nJ. FUNCTION P(X,M) INTEGER X Y = FLOAT (M) P = EXP(-Y) * M / X / FACT (X) RETURN END\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1832, "output_tokens": 408, "total_tokens": 2240}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9326", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: DIMENSION A(10,10,10) Assuming that elements of the array are stored in lexicographic order of their indices, find displacements of the locations of: (a) A(5,6,7)(b) A(10,9,8)(c) A(1,5,9) relative to the location of A(1,1,1).\n\nOptions: \nA. 354, 987, 48\nB. 456, 987, 84\nC. 456, 987, 48\nD. 456, 879, 48\nE. 456, 798, 84\nF. 345, 789, 84\nG. 546, 987, 48\nH. 345, 987, 48\nI. 354, 798, 84\nJ. 546, 879, 84\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1247, "output_tokens": 928, "total_tokens": 2175}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9329", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Python 3, what is the output of ['Hi!'] * 4?\n\nOptions: \nA. ['Hi!', 4]\nB. ['Hi!', 'Hi!', 'Hi!', 'Hi!', 'Hi!']\nC. 4 * ['Hi!']\nD. ['Hi!4']\nE. Error\nF. ['Hi!', 'Hi!', 'Hi!', 'Hi!']\nG. ['Hi!Hi!Hi!Hi!']\nH. ['Hi!'] * 4\nI. ['Hi!', 'Hi!', 'Hi!', 'Hi!', 'Hi!', 'Hi!', 'Hi!', 'Hi!']\nJ. None of the above.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_token