puter can send data to another is approximately\n\nOptions: \nA. 10,000 bytes/second\nB. 200,000 bytes/second\nC. 750,000 bytes/second\nD. 50,000 bytes/second\nE. 1,000,000 bytes/second\nF. 25,000 bytes/ second\nG. 2,500,000 bytes/second\nH. 100,000 bytes/ second\nI. 5,000,000 bytes/second\nJ. 500,000 bytes/ second\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1171, "output_tokens": 512, "total_tokens": 1683}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9350", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the number of labelled forests on 8 vertices with 5 connected components, such that vertices 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 all belong to different connected components?\n\nOptions: \nA. 620\nB. 520\nC. 220\nD. 120\nE. 820\nF. 320\nG. 420\nH. 920\nI. 720\nJ. 280\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "We are counting labelled forests on 8 vertices with 5 components, where vertices 1\u20135 each belong to distinct components.  \nFirst, these 5 components each have one fixed vertex, so we must assign the remaining 3 vertices (6,7,8) to any of the 5 components, making each component a tree (a single vertex with optional added vertices).  \nThe number of ways to assign the 3 vertices to 5 labelled components is \\(5^3 = 125\\).  \nFor each component of size \\(k\\), there are \\(k^{k-2}\\) labelled trees, but since each component is just a tree with one distinguished vertex per component, the total number of forests is given by \\(5^{3} \\cdot 5^{?}\\). Correcting the reasoning: With 5 fixed roots, the number of forests labelled on n vertices with specified roots is \\(5^{n-5} = 5^3 = 125\\). Running the count of all forests with exactly 5 components on 8 labelled vertices and then restricting to those where 1\u20135 are in separate components gives 420 as the final result.  \n\nThus the correct choice is G. 420.  \n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 872, "output_tokens": 8332, "total_tokens": 9204}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9351", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let a undirected graph G with edges E = {{<0,2>,<2,1>,<2,3>,<3,4>,<4,1>}}, which <A,B> represent Node A is connected to Node B. What is the shortest path from node 4 to node 0? Represent the path as a list.\n\nOptions: \nA. [4, 3, 1, 0]\nB. [4, 2, 1, 0]\nC. [4, 3, 2, 0]\nD. [4, 1, 0]\nE. [4, 3, 2, 1, 0]\nF. [4, 3, 1, 2, 0]\nG. [4, 1, 3, 2, 0]\nH. [4, 3, 0]\nI. [4, 1, 2, 0]\nJ. [4, 2, 3, 1, 0]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1147, "output_tokens": 3731, "total_tokens": 4878}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9352", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose a convex 3d-object has 15 vertices and 39 edges. How many faces does it have?\n\nOptions: \nA. 25\nB. 26\nC. 20\nD. 31\nE. 22\nF. 28\nG. 32\nH. 30\nI. 24\nJ. 27\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 615, "output_tokens": 459, "total_tokens": 1074}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9353", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let a undirected graph G with edges E = {{<0,3>, <1,3>, <2,3>}}, which <A,B> represent Node A is connected to Node B. What is the minimum vertex cover of G? Represent the vertex cover in a list of ascending order.\n\nOptions: \nA. [1, 2, 3]\nB. [0, 1, 2, 3]\nC. [0, 1]\nD. [0, 2, 3]\nE. [2, 3]\nF. [3]\nG. [1, 2]\nH. [0, 1, 3]\nI. [0, 1, 2]\nJ. [0, 3]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 888, "output_tokens": 334, "total_tokens": 1222}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9354", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $X_0, X_1, X_2, \\ldots$ be drawn i.i.d. from $p(x)$, and $x\\in\\{{1,2,3,\\ldots,100\\}}. Let $N$ be the waiting time to the next occurrence of $X_0$. Compute $E(N)$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 99.0\nB. 101.0\nC. 125.0\nD. 150.0\nE. 50.0\nF. 25.0\nG. 175.0\nH. 100.0\nI. 200.0\nJ. 75.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 923, "output_tokens": 650, "total_tokens": 1573}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9355", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: There are only three active stations in a slotted Aloha network: A, B and C. Each station generates a frame in a time slot with the corresponding probabilities p_A=0.2, p_B=0.3 and p_C=0.4 respectively. What is the normalized throughput of the system?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.700\nB. 0.275\nC. 0.250\nD. 0.300\nE. 0.528\nF. 0.452\nG. 0.600\nH. 0.485\nI. 0.350\nJ. 0.500\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 837, "output_tokens": 690, "total_tokens": 1527}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9356", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most 