a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9387", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Write the necessary statement function(s) to compute the area of a triangle, given 3 sides. Use Hero's formula.\n\nOptions: \nA. S(A,B,C) = SQRT((A + B + C) / 2), AREA(A,B,C,X) = X*(X-A)*(X-B)*(X-C)\nB. S(A,B,C) = (A + B + C) / 2, AREA(A,B,C,X) = SQRT(X*(X+A)*(X+B)*(X+C))\nC. S(A,B,C) = (A + B + C), AREA(A,B,C,X) = SQRT((X-A)*(X-B)*(X-C))\nD. S(A,B,C) = (A + B - C) / 2, AREA(A,B,C,X) = SQRT(X*(X-A)*(X-B)*(X-C))\nE. S(A,B,C) = (A^2 + B^2 + C^2) / 2, AREA(A,B,C,X) = SQRT(X*(X-A)*(X-B)*(X-C))\nF. S(A,B,C) = 0.5 * (A + B + C), AREA(A,B,C,X) = SQRT(X*(X-A)*(X-B)*(X-C))\nG. AREA(A,B,C) = A*B*C\nH. S(A,B,C) = (A + B + C) / 3, AREA(A,B,C,X) = SQRT(X*(X-A)*(X-B)*(X-C))\nI. S(A,B,C) = (A + B + C) / 2, AREA(A,B,C,X) = X / ((X-A)*(X-B)*(X-C))\nJ. S(A,B,C) = A + B + C, AREA(A,B,C,X) = X*(X-A)*(X-B)*(X-C)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1803, "output_tokens": 556, "total_tokens": 2359}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9392", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question is based on the following declarations: String strA = \"CARROT\", strB = \"Carrot\", strC = \"car\"; Given that all uppercase letters precede all lowercase letters when considering alphabetical order, which is true?\n\nOptions: \nA. strC.compareTo(strB) > 0 && strB.compareTo(strA) > 0\nB. strA.compareTo(strC) > 0 && strC.compareTo(strB) < 0\nC. strB.compareTo(strC) < 0 && strB.compareTo(strA) > 0\nD. !(strB.compareTo(strA) == 0) && strA.compareTo(strB) > 0\nE. strB.compareTo(strC) > 0 && strA.compareTo(strB) < 0\nF. strC.compareTo(strB) < 0 && strB.compareTo(strA) < 0\nG. strA.compareTo(strB) < 0 && strB.compareTo(strC) > 0\nH. !(strA.compareTo(strB) == 0) && strB.compareTo(strA) < 0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}.  \n\nSince uppercase letters come before lowercase, \"CARROT\" (strA) is less than \"Carrot\" (strB), so strA.compareTo(strB) is negative (not zero) and strB.compareTo(strA) is positive, making option H true. The other options incorrectly compare the strings based on the given ordering rules.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1500, "output_tokens": 1177, "total_tokens": 2677}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9393", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An Insect class is to be written, containing the following data fields: age, which will be initialized to 0 when an Insect is constructed. nextAvailableID, which will be initialized to 0 outside the constructor and incremented each time an Insect is constructed. idNum, which will be initialized to the current value of nextAvailableID when an Insect is constructed. position, which will be initialized to the location in a garden where the Insect is placed when it is constructed. direction, which will be initialized to the direction the Insect is facing when placed in the garden. Which variable in the Insect class should be static?\n\nOptions: \nA. position and direction\nB. age and idNum\nC. All of them\nD. idNum\nE. nextAvailableID and position\nF. None of them\nG. direction\nH. position\nI. age\nJ. nextAvailableID\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1012, "output_tokens": 281, "total_tokens": 1293}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9394", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Bob writes down a number between 1 and 1,000. Mary must identify that number by asking \"yes/no\" questions of Bob. Mary knows that Bob always tells the truth. If Mary uses an optimal strategy, then she will determine the answer at the end of exactly how many questions in the worst case?\n\nOptions: \nA. 250\nB. 20\nC. 500\nD. 100\nE. 2\nF. 1,000\nG. 999\nH. 50\nI. 10\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 768, "output_tokens": 352, "total_tokens": 1120}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9397", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One approach to handling fuzzy logic data might be to design a computer using ternary (base-3) logic so that data could be stored as \u201ctrue,\u201d \u201cfalse,\u201d and \u201cunknown.\u201d If each ternary logic element is called a flit, how many flits are required to represent at least 256 different values?\n\nOptions: \nA. 9\nB. 4\nC. 2\nD. 11\nE. 10\nF. 5\nG. 3\nH. 6\nI. 8\nJ. 7\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 744, "output_tokens": 437, "total_tokens": 1181}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9399", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let us say that we have computed the gradient of our cost function and stored it in a vector g. What is the cost of one gradient descent update given the gradient?\n\nOptions: \nA. O(DN)\nB. O(D^3)\nC. O(1)\nD. O(N^3)\nE. O(ND^2)\nF. O(ND)\nG. O(N)\nH. O(N^2)\nI. O(D)\nJ. O(D^2)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 648, "output_tokens": 311, "total_tokens": 959}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9405", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $X$ be uniformly distributed over $\\{{1, 2, \\ldots, m\\}}$. Assume $m=2^n$ . We ask random questions: Is $X\\in S_1$? Is $X\\in S_2$? ... until only one integer remains. All $2^m$ subsets of $\\{{1, 2, \\ldots, m\\}}$ are equally likely. Suppose we ask $n+\\sqrt{{n}}$ random questions. Use Markov's inequality to find the probability of error (one or more wrong objects remaining) when $n$ goes to infinity?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.3\nB. 0.4\nC. 0.1\nD. 0.0\nE. 0.7\nF. 0.2\nG. 0.5\nH. 1.0\nI. 0.8\nJ. 0.6\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1079, "output_tokens": 623, "total_tokens": 1702}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9406", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Given a color image of size 28 x 28 x 3 pixels, how many convolutional filters in the first layer of a Convolutional Neural Network if the first layer's output tensor has size 26 x 26 x 64?\n\nOptions: \nA. 96\nB. 512\nC. 1024\nD. 64\nE. 48\nF. 72\nG. 256\nH. 32\nI. 128\nJ. 192\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"i