: \nA. 1.25\nB. 1.0\nC. 2.0\nD. 1.5\nE. 0.5\nF. 0.75\nG. 0.9\nH. 0.0\nI. 0.25\nJ. 0.1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 676, "output_tokens": 496, "total_tokens": 1172}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9460", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If p(x) is the minimal-degree interpolating polynomial for the real-valued function f(x) at the n + 1 distinct real numbers x0, .... xn what is the maximum possible degree of p(x)?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2n\nB. n + 1\nC. 2n + 1\nD. n\u00b3\nE. n\u00b2 + 1\nF. n/2\nG. n\nH. n - 1\nI. n\u00b2\nJ. n + 2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 580, "output_tokens": 304, "total_tokens": 884}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9407", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The equation of a digital filter is given by $y(n)=1 / 3(x(n)+x(n-1)+x(n-2))$, where $y(n)$ and $x(n)$ are, respectively, the nth samples of the output and input signals. Determine the pole(s) of the filter.\n\nOptions: \nA. 1/2\nB. 3\nC. -3\nD. -2\nE. 0\nF. -1\nG. -1/2\nH. 1\nI. 1/3\nJ. 2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 630, "output_tokens": 303, "total_tokens": 933}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9321", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A cascade of $n$ identical independent binary symmetric channels each with raw error probability $p$, and $0<p<1$. What is the capacity of the cascade when $n$ goes to infinity?\n\nOptions: \nA. $n$\nB. 0.0\nC. 1.0\nD. $p$\nE. $\\frac{{1}}{{2}}$\nF. $n(1-p)$\nG. $2p$\nH. $1-p$\nI. $p^n$\nJ. $\\sqrt{{p}}$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 604, "output_tokens": 475, "total_tokens": 1079}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9471", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Statement 1| A U2F USB dongle prevents malware on the user\u2019s computer from stealing the user\u2019s second factor to authenticate as that user even when the user\u2019s computer is turned off. Statement 2| A server