), 8 (15), 9 (2). Applying Otsu's method to maximize between-class variance yields the best separation when the threshold lies between 5 and 6, specifically at the integer value 5.00, which corresponds to the partition {3,4,5} vs. {6,7,8,9}. This threshold is appropriate for segmenting the image into two regions based on the histogram.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1866, "output_tokens": 13345, "total_tokens": 15211}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9310", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Adding more basis functions in a linear model, pick the most probably option:\n\nOptions: \nA. Decreases model bias\nB. Increases estimation bias\nC. Doesn\u2019t affect bias and variance\nD. Increases both bias and variance\nE. Decreases variance\nF. Decreases both bias and variance\nG. Doesn\u2019t affect estimation bias\nH. Increases model bias\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 644, "output_tokens": 338, "total_tokens": 982}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9279", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let F: K \\times R \\to MF:K\u00d7R\u2192M be a secure PRF. For m \\in Mm\u2208M define E(k,m) = \\big[ r \\gets R,\\ \\text{{output }} \\big(r,\\ F(k,r) \\oplus m\\big)\\ \\big]E(k,m)=[r\u2190R, output (r, F(k,r)\u2295m) ] Is EE symantically secure under CPA?\n\nOptions: \nA. It depends on the size of R\nB. Yes, but only if R is large enough so r never repeats (w.h.p)\nC. Yes, but only if M is small enough so m never repeats (w.h.p)\nD. No, unless F is a weak PRF\nE. No, unless F is a strong PRF\nF. Yes, but only if K is large enough so k never repeats (w.h.p)\nG. It depends on the size of K\nH. No, there is always a CPA attack on this system\nI. It depends on what F is used\nJ. Yes, whenever F is a secure PRF\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 992, "output_tokens": 496, "total_tokens": 1488}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9268", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In building a linear regression model for a particular data set, you observe the coefficient of one of the features having a relatively high negative value. This suggests that\n\nOptions: \nA. The model will perform better without this feature\nB. This feature does not have a strong effect on the model (should be ignored)\nC. It is not possible to comment on the importance of this feature without additional information\nD. This feature has a strong effect on the model (should be retained)\nE. This feature negatively impacts the model (should be removed)\nF. The model is overfitting due to this feature\nG. This feature has a weak negative correlation with the target variable\nH. The negative coefficient value is a sign of data leakage\nI. Nothing can be determined.\nJ. This feature has a strong positive correlation with the target variable\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1152, "output_tokens": 428, "total_tokens": 1580}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9386", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is wrong in the following array declaration? int my _ array (200);\n\nOptions: \nA. The datatype for the array elements is not specified\nB. The array is not initialized\nC. The array size is too large\nD. The semicolon is missing at the end of the declaration\nE. The array size should be a constant expression\nF. The array size must be defined after the variable name\nG. The number of subscripts is not enclosed in square brackets\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 736, "output_tokens": 328, "total_tokens": 1064}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9345", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Assume that a TLS connection has been established successfully between a client and a server. Establishing the session included checking the server certificate and executing a DiffieHelmann exchange, but the client did not provide a client certificate. Further, assume that the client and server are honest, that the client and server don\u2019t leak their keys, and that the cryptography is good. Which of the following attacks does TLS protect against?\n1. An attacker replaying bytes that a client sent earlier.\n2. An attacker impersonating the server.\n\nOptions: \nA. True, True\nB. True for the first attack, but only if the server leaks its keys\nC. True, True for both attacks but only if the client provides a client certificate\nD. True for the first attack, False for the second attack\nE. False, False for both attacks\nF. False, False\nG. False for the first attack, but True for the second attack if the cryptography is not good\nH. False, True\nI. True, False\nJ. False for the first attack, True for the second attack\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1287, "output_tokens": 410, "total_tokens": 1697}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9193", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose sharing of tiles in a multilevel directory structure is achieved with directory entries that are links pointing to a node containing information about a shared file. Information in this node includes (1) the owner of the file, (2) a count of the number of links to the tile, and (3) the disk block numbers of the file. What is a primary drawback to this approach to sharing?\n\nOptions: \nA. If the owner modifies the file, another user who does not share will see the changes.\nB. If the owner changes the permissions of the file, other users will not be able to access it.\nC. If the owner changes the count of the number of links to the file, other users will lose access.\nD. If the owner renames the file, other users will not be able to access it.\nE. If the owner encrypts the file, other users will lose access.\nF. If the owner moves the file to a new disk block, all links to the file will become invalid.\nG. If the owner is allowed to delete a file, dangling links may result.\nH. If any user who shares the file appends to it, others who share it will not be able to access the new disk blocks.\nI. If any user who shares the file modifies it, the owner will not be able to see the changes.\nJ. If the owner logs out of the system, all links to the file will become invalid.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1596, "output_tokens": 438, "total_tokens": 2034}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9173", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let I = (S,V)I=(S,V) be a MAC. Suppose S(k,m)S(k,m) is always 5 bits long. Can this MAC be secure?\n\nOptions: \nA. Yes, the attacker cannot generate a valid tag for any message\nB. Yes, the PRG is pseudorandom\nC. No, an attacker can simply guess the tag for messages\nD. No, the attacker can simply guess the key\nE. Yes, the key length is sufficiently long\nF. No, the key length is not long enough\nG. Yes, the tag length is sufficiently long\nH. It depends on the complexity of the PRG\nI. It depends on the details of the MAC\nJ. It depends on the encryption algorithm used in the MAC\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 892, "output_tokens": 311, "total_tokens": 1203}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9470", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Assume that a TLS connection has been established successfully between a client and a server. Establishing the session included checking the server certificate and executing a DiffieHelmann exchange, but the client did not provide a client certificate. Further, assume that the client and server are honest, that the client and server don\u2019t leak their keys, and that the cryptography is good. Which of the following attacks does TLS protect against?\n1. An attacker replacing bytes sent by a client with bytes of the attacker\u2019s own choosing.\n2. An attacker reading the plaintext bytes sent by a client.\n\nOptions: \nA. False, True\nB. False, False\nC. False, Partly True\nD. Partly True, False\nE. True, False\nF. True, Partly False\nG. True, Partly True\nH. Partly False, True\nI. True, True\nJ. Partly True, True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1124, "output_tokens": 340, "total_tokens": 1464}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9277", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose Unix did not provide a way of passing file descriptors between processes, but still allowed inheriting file descriptors from a parent on fork and exec. What aspects of the OKWS design would break without file descriptor passing?\n1. It would be impossible for services to get a TCP connection to the client web browser.\n2. It would be impossible for okd to run as a non-root user.\n\nOptions: \nA. True, False\nB. Partially false, True\nC. Partially false, False\nD. True, True\nE. Partially true, True\nF. True, Partially true\nG. Partially true, False\nH. False, True\nI. False, Partially true\nJ. False, False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 920, "output_tokens": 408, "total_tokens": 1328}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9298", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A search engine has a trend-tracking feature that provides information on how popular a search term is. The data can be filtered by geographic region, date, and category. Categories include arts and entertainment, computers and electronics, games, news, people and society, shopping, sports, and travel. Which of the following questions is LEAST likely to be answerable using the trends feature?\n\nOptions: \nA. In which political candidates are people interested?\nB. Which region of the country has the greatest number of people searching for opera performances?\nC. What is the cost of a certain electronics product?\nD. In what month does a particular sport receive the most searches?\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 937, "output_tokens": 267, "total_tokens": 1204}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9469", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The openSSL implementation described in \u201cRemote Timing Attacks are Practical\u201d (by Brumley and Boneh) uses the following performance optimizations: Chinese Remainder (CR), Montgomery Representation (MR), Karatsuba Multiplication (KM), and Repeated squaring and Sliding windows (RS). Which of the following options would close the timing channel attack described in the paper if you turned the listed optimizations off?\n1. RS and KM\n2. RS and MR\n\nOptions: \nA. True, True\nB. False, False\nC. False, True\nD. True, False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 828, "output_tokens": 609, "total_tokens": 1437}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9381", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Given image \\begin{{tabular}}{{|llll|}} \\hline 7 & 1 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 7 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 6 & 5 & 7 \\\\ \\hline \\end{{tabular}} , and the bit-depth of the image is 4. Suppose you want to use the thresholding technique to segment the image. What is the appropriate threshold value based on the histogram of the image? Follow the following rule when you do thresholding or grouping: pixel $(i, j) \\in$ Group A pixels if $g(i, j) \\leq$ current threshold $\\mathrm{{T}}$; pixel $(i, j) \\in$ Group B pixels otherwise, where $g(i, j)$ is the intensity value of pixel $(i, j)$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 4\nB. 6\nC. 8\nD. 9\nE. 1\nF. 7\nG. 5\nH. 2\nI. 3\nJ. 0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 936, "output_tokens": 628, "total_tokens": 1564}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9317", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The openSSL implementation described in \u201cRemote Timing Attacks are Practical\u201d (by Brumley and Boneh) uses the following performance optimizations: Chinese Remainder (CR), Montgomery Representation (MR), Karatsuba Multiplication (KM), and Repeated squaring and Sliding windows (RS). Which of the following options would close the timing channel attack described in the paper if you turned the listed optimizations off?\n1. CR and MR\n2. CR\n\nOptions: \nA. KM and RS\nB. True, True\nC. False, True\nD. True, False\nE. False, False\nF. MR and CR\nG. KM, MR, RS, CR\nH. RS and MR\nI. KM, RS, CR\nJ. MR, KM, RS\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 910, "output_tokens": 644, "total_tokens": 1554}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9158", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mergesort works by splitting a list of n numbers in half, sorting each half recursively, and merging the two halves. Which of the following data structures will allow mergesort to work in O(n log n) time?\nI. A singly linked list\nII. A doubly linked list\nIII. An array\n\nOptions: \nA. nan\nB. III only\nC. I and II only\nD. I, II, and III\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 640, "output_tokens": 429, "total_tokens": 1069}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9178", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $X$ be uniformly distributed over $\\{{1, 2, \\ldots, 256\\}}$. We ask random questions: Is $X\\in S_1$? Is $X\\in S_2$? ... until only one integer remains. All $2^256$ subsets of $\\{{1, 2, \\ldots, 256\\}}$ are equally likely. How many deterministic questions are needed to determine $X$?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1024\nB. 64\nC. 1\nD. 512\nE. 8\nF. 16\nG. 4\nH. 32\nI. 256\nJ. 128\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 672, "output_tokens": 440, "total_tokens": 1112}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9281", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose Unix did not provide a way of passing file descriptors between processes, but still allowed inheriting file descriptors from a parent on fork and exec. What aspects of the OKWS design would break without file descriptor passing?\n1. It would be impossible for services to send messages to oklogd.\n2. It would be impossible for services to get a TCP connection to a database proxy.\n\nOptions: \nA. False, True\nB. False, False\nC. True, True\nD. True, False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 768, "output_tokens": 479, "total_tokens": 1247}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9100", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To compute the matrix product M_1M_2, where M_1 has p rows and q columns and where M_2 has q rows and r columns, takes time proportional to pqr, and the result is a matrix of p rows and r columns. Consider the product of three matrices N_1N_2N_3 that have, respectively, w rows and x columns, x rows and y columns, and y rows and z columns. Under what condition will it take less time to compute the product as (N_1N_2)N_3 (i.e., multiply the first two matrices first) than to compute it as N_1(N_2 N_3)?\n\nOptions: \nA. w > z\nB. 1/w + 1/y > 1/x + 1/z\nC. y > z\nD. 1/x + 1/z < 1/w + 1/y\nE. 1/w + 1/z > 1/x + 1/y\nF. There is no such condition; i.e., they will always take the same time.\nG. x > y\nH. 1/w + 1/x < 1/y + 1/z\nI. 1/x + 1/y > 1/w + 1/z\nJ. x < y\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1064, "output_tokens": 383, "total_tokens": 1447}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9461", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider a computer system in which processes can request and release one or more resources. Once a process has been granted a resource, the process has exclusive use of that resource until it is released. If a process requests a resource that is already in use, the process enters a queue for that resource, waiting until the resource is available. Which of the following will NOT deal effectively with the problem of deadlock?\n\nOptions: \nA. Giving priorities to processes and ordering the wait queues by priority\nB. Numbering the resources and requiring that processes request resources in order of increasing number\nC. Having a process request all its required resources when it first begins, and restarting if it cannot obtain them all\nD. Allowing processes to request resources only in order of decreasing number\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1124, "output_tokens": 405, "total_tokens": 1529}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9362", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An integer c is a common divisor of two integers x and y if and only if c is a divisor of x and c is a divisor of y. Which of the following sets of integers could possibly be the set of all common divisors of two integers?\n\nOptions: \nA. {{-10, -5, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 5, 10}}\nB. {{-6, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 6}}\nC. {{-6, -3, -2, -1, 1, 2, 3, 6}}\nD. {{-6, -3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 6}}\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 928, "output_tokens": 448, "total_tokens": 1376}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9089", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let a undirected graph G with edges E = {{<0,2>, <2,4>, <3,4>, <1,4>}}, which <A,B> represent Node A is connected to Node B. What is the minimum vertex cover of G if 0 is one of vertex cover? Represent the vertex cover in a list of ascending order.\n\nOptions: \nA. [0, 1, 2]\nB. [0, 2, 4]\nC. [0, 1, 4]\nD. [0, 4]\nE. [0, 3, 4]\nF. [0, 1, 3]\nG. [0, 1]\nH. [0, 2, 3]\nI. [0, 2]\nJ. [0, 3]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 688, "output_tokens": 376, "total_tokens": 1064}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9290", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the difference between a basic assemblerlanguage macroinstruction and a machine or imperative instruction. Indicate what, if any, relationship exists between them.\n\nOptions: \nA. Assembler instructions handle memory management, while macro instructions are solely for input/output operations.\nB. Assembler instructions are pre-defined operations in a CPU's instruction set, while macro instructions are user-defined and often vary between different assemblies.\nC. Macro instructions are complex codes that cannot be translated to object code\nD. Macro instructions and assembler instructions have no relation\nE. Macro instructions are typically used for arithmetic operations, whereas assembler instructions are used for control flow.\nF. Macro instructions are a form of high-level programming language, while assembler instructions are low-level codes directly executed by the hardware.\nG. Assembler instruction is a larger set than the macro\nH. Macro instructions are a sequence of assembler instructions that perform a specific task, with no need for expansion.\nI. Macro instructions are single abbreviations for groups of instructions, which must be expanded before translation to object code. Assembler instruction is usually a subset of the macro.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1461, "output_tokens": 376, "total_tokens": 1837}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9409", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let a undirected graph G with edges E = {{<0,1>,<4,1>,<2,0>,<2,1>,<2,3>,<1,3>}}, which <A,B> represent Node A is connected to Node B. What is the minimum vertex cover of G? Represent the vertex cover in a list of ascending order.\n\nOptions: \nA. [0, 1]\nB. [1, 3, 4]\nC. [1, 2, 3]\nD. [2, 3, 4]\nE. [0, 2, 4]\nF. [0, 1, 2]\nG. [0, 4]\nH. [1, 2]\nI. [2, 3]\nJ. [0, 2, 3]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 744, "output_tokens": 721, "total_tokens": 1465}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9189", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A student is recording a song on her computer. When the recording is finished, she saves a copy on her computer. The student notices that the saved copy is of lower sound quality than the original recording. Which of the following could be a possible explanation for the difference in sound quality?\n\nOptions: \nA. The song was saved using a higher quality compression technique.\nB. The song was saved using more bits per second than the original song.\nC. The song was saved on a part of the computer's hard drive that has less storage capacity.\nD. The song was saved using fewer bits per second than the original song.\nE. The student's computer has a virus that reduces the quality of saved files.\nF. The song was saved using a lossless compression technique.\nG. The student's computer speakers are not functioning correctly.\nH. The original recording was disrupted by background noise.\nI. Some information is lost every time a file is saved from one location on a computer to another location.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1304, "output_tokens": 247, "total_tokens": 1551}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9371", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Statement 1| The kernel density estimator is equivalent to performing kernel regression with the value Yi = 1/n at each point Xi in the original data set. Statement 2| The depth of a learned decision tree can be larger than the number of training examples used to create the tree.\n\nOptions: \nA. Both Statements are context-dependent\nB. True, True\nC. Statement 1 is True only for non-parametric Kernels, Statement 2 is False\nD. Both Statements are partially True\nE. False, False\nF. Statement 1 is True only for Gaussian Kernels, Statement 2 is False\nG. Statement 1 is False, Statement 2 is True only for Binary Decision Trees\nH. False, True\nI. True, False\nJ. Statement 1 is False, Statement 2 is True only for Multiclass Decision Trees\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1029, "output_tokens": 431, "total_tokens": 1460}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9378", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Statement 1| The ReLU's gradient is zero for $x<0$, and the sigmoid gradient $\\sigma(x)(1-\\sigma(x))\\le \\frac{{1}}{{4}}$ for all $x$. Statement 2| The sigmoid has a continuous gradient and the ReLU has a discontinuous gradient.\n\nOptions: \nA. Statement 1 is true for x < 0, statement 2 is false for x \u2260 0\nB. True, True\nC. True, False\nD. Statement 1 is only true for x > 0, statement 2 is always false\nE. False for statement 1, statement 2 is true if x \u2260 0\nF. Statement 1 is only false for x > 0, statement 2 is always true\nG. False for statement 1, statement 2 is true if x = 0\nH. False, True\nI. False, False\nJ. True for statement 1, statement 2 depends on the function\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 988, "output_tokens": 447, "total_tokens": 1435}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9396", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Of the following, which gives the best upper bound for the value of f(N) where f is a solution to the recurrence f(2N + 1) = f(2N) = f(N) + log N for N >= 1, with f(1) = 0?\n\nOptions: \nA. O(N log(log N))\nB. O(N^2)\nC. O(N)\nD. O(log N)\nE. O((log N)^2)\nF. O(N log N)\nG. O(2^N)\nH. O(1)\nI. O(log N) + 0(1)\nJ. O(N^2 log N)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 628, "output_tokens": 425, "total_tokens": 1053}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for