d-first millennium BCE\nG. At the start of the first millennium BCE\nH. Toward the end of the third millennium BCE\nI. At the start of the third millennium BCE\nJ. In the middle of the third millennium BCE\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 820, "output_tokens": 310, "total_tokens": 1130}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9856", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Singer claims that famine relief organizations direct our aid to distant refugees:\n\nOptions: \nA. with a focus on quantity over quality, leading to possible misallocation.\nB. very inefficiently, and are therefore not worth donating to.\nC. with a high level of bureaucracy and corruption, therefore not recommended.\nD. more effectively than we could get it to our close neighbors.\nE. extremely efficiently, making them the only viable option for aid distribution.\nF. very effectively, but only in certain regions.\nG. moderately efficiently, although there may be better alternatives.\nH. almost as effectively as we could get it to our close neighbors.\nI. effectively, but at a high operational cost.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1107, "output_tokens": 325, "total_tokens": 1432}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", 