 provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to Butler, it is impossible to:\n\nOptions: \nA. do that which is good and not to approve of it.\nB. be motivated by genuine benevolence.\nC. approve of the actions of others without understanding them.\nD. act without a sense of self-interest.\nE. feel empathy without taking action.\nF. approve of the actions of others without imitating them.\nG. have a sense of morality without having a conscience.\nH. act in ways that contradict societal norms.\nI. do something of which one does not oneself approve.\nJ. perceive the good without desiring it.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 831, "output_tokens": 328, "total_tokens": 1159}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9583", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which branch of Judaism founded by Zacharias Frankel is known for its \"Positive-Historical Judaism\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Orthodox\nB. Sephardic\nC. Conservative\nD. Hasidic\nE. Reconstructionism\nF. Secular\nG. Liberal\nH. Haredi\nI. Ultra-Orthodox\nJ. Reformed\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 556, "output_tokens": 215, "total_tokens": 771}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9663", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Foot's Rescue I and Rescue II cases are intended to\n\nOptions: \nA. contrast originating a harmful sequence with allowing a harmful sequence to continue.\nB. all of the above\nC. demonstrate the difference between passive and active harm.\nD. argue that good intentions can result in harmful sequences.\nE. show that harmful sequences can be stopped by good intentions.\nF. contrast intentional harm with accidental harm.\nG. argue that all harmful sequences are the result of evil intentions.\nH. highlight the importance of intentions in determining the morality of an action.\nI. show that evil intentions always involve the origination of harmful sequences.\nJ. contrast evil intentions with good intentions.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Foot's Rescue I and Rescue II cases are classic examples used to illustrate the moral distinction between actively causing harm (originating a harmful sequence) and passively allowing harm (allowing a harmful sequence to continue). This aligns with option A, which directly captures this distinction using Foot's own terminology. Options like C (passive vs. active harm) are similar but less precise, while others misrepresent the cases' purpose.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 991, "output_tokens": 3127, "total_tokens": 4118}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9538", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  How does the Egyptian composition Ludul Bel Nemequi (\"I will praise the Lord of wisdom) portray Marduk?\n\nOptions: \nA. Indifferent and detached\nB. Judging and vengeful\nC. Peaceful and generous\nD. Loving and forgiving\nE. Humble and subservient\nF. Proud and self-absorbed\nG. Transcendent and immanent\nH. Wrathful and merciful\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 628, "output_tokens": 426, "total_tokens": 1054}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9662", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Thomson discusses a different version of the violinist case wherein the violinist only needs to use your kidneys for one hour to survive. Her own view about this case is that\n\nOptions: \nA. because the violinist's life is in danger, you have an absolute moral obligation to let them use your kidneys, regardless of the duration.\nB. you have no obligation to let the violinist use your kidneys, but if you choose to do so, the violinist has the right to use them for that hour.\nC. you have the right to disconnect the violinist at any point, regardless of the consequences for the violinist.\nD. because you ought to let the violinist use your kidneys for that hour, we should conclude that he or she has a right to use your kidneys for that hour.\nE. even though you ought to let the violinist use your kidneys for that hour, we should not conclude that he or she has a right to use your kidneys for that hour.\nF. you have no obligation to let the violinist use your kidneys for that hour.\nG. you have an obligation to let the violinist use your kidneys for that hour, but the violinist does not have a right to use your kidneys.\nH. the violinist has an obligation to disconnect him- or herself before that hour is over.\nI. you have an obligation to let the violinist use your kidneys for that hour, and the violinist also has a right to use your kidneys.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1562, "output_tokens": 410, "total_tokens": 1972}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9653", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the antecedent of the following conditional proposition: The Bees win their first game only if either the Aardvarks or the Chipmunks do not win their first games.\n\nOptions: \nA. The Bees do not win their first game.\nB. Both the Aardvarks and the Chipmunks do not win their first games.\nC. The Chipmunks do not win their first game.\nD. The Chipmunks win their first game.\nE. Both the Aardvarks and the Chipmunks win their first games.\nF. Either the Aardvarks or the Chipmunks do not win their first games.\nG. The Aardvarks do not win their first game.\nH. The Bees win their first game.\nI. The Aardvarks win their first game.\nJ. Either the Aardvarks or the Chipmunks win their first games.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1008, "output_tokens": 294, "total_tokens": 1302}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9718", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Aristotle says  that what makes things be what they are--their essence--does not exist apart from individ-uals that exist in the world.  So if all the members of a species were destroyed, then their essence or form:\n\nOptions: \nA. would remain preserved in the memories of the remaining species.\nB. would not be destroyed because there was no essence or form originally to be destroyed; there are only individuals, not universal essences or natures of things.\nC. would evolve into a different form or essence.\nD. would be destroyed only if the species was eliminated by unnatural causes.\nE. would be absorbed by another species.\nF. would transform into the essence of another existing species.\nG. would be destroyed only if there were no one around to remember the species.\nH. would exist as long as there are traces or remnants of the species left in the world.\nI. would continue existing (as with Plato's Forms) in some other realm of being.\nJ. would likewise be destroyed.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1288, "output_tokens": 355, "total_tokens": 1643}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9847", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: By \u201canimal motion,\u201d Hobbes means:\n\nOptions: \nA. instinctive behavior, such as nursing young.\nB. irrational behavior.\nC. involuntary operations such as heartbeat and breathing.\nD. the physical actions and reactions of animals.\nE. human behavior that is driven by basic needs.\nF. all forms of non-human animal behavior.\nG. the process by which animals move from one place to another.\nH. behavior that is driven by fear or survival instincts.\nI. all voluntary behavior.\nJ. the movement and behavior of animals in the wild.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 737, "output_tokens": 315, "total_tokens": 1052}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9501", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Baron cites a summary of Ali Soufan's Senate testimony to suggest that\n\nOptions: \nA. torture is always wrong without exception.\nB. torture is the most effective method of interrogation.\nC. successful interrogation may not require torture.\nD. all successful interrogations involve some form of torture.\nE. Ali Soufan was subjected to torture during his testimony.\nF. Ali Soufan denounced the use of torture entirely in his testimony.\nG. endorsing a single act of torture requires endorsing torture as a practice.\nH. Ali Soufan supports the use of torture in interrogation.\nI. torture can be ethically justified in some situations.\nJ. torture works in only limited situations.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 941, "output_tokens": 350, "total_tokens": 1291}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9817", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the antecedent of the following conditional proposition: The university raises tuition if, and only if, both the governor approves of it and the board of trustees recommends it.\n\nOptions: \nA. The university raises tuition.\nB. The governor approves of it.\nC. The board of trustees recommends it.\nD. None of the above\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 606, "output_tokens": 479, "total_tokens": 1085}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9810", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to Parfit, both Taurek and Lewis assume that for there to be a \u201csum of pain,\u201d it must be:\n\nOptions: \nA. all be avoidable.\nB. only felt by multiple people at different times.\nC. all be experienced in the same way.\nD. all be of the same intensity.\nE. all felt by a single person.\nF. all be caused by a single source.\nG. all be caused by multiple sources.\nH. all be caused by a single event.\nI. all felt at a single time.\nJ. all of the above.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 752, "output_tokens": 380, "total_tokens": 1132}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9896", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  According to Lukianoff and Haidt, the recent trend to uncover microaggressions encourages\n\nOptions: \nA. students to confabulate reasons.\nB. the pursuit of justice by marking out racism, sexism, and classism.\nC. labeling, by assigning global negative traits to persons.\nD. universities to bear overly burdensome legal obligations.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 614, "output_tokens": 410, "total_tokens": 1024}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9669", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Van den Haag thinks that we can't know whether a murderer who receives the death penalty\n\nOptions: \nA. is morally degraded.\nB. is remorseful for his actions.\nC. is a threat to society.\nD. is justly punished.\nE. is mentally stable.\nF. is a repeat offender.\nG. is punished in a humane manner.\nH. suffers more than the victim.\nI. is punished excessively.\nJ. is capable of rehabilitation.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 651, "output_tokens": 279, "total_tokens": 930}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9922", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the antecedent of the following conditional proposition: The university raises tuition only if both the governor approves of it and the board of trustees recommends it.\n\nOptions: \nA. The board of trustees does not recommend it.\nB. The governor approves of it.\nC. The board of trustees recommends it.\nD. The governor disapproves of it and the board of trustees does not recommend it.\nE. The governor approves of it and the board of trustees recommends it.\nF. The university does not raise tuition.\nG. Both the governor and the board of trustees do not approve of it.\nH. The university raises tuition.\nI. The governor disapproves of it.\nJ. The governor approves of it or the board of trustees recommends it.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 987, "output_tokens": 360, "total_tokens": 1347}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9930", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  In the context of Gardiner's article, \"the fragmentation of agency\" refers to what?\n\nOptions: \nA. an agent's inability to acknowledge his or her contribution to climate change\nB. the fragmentation of the effects of greenhouse gas emissions across generations\nC. the vast number of individuals and agents who contribute to climate change\nD. the idea that it's not rational for each individual to restrict his or her own pollution\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 703, "output_tokens": 318, "total_tokens": 1021}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9532", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  According to Singer, international corporations that deal with corrupt dictators are akin to\n\nOptions: \nA. accomplices in the dictator's crimes.\nB. people who knowingly buy stolen goods.\nC. thieves who steal from the poor.\nD. merchants who sell harmful products.\nE. war profiteers exploiting conflict.\nF. prostitutes who knowingly spread disease.\nG. bystanders who ignore injustice.\nH. politicians who accept bribes.\nI. all of the above\nJ. murderers of those who witness crimes.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 762, "output_tokens": 406, "total_tokens": 1168}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9691", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the antecedent of the following conditional proposition: When the university raises tuition, then either the governor approves of it or the board of trustees doesn't prevent it.\n\nOptions: \nA. The board of trustees prevents it.\nB. The university raises tuition.\nC. The board of trustees approves it.\nD. The governor and the board of trustees don't prevent it.\nE. The governor approves of it.\nF. The board of trustees doesn't prevent it.\nG. The governor and the board of trustees prevent it.\nH. The governor disapproves of it.\nI. The university doesn't raise tuition.\nJ. The university lowers tuition.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 852, "output_tokens": 299, "total_tokens": 1151}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9826", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  According to Mill, censoring speech that is possibly true\n\nOptions: \nA. is a good way to maintain public order.\nB. is a risk worth taking of the speech is dangerous enough.\nC. diminishes intellectual growth.\nD. is acceptable if the speech is offensive.\nE. is a violation of the speaker's freedom of expression.\nF. is a fundamental right of society.\nG. fails a prima facie duty of honesty.\nH. violates human dignity.\nI. is tantamount to asserting that you are infallible.\nJ. is necessary to maintain societal harmony.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 828, "output_tokens": 355, "total_tokens": 1183}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9494", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  If a global ban would not be effective in prohibiting genetic engineering that goes beyond eliminating obvious defects, then Singer suggests which \"bolder\" strategy?\n\nOptions: \nA. none of the above\nB. using a lottery system so everyone gets a fair chance at the benefits of genetic engineering\nC. using sanctions and trade restrictions against countries that violate the ban\nD. allowing genetic engineering only for medical purposes\nE. promoting genetic engineering only for the wealthy\nF. creating a global consensus on acceptable genetic engineering practices\nG. developing a global regulatory body to monitor and control genetic engineering activities\nH. implementing a global education program to convince people of the dangers of excessive genetic engineering\nI. requiring genetic engineering for every newborn child\nJ. creating a world military that would enforce the ban with greater strength\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{J}. Singer suggests that if a global ban is ineffective, then a \"bolder\" strategy would involve creating a world military to enforce the ban with greater strength. This approach aims to ensure compliance through force rather than relying solely on voluntary agreement or lesser penalties.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1203, "output_tokens": 355, "total_tokens": 1558}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9931", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  In Baxter's view, the first and foremost step toward a solution of our environmental problems is a clear recognition that our objective is not pure air or water but rather\n\nOptions: \nA. the introduction of new species to balance the ecosystem.\nB. maintaining current levels of pollution.\nC. an overall maximally clean environment.\nD. the total elimination of harmful species.\nE. some maximal state of pollution.\nF. the eradication of all pollution.\nG. an environment free from human interference.\nH. a state of pollution that supports human health and well-being.\nI. some optimal state of pollution.\nJ. the preservation of all living species.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 868, "output_tokens": 321, "total_tokens": 1189}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9510", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If you argued something is flawed because it fails to do something, when it was never intended to do that, you may have committed which of the following fallacies?\n\nOptions: \nA. ad ignorantium\nB. Many questions\nC. Extension\nD. Compound proposition\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 476, "output_tokens": 396, "total_tokens": 872}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9706", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the following is an example of a duty that corresponds to a right to goods and service?\n\nOptions: \nA. John's duty to return to Mary that car that he borrowed from her\nB. John's duty to allow Mary to pursue goals that she values\nC. John's duty to not harm Mary\nD. John's duty to not commit suicide\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 598, "output_tokens": 392, "total_tokens": 990}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9802", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a hypothetical syllogism, when the minor premise affirms the antecedent\n\nOptions: \nA. no valid conclusion can be drawn\nB. the conclusion must affirm the consequent\nC. the conclusion must deny the consequent\nD. the conclusion must deny the antecedent\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 545, "output_tokens": 271, "total_tokens": 816}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9838", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a conditional syllogism, when the minor premise denies the antecedent\n\nOptions: \nA. no valid conclusion can be drawn\nB. the conclusion must affirm the antecedent\nC. the conclusion must be a tautology\nD. the conclusion must affirm the consequent\nE. the conclusion must be an inverse statement\nF. the conclusion must be a conditional statement\nG. the conclusion must be a converse statement\nH. the conclusion must deny the consequent\nI. the conclusion must be a contradiction\nJ. the conclusion must deny the antecedent\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 809, "output_tokens": 286, "total_tokens": 1095}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9690", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the given formulas of PL is the best symbolization of the following sentence?\nA person is considered to have lived with you for all of the present year if the person was born or died in the present year and your home was this person's home for the entire time this person was alive.\n\nOptions: \nA. H \u2283 [(B \u2228 D) \u2022 L]\nB. (L \u2228 B) \u2022 (D \u2283 H)\nC. [L \u2283 (B \u2228 D)] \u2022 H\nD. (B \u2228 D) \u2283 (H \u2022 L)\nE. L \u2283 (B \u2228 D \u2022 H)\nF. [(B \u2228 D) \u2022 H] \u2283 L\nG. L \u2283 [(B \u2228 D) \u2022 H]\nH. L \u2283 [(H \u2022 B) \u2228 D]\nI. [(B \u2228 D) \u2228 H] \u2283 L\nJ. (B \u2228 D \u2022 H) \u2283 L\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1044, "output_tokens": 378, "total_tokens": 1422}, "mo