kely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: John Stuart Mill: Each person's happiness is a good to that person, and the general happiness, therefore, a good to the aggregate of all persons.\n\nOptions: \nA. Fallacy of Composition\nB. Fallacy of Division\nC. Gambler's Fallacy\nD. Equivocation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 536, "output_tokens": 402, "total_tokens": 938}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9952", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If the world that we individually perceive is limited to an internal perspective, then there is no way that we could determine whether our own perspective is useful, true, or valuable because:\n\nOptions: \nA. without limiting our perspective to an internal dreamworld, we cannot achieve any objective, external knowledge of the real world.\nB. whatever we appeal to in order to prove that our perspective is right itself would be part of the standard we use in evaluating that perspective.\nC. we know whether our internal perspective is correct only by comparing it with an objective, external perspective (the \"real\" world).\nD. our individual perspective is inherently biased and therefore cannot be trusted.\nE. scientific research that reveals facts about the world would cause us to challenge our perceptions in a dreamworld of our own making.\nF. we are unable to fully comprehend the complexity of the world from an internal perspective.\nG. we can only perceive the world through our senses, which may be flawed or limited.\nH. our perception of the world is shaped by our experiences and therefore cannot be compared to others' perceptions.\nI. our internal perspective is influenced by our emotions, which may distort our perception of the world.\nJ. we can never fully understand the world because our perceptions are limited.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1547, "output_tokens": 364, "total_tokens": 1911}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9762", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: We must assume that he is a Communist, because he says that he is not, and we know that Communists are taught always to deny party membership.\n\nOptions: \nA. Argument from Ignorance\nB. Affirming the Consequent\nC. Denying the Antecedent\nD. Begging the Question\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 542, "output_tokens": 305, "total_tokens": 847}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9492", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: 