g multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: MRI is preferred over CT (computed tomography) in all of the following scenarios, EXCEPT:\n\nOptions: \nA. The detection of spinal cord injuries\nB. The detection of white matter abnormalities\nC. The detection of soft tissue injuries\nD. The detection of a small tumor\nE. The detection of lung cancer\nF. The detection of acute cerebral infarct\nG. The detection of brain aneurysms\nH. The detection of a skull fracture\nI. The detection of heart disease\nJ. The detection of liver abnormalities\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "MRI is generally preferred for soft tissue, neurological, and certain vascular evaluations, while CT is optimal for bone detail and rapid assessment of acute hemorrhage or fractures.  \nIn this list, the detection of a skull fracture is best done with CT due to its sensitivity to bone, not MRI.  \n\n\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 967, "output_tokens": 447, "total_tokens": 1414}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2173", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Buckley Amendment establishes:\n\nOptions: \nA. the requirement for hospitals to make reasonable modifications to procedures for patients with disabilities.\nB. the right of parents or legal guardians of a child to inspect the child\u2019s medical records.\nC. the requirement for schools to provide a \u201cfree appropriate public education\u201d to students with disabi