ect answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Define language. List and define its elements.\n\nOptions: \nA. Language is the visual representation of ideas through art. The elements include: lines, shapes, colors, and textures.\nB. Language is the genetic transmission of information from parent to offspring. The elements include: genes, chromosomes, DNA, and mutations.\nC. Language is the written form of communication using an alphabet. The elements include: letters, words, punctuation, and grammar.\nD. Language is the complex arrangement of sounds that have accepted referents and can be arranged to derive meanings. The units of language include: phonemes, morphemes, syntax, and prosody.\nE. Language is a tool for communication\nF. Language is the process of transferring thoughts through telepathy. The elements include: sender, receiver, thought waves, and mental clarity.\nG. Language is the combination of words to form sentences\nH. Language is a system of gestures used exclusively by primates. The elements include: signals, movements, expressions, and gestures.\nI. Language is the use of signs and symbols\nJ. Language is the method of communication using mathematical symbols and numbers. The elements include: numerals, equations, operations, and proofs.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1458, "output_tokens": 385, "total_tokens": 1843}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2231", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sampling error refers to the\n\nOptions: \nA. tendency of sample statistics to be identical with each other\nB. consequences of generalizing from a sample thar is too small\nC. tendency of sample statistics to always match the population parameters\nD. consequences of generalizing from a population to a sample\nE. error in the method of data collection in the sample\nF. consequences of generalizing from a large sample to a small population\nG. tendency of some sample statistics to differ systematically from the corresponding population parameters\nH. tendency of sample statistics to differ from population parameters\nI. consequences of generalizing from a sample to a population\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 933, "output_tokens": 397, "total_tokens": 1330}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1861", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Curtis stares at an image of a yellow star for a full minute. When he moves his gaze to a blank piece of white paper, he is likely to see an afterimage that is\n\nOptions: \nA. orange\nB. pink\nC. brown\nD. red\nE. black\nF. purple\nG. green\nH. white\nI. blue\nJ. yellow\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 576, "output_tokens": 282, "total_tokens": 858}, "model_