e mode or modes of the sample 6, 7, 7, 3, 8, 5, 3, 9.\n\nOptions: \nA. No mode\nB. 6, 7, and 8\nC. 7 only\nD. 6 and 9\nE. 6 and 8\nF. 6, 7, and 3\nG. 5 and 9\nH. 3 only\nI. 3 and 7\nJ. 8 and 9\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 608, "output_tokens": 276, "total_tokens": 884}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1851", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Ethnic identity refers to\n\nOptions: \nA. a rejection of Caucasian social, cultural, and institutional standards\nB. the rejection of all cultural traditions and practices\nC. the extent to which an individual endorses and practices the ethnocultural traditions of a given group\nD. cultural practices and beliefs char are non-Western in orientation and perspective\nE. the adherence to only Western cultural traditions and practices\nF. the extent to which an individual rejects their own ethnocultural traditions and practices\nG. the adoption of multiple ethnic identities and practices\nH. the extent to which an individual practices the traditions of the majority culture\nI. the collective cultural practices, traditions, and orientations of ethnic minority communities\nJ. the adoption of the cultural practices of the dominant group\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1075, "output_tokens": 369, "total_tokens": 1444}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2068", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is areinforcer?\n\nOptions: \nA. A reinforcer is a constant condition that sustains a particular behavior without change.\nB. A reinforcer is a psychological punishment.\nC. A reinforcer is a neutral signal that predicts the occurrence of a punishment.\nD. A reinforcer is a physical barrier that prevents a response.\nE. A reinforcer is an event that only temporarily increases the probability of a response.\nF. A reinforcer is a stimuli that has no effect on the response.\nG. A reinforcer is any event which increases the probability of a response in a particular situation.\nH. A reinforcer is a type of medication that alters mental states.\nI. A reinforcer is a genetic trait that influences behavior.\nJ. A reinforcer is an event that decreases the probability of a response.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1045, "output_tokens": 275, "total_tokens": 1320}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2117", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Alpha waves are most closely associated with\n\nOptions: \nA. Stage 4 sleep\nB. Stage 1 sl