s, usually in the form of guilt and depression\nC. women who have abortions are more likely to have difficulty conceiving in the future\nD. the experience often leads to long-term physical health issues\nE. the psychological consequences are no worse than they are for women who have chosen to continue their pregnancies and give birth\nF. most women who have abortions think no more about the event than they would about having a wisdom tooth removed\nG. subsequent problems in sexual adjustment and in relationships with men are common\nH. women who have abortions are less likely to want children in the future\nI. the majority of women experience severe post-traumatic stress disorder\nJ. most women who have abortions suffer from severe depression and anxiety for years afterward\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1138, "output_tokens": 333, "total_tokens": 1471}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2299", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Approximately what percent of the population scores between 70 and 130 on the WISC?\n\nOptions: \nA. 25\nB. 90\nC. 75\nD. 68\nE. 95\nF. 50\nG. 34\nH. 85\nI. 80\nJ. 60\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 558, "output_tokens": 337, "total_tokens": 895}, "model_us