al_tokens": 988}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2189", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Detection of a just-noticeable difference (JND) depends on the\n\nOptions: \nA. presence of a \"no stimulus\" control and the sensitivity of the signal-detection equipment\nB. initial determination of the absolute threshold and the variation of the difference threshold\nC. frequency of the existing stimulus and the presence of one or more sensory modalities\nD. intensity of the new stimulus and that of the stimulus already present\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 636, "output_tokens": 350, "total_tokens": 986}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2521", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: While treating a client, you decide that you want to consult with a colleague to discuss a specific aspect of the case that is giving you trouble. According to APA\u2019s Ethics Code and the Canadian Code of Ethics:\n\nOptions: \nA. you should obtain permission from both the client and the consultant before discussing the case.\nB. you must always obtain permission from the client before talking to a consultant.\nC. you must obtain permission from the client only if you will be revealing sensitive information to the consultant.\nD. you only need to obtain permission from the client if the consultant is not part of the same organization.\nE. you must obtain permission from the client only if you will be revealing the client's identity to the consultant.\nF. you can consult with a colleague without client's permission only if it's an emergency situation.\nG. \"you do not have to obtain permission from the client under any circumstances since the consultant is \u201cclearly connected\"\" with the case.\"\nH. you don't have to obtain permission from the client as long as he/she has already signed a general waiver.\nI. you should discuss the matter with the client but the final decision is up to the professional's discretion.\nJ. you don't need to obtain permission if the consultation is about a general aspect of the case and not about the client specifically.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1494, "output_tokens": 391, "total_tokens": 1885}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2182", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The risk of withdrawal delirium is greatest following discontinuation of which of the following substances\n\nOptions: \nA. Ecstasy\nB. Marijuana\nC. Alcohol\nD. Cocaine\nE. Tobacco\nF. Phenobarbital\nG. Heroin\nH. LSD\nI. Methamphetamine\nJ. Caffeine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 552, "output_tokens": 402, "total_tokens": 954}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2318", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What are the vestibular organs, and how do the operate?\n\nOptions: \nA. The vestibular organs are the semicircular canals and theotolithorgans. They provide us with a sense of balance through information about the movements and position of our head.\nB. The vestibular organs are the malleus and incus, which are involved in the amplification of sound within the ear.\nC. The vestibular organs are the hair cells and basilar membrane, which are critical for the perception of pitch and volume in hearing.\nD. The vestibular organs are the pinna and earlobe\nE. The vestibular organs are the auditory canal and eardrum\nF. The vestibular organs are the cochlea and auditory nerves\nG. The vestibular organs are the stapes and round window, which play roles in the conversion of sound waves into mechanical energy.\nH. The vestibular organs are the tympanic membrane and stapedius muscle, which contribute to the detection of sound frequency.\nI. The vestibular organs are the Eustachian tube and mastoid process, which are related to the regulation of air pressure in the middle ear.\nJ. The vestibular organs are the vestibular nerve and cochlear duct, which are responsible for transmitting sound vibrations to the brain.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1368, "output_tokens": 301, "total_tokens": 1669}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2414", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When one uses a time-series design to evaluate a program, fluctuation in the outcome slope can be accounted for by various alternative hypotheses. According to Campbell and Stanley, the most probable alternative is that\n\nOptions: \nA. the outcome measure was not sensitive enough\nB. a simultaneous event produced the fluctuation\nC. the participants did not understand the program\nD. the data was not analyzed correctly\nE. the program was not implemented correctly\nF. the fluctuation was due to random chance\nG. participants dropped out of the group, reducing the size of the sample\nH. aging effects were unduly influential\nI. test\u2014retest reliability is inadequate\nJ. the time-series design was flawed\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 926, "output_tokens": 401, "total_tokens": 1327}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2490", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to gate-control theory, which condition tends to close the gate?\n\nOptions: \nA. anxiety\nB. sleep deprivation\nC. focusing on the pain\nD. stress\nE. electrical stimulation\nF. depression\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 468, "output_tokens": 304, "total_tokens": 772}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2186", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Xavier is beginning his first year of college. He is eager to find a few other freshmen to \"hang out\" with. Psychologists would say that Xavier is motivated by a(n)\n\nOptions: \nA. conformity need\nB. affiliation need\nC. appreciation need\nD. assimilation need\nE. acclimatization need\nF. attachment need\nG. recognition need\nH. validation need\nI. independence need\nJ. fraternization need\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 636, "output_tokens": 219, "total_tokens": 855}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2539", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Research comparing heterogeneous and homogeneous work groups has found that, in general, heterogeneous groups:\n\nOptions: \nA. are more creative but worse at decision-making.\nB. are more creative and better at decision-making.\nC. make better decisions but are less creative overall.\nD. are less creative and less productive overall.\nE. are more productive but worse at decision-making.\nF. make worse decisions but are more productive overall.\nG. are less creative and worse at decision-making.\nH. make better decisions but are less productive overall.\nI. are less creative but better at decision-making.\nJ. are more creative but less productive overall.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 814, "output_tokens": 292, "total_tokens": 1106}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1969", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The STANDARD SCORES express raw score distance from mean by SD and considered the most satisfactory type of NR score. Which statement out of the following ones is about T-scores?\n\nOptions: \nA. M=0, SD=1, often used in research studies\nB. M=100, SD=15 or 16\nC. They express raw scores in terms of percentiles\nD. M=500, SD=100, often used in college entrance exams\nE. Shows how many standard deviations a score is above or below the mean: a score of +1.0 means it\u2019s 1 SD above the mean\nF. M=100, SD=10, commonly used in IQ tests\nG. M=100, SD=24, typically used in personality assessments\nH. M=50, SD=10- it is used on many psychological tests, MMPI\nI. They express raw scores in terms of ranks\nJ. standard nine: M=5, SD=approx 2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X 