he most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nearsightedness results from\n\nOptions: \nA. too little curvature of the cornea and lens\nB. too much curvature of the retina and lens\nC. too much curvature of the cornea and lens\nD. too much curvature of the iris and cornea\nE. incorrect alignment of the cornea and retina\nF. incorrect alignment of the cornea and lens\nG. too much curvature of the iris and lens\nH. incorrect alignment of the iris and lens\nI. too little curvature of the iris and lens\nJ. too little curvature of the retina and lens\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 774, "output_tokens": 273, "total_tokens": 1047}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2164", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Trend analysis is a type of analysis of variance that is used when:\n\nOptions: \nA. a sequential research design has been used.\nB. a factorial research design has been used.\nC. a study\u2019s independent variable is quantitative.\nD. a cross-sectional research design has been used.\nE. a longitudinal research design has been used.\nF. a mixed methods research design has been used.\nG. a study\u2019s dependent variable is quantitative.\nH. a study\u2019s dependent variable is qualitative.\nI. a correlational research design has been used.\nJ. a study\u2019s independent variable is qualitative.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 814, "output_tokens": 305, "total_tokens": 1119}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1967", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why is an array of equally spaced dots perceived asrows and columns ?\n\nOptions: \nA. Perception of rows and columns is due to the magnetic field of the Earth influencing visual processing.\nB. The dots are perceived as rows and columns due to color contrast.\nC. It is because the human brain is programmed to recognize faces, and this pattern is similar to facial features.\nD. The dots are seen in rows and columns because of the repetitive motion in which the observer moves their eyes.\nE. Columns and rows are organized figures that the eye sees easily and it tends to organize unconnected, yet closely placed objects into a familiar pattern.\nF. The dots form a grid pattern due to the optical illusion caused by light refraction.\nG. The perception is due to the varying size of the dots.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 996, "output_tokens": 293, "total_tokens": 1289}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2187", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After she used address stickers sent by a charity in the mail, Brittany felt obligated to mail a donation to the organization that sent the stickers. Brittany's behavior illustrates\n\nOptions: \nA. stereotyping\nB. the reciprocity norm\nC. the halo effect\nD. the bystander effect\nE. the door-in-the-face technique\nF. the cognitive dissonance theory\nG. the just-world phenomenon\nH. the self-serving bias\nI. the fundamental attribution error\nJ. the mere exposure effect\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 704, "output_tokens": 286, "total_tokens": 990}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2412", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: You would use the Solomon four-group design in order to:\n\nOptions: \nA. improve external validity.\nB. evaluate the impact of pretesting.\nC. eliminate carryover effects.\nD. increase the sample size.\nE. control for confounding variables.\nF. evaluate the effects of history and maturation.\nG. eliminate selection bias.\nH. measure the dependent variable.\nI. increase statistical power.\nJ. reduce demand characteristics.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 666, "output_tokens": 361, "