r the test population lie within 15 points of the mean score\nE. about 68% of the observed scores for the test population lie within 30 points of the mean score\nF. about 68% of the observed scores will lie between 15 points below and above the true score\nG. about 32% of the individuals with a given cure score will have observed scores within 15 points of the true score\nH. about 15% of the individuals with a given score will have observed scores within 15 points of the true score\nI. differences of up to 30 points represent the same true score\nJ. about 15% of the scores are in error (i.e., they are not measuring the trait reliably)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1352, "output_tokens": 381, "total_tokens": 1733}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2053", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Heteroscedasticity in a scattergram suggests that:\n\nOptions: \nA. there is a restriction of range of scores on the predictor and/or the criterion.\nB. the variability (range) of scores on the criterion varies for different scores on the predictor.\nC. there is a statistically significant correlation between the predictor and criterion.\nD. the predictor and criterion have a negative correlation.\nE. there is a perfect correlation between the predictor and the criterion.\nF. the predictor and criterion are independent of each other.\nG. the relationship between the predictor and criterion cannot be described by a straight line.\nH. the variability (range) of scores on the predictor is constant for all scores on the criterion.\nI. the scores on the criterion are uniformly distributed across the range of the predictor.\nJ. the variability (range) of scores on the predictor varies for different scores on the criterion.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1102, "output_tokens": 297, "total_tokens": 1399}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1960", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the CPI ? How is it different from the MMPI ?\n\nOptions: \nA. CPI stands for Clinical Psychopathy Index, a variant of the MMPI\nB. CPI is a clinical tool for diagnosing mental illnesses\nC. CPI is a cognitive performance test, unlike the MMPI which assesses personality\nD. The CPI is a projective test that measures subconscious traits, while the MMPI is an objective test\nE. CPI is primarily used for educational testing, whereas MMPI is used in clinical psychology\nF. CPI is a measure of inflation, whereas MMPI is a personality assessment\nG. The California Psychological Inventory (CPI) is an objective personality inventory developed for use with less clinical less deviant groups of subjects than the MMPI.\nH. CPI is used to measure gross psychopathy\nI. CPI and MMPI are the same\nJ. CPI is a newer version of the MMPI with updated scales and norms\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1098, "output_tokens": 346, "total_tokens": 1444}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2423", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a cartoon, an angel is perched on one shoulder and a devil is perched on the other shoulder of a character who needs to decide whether to give money to a homeless man or not. The devil says, \"Don't give him anything, you'll make better use of the money than he will.\" The angel says, \"Give him the money because he needs it more than you do.\" The character gives the homeless man half of his money. In a Freudian interpretation, the angel represents the character's\n\nOptions: \nA. Pleasure principle\nB. Unconscious\nC. id\nD. ego\nE. Conscious\nF. Defense mechanism\nG. superego\nH. libido\nI. Reality principle\nJ. Preconscious\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 921, "output_tokens": 311, "total_tokens": 1232}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1983", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The denominator term in the F-ratio is reduced in magnitude by:\n\nOptions: \nA. decreasing both within-group and between-group variability.\nB. increasing both within-group and between-group variability.\nC. increasing between-group variability only.\nD. increasing within-group variability.\nE. decreasing between-group variability only.\nF. increasing between-group variability and decreasing within-group variability.\nG. decreasing between-group variability and increasing within-group variability\nH. increasing between-group variability and decreasing between-group variability.\nI. decreasing within-group variability and increasing between-group variability.\nJ. decreasing within-group variability.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 864, "output_tokens": 322, "total_tokens": 1186}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2350", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is the best example of constant error\n\nOptions: \nA. A subject consistently provides correct answers to every test item\nB. A psychometrician consistently underestimates IQ scores by 10 points\nC. A test item is answered correctly by every student in a given class\nD. A subject consistently provides wrong answers to every test item\nE. A test-retest reliability coefficient is high for several samples\nF. A subject inconsistently provides wrong answers to every test item\nG. A psychometrician inconsistently overestimates IQ scores\nH. A test item is answered incorrectly by every student in a given class\nI. A test-retest reliability coefficient is low for several samples\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 880, "output_tokens": 281, "total_tokens": 1161}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2038", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The function of the correction for attenuation is to\n\nOptions: \nA. adjust the correlation coefficient for any potential influence of a third variable\nB. reduce the correlation between two variables by accounting for measurement errors\nC. provide a method for correcting bias in the distribution of scores\nD. provide an estimate of the predictive validity of a test-thar is independent of chance factors in any specific validation sample\nE. estimate the correlation between more than two variables if one or more could be measured without error\nF. show how adding or subtracting items affects the reliability of a test\nG. estimate the correlation between wo variables if one or both could be measured without error\nH. correct an obtained correlation coefficient for restriction of range in either variable\nI. adjust the value of the correlation coefficient to account for sample size\nJ. provide a means to increase the reliability of a test by eliminating outliers\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1051, "output_tokens": 243, "total_tokens": 1294}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2528", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When the corpus callosum is cut in a right-handed patient, often the patient\n\nOptions: \nA. Cannot name objects placed in the right hand if the patient can see them\nB. cannot recognize objects placed in the right hand\nC. cannot name objects placed in the left hand if the patient cannot see them\nD. cannot carry out well-learned motor tasks with the left hand\nE. shows a decline in verbal intelligence\nF. loses the ability to speak\nG. Cannot name objects placed in the right hand if the patient cannot see them\nH. cannot carry out well-learned motor tasks with the right hand\nI. shows a decline in spatial intelligence\nJ. can no longer write with their right hand\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 918, "output_tokens": 420, "total_tokens": 1338}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2579", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The correction for attenuation formula is used to measure the impact of increasing:\n\nOptions: \nA. the number of test takers on the test\u2019s validity.\nB. the number of test takers on the test\u2019s reliability.\nC. the test's difficulty on its validity.\nD. a test\u2019s validity on its difficulty.\nE. a test\u2019s reliability on its difficulty.\nF. a test\u2019s validity on its reliability.\nG. the test's difficulty on its reliability.\nH. the number of test items on the test\u2019s validity.\nI. a test\u2019s reliability on its validity.\nJ. the number of test items on the test\u2019s reliability.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 900, "output_tokens": 435, "total_tokens": 1335}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2040", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Most people who are suicidal are more dangerous to themselves\n\nOptions: \nA. when they are not on any form of medication\nB. just before beginning antidepressant medication\nC. during the first few days after starting antidepressant medication\nD. as they begin to recover from their depression\nE. during periods of remission from depression\nF. when they first experience symptoms of depression\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 634, "output_tokens": 322, "total_tokens": 956}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2166", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When we convert total number of errors on a test to percent correct, or vice versa, we are performing which type of transformation\n\nOptions: \nA. Exponential\nB. Sinusoidal\nC. Polynomial\nD. Quadratic\nE. Rational\nF. Cumulative\nG. Nonlinear\nH. Logarithmic\nI. Linear\nJ. Curvilinear\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 573, "output_tokens": 294, "total_tokens": 867}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2337", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Exposing individuals to arguments against their views, arguments that are then strongly refuted, may serve to\n\nOptions: \nA. make them more argumentative\nB. make them more susceptible to accepting opposing views\nC. weaken their resistance to later persuasive appeals\nD. increase their attitudinal ambivalence\nE. strengthen their existing views\nF. lead them to develop new, unrelated opinions\nG. render them indifferent to the attitude object\nH. inoculate chem against later persuasive appeals\nI. confuse them about their original beliefs\nJ. cause them to reject all future arguments\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 812, "output_tokens": 273, "total_tokens": 1085}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2210", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is cross-validation and why is it important?\n\nOptions: \nA. Cross-validation is only used for validating models in large datasets and is not suitable for small datasets\nB. Cross-validation is a method for enhancing the complexity of a model to improve its performance on a single data set\nC. Cross-validation is not important in small samples\nD. Cross-validation is a method to independently determine the validity of a test on additional samples, it is necessary especially when the initial validation sample is small, to avoid errors and chance factors.\nE. Cross-validation involves using different tests to measure the same variable to ensure the tests agree with each other\nF. Cross-validation is a process where the performance of a test is only assessed once to ensure speed and efficiency\nG. Cross-validation is a method to validate a test without additional samples\nH. Cross-validation is a technique to assess the performance of a model by splitting the data into two sets: one for training and one for final testing\nI. Cross-validation is the replication of a test using the same dataset to confirm the initial results\nJ. Cross-validation is a method to determine the validity of a test on the same sample\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1366, "output_tokens": 327, "total_tokens": 1693}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2045", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A measure of __________ would be most useful for determining the likelihood that employees will remain on the job for a long period of time.\n\nOptions: \nA. job productivity\nB. salary\nC. motivation\nD. previous employment history\nE. age\nF. ambition\nG. job satisfaction\nH. educational background\nI. physical health\nJ. intelligence\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 619, "output_tokens": 317, "total_tokens": 936}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1996", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In client-centered case consultation, the consultant's primary goal is to:\n\nOptions: \nA. work independently to provide the optimal intervention to a client.\nB. help the consultee develop a stronger professional identity and sense of self.\nC. help the consultee identify methods for evaluating his/her own professional services.\nD. help the consultee to improve his/her communication skills with clients.\nE. help the consultee determine how to work more effectively with a particular client.\nF. help the consultee learn to manage his/her own professional stress and burnout.\nG. help the consultee establish a structured plan for future client interactions.\nH. work collaboratively with the consultee in delivering the optimal intervention to a client.\nI. help a consultee enhance his/her skills and knowledge so that the consultee functions more effectively in the future.\nJ. help the consultee identify areas of personal growth and development.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1052, "output_tokens": 263, "total_tokens": 1315}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2241", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Shannon forgot her pillow when she went camping, so she complained about having to sleep with her head flat on the ground the whole night. Her failure to fold up her jeans and sweater to use as a pillow-substitute best illustrates the effects of\n\nOptions: \nA. functional fixedness\nB. the availability heuristic\nC. the overconfidence effect\nD. the representativeness heuristic\nE. confirmation bias\nF. the framing effect\nG. the hindsight bias\nH. the illusion of control\nI. cognitive dissonance\nJ. the anchoring effect\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 774, "output_tokens": 342, "total_tokens": 1116}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1862", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"Mommy gived me a cookie\" best illustrates a basic understanding of\n\nOptions: \nA. prelinguistic speech\nB. overgeneralization\nC. syntax\nD. semantics\nE. grammar\nF. holophrases\nG. phonology\nH. pragmatics\nI. phonemes\nJ. morphemes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 540, "output_tokens": 271, "total_tokens": 811}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2088", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Discuss complications that may arise during labor.\n\nOptions: \nA. Breach presentation, Cesarean section, use of forceps, effects of pain-killing drugs, and Anoxia\nB. Prenatal Anxiety\nC. Postpartum Depression\nD. Parent-Child Attachment Issues\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 522, "output_tokens": 301, "total_tokens": 823}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2435", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and 