) the pupil would constrict slightly, (c) the heart rate would increase dramatically.\nD. (a) Digestion would be slightly inhibited, (b) the pupil would dilate, (c) the heart rate would remain unchanged.\nE. (a) Digestion is facilitated or enhanced, (b) the pupil would reduce in size, (c) the heart beat would slow and weaken.\nF. (a) Digestion is inhibited, (b) the pupil would enlarge, (c) the heart beat would increase and strengthen.\nG. (a) Digestion would be unaffected, (b) the pupil would fluctuate in size, (c) the heart rate would decrease slightly.\nH. (a) Digestion would slow down, (b) the pupil would remain the same size, (c) the heart beat would quicken.\nI. (a) Digestion would speed up dramatically, (b) the pupil would dilate significantly, (c) the heart rate would increase slightly.\nJ. (a) Digestion remains unaffected, (b) the pupil would dilate, (c) the heart beat would remain the same.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1729, "output_tokens": 313, "total_tokens": 2042}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2049", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Operant extinction would NOT be the treatment-of-choice when:\n\nOptions: \nA. the behavior has been reinforced on a continuous schedule.\nB. the behavior is not causing significant distress or dysfunction.\nC. the behavior is a part of the individual's cultural or religious practices.\nD. an alternative behavior cannot be identified.\nE. a temporary increase in the behavior cannot be tolerated.\nF. the baseline levels of the behavior cannot be established.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 643, "output_tokens": 348, "total_tokens": 991}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1970", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A physician refers an asthmatic patient to you for therapy and requests regular progress reports. The most appropriate course of action for you to take is to\n\nOptions: \nA. agree to send reports, but only provide vague and generalized information about the patient's progress\nB. inform the physician that you can only send progress reports after the therapy is complete.\nC. comply with this request, since a physician must be involved whenever you treat someone for a physical condition\nD. refuse the request, stating that patient confidentiality prevents you from sharing any information\nE. tell the physician that you will need the patient's family's written permission as well\nF. comply with this request, since the physician needs your input for best treatment of the patient's physical condition\nG. tell the physician that you can only provide verbal updates, not written reports\nH. tell the physician chat psychological reports can be sent only to a psychiatrist or to another psychologist\nI. comply with the request, but only send reports sporadically when you deem necessary\nJ. tell the physician thar you can send progress reports only with a written release by the patient\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1332, "output_tokens": 289, "total_tokens": 1621}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1945", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the mean weight of the sample of rats that weighed 2 lbs., 3 lbs., 6 lbs., 8 lbs., and 9 lbs.\n\nOptions: \nA. 6 lbs\nB. 7 lbs\nC. 4.5 lbs\nD. 5.8 lbs\nE. 6.2 lbs\nF. 5.6 lbs\nG. 4.8 lbs\nH. 7.2 lbs\nI. 5.2 lbs\nJ. 6.5 lbs\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 570, "output_tokens": 192, "total_tokens": 762}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2336", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The items for 2 machinist proficiency test have been based on 2 job analysis of machinists in 50 plants, each employing five or more machinists doing comparable work. Such 2 procedure would contribute directly to the test's\n\nOptions: \nA. face validity\nB. concurrent validity\nC. internal validity\nD. criterion validity\nE. convergent validity\nF. construct validity\nG. empirical validity\nH. predictive validity\nI. d