ter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1020, "output_tokens": 294, "total_tokens": 1314}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2116", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In class, John's teacher tells him that she will give him the coin and bill for each picture he can correctly identify on the face of the penny, nickel, dime, quarter, half-dollar, dollar bill, and five-dollar bill. John cannot identify any of them although he has been handling money for 17 years. His inability to remember the pictures most likely results from\n\nOptions: \nA. sensory memory decay\nB. retroactive interference\nC. failure to encode\nD. failure to reconstruct\nE. false memory formation\nF. lack of attention\nG. failure to retrieve\nH. confabulation\nI. deep processing\nJ. proactive interference\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 832, "output_tokens": 283, "total_tokens": 1115}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2325", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If a group of five people are watching a movie and upon conclusionfour of them state that the movie was terrible, whatwill the fifth person (who happened to like the movie) probablysay?\n\nOptions: \nA. it was a terrible movie\nB. it was an excellent movie\nC. I liked the movie, despite what others think\nD. the movie was okay\nE. The movie was not as bad as you're saying\nF. The special effects were good, but the story was lacking\nG. The acting was good, but the plot didn't make sense\nH. no opinion about the movie\nI. The movie had its moments but wasn't great overall\nJ. Everyone has their own taste in movies\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 903, "output_tokens": 296, "total_tokens": 1199}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2254", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the relative measure ofskewnessfor the datalisted below? This data represents the waist measurements of six randomlyselected chocolate rabbits. 3 inches,2 inches,3.7 inches,5 inches, 2.7 inches,3 inches.\n\nOptions: \nA. The distribution is positively skewed\nB. The distribution has a skewness coefficient of zero\nC. The distribution is negatively skewed\nD. The distribution is perfectly normal\nE. The distribution is uniform\nF. The distribution is bimodal\nG. The distribution is multimodal\nH. The skewness cannot be determined from the given data\nI. The distribution has no skewness\nJ. The distribution is symmetrical\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 886, "output_tokens": 332, "total_tokens": 1218}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2126", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Dr. Ramchandran found that his patients who brushed their teeth after lunch had 1/20 the number of cavities in their teeth as those who didn't. After interviewing the dentist, a local newswriter reports that brushing teeth after lunch prevents cavities. Based on the dentist's research, which of the following statements is true?\n\nOptions: \nA. The writer's statement would be justified if at least half of the patients brushed their teeth after lunch.\nB. If a minimum of 200 patients were studied, the writer's statement is justified.\nC. No matter how many participants, the writer's statement is not justified.\nD. The writer's statement would only be justified if no patients brushed their teeth after lunch.\nE. The writer's statement could only be justified if the study was conducted over a prolonged period of time.\nF. At least 100 of the patients needed to have brushed their teeth after lunch for the writer's statement to be justified.\nG. If all the patients were studied, the writer's statement is justified.\nH. If at least 100 patients were studied, the writer's statement is justified.\nI. If only the patients who brushed their teeth after lunch were studied, the writer's statement is justified.\nJ. If a minimum of 500 patients were studied, the writer's statement is justified.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1432, "output_tokens": 299, "total_tokens": 1731}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2598", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Today Susan took a pill for her allergy that raised her blood pressure, caused her heart to beat faster, and raised her body temperature. Now caught in traffic, she feels angry. Yesterday, when she took the pill, she was with her husband. When her blood pressure rose, her heart speeded up, she got hotter, and she felt amorous. This description exemplifies\n\nOptions: \nA. two-factor theory\nB. Incentive theory\nC. Opponent-process theory\nD. the adaptation-level phenomenon\nE. Cognitive dissonance theory\nF. Arousal theory\nG. Cannon-Bard theory\nH. Cognitive Appraisal theory\nI. James-Lange theory\nJ. Drive-reduction theory\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 892, "output_tokens": 337, "total_tokens": 1229}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2545", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Answering multiple-choice questions is often easier than answering fill-in or completion questions, because multiple choice questions\n\nOptions: \nA. are definitional rather than conceptual\nB. check memorization rather than critical thinking\nC. encourage rote learning rather than comprehension\nD. require less time to answer\nE. enhance retention of information\nF. provide more retrieval cues\nG. are always easier to understand\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 621, "output_tokens": 274, "total_tokens": 895}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2178", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"A friend of yours says, \u201cEvery time I plan a vacation, there's always a crisis at home or work so that I can't go.\"\" Assuming that this is not really true, your friend's statement best illustrates which of the following?\"\n\nOptions: \nA. illusory correlation\nB. base rate fallacy\nC. cognitive dissonance\nD. anchoring bias\nE. availability heuristic\nF. fundamental attribution bias\nG. hindsight bias\nH. self-serving bias\nI. psychological reactance\nJ. confirmation bias\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 723, "output_tokens": 272, "total_tokens": 995}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2425", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Although they disagreed with his personal infidelities, many Americans supported President Bill Clinton's position and policy decisions during his term in office. This dichotomy of opinion demonstrates a split in\n\nOptions: \nA. external locus of control\nB. situational ethics\nC. internal validity\nD. cognitive dissonance\nE. social desirability bias\nF. attitudinal coherence\nG. attributional bias\nH. moral relativism\nI. self-representation\nJ. behavioral consistency\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 720, "output_tokens": 323, "total_tokens": 1043}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1938", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Lizette and her family watch the sunset over the ocean. While walking home in the increasing darkness, Lizette notices that she can no longer distinguish the colors of objects. Which of the following best explains why Lizette cannot see color in dim light?\n\nOptions: \nA. Lizette's eyes are adjusting to the darkness, hence she cannot distinguish the colors of objects.\nB. Cones, which are specialized for color vision, require more light to be activated, whereas rods, which produce images in black, white, and gray, allow for vision in dim light.\nC. The retina does not respond to changes in light intensity, therefore colors are not visible in dim light.\nD. The receptive fields in the retina respond to the loss of light through light adaptation, the process of rapidly adjusting to a diminution of light.\nE. Cones, which are specialized for black and white vision, require a small amount of light to be activated, whereas rods, which produce images in color, require greater amounts of light for vision.\nF. Rods and cones both require a high amount of light to be activated, hence color vision is not possible in dim light.\nG. The cones, which are responsible for color vision, are deactivated in dim light.\nH. The color vision is not possible in the dark because the photoreceptor cells in the retina require light to detect colors.\nI. The colors are not visible in dim light because the rods, which detect colors, are deactivated.\nJ. Rods, which are specialized for color vision, require more light to be activated, whereas cones, which produce images in black, white, and gray, allow for vision in dim light.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1688, "output_tokens": 282, "total_tokens": 1970}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2433", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Normally, one would expect the brightness of an object to increaseas more light is reflected from it, however, the perceivedbrightness of an object also depends on the field thatsurrounds it. Discuss this phenomenon including a methodfor its demonstration.\n\nOptions: \nA. The perceived brightness of an object depends on the light source's distance from the object, with closer light sources making the object appear brighter.\nB. The perceived brightness of an object depends on the viewer's distance from the object, with objects appearing brighter when the viewer is closer.\nC. The perceived brightness of an object depends on its size\nD. The perceived brightness of an object depends on the angle at which light hits it, with direct angles increasing brightness.\nE. The perceived brightness of an object depends on the spectral composition of the light source, with certain wavelengths enhancing brightness more than others.\nF. The perceived brightness of an object only depends on the amount of light reflected from it\nG. The perceived brightness of an object is influenced by the color of the object itself, with lighter colors always appearing brighter than darker colors.\nH. The brightness of an object will always increase when more light is reflected from it\nI. The perceived brightness of an object can be demonstrated by the use of polarized lenses to reduce glare and enhance brightness.\nJ. The perceived brightness of an object depends on the contrast between the object and its surrounding field. This can be demonstrated by placing samples of medium gray paper on different colored backgrounds.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1684, "output_tokens": 396, "total_tokens": 2080}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2130", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Functionally, receptors in the retina of the eye differ most from receptors in the cochlea of the ear in the\n\nOptions: \nA. magnitude of the resting potentials of their membranes\nB. size and structure of their cells\nC. ability to regenerate after damage\nD. speed at which they transmit signals\nE. number of axons each cell possesses\nF. ions involved in their action potentials\nG. degree of sensitivity to external stimuli\nH. length of their refractory periods\nI. location of their synapses\nJ. types of energy they transduce\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 780, "output_tokens": 290, "total_tokens": 1070}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2106", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When cross-validation of a set of predictors results in great shrinkage of an initially encouraging multiple correlation coefficients, it is most likely chat\n\nOptions: \nA. the criterion variable was unreliable\nB. the criterion variable was overvalued\nC. the selection of weights for the predictors capitalized on chance\nD. the number of independent variables used in the first study was too small\nE. the model was not properly validated\nF. the predictor variables were not independent\nG. the predictor variables were too diverse\nH. none of the predictor variables was sufficiency reliable\nI. the selection of weights for the predictors was biased\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 812, "output_tokens": 396, "total_tokens": 1208}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2581", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A stroke that affects the posterior region of the corpus callosum, thus disconnecting the visual centers of the brain from the language centers of the brain, may result in this syndrome:\n\nOptions: \nA. Aphasia\nB. Broca's aphasia\nC. Hemianopsia\nD. Alexia without agraphia\nE. Apraxia\nF. Agraphia without alexia\nG. Dysarthria\nH. Prosopagnosia\nI. Wernicke's aphasia\nJ. Agnosia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 702, "output_tokens": 375, "total_tokens": 1077}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2342", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Unilateral damage to the left (dominant) hemisphere is least likely to result in an inability to:\n\nOptions: \nA. use the process of elimination to answer multiple-choice questions.\nB. interpret visual cues.\nC. read a map.\nD. perform mathematical calculations.\nE. write a coherent sentence.\nF. perform physical tasks with the right side of the body.\nG. memorize vocabulary words.\nH. construct a daily schedule.\nI. understand spoken language.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The left hemisphere is typically dominant for language, analytical tasks, and controlling the right side of the body. Interpreting visual cues is more closely associated with the right hemisphere\u2019s visuospatial functions. Therefore, unilateral left hemisphere damage would least impair this ability.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 843, "output_tokens": 410, "total_tokens": 1253}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1961", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Define a hormone. How would you go about proving that a particular gland is responsible for a specific function?\n\nOptions: \nA. A hormone is a type of organ\nB. A hormone is a type of tissue\nC. A hormone is an electrical signal sent through the nervous system to communicate between different parts of the body.\nD. A hormone is a mineral that is involved in maintaining the balance of water in the body.\nE. A hormone is a chemical substance synthesized by a specific organ or tissue and secreted directly into the blood.\nF. A hormone is a structural protein that makes up the components of muscles and tissues.\nG. A hormone is a digestive enzyme that breaks down food in the stomach and intestines.\nH. A hormone is a type of vitamin that the body needs in small amounts to function properly.\nI. A hormone is a type of cell\nJ. A hormone is a biological molecule that remains within the organ it is produced in and affects only that specific organ.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1103, "output_tokens": 307, "total_tokens": 1410}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1968", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The concept of bureaucracy has come to have very negative connotationstoday. Discuss those factors you believe are responsiblefor this negative attitude.\n\nOptions: \nA. The bureaucratic approach is considered negative due to its overemphasis on innovation and risk-taking, leading to instability.\nB. The bureaucratic approach is outdated and inefficient.\nC. Weber's bureaucratic approach, with its lack of regard for the individual, assumption that humans are predictably alike, confusing rules and regulations, 'red tape', and clearly defined job descriptions detracting from cooperation and problem solving.\nD. The perception of bureaucracy is poor because it prioritizes speed and efficiency over thoroughness and accuracy.\nE. Negative attitudes towards bureaucracy arise from its encouragement of personal connections and favoritism over merit-based advancement.\nF. Bureaucracies often receive criticism for promoting equality and fairness, which is seen as a hindrance to competitive advantage.\nG. Bureaucracies are viewed negatively because they are too decentralized, allowing for a lack of accountability and coordination.\nH. The bureaucratic approach is too flexible and lacks clear rules and procedures.\nI. Bureaucracies are often disliked for their flexibility in adapting to new situations, which leads to inconsistency and confusion.\nJ. Weber's bureaucratic approach encourages individuality and creativity.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1506, "output_tokens": 306, "total_tokens": 1812}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1901", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 66-year-old client who is depressed, has rhythmic hand movements, and has a flattened affect is probably suffering from\n\nOptions: \nA. Huntington's disease\nB. Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease\nC. Multiple Sclerosis\nD. Alzheimer's disease\nE. Parkinson's disease\nF. Vascular Dementia\nG. Frontotemporal Dementia\nH. Schizophrenia\nI. a right frontal lobe tumor\nJ. Bipolar Disorder\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 670, "output_tokens": 351, "total_tokens": 1021}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2512", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider the distribution of the previous problem. Let us add 2 relatively high values in order to observe the differential effecton the three measures of central tendency. Use the followingeight ordered values: 3, 5, 6, 6, 7, 9, 16, 20.\n\nOptions: \nA. Mean is unaffected, median is somewhat affected, mode is most affected\nB. Median is most affected, mean is somewhat affected, mode is unaffected\nC. All measures are unaffected\nD. Mean and median are equally affected, mode is most affected\nE. All measures are equally affected\nF. Mean is most affected, median is somewhat affected, mode is unaffected\nG. Median is unaffected, mean and mode are equally affected\nH. Mode and median are equally affected, mean is unaffected\nI. Mode is unaffected, mean is somewhat affected, median is most affected\nJ. Mode is most affected, median is somewhat affected, mean is unaffected\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1120, "output_tokens": 451, "total_tokens": 1571}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2488", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A listener-sponsored radio station wants to estimate the amount of money the typical supporter contributes during a fund-drive. In a sample of 30 supporters, it was discovered that 22 of them gave $60, six of them gave $1,000, and two of them gave $10,000. Based on this sample, which of the following measures of central tendency would provide the most useful information to the radio station?\n\nOptions: \nA. Range\nB. Variance\nC. Standard Deviation\nD. Median\nE. Frequency Distribution\nF. Histogram\nG. Quartiles\nH. Mode\nI. ANOVA\nJ. Mean\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 827, "output_tokens": 230, "total_tokens": 1057}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2406", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: At the termination of an extensive training program, management may expect to find chat\n\nOptions: \nA. primarily high-ability trainees have improved in performance\nB. most trainees have improved, but relative standing is generally maintained\nC. all trainees have significantly decreased in performance\nD. there is no noticeable change in the performance of the trainees\nE. the performance of the trainees is directly proportional to their initial ability\nF. only the trainees who were initially performing poorly have improved\nG. the improvement in performance of trainees is not related to the training program\nH. primarily low-ability trainees have improved in performance\nI. all trainees are at the same performance level\nJ. only the trainees with previous experience have improved\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 880, "output_tokens": 240, "total_tokens": 1120}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2133", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To treat Zoe's anorexia nervosa, her doctors put her on intravenous feeding tubes, tried to change her irrational belief that she was too fat, and discussed how her early family relationships may have contributed to her current problems. This approach would best be classified as\n\nOptions: \nA. Behaviorist.\nB. cognitive behavioral.\nC. Humanistic.\nD. Psychoanalytic.\nE. Socio-cultural.\nF. psychodynamic.\nG. eclectic.\nH. biological.\nI. Gestalt.\nJ. Existential.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 684, "output_tokens": 254, "total_tokens": 938}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1981", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: TYPE II ERROR is the failure to reject a false null hypothesis. The Power is the probability of NOT making a Type II error and is effected by several factors. Which factor out of the following ones that have influence on the power is incorrectly defined?\n\nOptions: \nA. Variability\u2192 power decreases as variability increases\nB. as differences between populations means increase, power increases\nC. Sample Size\u2192 power decreases with sample size increase\nD. Confidence level\u2192 power decreases as confidence level increases\nE. 1-tailed tests have higher power\nF. Alpha\u2192 power increases as alpha level increases\nG. Population size\u2192 power decreases as population size increases\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 888, "output_tokens": 222, "total_tokens": 1110}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2151", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: LSD used to be called a \"psychomimetic\" drug because it caused effects similar to those of mental illness. Why has this explanation been refuted?\n\nOptions: \nA. LSD has been found to improve mental health in patients\nB. The effects of LSD and the schizophrenic state are different\nC. LSD and schizophrenia have identical symptoms\nD. LSD does not cause hallucinations\nE. Schizophrenia is caused by LSD use\nF. The effects of LSD are universally the same for all individuals\nG. LSD only affects the visual cortex of the brain\nH. LSD causes permanent mental illness\nI. LSD's effects last for the duration of the drug's presence in the body\nJ. LSD's effects are only physical, not psychological\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 872, "output_tokens": 271, "total_tokens": 1143}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2224", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: As a child, Fara\u2019s responsibilities were to help her mother in the kitchen while her brother and father mowed the lawn. She was expected to do the housework like her mother while her brother did yard work like their father. What part of Feminist Therapy addresses these issues?\n\nOptions: \nA. Self-Concept Therapy\nB. Feminist Object Relations\nC. Household Responsibilities\nD. Maternal Role Therapy\nE. Empowerment Therapy\nF. Family Dynamics Therapy\nG. Child Responsibility Therapy\nH. Women's Rights Therapy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 729, "output_tokens": 325, "total_tokens": 1054}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2101", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The most frequent training types are occupation-specific technical training, computer related and managerial/supervision training; Needs Analysis is used for determining if and what kind of training is necessary. Which component out of the following ones is not of the Need Analysis?\n\nOptions: \nA. organization analysis\nB. skills analysis\nC. task analysis\nD. performance analysis\nE. job analysis\nF. person analysis\nG. program design\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 672, "output_tokens": 341, "total_tokens": 1013}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2199", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Distinguish between the white and gray matter of the central nervous system.\n\nOptions: \nA. \"White matter\" and \"gray matter\" are terms used to describe the coloration of neurons during staining procedures.\nB. \"White matter\" is the nerve fiber pathways and \"gray matter\" is the collections of cell bodies.\nC. \"White matter\" refers to unmyelinated axons, while \"gray matter\" refers to myelinated axons.\nD. \"White matter\" consists of dendrites and \"gray matter\" consists of neuron cell bodies and axons.\nE. \"White matter\" and \"gray matter\" are both types of neurons.\nF. \"White matter\" is found only in the spinal cord, while \"gray matter\" is found only in the brain.\nG. \"White matter\" is composed of glial cells only, while \"gray matter\" consists of both neurons and glial cells.\nH. \"White matter\" contains the synapses and \"gray matter\" contains the neurotransmitters.\nI. \"White matter\" is the myelin sheath and \"gray matter\" is the axons.\nJ. \"White matter\" is the collections of cell bodies and \"gray matter\" is the nerve fiber pathways.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is B. White matter consists primarily of myelinated axon tracts (nerve fiber pathways), while gray matter contains neuron cell bodies, dendrites, and unmyelinated axons. This distinction is fundamental to the structure of the central nervous system.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1609, "output_tokens": 446, "total_tokens": 2055}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1935", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Research has shown that people who read a job description written only with male pronouns (e.g., he, his) are more likely to think of an employee as male than people who read a description that uses gender-neutral language (e.g., he or she). This finding is most closely linked to\n\nOptions: \nA. the linguistic relativity hypothesis.\nB. gender schema theory.\nC. the social role hypothesis.\nD. modeling.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 683, "output_tokens": 419, "total_tokens": 1102}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2506", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Discuss transfer of training in everyday life and in formal education.\n\nOptions: \nA. Direct transfer, indirect transfer, and transfer of principles\nB. Transfer of training, transfer of elements, and transfer of theory\nC. Horizontal transfer, vertical transfer, and random transfer\nD. Cognitive transfer, affective transfer, and psychomotor transfer\nE. Immediate transfer, delayed transfer, and ultimate transfer\nF. Positive transfer, negative transfer, and zero transfer\nG. General transfer, specific transfer, and non-transferable skills\nH. Negative transfer, positive transfer, and maximum transfer\nI. Proactive transfer, retroactive transfer, and situational transfer\nJ. Transfer of elements, formal-discipline theory, and mental-faculty theory\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 913, "output_tokens": 273, "total_tokens": 1186}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2104", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following correctly completes the analogy: \u201cVision is to hearing as\n\nOptions: \nA. parietal lobe is to frontal lobe.\"\nB. temporal lobe is to parietal lobe.\"\nC. temporal lobe is to frontal lobe.\"\nD. occipital lobe is to parietal lobe.\u201d\nE. parietal lobe is to occipital lobe.\"\nF. parietal lobe is to temporal lobe.\u201d\nG. occipital lobe is to temporal lobe.\u201d\nH. frontal lobe is to parietal lobe.\"\nI. frontal lobe is to occipital lobe.\u201d\nJ. occipital lobe is to frontal lobe.\"\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 844, "output_tokens": 226, "total_tokens": 1070}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2614", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why is the time required to produce associations to pictures greater than the time required to produce associations to words?\n\nOptions: \nA. The color and detail in pictures require additional time for the brain to process.\nB. The picture produces visual associations which have to be transformed into words.\nC. Words trigger immediate linguistic responses, whereas pictures require conversion to linguistic concepts.\nD. Pictures provoke emotional responses.\nE. Pictures require more cognitive processing.\nF. Pictures are more complex than words.\nG. The brain processes pictures in a different hemisphere than words, causing a delay.\nH. Pictures are often ambiguous, leading to a delay in association.\nI. Words are processed sequentially while pictures are processed in parallel, requiring more time to integrate.\nJ. Words are universally standardized while pictures are subject to individual interpretation.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 974, "output_tokens": 259, "total_tokens": 1233}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2357", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of the key features for making a differential diagnosis between bulimia nervosa and anorexia nervosa is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Use of laxatives\nB. Purging\nC. Fear of gaining weight\nD. Bingeing\nE. Excessive exercise\nF. All of the above\nG. Maintaining a normal body weight\nH. Overeating in short periods\nI. None of the above\nJ. Self-imposed starvation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 646, "output_tokens": 425, "total_tokens": 1071}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2029", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a family where all male members have been doctors for generations, Peter decides to become an artist. Although his parentsclaim to love him they are very upset over his choice. How would Rogers explain this attitude shownby Peter's parents?\n\nOptions: \nA. Peter's parents wanted him to continue the family legacy.\nB. Peter's parents' attitude can be explained by the threat to their self-structure, which contains the notion that to be of value, a male family member must be a doctor. This idea is incongruent with their love for their son, causing distress.\nC. Peter's parents believe that being a doctor is the only respectable profession in society.\nD. Peter's parents are afraid that Peter's choice indicates a rejection of family values.\nE. Peter's parents think Peter is not talented enough to be a successful artist.\nF. Peter's parents are worried about the social stigma associated with not following family traditions.\nG. Peter's parents are concerned about the financial stability of being an artist.\nH. Peter's parents are upset because they don't value the arts.\nI. Peter's parents are upset because they fear he will not be able to contribute to the family's reputation.\nJ. Peter's parents assume that Peter's decision is a phase and he will eventually become a doctor.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1304, "output_tokens": 331, "total_tokens": 1635}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2329", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What evidence is there that there are specialized sound detectorsfor human speech ?\n\nOptions: \nA. Auditory complex neurons primarily respond to tactile stimulation instead of auditory signals.\nB. Only a small minority of neurons in the auditory complex are dedicated to processing speech sounds.\nC. 40% of the neurons in the auditory complex do not even respond to pure tones, but only to more complex sounds such as bursts of noise or clicks.\nD. Neurons in the auditory complex are equally responsive to all sound frequencies.\nE. Neurons in the auditory complex respond to changes in light intensity.\nF. Neurons in the auditory complex have been found to respond exclusively to musical tones, not speech.\nG. Auditory complex neurons show a heightened response to visual motion cues rather than sounds.\nH. All neurons in the auditory complex respond only to pure tones.\nI. Neurons in the auditory complex respond to simple, uniform sounds.\nJ. The majority of neurons in the auditory complex are specialized for detecting water sounds.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1064, "output_tokens": 336, "total_tokens": 1400}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2328", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Discuss the segmentation problem in speech recognition as itcontributes to the pattern recognition theory of human perception.\n\nOptions: \nA. The segmentation problem arises when the speech recognition system cannot cope with homophones, words that sound the same but have different meanings.\nB. The segmentation problem is the result of a lack of sufficient training data for the speech recognition system to learn from.\nC. The segmentation problem is due to the speed of speech.\nD. The segmentation problem in speech recognition is that there is no apparent break in the spoken waveform at the beginnings and endings of words, the distinction we hear is a result of neural analysis done by a pattern recognition system.\nE. The segmentation problem occurs because the speech recognition system cannot handle the variations in pitch and tone of the speaker's voice.\nF. The segmentation problem is the result of the speaker's accent.\nG. The segmentation problem is the inability of the speech recognition system to differentiate between different languages.\nH. The segmentation problem is caused by the volume of speech.\nI. The segmentation problem is attributed to the speech recognition system's inability to process multiple speakers simultaneously.\nJ. The segmentation problem is due to background noise interfering with the speech recognition system's ability to accurately process spoken words.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1476, "output_tokens": 325, "total_tokens": 1801}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1986", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A ten-year-old boy, tested with a paper-and-pencil intelligence test, obtained an IQ score of 130. Two years later, he was tested with an alternate form of the same test. Most likely, the obtained score on the second testing would be\n\nOptions: \nA. 130, but with a significant decrease in subtest scores\nB. more than 130\nC. 140, indicating significant intellectual growth\nD. 130\nE. 130, but with a different pare of subtest scores\nF. less than 130\nG. 130, but with a significant increase in subtest scores\nH. 100, showing a significant drop in intelligence quotient\nI. 120, indicating a decrease in intellectual capabilities\nJ. Unpredictable as the test used was different\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 987, "output_tokens": 358, "total_tokens": 1345}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2169", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The principal effect of the current concern co improve the employment opportunities of the educationally or socially disadvantaged has been to encourage the use in employment testing of\n\nOptions: \nA. intelligence quotient tests\nB. norm-referenced test\nC. tests that assess physical abilities\nD. work-sample types of tests\nE. timed tests of a narrow range of abilities\nF. personality assessment tests\nG. tests based solely on academic performance\nH. tests based on social skills\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 714, "output_tokens": 345, "total_tokens": 1059}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1947", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Briefly trace historical attitudes toward human development emphasizing the debate between biological determinism and environmental determinism.\n\nOptions: \nA. Both endogenous (biological) and environmental factors are recognized as essential in human development.\nB. Development is solely determined by biological factors.\nC. Environmental factors shape development until adolescence, after which biology takes over completely.\nD. Biological factors set the potential for development, which is then unchangeable by environmental influences.\nE. Human development is a random process, not influenced by either biological or environmental factors.\nF. Human development is exclusively the result of personal choices, independent of biology or environment.\nG. Human development is predetermined at birth, with no influence from life experiences.\nH. Human development is entirely influenced by the environment.\nI. Development is solely determined by social interactions, with no biological influence.\nJ. Children are innately evil and need to redeem themselves.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1071, "output_tokens": 332, "total_tokens": 1403}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1903", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A father brings his 22-year-old son to you for evaluation. Within the past 6 weeks, this formerly socially active young man has quit his job as a restaurant manager, has become withdrawn, and now spends most of his time in his room watching TV. He reports that he occasionally receives messages from aliens through the TV. Based on this information, which of the following is the most appropriate DSM-IV diagnosis\n\nOptions: \nA. Schizophrenia\nB. Paranoid Personality Disorder\nC. Brief Reactive Psychosis\nD. Bipolar Disorder\nE. Schizophreniform Disorder\nF. Antisocial Personality Disorder\nG. Dissociative Identity Disorder\nH. Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder\nI. Generalized Anxiety Disorder\nJ. Major Depressive Disorder\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 995, "output_tokens": 442, "total_tokens": 1437}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1893", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When an adult mouse or bird is castrated, its sexual behavior virtually disappears. Compare the effects of castration of highly developed primates with the less developed animals.\n\nOptions: \nA. In higher primates such as man, castration does not affect the ability to perform the sexual act, provided the male is sexually mature and experienced.\nB. In primates, castration after sexual maturity reduces aggression but has no effect on sexual behavior.\nC. Primates show a temporary decline in sexual behavior post-castration, but it fully recovers within weeks.\nD. Castration in primates results in complete loss of sexual behavior\nE. Castration in primates has no effect on their sexual behavior at any stage of development.\nF. Castration of primates leads to an increase in sexual behavior due to hormonal imbalances.\nG. Castration affects the ability to perform sexual acts in all animals\nH. Primates can't learn sexual behavior through experience\nI. Castration of primates causes a permanent shift to non-sexual social behavior patterns.\nJ. In higher primates, castration before puberty prevents the development of sexual behavior entirely.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1320, "output_tokens": 378, "total_tokens": 1698}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2530", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: You regularly waive the co-payment for your low-income clients who are covered by insurance and believe this is acceptable since you normally bill your clients on a sliding fee scale. This is:\n\nOptions: \nA. ethical, as long as you are not profiting from the insurance company.\nB. a common and ethical practice.\nC. unethical, as it is considered insurance fraud.\nD. a common practice, but unethical.\nE. ethical, only if the co-payment is waived for all clients, regardless of income.\nF. ethical as long as you don't bill the insurance company for an increased hourly fee in order to collect your full fee.\nG. ethical, only if the clients are made aware of the potential implications to their insurance coverage.\nH. ethical only if the insurance company is aware of the arrangement.\nI. unethical, unless the client agrees to pay the co-payment at a later date.\nJ. ethical as long as the insurance company does not explicitly prohibit such arrangements.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1096, "output_tokens": 269, "total_tokens": 1365}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2271", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Whenever her clients cancel an appointment with Dr. Penny Pincher within less than 24 hours of the appointment, Dr. Pincher routinely bills the client\u2019s insurance company for her full hourly fee. This practice is:\n\nOptions: \nA. typically legal, but considered unethical in certain jurisdictions.\nB. illegal and unethical.\nC. neither legal nor illegal, but ethical.\nD. legal but unethical.\nE. legal, but not considered best practice.\nF. legal and ethical.\nG. illegal, but considered best practice.\nH. illegal but ethical.\nI. neither legal nor illegal, but unethical.\nJ. illegal, but depends on the specific insurance policy.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 826, "output_tokens": 297, "total_tokens": 1123}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2287", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A community bank consists of four branch offices with approximately 60 employees each. The general management would like to institute 2 health risk-reduction program by encouraging weight loss and smoking cessation among the employees. Which of the following programs would be most effective\n\nOptions: \nA. Development of, and participation in, local community group sessions focusing on weight loss and smoking cessation\nB. Employee reimbursement for costs and fees associated with professional help for weight loss and smoking cessation\nC. A competition among the four branches focusing on stepwise reductions in weight and smoking\nD. Providing gym memberships and nicotine patches to all employees\nE. Instituting a penalty system for employees who do not lose weight or quit smoking\nF. Mandatory weight loss and smoking cessation classes during work hours\nG. Distribution of health information and self-help materials related to weight loss and smoking cessation\nH. Implementing a company-wide ban on smoking and unhealthy food in the office.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1270, "output_tokens": 368, "total_tokens": 1638}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2434", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Pay incentives are not always a feasible or effective way of improvingemployee performance or behavior. Discuss the limitingconditions for this program to be effective.\n\nOptions: \nA. Pay incentives work best when they are given randomly rather than based on performance metrics.\nB. The effectiveness of pay incentives largely depends on how the worker perceives the system in relation to all of his needs both material and psychological.\nC. Pay incentives are most effective when applied uniformly across all departments without consideration for individual performance.\nD. Pay incentives are ineffective for employees who are intrinsically motivated and therefore should be avoided in all situations.\nE. The success of pay incentives is solely dependent on the competitiveness of the industry.\nF. Pay incentives always improve employee performance\nG. Workers always trust the job analyst\nH. Pay incentives are only effective when they are kept secret from the employees until after their performance is evaluated.\nI. The effectiveness of pay incentives is guaranteed regardless of the organizational culture and employee engagement levels.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1242, "output_tokens": 346, "total_tokens": 1588}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2090", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What are the selection procedures you would use to select a manager ?Discuss your answer.\n\nOptions: \nA. Marital status, Place of birth, Favorite color\nB. Personality test results, Social media presence, Volunteer work history\nC. Social maturity and breadth, Intelligence, Motivation and drive for achievement, Human relations development, Leadership style\nD. Height and weight, Zodiac sign, Shoe size\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 644, "output_tokens": 332, "total_tokens": 976}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2393", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: As psychologists began to study the effects of mass communication, they saw the need to distinguish between education and propaganda. Is there a distinction, and if so, what is it?\n\nOptions: \nA. The distinction is dependent on which view you choose to take\nB. Propaganda disseminates false information, while education provides only true information\nC. Education is designed for individual learning, while propaganda targets groups\nD. Propaganda is always biased\nE. Propaganda is a form of education that focuses on cultural knowledge\nF. Education is always unbiased\nG. Education aims to inform, while propaganda aims to persuade\nH. Education and propaganda are the same thing\nI. Propaganda uses only emotional appeals, while education relies solely on facts\nJ. Education is a government tool, while propaganda is used by private organizations\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 994, "output_tokens": 374, "total_tokens": 1368}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1989", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The best conclusion that can be drawn about the four-day ( compressed) workweek is that it has:\n\nOptions: \nA. negative effects on productivity but little or no impact on attitudes.\nB. positive effects on productivity but negative effects on attitudes.\nC. long-lasting negative effects on attitudes and productivity.\nD. positive effects on attitudes but little or no impact on productivity.\nE. positive effects on productivity but little or no impact on attitudes.\nF. negative effects on attitudes but positive effects on productivity.\nG. no significant effects on either attitudes or productivity.\nH. negative effects on attitudes initially but, over time, increasingly positive effects on both attitudes and productivity.\nI. positive effects on attitudes initially but, over time, increasingly negative effects on both attitudes and productivity.\nJ. long-lasting positive effects on attitudes and productivity.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 912, "output_tokens": 336, "total_tokens": 1248}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1839", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Electrical stimulation of the brain for the treatment of chronic pain\n\nOptions: \nA. is not effective and can lead to further health complications\nB. is of no practical significance, since it can only provide temporary relief.\nC. may produce its effects by suppressing the central nervous system\nD. is of no practical significance, since stimulation-produced analgesia has been demonstrated only in rats\nE. may produce its effects by blocking the pain signals to the brain\nF. is generally effective, but medically ill-advised because such stimulation has aversive properties\nG. is generally effective, but can lead to addiction\nH. may produce its effects by promoting the release of the neurotransmitter norepinephrine\nI. may produce its effects by promoting the release of the neurotransmitter serotonin\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1057, "output_tokens": 489, "total_tokens": 1546}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1929", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"To \"\"inoculate\"\" someone against a persuasive message. you would:\"\n\nOptions: \nA. provide the person with strong arguments against her beliefs.\nB. Discredit the source of the persuasive message.\nC. warn the person that she is about to hear a message designed to change her beliefs.\nD. Ignore the message and avoid discussing it with the person.\nE. provide the person with arguments against her beliefs and weak refutations of those arguments.\nF. Reiterate the person's current beliefs to strengthen them.\nG. Distract the person during the presentation of the persuasive message.\nH. Provide the person with weak arguments supporting her beliefs.\nI. Encourage the person to disregard any opposing beliefs.\nJ. provide the person with information that supports her current beliefs.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 986, "output_tokens": 357, "total_tokens": 1343}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2191", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: We know less about why certain stimuli are attractive to humansthan we do about what is attractive to fish. Discuss thisstatement.\n\nOptions: \nA. Attractiveness can be precisely measured and quantified in all individuals.\nB. We fully understand the factors that determine human attractiveness.\nC. Attractiveness is a trait that humans are born understanding completely.\nD. Human attractiveness is determined by a single genetic marker.\nE. The principles of attractiveness in humans have been fully mapped out by neuroscience.\nF. Attractiveness is universally consistent across all human cultures.\nG. The attractiveness of stimuli in humans is only influenced by visual cues.\nH. Attractiveness is solely determined by physical appearance.\nI. Attractiveness is a learned behavior.\nJ. Our knowledge about the specific characteristics that determine attractiveness remains on the level of intuition.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 995, "output_tokens": 309, "total_tokens": 1304}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2170", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The diagnosis of Alzheimer's disease can be most accurately verified by\n\nOptions: \nA. Blood test showing elevated levels of certain proteins\nB. Electroencephalogram (EEG) showing abnormal brain activity\nC. ruling out other etiologies through a comprehensive psychodiagnostics workup\nD. neuropsychological testing showing the expected profile of deficits and spared functions\nE. Physical examination and patient history\nF. brain biopsy\nG. computerized tomography (CT) or magnetic resonance imaging scan showing cerebral atrophy\nH. Spinal tap or lumbar puncture\nI. Positron emission tomography (PET) scan showing high glucose levels\nJ. Genetic testing for Alzheimer's related genes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 875, "output_tokens": 388, "total_tokens": 1263}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2377", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If twosubculturalgroups have different mean IQ's (e.g., Blacks and whites) can it be concluded from that evidence that heredity is the most important and influential determinant of intelligence ?\n\nOptions: \nA. Yes\nB. Yes, but only within the same socioeconomic status\nC. Only if the differences are consistent across all environments\nD. Not always\nE. No\nF. Maybe, if other factors like education and access to resources are equal\nG. Maybe\nH. Only if twin studies support the heredity hypothesis\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 732, "output_tokens": 299, "total_tokens": 1031}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2461", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Group A consists of people whose measured interests are highly similar to the interests of engineers, Group B consists of people whose measured interests are highly dissimilar to those of engineers. Which of the following statements would be justified, given that both Group A and Group B entered engineering\n\nOptions: \nA. Group B members would achieve levels of success equal to those of Group A, but would do so more slowly\nB. Group A and Group B would both have equal levels of success and satisfaction in the occupation\nC. Both Group A and Group B would likely be unsuccessful in the occupation\nD. Group B members would be more likely to persist in the occupation\nE. Group A members would be less likely to persist in the occupation\nF. Group B members would be more likely to succeed in the occupation\nG. Group A and Group B would nor differ in success at or satisfaction with the occupation\nH. Group A members would achieve levels of success equal to those of Group B, but would do so more slowly\nI. Group A members would be more likely to persist in the occupation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1256, "output_tokens": 363, "total_tokens": 1619}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1849", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A college freshman obtains a score of 150 on his English final exam, a score of 100 on his math exam, a score of 55 on his chemistry exam, and a score of 30 on his history exam. The means and standard deviations for these tests are, respectively, 125 and 20 for the English exam, 90 and 10 for the math exam, 45 and 5 for the chemistry exam, and 30 and 5 for the history exam. Based on this information, you can conclude that the young man's test performance was best on which exam?\n\nOptions: \nA. Math and History\nB. math\nC. Chemistry and History\nD. English and Math\nE. All of the above\nF. history\nG. English\nH. chemistry\nI. English and History\nJ. None of the above\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 994, "output_tokens": 434, "total_tokens": 1428}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1916", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In personnel selection, it is appropriate to ask a person's age when\n\nOptions: \nA. standardized test results show thar the incumbent does not have all the aptitudes expected for the particular job\nB. age is a bona fide occupational requirement\nC. properly administered intelligence and personality tests suggest that the incumbent is not likely to perform satisfactorily in the future\nD. the interviewer is curious about the applicant's age\nE. it is for the purposes of company demographics and statistics\nF. the incumbent is nearing the typical retirement age\nG. the company has a policy of hiring only individuals of a certain age group\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 768, "output_tokens": 243, "total_tokens": 1011}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2457", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A graduate student designed and conducted a research project for her dissertation and subsequently wrote a journal article describing the study and its results. The original idea for the study was derived from the work of the student\u2019s faculty advisor who also provided the facilities for the student's research. The faculty advisor wants to be listed as first author on the article when it is published. In this situation:\n\nOptions: \nA. authorship should be determined by the dean of the school.\nB. the student and advisor should decide authorship through a coin flip.\nC. the student should file a complaint against the advisor with the Ethics Committee.\nD. the student should abandon the project to avoid conflict.\nE. it is up to the student to determine authorship credit.\nF. the advisor should be listed as the only author.\nG. the student should be listed as the first author.\nH. it is up to the advisor to determine authorship credit.\nI. both the student and advisor should be listed as co-first authors.\nJ. the advisor should be listed as the first author.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1108, "output_tokens": 268, "total_tokens": 1376}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1884", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Is there a relationship between intelligence and personality ?\n\nOptions: \nA. Intelligence is a subset of personality traits\nB. Personality completely determines intelligence\nC. Intelligence enhances personality traits\nD. Personality and intelligence are the same concept\nE. Intelligence and personality have no connection\nF. Personality affects test-taking behavior and resultant scores\nG. Intelligence determines personality traits\nH. Personality only affects emotional intelligence\nI. Personality has no impact on test scores\nJ. Intelligence is not affected by personality\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 770, "output_tokens": 325, "total_tokens": 1095}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2282", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Dr. Ryan is a psychotherapist in a small town. She receives a phone call from a man she was sexually involved with several years ago. The relationship lasted only three months and ended amicably. The man is now married and is having problems unrelated to their past relationship. He has called to see if he can begin seeing Dr. Ryan in therapy. Dr. Ryan should:\n\nOptions: \nA. see the man but disclose their past relationship to a supervisor or colleague for transparency.\nB. deny the man's request without providing a reason.\nC. see the man only if their relationship ended more than two years ago and she determines that it will not interfere with her objectivity.\nD. see the man only if she feels she can maintain professional boundaries despite their past.\nE. refer the man to a colleague.\nF. continue therapy with the man but avoid discussing their past relationship.\nG. see the man only if she determines that their past relationship will not interfere with her objectivity.\nH. provide therapy for the man over the phone or through online sessions to maintain physical boundaries.\nI. see the man only if his wife is aware of their past relationship and consents to the therapy.\nJ. see the man but discuss the potential for con\ufb02icts with him before beginning treatment.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1442, "output_tokens": 398, "total_tokens": 1840}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2075", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: discuss these two points of view andgive evidence for both sides.\n\nOptions: \nA. Perception develops independently of innate abilities and is entirely shaped by cultural influences.\nB. The development of perception is a fixed process that remains constant across different environmental conditions.\nC. Human perception is purely innate.\nD. Perception is a learned skill that has no basis in biology or innate structures.\nE. Perception only involves individual sensations coming together.\nF. Perception is the result of a complex interplay between genetic predispositions and sensory experiences.\nG. Perceptual abilities are determined solely by the immediate physical environment, with no influence from biology or past experiences.\nH. Innate perceptual abilities are completely unchangeable and unaffected by learning or experience.\nI. It is likely that we do have some innate perceptual abilities, and also that they can, to some extent, be modified by experience.\nJ. Perception is solely based on past experiences.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1082, "output_tokens": 344, "total_tokens": 1426}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1904", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Research suggests children\u2019s successful adjustment to the divorce of their parents is most related to:\n\nOptions: \nA. the quality of the parent-child relationships prior to the divorce.\nB. the degree of post-divorce conflict between the parents.\nC. the child's academic performance prior to the divorce.\nD. the frequency of contact with the noncustodial parent.\nE. the gender of the child.\nF. the socio-economic status of the parents.\nG. the remarriage of the custodial parent.\nH. the number of siblings the child has.\nI. the age of the child at the time of the divorce.\nJ. the child\u2019s ability to understand the cause(s) of the divorce.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 827, "output_tokens": 227, "total_tokens": 1054}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1920", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If adverse impact on some minority group has been observed, which of the following types of tests probably has the best chance of withstanding legal challenge\n\nOptions: \nA. Projective\nB. Empirically keyed\nC. Personality test\nD. Multiple-choice\nE. Computer adaptive test\nF. Integrity test\nG. Work sample\nH. Situational judgement test\nI. Cognitive ability test\nJ. Polygraph test\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 650, "output_tokens": 301, "total_tokens": 951}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1843", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: You have been treating a teenage male you suspect may have some neurologic difficulties. You inform his parents about your concerns and suggest they send him to a neurologist for an evaluation. Sometime later, the neurologist contacts you and requests your progress notes. You should ___________.\n\nOptions: \nA. Ask your client's parents to send the records\nB. Ask the neurologist to sign a confidentiality agreement before sending the records\nC. Inform the neurologist that you would need a release of information signed by your client\u2019s parents\nD. Request that the neurologist obtain the records from the hospital\nE. Send the records only if the parents give verbal consent\nF. Refuse to send the records, citing patient confidentiality\nG. Ask your client whether he wishes to have the records released to the neurologist\nH. Tell the neurologist the parents need to request the records\nI. Send a summary of your notes, but withhold the full records\nJ. Send the records as requested\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1196, "output_tokens": 291, "total_tokens": 1487}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2612", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What are the advantages and disadvantages of cross-cultural tests ?\n\nOptions: \nA. Advantages: eliminates cultural bias. Disadvantages: may not reflect real-world success\nB. Advantages: encourages the development of universal cognitive models. Disadvantages: may neglect the importance of cultural context in cognitive development.\nC. Advantages: more cost-effective and easier to administer. Disadvantages: may oversimplify complex cultural traits and intelligence.\nD. Advantages: increases the comparability of scores across cultures. Disadvantages: may inadvertently introduce new forms of bias.\nE. Advantages: compensate for cultural disadvantages and measure innate abilities fairly. Disadvantages: lose predictive and diagnostic value, and may not provide useful information for success within the culture.\nF. Advantages: reduces the need for translation and adaptation of tests. Disadvantages: may not capture the full spectrum of cognitive abilities across cultures.\nG. Advantages: enhances cross-cultural understanding. Disadvantages: may require frequent updates to remain culturally relevant.\nH. Advantages: can be used globally. Disadvantages: may not accurately measure intelligence\nI. Advantages: provides a universal standard for intelligence. Disadvantages: may favor certain cultures over others\nJ. Advantages: allows for a more diverse sample of test-takers. Disadvantages: can be less reliable due to varying interpretations of test material.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1472, "output_tokens": 274, "total_tokens": 1746}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1892", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Have studies on learning supported the Incremental or the One-trial Theory of learning?\n\nOptions: \nA. Incremental Theory is supported in cognitive tasks, while One-trial Theory is supported in motor tasks.\nB. The Incremental Theory is universally supported, while the One-trial Theory has been completely discredited.\nC. Studies support the One-trial Theory in the short term, but the Incremental Theory in the long term.\nD. Studies support a hybrid model that combines elements of both theories.\nE. One-trial Theory is supported for simple tasks, while Incremental Theory is for complex tasks.\nF. Neither theories of learning are correct.\nG. Both theories of learning are correct, depending on the context.\nH. The Incremental Theory is only supported in animal studies, while the One-trial Theory is supported in human studies.\nI. Only One-trial Theory of learning is supported.\nJ. Only Incremental Theory of learning is supported.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1028, "output_tokens": 341, "total_tokens": 1369}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1877", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Verbal stimuli may be an acquired source of drive. Discuss.\n\nOptions: \nA. Verbal cues are effective as motivational sources only in specific cultural contexts.\nB. Only non-verbal stimuli can serve as sources of drive.\nC. Verbal stimuli serve as a source of drive exclusively in early childhood development.\nD. Verbal stimuli are an innate source of drive, not acquired.\nE. Verbal stimuli are not an acquired source of drive.\nF. Verbal stimuli only affect animals, not humans.\nG. Verbal stimuli can only motivate if accompanied by physical reinforcement.\nH. Verbal stimuli have no motivational properties and are purely informational.\nI. Language has no influence on human behavior.\nJ. Certain verbal cues may become acquired motivational sources, mainly through the learned responses that they evoke.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 950, "output_tokens": 299, "total_tokens": 1249}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1827", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: You receive a phone call from Hermann H., age 28, who says he is \u201ctotally miserable\u201d because of the recent breakup with his girlfriend and that he would like to begin therapy with you. During the first session with Hermann, you find out that his political views are completely repugnant to you, and you feel that you would not enjoy working with him. As an ethical psychologist, you should:\n\nOptions: \nA. Discuss your discomfort with Hermann's political views in the first session.\nB. Ignore your personal feelings and continue therapy without discussing the difference in political views.\nC. discuss the difference in political views with Hermann only if they become relevant to the psychotherapy process.\nD. Suggest Hermann to find a psychologist who shares his political views.\nE. Decline Hermann's request for therapy because of the difference in political views.\nF. see Hermann in therapy until his current crisis is over and then make a referral if necessary.\nG. Tell Hermann outright that his political views are repugnant and continue the therapy.\nH. Offer to treat Hermann only if he changes his political views.\nI. provide Hermann with appropriate referrals.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1418, "output_tokens": 477, "total_tokens": 1895}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2578", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A graduate student\u2019s dissertation chair, Dr. X, turns out to be of little help, and the student ends up obtaining advice and assistance from an associate professor, Dr. Z. Dr. X does review the dissertation when it is completed and she is listed as the dissertation chair. Several months later, the student decides to write an article for a professional journal that is based his dissertation research. In terms of publication credit:\n\nOptions: \nA. Dr. Z should not be listed as an author since she is not the student's official dissertation chair.\nB. Dr. Y and Dr. Z should be listed as co-authors.\nC. Dr. X should be listed as second author since she was the student\u2019s official dissertation chair.\nD. The student should be the sole author as the research is based on his dissertation.\nE. Dr. X should be listed as first author since she was the student\u2019s official dissertation chair.\nF. Dr. Z should be listed as first author if her contribution was substantial.\nG. Dr. X and Dr. Z should be listed as co-authors with no particular order.\nH. Dr. Z should be listed as second author if her contribution warrants it.\nI. Dr. X should be listed as second author and Dr. Z should not be included as an author.\nJ. Dr. Z should be listed as first author, and the student should be listed as second author.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1512, "output_tokens": 373, "total_tokens": 1885}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2220", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Dr. Harry Holliday, a clinical psychologist, is planning to take a three-week cruise. In terms of his clinical practice, Dr. Holliday\u2019s best course of action would be to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Leave without informing his clients of his absence.\nB. give his clients a phone number where he can be reached.\nC. Provide his clients with online resources to manage their issues in his absence.\nD. Continue his sessions via phone calls or video conferencing while on vacation.\nE. Inform his clients only a day before his departure about his unavailability.\nF. Cancel all appointments for the duration of his vacation without informing his clients.\nG. discuss his vacation plans with his current clients ahead of time so that they know he\u2019ll be unavailable during that time.\nH. hire a colleague to take over his appointments while he is on vacation.\nI. give his clients the phone number of a colleague who has agreed to accept phone calls in emergencies.\nJ. Arrange for a colleague to provide only emergency sessions, while regular appointments are paused.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1096, "output_tokens": 260, "total_tokens": 1356}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1926", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Of the following, the best way to increase the amount of helping behavior within a community is to\n\nOptions: \nA. decrease the number of individuals in the community\nB. implement strict punishments for non-helping behavior\nC. encourage competition among community members\nD. diffuse the responsibility among all members of the community\nE. decrease the anonymity of individuals in the community\nF. increase the wealth of individuals in the community\nG. decrease the self-esteem of community members\nH. increase the number of individuals in the community\nI. develop programs that promote self-reliance\nJ. initiate programs to raise the self-esteem of community members\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 880, "output_tokens": 335, "total_tokens": 1215}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2430", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of doing field researchand laboratory research with human subjects.\n\nOptions: \nA. Laboratory research results are less valid than field research because they are always artificial.\nB. Laboratory research is always preferable over field research\nC. Field research is always better than laboratory research\nD. Field research is less ethical than laboratory research because it involves real-world scenarios.\nE. Field research yields quicker results than laboratory research.\nF. Field research focuses on real people in real-world situations offering more impact but less control and laboratory research provides controlled situations with less impact but more control. There is a basic tradeoff between impact and control in these two methods.\nG. Field research provides more control than laboratory research\nH. Laboratory research can be conducted in any environment, while field research is limited to specific settings.\nI. Field research typically requires more resources than laboratory research.\nJ. Laboratory research allows for studying larger groups than field research does.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1008, "output_tokens": 316, "total_tokens": 1324}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1919", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Research that demonstrates parents who play more roughly with male children and are more protective of female children is most consistent with which theory of gender-role identity development?\n\nOptions: \nA. Cognitive development\nB. Identity theory\nC. Cultural theory\nD. Biological theory\nE. Constructivist theory\nF. Social learning\nG. Psychoanalytic theory\nH. Gender schema\nI. Psychodynamic\nJ. Evolutionary psychology theory\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 703, "output_tokens": 411, "total_tokens": 1114}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1915", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: You receive an e-mail from Dr. Brenda Browne, a licensed psychologist, who is currently seeing one of your former clients for a substance abuse disorder. Dr. Browne asks you to forward the client\u2019s file to her and states that the client has signed a release authorizing you to do so. You should:\n\nOptions: \nA. Refuse to forward the file as it violates patient privacy laws.\nB. wait until you receive a request from the client before taking any action.\nC. Directly send the original file to the psychologist without any prior discussion with the client.\nD. forward a photocopy of the file to the psychologist as requested.\nE. Delete all the records related to the client's substance abuse disorder before sending the file.\nF. Send only the parts of the file that were created during your treatment of the client.\nG. forward a summary of the file to the psychologist that includes only information related to the client\u2019s current condition.\nH. Ask Dr. Browne for a copy of the signed release before sending the file.\nI. Forward the entire file digitally to the psychologist as requested.\nJ. contact the client to discuss the release of information.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1266, "output_tokens": 285, "total_tokens": 1551}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2290", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following possible outcomes of an experiment is least informative\n\nOptions: \nA. Statistical nonsignificance under low power\nB. Statistical significance under low power\nC. Statistical nonsignificance under high power\nD. Statistical significance under high power\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 490, "output_tokens": 316, "total_tokens": 806}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2042", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A colleague, a licensed psychologist, confides in you that he has just ended a sexual relationship with one of his clients. As he describes the client, you realize that she is someone you referred to him about 18 months ago. As an ethical psychologist, you should:\n\nOptions: \nA. Advise the colleague to inform the Ethics Committee himself.\nB. Contact the local authorities and report the colleague.\nC. Advise the colleague to apologize to the client.\nD. file a complaint against the colleague immediately with the Ethics Committee.\nE. Ignore the matter as it's not your responsibility.\nF. Inform the Ethics Committee without notifying the colleague.\nG. contact the client and discuss the matter with her.\nH. Discuss the matter with other colleagues to seek their advice.\nI. discuss the matter further with the colleague to see what course of action he plans to take.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1068, "output_tokens": 316, "total_tokens": 1384}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_7", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the antecedent of the following conditional proposition: If the university does not increase financial aid, either the president fails to approve it or the board of trustees prevents it.\n\nOptions: \nA. The university increases financial aid.\nB. The university does not increase financial aid.\nC. The board of trustees prevents it.\nD. The president fails to approve it.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 548, "output_tokens": 228, "total_tokens": 776}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_33", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the antecedent of the following conditional proposition: If the Bees don't win their first game, then both the Aardvarks and the Chipmunks win their first games.\n\nOptions: \nA. The Aardvarks win their first game.\nB. The Bees don't win their first game.\nC. The Chipmunks win their first game.\nD. Both the Aardvarks and the Chipmunks win their first games.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 650, "output_tokens": 304, "total_tokens": 954}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_38", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Identify the antecedent of the following conditional proposition: The restaurant does not have peas, so instead they serve corn and potatoes.\n\nOptions: \nA. The restaurant has peas.\nB. The restaurant does not have peas.\nC. The restaurant serves corn.\nD. The restaurant serves potatoes.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 492, "output_tokens": 293, "total_tokens": 785}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_16", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the antecedent of the following conditional proposition: The university raises tuition if, and only if, both the governor approves of it and the board of trustees recommends it.\n\nOptions: \nA. The university raises tuition.\nB. The governor approves of it.\nC. The board of trustees recommends it.\nD. None of the above\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is a biconditional, which can be expressed as two conditionals: \"if both the governor approves and the board recommends, then the university raises tuition\" and \"if the university raises tuition, then both the governor approves and the board recommends.\" The antecedent of the first conditional is the conjunction \"both the governor approves and the board recommends,\" which is not listed as a single option. Therefore, the correct answer is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 654, "output_tokens": 1428, "total_tokens": 2082}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_37", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the antecedent of the following conditional proposition: The university raises tuition if both the governor approves of it and the board of trustees recommends it.\n\nOptions: \nA. The university raises tuition.\nB. The governor approves of it.\nC. The board of trustees recommends it.\nD. The governor approves of it and the board of trustees recommends it.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 572, "output_tokens": 310, "total_tokens": 882}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_53", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the antecedent of the following conditional proposition: The Bees winning their first game is necessary for either the Aardvarks or the Chipmunks not winning their first game.\n\nOptions: \nA. The Aardvarks do not win their first game.\nB. The Bees win their first game.\nC. The Chipmunks do not win their first game.\nD. Either the Aardvarks or the Chipmunks do not win their first game.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 683, "output_tokens": 406, "total_tokens": 1089}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_54", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the antecedent of the following conditional proposition: The Bees win their first game only if either the Aardvarks or the Chipmunks do not win their first games.\n\nOptions: \nA. The Aardvarks do not win their first game.\nB. The Bees win their first game.\nC. The Chipmunks do not win their first game.\nD. Either the Aardvarks or the Chipmunks do not win their first games.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 664, "output_tokens": 364, "total_tokens": 1028}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_91", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the antecedent of the following conditional proposition: The university raises tuition only if both the governor approves of it and the board of trustees recommends it.\n\nOptions: \nA. The university raises tuition.\nB. The governor approves of it.\nC. The board of trustees recommends it.\nD. The governor approves of it and the board of trustees recommends it.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 544, "output_tokens": 336, "total_tokens": 880}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_93", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the antecedent of the following conditional proposition: When the university raises tuition, then either the governor approves of it or the board of trustees doesn't prevent it.\n\nOptions: \nA. The university raises tuition.\nB. The governor approves of it.\nC. The board of trustees prevents it.\nD. The board of trustees doesn't prevent it.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 624, "output_tokens": 331, "total_tokens": 955}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_121", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Use indirect truth tables to determine whether the following argument is valid. If the argument is invalid, choose an option which presents a counterexample. (There may be other counterexamples as well.)\n(K \u00b7 L) \u2283 M\nN \u2283 ~M\nN \u2228 K / L \u2283 K\n\nOptions: \nA. Valid\nB. Invalid. Counterexample when L, M, and N are true and K is false\nC. Invalid. Counterexample when L and M are true and K and N are false\nD. Invalid. Counterexample when L and N are true and K and M are false\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 760, "output_tokens": 676, "total_tokens": 1436}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_43", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Construct a complete truth table for the following pairs of propositions. Then, using the truth tables, determine whether the statements are logically equivalent or contradictory. If neither, determine whether they are consistent or inconsistent. Justify your answers.\n~O \u2283 P and O \u2228 P\n\nOptions: \nA. Logically equivalent\nB. Contradictory\nC. Neither logically equivalent nor contradictory, but consistent\nD. Inconsistent\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 604, "output_tokens": 360, "total_tokens": 964}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_72", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the given formulas of PL is the best symbolization of the following sentence?\nA person is considered to have lived with you for all of the present year if the person was born or died in the present year and your home was this person's home for the entire time this person was alive.\n\nOptions: \nA. [(B \u2228 D) \u2022 H] \u2283 L\nB. [L \u2283 (B \u2228 D)] \u2022 H\nC. L \u2283 [(B \u2228 D) \u2022 H]\nD. (B \u2228 D \u2022 H) \u2283 L\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 737, "output_tokens": 370, "total_tokens": 1107}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_118", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the given formulas of PL is the best symbolization of the following sentence?\nSince the university raised tuition, the president approved of it and the board didn't prevent it.\n\nOptions: \nA. (P \u2022 ~B) \u2283 U\nB. (U \u2283 P) \u2022 B\nC. U \u2283 (P \u2022 ~B)\nD. U \u2283 (P \u2228 ~B)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 590, "output_tokens": 292, "total_tokens": 882}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_opti