r.\n\nOptions: \nA. Sx\nB. xS\nC. sP\nD. Ps\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 408, "output_tokens": 298, "total_tokens": 706}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_13", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Use indirect truth tables to determine whether the following argument is valid. If the argument is invalid, choose an option which presents a counterexample. (There may be other counterexamples as well.)\nE \u2283 (F \u2228 ~G)\nF \u2283 (~E \u2228 ~G) / ~(E \u2261 F)\n\nOptions: \nA. Valid\nB. Invalid. Counterexample when E, F, and G are true\nC. Invalid. Counterexample when E and F are true and G is false\nD. Invalid. Counterexample when E, F, and G are false\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "We need to test if the premises can be true while the conclusion false.  \nThe conclusion ~(E \u2261 F) is false if E and F have the same truth value.  \n\nTry E = T, F = T, G = T:  \nFirst premise: T \u2283 (T \u2228 F) \u2192 T \u2283 T = T.  \nSecond premise: T \u2283 (F \u2228 F) \u2192 T \u2283 F = F.  \nSince the second premise is false, this is not a counterexample; both premises must be true.\n\nTry E = F, F = F, G = F:  \nFirst premise: F \u2283 (F \u2228 T) \u2192 F \u2283 T = T.  \nSecond premise: F \u2283 (T \u2228 T) \u2192 F \u2283 T = T.  \nConclusion ~(F \u2261 F) = ~T = F.  \nBoth premises true, conclusion false, so the argument is invalid.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 929, "output_tokens": 617, "total_tokens": 1546}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_116", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the given formulas of PL is the best symbolization of the following sentence?\nDylan likes neither math nor science.\n\nOptions: \nA. M \u2228 S\nB. ~(M \u2022 S)\nC. ~(M \u2228 S)\nD. ~M \u2228 ~S\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 492, "output_tokens": 249, "total_tokens": 741}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_9", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the given formulas of PL is the best symbolization of the following sentence?\nEverybody loves Raymond, or not.\n\nOptions: \nA. L\nB. ~L\nC. L \u2022 ~L\nD. L \u2228 ~L\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 463, "output_tokens": 314, "total_tokens": 777}, "model_used"