e-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the given formulas of PL is the best symbolization of the following sentence?\nPablo will go to the store if, and only if, his brother drives him and pays for gas.\n\nOptions: \nA. (P \u2261 D) \u2261 G\nB. (D \u2022 G) \u2283 P\nC. P \u2283 (D \u2022 G)\nD. P \u2261 (D \u2022 G)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 578, "output_tokens": 470, "total_tokens": 1048}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_114", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the given formulas of PL is the best symbolization of the following sentence?\nEither England's importing beef is a necessary condition for France's subsidizing agriculture or China promotes human rights given that South Africa doesn't supply diamonds.\n\nOptions: \nA. (E \u2283 F) \u2228 (C \u2261 ~S)\nB. (F \u2283 E) \u2228 (~S \u2261 C)\nC. (E \u2283 F) \u2228 (S \u2283~C)\nD. (F \u2283 E) \u2228 (~S \u2283 C)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 712, "output_tokens": 569, "total_tokens": 1281}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_75", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the given formulas of PL is the best symbolization of the following sentence?\nIf either George enrolls or Harry enrolls, then Ira does not enroll.\n\nOptions: \nA. (G \u2283 H) \u2228 I\nB. (G \u2228 H) \u2283 I\nC. (G \u2283 H) \u2228 ~I\nD. (G \u2228 H) \u2283 ~I\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 604, "output_tokens": 346, "total_tokens": 950}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_115", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the given formulas of PL is the best symbolization of the following sentence?\nEither England's importing beef is a sufficient condition for France's subsidizing agriculture or China's promoting human rights is a necessary condition for South Africa's supplying diamonds.\n\nOptions: \nA. (E \u2283 F) \u2228 (S \u2283 C)\nB. (F \u2283 E) \u2228 (C \u2283 S)\nC. (E \u2283 F) \u2228 (C \u2283 S)\nD. (F \u2283 E) \u2228 (S \u2283 C)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 718, "output_tokens": 452, "total_tokens": 1170}, "model_used": "qwen/q