na reads a Percy Jackson book.\nB: Izzy plays Minecraft.\nC: Emily stops working.\nD: Russell makes dinner.\nE: Ashleigh stops by.\n~C \u2228 D\n\nOptions: \nA. If Emily doesn't stop working then Russell makes dinner.\nB. Emily stops working unless Russell makes dinner.\nC. Emily stops working unless Russell doesn't make dinner.\nD. Emily doesn't stop working unless Russell makes dinner.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 738, "output_tokens": 214, "total_tokens": 952}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_125", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Select the best translation into predicate logic. All children go to some school. (Cx: x is a child; Sx: x is a school; Gxy: x goes to y)\n\nOptions: \nA. (\u2200x)(\u2203y)[(Cx \u2022 Sy) \u2022 Gxy)\nB. (\u2200x)[Sx \u2283 (\u2203y)(Cy \u2022 Gxy)]\nC. (\u2200x)[Cx \u2283 (\u2203y)(Sy \u2022 Gxy)]\nD. (\u2200x)[Sx \u2022 (\u2203y)(Cy \u2022 Gxy)]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 695, "output_tokens": 345, "total_tokens": 1040}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_84", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Use the following key to translate the given formula of PL to natural, English sentences.\nA: Marina reads a Percy Jackson book.\nB: Izzy plays Minecraft.\nC: Emily stops working.\nD: Russell makes dinner.\nE: Ashleigh stops by.\n(A \u2228 ~E) \u2261 (D \u2022 ~B)\n\nOptions: \nA. Either Marina reading a Percy Jackson book or Ashleigh not stopping by is a necessary condition for both Russell making dinner and Izzy not playing Minecraft.\nB. Either Marina reading a Percy Jackson book or Ashleigh not stopping by is a necessary and sufficient condition for Russell making dinner and Izzy playing Minecraft.\nC. Marina reads a Percy Jackson book unless Ashleigh stops by if, and only if, both Russell makes dinner and Izzy doesn't play Minecraft.\nD. Either Marina reads a Percy Jackson book or Ashleigh does not stop by just in case both Russell makes dinner and Izzy doesn't play Minecraft.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1068, "output_tokens": 386, "total_tokens": 1454}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_10", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Select the best translation into predicate logic. All kings are luckier than all paupers. (Kx: x is a king; Px: x is a pauper; Lxy: x is luckier than y)\n\nOptions: \nA. (\u2200x)[Kx \u2283 (\u2200y)(Py \u2283 Lxy)]\nB. (\u2200x)[Kx \u2283 (\u2200y)(Lxy \u2283 Py)]\nC. (\u2200x)(\u2200y)[(Kx \u2022 Py) \u2283 Lyx]\nD. (\u2200x)[(Kx \u2022 (\u2200y)(Py)) \u2283 Lxy]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 741, "output_tokens": 451, "total_tokens": 1192}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_105", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Select the best translation into predicate logic: Some folks are lucky.\n\nOptions: \nA. (\u2203x)(Fx \u2022 Lx)\nB. Fl\nC. Lf\nD. (\u2200x)(Fx \u2022 Lx)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 455, "output_tokens": 294, "total_tokens": 749}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_22", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Select the best English interpretation of the given proposition, using the following translation key: Ax: x is an apartment Hx: x is a house Lx: x is large Bxy: x is bigger than y (\u2200x){{Ax \u2283 (\u2200y)[(Hy \u2022 Ly) \u2283 \u223cBxy]}}\n\nOptions: \nA. All apartments are not bigger than some large house.\nB. No apartment is bigger than any large house.\nC. All l