n \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{Alfred North Whitehead}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 400, "output_tokens": 353, "total_tokens": 753}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_518", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This book proposes that Socrates dies at the moment of the death verdict and considers his response to the verdict as his last words.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question appears to reference a philosophical or literary interpretation rather than a historical account. In Plato's *Phaedo*, Socrates' last words are recorded after the death verdict, during his final hours before drinking the hemlock. Therefore, the premise that Socrates dies at the moment of the verdict is incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{False}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 340, "output_tokens": 316, "total_tokens": 656}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_143", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This work argues that scientific laws are used as \"inference-tickets\" between factual statements as part of its argument that not all indicative sentences report facts.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is likely \"Gilbert Ryle\" or \"Ryle,\" as the concept of \"inference-tickets\" is associated with his work on the function of scientific laws in his book *The Concept of Mind*. Ryle argued that laws are not factual statements but rules for making inferences. Thus, the answer is \\boxed{Gilbert Ryle}.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 464, "output_tokens": 556, "total_tokens": 1020}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_325", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A book about this concept likens it to the capacity to chop, possessed by an axe, and the power of sight, possessed by an eye.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The concept being described is \"virtue,\" specifically in a philosophical sense, as Aristotle uses the analogy of an axe's ability to chop and an eye's ability to see to illustrate that virtue is the proper function or excellence of a human being.  \n\n\\boxed{virtue}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 457, "output_tokens": 359, "total_tokens": 816}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_373", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This man justified the acquisition of property as long as that property is not left to spoil and \"enough and as good\" are left for others.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{John Locke}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 356, "output_tokens": 319, "total_tokens": 675}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_790", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This book compares modern society to a \"sorcerer who is no longer able to control the powers of the nether world whom he has called up by his spells.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is that this quote is from Karl Marx and Friedrich Engels' *The Communist Manifesto*. The phrase describes how the bourgeoisie, like a sorcerer, has unleashed productive forces it cannot control. This metaphor captures Marx's critique of capitalism's tendency toward crisis and instability.\n\n\\boxed{The Communist Manifesto}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 472, "output_tokens": 427, "total_tokens": 899}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1224", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This book argues that the automation of labor turns \"apparatuses we once handled freely\" into \"shells...as...belong to the body of the turtle.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{Heidegger}. This refers to Martin Heidegger's concept of \"standing-reserve\" and his critique of technology in *The Question Concerning Technology*. He argues that modern technology reduces human relationships with tools to a mere \"enframing,\" where they become like shells attached to a turtle rather than freely handled.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 472, "output_tokens": 367, "total_tokens": 839}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1270", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In one paper, this philosopher muses that realism solves Nelson Goodman's new \"riddle of induction\" by positing \"perfectly natural\" properties that \"carve nature at the joints.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{David Lewis}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 403, "output_tokens": 281, "total_tokens": 684}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Philosophy_1458", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A thinker described how complex \"molecular\" versions of these entities arise from four \"inc