iagonally\nG. Circularly\nH. Laterally\nI. Outside to inside\nJ. Vertically from bottom to top\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 540, "output_tokens": 218, "total_tokens": 758}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_424", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: AIDA stands for awareness, ________, desire and _________.\n\nOptions: \nA. Intensity; appeal.\nB. Interest; achievement.\nC. Interest; appeal.\nD. Involvement; appeal.\nE. Involvement; action.\nF. Intensity; action.\nG. Importance; action.\nH. Inclusion; action.\nI. Involvement; adjustment.\nJ. Interest; action.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 592, "output_tokens": 185, "total_tokens": 777}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_4", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Some of key differences between Islamic finance and conventional finance include - prohibition of charging and paying _______, prohibition on ______ and ______ transactions, prohibition of sinful investment and requirement for all financial products to be backed by __________.\n\nOptions: \nA. Interest, Certain, Assured, Both tangible and intangible assets\nB. Interest, Uncertain, Assured, Both tangible and intangible assets\nC. Interest, Uncertain, Speculative, Intangible assets\nD. Interest, Certain, Assured, Tangible assets\nE. Interest, Uncertain, Assured, Intangible assets\nF. Profit, Uncertain, Speculative, Tangible assets\nG. Interest, Uncertain, Speculative, Tangible assets\nH. Interest, Certain, Speculative, Intangible assets\nI. Profit, Certain, Assured, Tangible assets\nJ. Interest, Certain, Speculative, Both tangible and intangible assets\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1012, "output_tokens": 388, "total_tokens": 1400}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_684", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  These store goods for moderate to long periods:\n\nOptions: \nA. Storage warehouses.\nB. Inventory management systems.\nC. Freight trains.\nD. Production factories.\nE. Haulage transport.\nF. Retail outlets.\nG. Wholesale markets.\nH. Shipping containers.\nI. Electronic data interchange.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 522, "output_tokens": 255, "total_tokens": 777}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_25", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Where in the balance sheet does each of the following belong? (A) Taxes payable (B) Capital stock (C) Retailed earnings (D) Administrative expense (E) Prepaid expenses\n\nOptions: \nA. (A) Liability section, (B) Asset side, (C) Owner's Equity section, (D) Asset side, (E) Owner's Equity section\nB. (A) Owner's Equity section, (B) Asset side, (C) Income Statement, (D) Liability section, (E) Liability section\nC. (A) Asset side, (B) Liability section, (C) Income Statement, (D) Owner's Equity section, (E) Income Statement\nD. (A) Owner's Equity section, (B) Liability section, (C) Asset side, (D) Asset side, (E) Income Statement\nE. (A) Income Statement, (B) Liability section, (C) Asset side, (D) Owner's Equity section, (E) Owner's Equity section\nF. (A) Owner's Equity section, (B) Income Statement, (C) Asset side, (D) Asset side, (E) Liability section\nG. (A) Liability section, (B) Asset side, (C) Liability section, (D) Income Statement, (E) Income Statement\nH. (A) Income Statement, (B) Owner's Equity section, (C) Income Statement, (D) Liability section, (E) Asset side\nI. (A) Asset side, (B) Income Statement, (C) Liability section, (D) Owner's Equity section, (E) Liability section\nJ. (A) Liability section, (B) Owner's Equity section, (C) Owner's Equity section, (D) Income Statement, (E) Asset side\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1708, "output_tokens": 335, "total_tokens": 2043}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_148", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the event of bankruptcy, what is the order of payment of bonds, common stock, and preferred stock?\n\nOptions: \nA. Preferred stockholders, common stockholders, bondholders\nB. Bondholders, common stockholders, preferred stockholders\nC. Preferred stockholders, bondholders, common stockholders\nD. Common stockholders, bondholders, preferred stockholders\nE. Bondholders and common stockholders equally, then preferred stockholders\nF. Preferred stockholders, then bondholders and common stockholders equally\nG. Bondholders equally with preferred stockholders, then common stockholders\nH. Common stockholders, preferred stockholders, bondholders\nI. Bondholders, preferred stockholders, common stockholders\nJ. Common stockholders and preferred stockholders equally, then bondholders\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 950, "output_tokens": 263, "total_tokens": 1213}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_748", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The owners of independent gasoline stations in a community meet secretly and agree to keep their prices high to protect their profitability. If their plan is discovered and they are charged with a crime, they could be\n\nOptions: \nA. found guilty under the Sherman Antitrust Act and face prison time\nB. found guilty under the Robinson-Patman Act and face prison time\nC. found guilty under the Magnuson-Moss Warranty Act and face large fines\nD. found not guilty because they did not engage in any form of price fixing\nE. found guilty under the Adamson Act and face prison time and fines\nF. found guilty under the Clayton Act and face both prison time and fines\nG. found not guilty because there is no law against price collusion in this industry\nH. found guilty under the Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act and face fines\nI. found not guilty because retailers are allowed to set their own price levels\nJ. found guilty under the Federal Trade Commission Act and face fines\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1080, "output_tokens": 234, "total_tokens": 1314}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_614", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What does the acronym SMART stand for?\n\nOptions: \nA. Standardised, measurable, achievable, rewarded, and timely\nB. Standardized, measurable, actionable, rewarded and timely\nC. Specific, measurable, actionable, rewarded and time-limited\nD. Specific, measurable, achievable, resourced and time-bound\nE. Suitable, measurable, achievable, resourced and timely\nF. Specific, measurable, achievable, rewarded and timely\nG. Specific, manageable, actionable, rewarded and timely\nH. Suitable, measurable, actionable, rewarded and timely\nI. Specific, measurable, actionable, resourced and timely\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 764, "output_tokens": 316, "total_tokens": 1080}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_605", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What are, according to Wood (1991), the three outcomes of CSR?\n\nOptions: \nA. Social policies, Social responsibility and Social impacts\nB. Social policies, Social evidencing and Social impacts\nC. Social policies, Social audits, and Social impacts\nD. Social policies, Social programmes and Social analysis\nE. Social evaluations, Social programmes and Social impacts\nF. Social policies, Social programmes and Social discussions\nG. Social policies, Social impacts and Social justice\nH. Social assessments, Social programmes and Social impacts\nI. Social planning, Social programmes and Social impacts\nJ. Social policies, Social programmes and Social impacts\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 784, "output_tokens": 220, "total_tokens": 1004}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_237", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: _______ and _______ are both examples of _______ -based theories which are based on basic universal principles of right and wrong.\n\nOptions: \nA. Egoism, Ethics of rights and justice, Consequentialist\nB. Ethics of rights and justice, Egoism, Deontological\nC. Egoism, Utilitarianism, Deontological\nD. Utilitarianism, Ethics of duty, Relativist\nE. Utilitarianism, Egoism, Principle\nF. Ethics of rights and justice, Utilitarianism, Virtue\nG. Ethics of duty, Ethics of rights and justice, Principle\nH. Egoism, Ethics of duty, Relativist\nI. Ethics of duty, Utilitarianism, Consequentialist\nJ. Ethics of duty, Egoism, Virtue\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 930, "output_tokens": 319, "total_tokens": 1249}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_282", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the difference between assets and liabilities called?\n\nOptions: \nA. Balance sum\nB. Debt\nC. Expenses\nD. Net worth\nE. profit\nF. capital\nG. investment\nH. Cash flow\nI. Revenue\nJ. equity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 482, "output_tokens": 211, "total_tokens": 693}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_690", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is not part of Schein's model of the formation of culture?\n\nOptions: \nA. Group dynamics\nB. Norms\nC. Leadership style\nD. Communication methods\nE. Shared values\nF. Pre-conceptions\nG. Decision-making processes\nH. Shared beliefs\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. Shared beliefs are typically considered a component of culture itself, not a distinct mechanism in Schein's model of how culture forms. Schein's model emphasizes group dynamics, norms, leadership style, communication methods, shared values, pre-conceptions, and decision-making processes as key elements in cultural formation. Therefore, \"shared beliefs\" is the least fitting as a standalone part of the formation process.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 626, "output_tokens": 413, "total_tokens": 1039}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_749", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  When there is little or no personal contact between customer and service provider, this is classified as:\n\nOptions: \nA. Medium-contact service.\nB. Indirect-contact service.\nC. Intense-contact service.\nD. Remote-contact service.\nE. Non-personal service.\nF. Infrequent-contact service.\nG. Low-contact service.\nH. Zero-contact service.\nI. Minimal-contact service.\nJ. High-contact service.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 600, "output_tokens": 194, "total_tokens": 794}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_427", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  This is a form of targeted advertising, on websites, with advertisements selected and served by automated systems based on the content displayed to the user.\n\nOptions: \nA. Social media marketing.\nB. Display advertising.\nC. Mobile advertising.\nD. Search engine marketing.\nE. Contextual advertising.\nF. Email advertising.\nG. Direct marketing.\nH. Affiliate marketing.\nI. Interactive marketing.\nJ. Internet advertising.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 592, "output_tokens": 203, "total_tokens": 795}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_290", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is the name for a coupon that is included in a package for later purchase?\n\nOptions: \nA. an in-store coupon\nB. a rebate coupon\nC. a discount coupon\nD. a mail-in coupon\nE. a digital coupon\nF. a promotional coupon\nG. a bounce-back coupon\nH. a peel-off coupon\nI. an instant-redemption coupon\nJ. a free-standing coupon\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 621, "output_tokens": 241, "total_tokens": 862}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_3", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: _______ locate morality beyond the sphere of rationality in an emotional 'moral impulse' towards others.\n\nOptions: \nA. Ethical egoism\nB. Ethics of duty\nC. Postmodern ethics\nD. Consequentialist ethics\nE. Utilitarian ethics\nF. Deontological ethics\nG. Virtue ethics\nH. Ethics of care\nI. Ethics of rights\nJ. Relativist ethics\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 604, "output_tokens": 238, "total_tokens": 842}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_15", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How does lateral communication in an organisation occur?\n\nOptions: \nA. Information is shared only during official meetings.\nB. Information is restricted within a single department.\nC. Information is transferred through external stakeholders.\nD. Information is transferred only through the head of the organisation.\nE. Information is disseminated through public announcements.\nF. Information passes upwards.\nG. Information passes downwards.\nH. Information is a two-way process.\nI. Information passes diagonally between different levels of hierarchy.\nJ. Information passes between different departments and functions.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 742, "output_tokens": 263, "total_tokens": 1005}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_63", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Workers' acceptance of change is characteristic of what type of culture?\n\nOptions: \nA. Process culture\nB. Hierarchical culture\nC. Power culture\nD. Competitive culture\nE. Collaborative culture\nF. Individualistic culture\nG. Task culture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 486, "output_tokens": 235, "total_tokens": 721}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_187", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  _______ can be a likened to their natural counterparts, comprising of a balanced network of interdependent organisms and their environments thus adding value to sustainability thinking due to the consideration of companies and industries as being bound together, and interdependent due to all kinds of resources and wastes.\n\nOptions: \nA. Corporate ecosystems\nB. Natural supply chains\nC. Industrial ecosystems\nD. Corporate supply chains\nE. Ecological ecosystems\nF. Corporate food webs\nG. Industrial supply loops\nH. Industrial food webs\nI. Ecological supply loops\nJ. Industrial food chains\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 724, "output_tokens": 244, "total_tokens": 968}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_228", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Describe a procedure that can be used to determine inventory turnover rate.\n\nOptions: \nA. Inventory turnover rate is calculated by dividing total sales by ending inventory.\nB. Inventory turnover rate is calculated by dividing total sales by average inventory.\nC. Inventory turnover rate is calculated by subtracting the cost of goods sold from the average inventory.\nD. Inventory turnover rate is determined by adding the cost of goods sold to the ending inventory.\nE. Inventory turnover rate is found by dividing average inventory by the cost of goods sold.\nF. Inventory turnover rate is calculated by dividing the beginning inventory by the cost of goods sold.\nG. Inventory turnover rate is calculated by dividing the sum of the beginning and ending inventory by the cost of goods sold.\nH. The inventory turnover rate can be calculated by dividing the cost of goods sold by the average inventory.\nI. Inventory turnover rate is calculated by multiplying the cost of goods sold by the average inventory.\nJ. The inventory turnover rate is found by subtracting the average inventory from the total sales.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1158, "output_tokens": 258, "total_tokens": 1416}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_365", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the following is a type of consumer product bought relatively infrequently and which requires consumers to update their knowledge prior to purchase?\n\nOptions: \nA. Service product.\nB. Durable product.\nC. Shopping product.\nD. Generic products.\nE. Impulse product.\nF. Luxury product.\nG. Promotional product.\nH. Speciality product.\nI. Unsought product.\nJ. Branded products.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 644, "output_tokens": 246, "total_tokens": 890}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_388", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Explain what the term (7/10) EOM means.\n\nOptions: \nA. A customer may deduct 7% of the amount of the invoice if payment is made no later than the tenth day after the end of the month\nB. A customer may deduct 10% of the amount of the invoice if payment is made within 7 days of receiving the invoice\nC. A customer may deduct 7% of the amount of the invoice if payment is made on the tenth day of the month\nD. A customer must pay the full amount of the invoice within 7 days of the end of the month\nE. A customer may deduct 10% of the amount of the invoice if payment is made no later than the seventh day after the end of the month\nF. A customer may deduct 7% of the amount of the invoice if payment is made within 10 days of receiving the invoice\nG. A customer may deduct 10% of the amount of the invoice if payment is made on the 7th day after the end of the month\nH. A customer may deduct 7% of the amount of the invoice if payment is made on the 10th day of the month\nI. A customer must pay the full amount of the invoice within 10 days of the end of the month\nJ. A customer may deduct 10% of the amount of the invoice if payment is made no later than the seventh day of the month\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1484, "output_tokens": 320, "total_tokens": 1804}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_430", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: ________________reflect a purchaser's high level of involvement in the purchase decision. There is high perceived risk in these decisions so consumers spend a great deal of time, care, and energy searching, formulating, and making the final decision.\n\nOptions: \nA. Services.\nB. Perishable items.\nC. Impulse purchases.\nD. Non-durable goods.\nE. Discounted items.\nF. Fast-moving consumer goods.\nG. Durable goods.\nH. Generic products.\nI. Convenience products.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 668, "output_tokens": 235, "total_tokens": 903}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_752", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How can you describe the thinking and outlook of transformational leaders?\n\nOptions: \nA. Functional\nB. Tactical\nC. Narrow-minded\nD. Transactional\nE. Operational\nF. Procedural\nG. Strategic\nH. Micromanaging\nI. Reactive\nJ. Developmental\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 514, "output_tokens": 296, "total_tokens": 810}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_378", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: (a) Convert 678 cm to feet. (b) Convert 316 liters to dry pints. (c) Convert 50 kg to pounds.\n\nOptions: \nA. 21 ft, 625 pints, 105 pounds\nB. 22 ft, 575.12 pints, 110 pounds\nC. 19 ft, 650 pints, 140 pounds\nD. 22 ft, 668 pints, 150 pounds\nE. 24 ft, 600 pints, 120 pounds\nF. 23 ft, 560 pints, 125 pounds\nG. 20 ft, 613 pints, 111 pounds\nH. 25 ft, 580 pints, 115 pounds\nI. 20 ft, 550 pints, 100 pounds\nJ. 18 ft, 590 pints, 130 pounds\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1224, "output_tokens": 533, "total_tokens": 1757}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_727", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Record the maturity date for a draft dated (a) November 12 and payable 60 days after date, (b) June 10 and payable 3 months after date, (c) March 3 and payable 30 days after sight if it is accepted March 15, and (d) October 4 and payable 6 months after sight if it is acceptedOctober 25.\n\nOptions: \nA. January 12, September 10, April 14, April 26\nB. January 12, September 8, April 14, April 23\nC. January 10, September 11, April 15, April 26\nD. January 12, September 9, April 13, April 24\nE. January 11, September 12, April 15, April 26\nF. January 13, September 10, April 16, April 27\nG. January 11, September 11, April 13, April 24\nH. January 10, September 9, April 15, April 25\nI. January 13, September 12, April 16, April 27\nJ. January 11, September 10, April 14, April 25\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1376, "output_tokens": 387, "total_tokens": 1763}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_530", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: You have just redesigned your kitchen. The new floor dimensions are 7'6\" \u00d7 11'8\". Now you want to cover the floor with linoleum, which sells for $1.79 per running foot in 6' width, what is the best way to cover the floor? How much will it cost?\n\nOptions: \nA. $48.60\nB. $26.85\nC. $30.99\nD. $42.56\nE. $29.99\nF. $38.40\nG. $31.50\nH. $23.94\nI. $20.12\nJ. $35.70\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 842, "output_tokens": 855, "total_tokens": 1697}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_227", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mrs. Bracken is a widow who maintains a home for herself, her dependent father, and her two children. (a) What filing status should she claim? (b) How many exemptions is she allowed?\n\nOptions: \nA. Single, four exemptions\nB. Qualifying widow(er), three exemptions\nC. Qualifying widow(er), six exemptions\nD. Married filing jointly, three exemptions\nE. Qualifying widow(er), five exemptions\nF. Married filing jointly, four exemptions\nG. Married filing separately, two exemptions\nH. Single, three exemptions\nI. Head of household, three exemptions\nJ. Head of household, four exemptions\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 820, "output_tokens": 363, "total_tokens": 1183}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_640", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose Q is a measure of output, K is a measure of capital stock in use, and L is a measure of the size of the employed labor force. Q =AK^\\betaL^\\gamma is a much used form of production function. When \\beta + \\gamma = 1, it is known as a Cobb-Douglas production function. This function has many convenient properties: Marginal products of both labor and capital are positive if \\beta and \\gamma are. If \\beta + \\gamma = 1, the function has constant returns to scale. That is, if both inputs are increased in like proportion, output will increase in that same proportion. A doubling of both inputs, for example, will result in doubled output. Discuss how the concept of linear regression might be applied to estimate \\beta and \\gamma .\n\nOptions: \nA. Polynomial regression\nB. Linear progression\nC. Quantile regression\nD. Ridge regression\nE. Logistic regression\nF. Exponential regression\nG. Lasso regression\nH. Multiple regression\nI. Single regression\nJ. Non-linear regression\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1148, "output_tokens": 550, "total_tokens": 1698}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_135", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Traders in major financial institutions use the Black-Scholes formula in a backward fashion to infer other traders' estimation of $\\sigma$ from option prices. In fact, traders frequently quote sigmas to each other, rather than prices, to arrange trades. Suppose a call option on a stock that pays no dividend for 6 months has a strike price of $35, a premium of $2.15, and time to maturity of 7 weeks. The current short-term T-bill rate is 7%, and the price of the underlying stock is $36.12. What is the implied volatility of the underlying security?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.275\nB. 0.225\nC. 0.165\nD. 0.195\nE. 0.210\nF. 0.350\nG. 0.300\nH. 0.180\nI. 0.320\nJ. 0.251\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1054, "output_tokens": 489, "total_tokens": 1543}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_183", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: (A) How many gallons are there in 12 liters? (B) How many liters are there in 10 quarts? Metric to Customary Units Customary to Metric Units 1 liter = 1.057 quarts .264 gallon 1 quart = .946 liter 1 gallon = 3.785 liters 1 milliliter = .0338 ounce 1 ounce = 29.57 milliliters\n\nOptions: \nA. (A) 3.168 gallons (B) 9.46 liters\nB. (A) 3.18 gallons (B) 9.6 liters\nC. (A) 2.64 gallons (B) 9.46 liters\nD. (A) 2.5 gallons (B) 9 liters\nE. (A) 2.64 gallons (B) 10.5 liters\nF. (A) 3.5 gallons (B) 9.46 liters\nG. (A) 3 gallons (B) 9.5 liters\nH. (A) 3.168 gallons (B) 10.46 liters\nI. (A) 3.168 gallons (B) 11 liters\nJ. (A) 3.2 gallons (B) 10 liters\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1468, "output_tokens": 309, "total_tokens": 1777}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_591", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the date of maturity of a note dated January 30with aterm of one month?\n\nOptions: \nA. January 30\nB. March 1\nC. March 30\nD. February 25\nE. January 31\nF. March 2\nG. February 1\nH. February 30\nI. February 27\nJ. February 29 or February 28\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 615, "output_tokens": 324, "total_tokens": 939}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_352", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the date of maturity of a 60-day note dated March 15?\n\nOptions: \nA. May 15\nB. April 15\nC. July 14\nD. April 14\nE. April 13\nF. June 15\nG. June 14\nH. March 16\nI. May 14\nJ. May 13\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 620, "output_tokens": 467, "total_tokens": 1087}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_600", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the number of single rolls required to paper a room 18 feet long, 12 feet wide, and 10 feet high, allowing for a 10% waste of paper. A single roll consists of 36 square feet of paper. Make allowance for openings, which include one window 3 feet by 8 feet and one door 4 feet by 9 feet.\n\nOptions: \nA. 17 rolls\nB. 20 rolls\nC. 16 rolls\nD. 23 rolls\nE. 14 rolls\nF. 19 rolls\nG. 18 rolls\nH. 21 rolls\nI. 15 rolls\nJ. 22 rolls\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 834, "output_tokens": 686, "total_tokens": 1520}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_445", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A man shipped his car to Israel. In the United States his car averaged 10 miles to the gallon of gas. He now wishes to convert this figure in order to compare his car's efficiency to that of the Israeli cars. Convert the miles per gallon to kilometers per liter.\n\nOptions: \nA. 7.2 kilometers per liter\nB. 6.5 kilometers per liter\nC. 3.7 kilometers per liter\nD. 2.8 kilometers per liter\nE. 3.0 kilometers per liter\nF. 8.1 kilometers per liter\nG. 4.16 kilometers per liter\nH. 2.2 kilometers per liter\nI. 9.4 kilometers per liter\nJ. 5.3 kilometers per liter\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 896, "output_tokens": 523, "total_tokens": 1419}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_504", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Your company has just written one million units of a one-year European asset-or-nothing put option on an equity index fund. The equity index fund is currently trading at 1000. It pays dividends continuously at a rate proportional to its price; the dividend yield is 2%. It has a volatility of 20%. The option\u2019s payoff will be made only if the equity index fund is down by more than 40% at the end of one year. The continuously compounded risk-free interest rate is 2.5% Using the Black-Scholes model, determine the price of the asset-or-nothing put options. Give the answer in millions.\n\nOptions: \nA. 7.5\nB. 5.2\nC. 3.6\nD. 2.2\nE. 2.5\nF. 4.1\nG. 4.7\nH. 5.9\nI. 1.9\nJ. 6.8\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The asset-or-nothing put pays the asset price at expiration if the final price is below the strike. Here, the strike is 60% of the current price, so \\(K = 600\\). Using the Black-Scholes formula for an asset-or-nothing put, the price is \\(S_0 e^{-qT} N(-d_1)\\), with  \n\\(d_1 = \\frac{\\ln(1000/600) + (0.025 - 0.02 + 0.5 \\times 0.2^2) \\times 1}{0.2 \\times 1} \\approx 2.581\\).  \nThen \\(N(-2.581) \\approx 0.00492\\), so the price per option is \\(1000 e^{-0.02} \\times 0.00492 \\approx 4.82\\), and for one million units it is approximately 4.82 million, which rounds to 4.7 million.  \n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1297, "output_tokens": 3776, "total_tokens": 5073}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_382", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the total cost of mailing to an overseas country a 3% ounce letter that contains documents valued at $225 by registered mail? The overseas postal rates are 31\\textcent for each (1 / 2) ounce up to 2 ounces, and 26$ for each additional (1 / 2) ounce. The registry fee for a letter worth $225 is $2.60.\n\nOptions: \nA. $6.22\nB. $4.42\nC. $5.92\nD. $5.62\nE. $4.62\nF. $5.32\nG. $4.72\nH. $3.62\nI. $3.92\nJ. $3.82\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 955, "output_tokens": 642, "total_tokens": 1597}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_404", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A research worker was interested in racial differences in the standard of living of farm operators in the southeastern United States. He used the presence of running water in farm dwellings as a crude index of the standard of living. For each of 31 economic areas in North Carolina, South Carolina, and Georgia in 1945, he calculated two mea-sures : X = farms operated by nonwhites per 100 white farm operators and Y = percent of farms having running water in dwellings. The fol-lowing values were obtained: \\sum X = 1,860\\sum Y = 465\\sum XY = 23,400 \\sum X^2 = 201,600\\sum Y^2 = 7,925n = 31 Compute the regression line and the correlation of X and Y.\n\nOptions: \nA. Y = 18 - 0.05 X, r = - .4867\nB. Y = 16 - 0.08 X, r = -0.6000\nC. Y = 20 - 0.05 X, r = - .4867\nD. Y = 18 - 0.05 X, r = - .4000\nE. Y = 20 - 0.07 X, r = -0.5500\nF. Y = 18 + 0.06 X, r = 0.4867\nG. Y = 18 - 0.06 X, r = - .4867\nH. Y = 22 - 0.04 X, r = -0.3000\nI. Y = 15 + 0.03 X, r = 0.3500\nJ. Y = 19 - 0.05 X, r = 0.4867\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1984, "output_tokens": 1129, "total_tokens": 3113}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_433", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: assume you are Indonesian. In 2010, the rupiah exchange rate was around IDR15,000/USD, and the consumer price index in Indonesia and the United States was at 100. In 2019, the exchange rate changed to IDR14,000/USD. Simultaneously, Indonesia\u2019s inflation rose 5% due to the consumer price index rising to 105. Meanwhile, the United States\u2019 inflation rate rose 10% due to the consumer price index rising to 110. Whats the real exchange rate?\n\nOptions: \nA. 14000.00\nB. 15500.00\nC. 15000.00\nD. 16000.00\nE. 13500.00\nF. 14666.67\nG. 13888.89\nH. 14800.00\nI. 15200.00\nJ. 13333.33\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1248, "output_tokens": 380, "total_tokens": 1628}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_553", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  An organization can offer standard products at acceptable levels of quality, yet still generate above-average profit margin by adopting _____________\n\nOptions: \nA. Differentiation.\nB. Cost leadership.\nC. Focus strategy.\nD. Branding strategy.\nE. Growth strategy.\nF. Market penetration strategy.\nG. Diversification strategy.\nH. Market development strategy.\nI. Product development strategy.\nJ. Market follower strategy.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 626, "output_tokens": 267, "total_tokens": 893}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_479", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Angela Rodriguez is single, not head of any household, and claims one exemption. She earned $9,357 duringthe year, of which $1,397 was withheld as federal tax. She has decided to take a standard deduction. Using the table for standard deductions, calculate how much additional tax Angela must pay.\n\nOptions: \nA. $6\nB. $0 (No additional tax due)\nC. $5\nD. $7\nE. $12\nF. $8\nG. $15\nH. $10\nI. $20\nJ. $3\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 768, "output_tokens": 465, "total_tokens": 1233}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_370", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let\u2019s assume Mutual Fund A has an annualized return of 15% and a downside deviation of 8%. Mutual Fund B has an annualized return of 12% and a downside deviation of 5%. The risk-free rate is 2.5%. What is the Sortino ratio for Fund A?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.2\nB. 0.8\nC. 2.0\nD. 1.0\nE. 1.4\nF. 0.95\nG. 1.8\nH. 2.3\nI. 1.56\nJ. 2.5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 812, "output_tokens": 324, "total_tokens": 1136}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_742", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Round .1476 to (a) 2 decimal places (b) 3 decimal places (c) 1 decimal place.\n\nOptions: \nA. (a) .15 (b) .148 (c) .1\nB. (a) .15 (b) .147 (c) .14\nC. (a) .14 (b) .148 (c) .2\nD. (a) .14 (b) .149 (c) .14\nE. (a) .15 (b) .149 (c) .15\nF. (a) .14 (b) .147 (c) .2\nG. (a) .15 (b) .147 (c) .2\nH. (a) .15 (b) .149 (c) .1\nI. (a) .14 (b) .147 (c) .1\nJ. (a) .14 (b) .148 (c) .15\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1236, "output_tokens": 441, "total_tokens": 1677}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_51", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Assume the following model (from the preceding problem). Y = C + I + G C = 100 + 0.6Y I = 0.2Y - 50i M_D = 0.25Y - 30i M_s = 65 G = 100 whose equilibrium level was found to be 500. Suppose that full employment level of income is 600, so that the desired change is 100. If the money supply is held constant, what change in govern-ment spending will be required to close the deflationary gap?\n\nOptions: \nA. 80\nB. 75\nC. 55\nD. 90\nE. 50\nF. 61.5\nG. 70\nH. 85\nI. 100\nJ. 65\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1032, "output_tokens": 620, "total_tokens": 1652}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_463", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: You are planning to carpet a room 14'6\" by 11'3\". The price is $11.95 per sq. yd. Assuming that available widths are 15' and 12'. which is more economical? What is the cost?\n\nOptions: \nA. 15' width is more economical, $199.99\nB. 12' width is more economical, $275.95\nC. 12' width is more economical, $250.00\nD. 12' width is more economical, $199.99\nE. 15' width is more economical, $300.00\nF. 15' width is more economical, $250.00\nG. 15' width is more economical, $275.95\nH. 12' width is more economical, $224.06\nI. 15' width is more economical, $224.06\nJ. 12' width is more economical, $300.00\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1172, "output_tokens": 821, "total_tokens": 1993}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_68", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose the demand curve for oPads is given by $p=\\frac{{500-x}}{{10}}, What is the elasticity value of this demand function.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.0\nB. -0.75\nC. -2.5\nD. -3.0\nE. 2.5\nF. -2.0\nG. 1.0\nH. 1.5\nI. -1.5\nJ. -0.5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 684, "output_tokens": 14420, "total_tokens": 15104}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_503", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose a stock has the following information. It is listed on the London stock exchange and operates throughout Europe. The yield on a UK 10 year treasury is 2.8%. The stock in question will earn 8.6% as per historical data. The Beta for the stock is 1.4, i.e., it is 140% volatile to the changes in the general stock market. What is the expected rate of return?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5.6\nB. 2.8\nC. 1.4\nD. 10.92\nE. 7.98\nF. 6.2\nG. 9.4\nH. 8.6\nI. 11.76\nJ. 12.34\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 951, "output_tokens": 537, "total_tokens": 1488}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_149", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Distribution of overhead is based on floor space. Department Aoccupied 8,100 sq. ft. of the 121,500 sq. ft. of space used byHar-rison Manufacturing Company. Find department A's shareof overhead based on floor footage for a month in whichthe total overhead of the Harrison Manufacturing Company was $97,500.\n\nOptions: \nA. $6,500\nB. $7,250\nC. $9,750\nD. $5,000\nE. $97,500\nF. $4,100\nG. $121,500\nH. $12,150\nI. $10,000\nJ. $8,100\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 960, "output_tokens": 326, "total_tokens": 1286}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_43", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Dermanand Klein are the sole stockholders of the Leather Products Corporation. It is estimated that Leather Products will have a taxable income of $30,000 this year. The stock is evenly divided between Mr.Dermanand Mr. Klein, so that resulting dividends will also be equally shared. Both Mr. Dermanand Mr. Klein expect to receive from other sources a net taxable income of $12,000. All profit after taxes Leather Products makes this year will be paid out as dividends. Mr.Dermanwants to introduce a new product. Should this venture succeed, the annual income before taxes will increase by $10,000. What will be the increase in stockholders' income after taxes? Use the tables \"Federal Taxes Rates on 1949 Net Incomes of Corporations in the United States\", and \"Federal Tax Rates on 1949 Incomes of Individuals in the United States.\"\n\nOptions: \nA. $1,129.88\nB. $850\nC. $1,050\nD. $2,250\nE. $2,400\nF. $1,500\nG. $2,000\nH. $900\nI. $3,000\nJ. $1,200\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "First, the corporation\u2019s additional $10,000 in pre-tax income is taxed at the 1949 corporate tax rate. For $40,000 total corporate income (from $30,000 + $10,000), the tax is $9,000 + 38% on income over $40,000 \u2014 but since it's exactly $40,000, the tax is $9,000 (using the 1949 corporate tax schedule: 38% on income over $25,000 up to $40,000, plus base tax). The original tax on $30,000 is $6,750, so the additional corporate tax is $2,250, leaving $7,750 in after-tax profit to be split as dividends.\n\nEach shareholder receives $3,875 in additional dividend income, taxed at individual rates. With their other income at $12,000, adding $3,875 brings them to $15,875. Using the 1949 individual tax rates, the additional tax on $3,875 at a marginal rate of ~22% is about $852.50 per shareholder, or $1,705 total. Thus, the total increase in stockholders\u2019 after-tax income is $7,750 - $1,705 = $6,045 total, but per the options, the increase **per shareholder** after tax is approximately $3,875 - $852.50 = $3,022.50, but the **combined** increase is about $6,045, which doesn't match.\n\nWait: the question asks for the **increase in stockholders' income after taxes**, meaning combined after-tax dividend income. The $10,000 pre-tax corporate income leads to $10,000 \u00d7 (1 - marginal corporate tax rate). At $30,000 base, corporate tax is $6,750 (22.5% effective); at $40,000, tax is $9,000 (22.5% on first $25k, then 38% on next $15k: $6,750 + 0.38\u00d7$15,000 = $6,750 + $5,700 = $12,450 \u2014 correction: this is wrong.\n\nCorrect 1949 corporate tax: For $30,000 income: $25,000 taxed at progressive rates up to 38%, but the table shows: 38% on income over $25,000 up to $40,000. Base tax on first $25,000 is $6,750. So on $30,000: $6,750 + 0.38\u00d7$5,000 = $6,750 + $1,900 = $8,650. On $40,000: $6,750 + 0.38\u00d7$15,000 = $6,750 + $5,700 = $12,450. So increase in corporate tax: $12,450 - $8,650 = $3,800. After-tax income increase: $10,000 - $3,800 = $6,200. This is paid as dividends: $3,100 each.\n\nEach shareholder now has $12,000 + $3,100 = $15,100. In 1949, individual tax on $12,000 is about $1,600 (est), on $15,100 is about $2,400 (est), so additional tax ~$800 each, or $1,600 total. So net increase in stockholders\u2019 after-tax income: $6,200 - $1,600 = $4,600 \u2014 not in options.\n\nWait \u2014 perhaps the corporate tax on $30k is lower. Rechecking standard 1949 rates: The normal tax plus surtax for corporations: 38% on income over $25,000. First $25,000 taxed at lower rates. Total tax on $30,000: $6,750 + 0.38\u00d7$5,000 = $6,750 + $1,900 = $8,650. On $40,000: $6,750 + 0.38\u00d7$15,000 = $6,750 + $5,700 = $12,450. Delta: $3,800 tax, so $6,200 after-tax dividends.\n\nNow dividends taxed at individual level. Each gets $3,100. Each had $12,000 income. In 1949, individual tax rate: for single filers, $12,000 to $15,100, marginal rate ~24%. But dividends are taxed as ordinary income. The additional $3,100 taxed at ~27.5% avg? But let's use the tables.\n\nStandard 1949 individual rates: First $2,000 at 2%, then increasing to 24% at $16,000. So $12,000 income: tax approx $1,800. $15,100: approx $2,400. So additional tax per shareholder: $600. Total additional tax: $1,200. So net increase in after-tax income: $6,200 - $1,200 = $5,000 \u2014 still not in options.\n\nWait \u2014 perhaps the original corporate tax is lower. Some sources show 1949 corporate tax: 38% on income over $25,000, but with a base tax of $6,750 on first $25,000. So same as above.\n\nAlternative approach: perhaps the $30,000 corporate income is taxed at a lower rate. For $30,000: tax = $6,750 + 0.38\u00d75,000 = $8,650. After-tax = $21,350. Dividends = $10,675 each.\n\nWith new $40,000: tax = $12,450, after-tax = $27,550, dividends = $13,775 each. Increase per shareholder: $13,775 - $10,675 = $3,100.\n\nNow individual tax: at $12,000 + $3,100 = $15,100. In 1949, tax on $12,000: let's say $1,800 (est), on $15,100: $2,400 (est), so additional tax $600 per shareholder. So net increase per shareholder: $3,100 - $600 = $2,500. Total for both: $5,000 \u2014 not in options.\n\nBut options are small: $1,050, $2,250, etc. Perhaps the increase in after-tax income **per shareholder** is asked? But question says \"stockholders' income\" \u2014 plural.\n\nWait \u2014 perhaps the corporate tax on the incremental $10,000 is 38%, so $3,800 tax, $6,200 after-tax, $3,100 each in dividends.\n\nEach shareholder's dividend income is $3,100. This is added to their $12,000, so $15,100 total income.\n\nIn 1949, the tax on $15,100 for an individual: using the rate schedule, the tax is approximately $2,250 (est). On $12,000: approximately $1,350. So additional tax: $900 per shareholder. So after-tax dividend income increase: $3,100 - $900 = $2,200 per shareholder. Total for both: $4,400 \u2014 still not matching.\n\nBut option D is $2,250 \u2014 close.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the corporate tax on $30,000 is lower. Some sources show the 1949 corporate tax as 38% flat on income over $25,000, but with lower brackets. But the base tax on $25,000 is $6,750, so same.\n\nPerhaps the additional $10,000 is taxed at 38%, so $3,800 corporate tax, $6,200 after-tax, paid as dividends.\n\nDividends are taxed at individual level. The additional $3,100 to each shareholder.\n\nIn 1949, individual tax rates: for income around $15,000, the marginal rate is 26% or so. But the average rate increase might be less.\n\nPerhaps the answer is the after-tax dividend increase per shareholder: $3,100 \u00d7 (1 - individual tax rate). But individual tax rate on additional income: at $12,000 base, marginal rate might be 22-24%.\n\nAssume 22%: $3,100 \u00d7 0.22 = $682 tax, so $2,418 after-tax. Total for two: $4,836 \u2014 not in options.\n\nWait \u2014 perhaps the question is asking for the increase in after-tax income from the venture, but only the net to shareholders.\n\nAnother approach: perhaps the corporate tax on $30,000 is $9,000 (30%), and on $40,000 is $12,000 (30%), so $3,000 corporate tax on $10,000, $7,000 after-tax, $3,500 each.\n\nEach shareholder has $12,000 + $3,500 = $15,500. Individual tax on $12,000: say $1,800, on $15,500: $2,500, so additional tax $700 each, $1,400 total. Net increase: $7,000 - $1,400 = $5,600 \u2014 no.\n\nPerhaps the corporate tax is 22.5% on $30,000: $6,750. On $40,000: at 38% on over $25,000: $6,750 + 0.38*15,000 = $6,750 + $5,700 = $12,450. So additional tax $12,450 - $6,750 = $5,700 on $10,000? No, on $30,000 tax is $6,750 + 0.38*5,000 = $6,750 + $1,900 = $8,650. So additional tax $12,450 - $8,650 = $3,800. After-tax increase $6,200.\n\nNow, dividends: $6,200, taxed at individual level. In 1949, dividends a