success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1040, "output_tokens": 454, "total_tokens": 1494}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_100", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A loan is made on December 17 for a time period of 120 days. When is it due (not a leap year)?\n\nOptions: \nA. April 15\nB. April 13\nC. April 18\nD. May 15\nE. April 16\nF. April 12\nG. April 17\nH. May 1\nI. March 17\nJ. April 14\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The loan starts on December 17 and lasts 120 days.  \nDecember has 31 days, so there are 14 days left in December after the 17th (31 - 17 = 14).  \nCounting forward: 14 days in December + 31 in January + 28 in February + 31 in March = 104 days, leaving 16 more days into April, making the due date April 16.  \n\n\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 713, "output_tokens": 476, "total_tokens": 1189}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_42", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How much will it cost to cover a floor 13'6\" \u00d7 18'8\" with asphalt tile if the price is 9 (3/4) \\textcent per 9\" tile?\n\nOptions: \nA. $42.50\nB. $49.99\nC. $46.25\nD. $40.75\nE. $47.50\nF. $48.95\nG. $43.88\nH. $51.20\nI. $45.00\nJ. $44.00\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 738, "output_tokens": 602, "total_tokens": 1340}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_510", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The premium rate on homeowners insurance for the ABC Insurance Company is $.96 per $100. In addition, ABC allows a discount of 20% of the premium if the homeowner accepts a policy containing a $250 deductible clause. Calculate the premium for a homeowners policy for $27,000 containing a $250 deductible clause.\n\nOptions: \nA. $51.84\nB. $220\nC. $184.80\nD. $259.20\nE. $145.20\nF. $207\nG. $246.40\nH. $102\nI. $123.84\nJ. $165.60\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 877, "output_tokens": 401, "total_tokens": 1278}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_40", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Determine the number of men needed to build a boat in 77 days if it takes 36 men 132 days to build one.\n\nOptions: \nA. 84 men\nB. 36 men\nC. 99 men\nD. 132 men\nE. 45 men\nF. 70 men\nG. 62 men\nH. 50 men\nI. 77 men\nJ. 120 men\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 639, "output_tokens": 389, "total_tokens": 1028}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_141", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Assume the Black-Scholes framework. For $t \\ge 0$, let $S(t)$ be the time-$t$ price of a nondividend-paying stock. You are given:\n(i) $S(0)=0.5\n(ii) The stock price process is $\\frac{{dS(t)}}{{S(t)}} = 0.05dt+0.2dZ(t)$ where $Z(t)$ is a standart Brownian motion.\n(iii) $E[S(1)^\\alpha]=1.4$, where $\\alpha$ is a negative constant.\n(iv) The continuously compounded risk-free interest rate is $3%$.\nConsider a contingent claim that pays $S(1)^\\alpha$ at time 1. What is the time-0 price of the contigent claim?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.450\nB. 1.475\nC. 1.415\nD. 1.250\nE. 1.360\nF. 1.390\nG. 1.325\nH. 1.500\nI. 1.287\nJ. 1.372\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1114, "output_tokens": 675, "total_tokens": 1789}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_198", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Aisha graduates college and starts a job. She saves $1000 each quarter, depositing it into a retirement savings account. Suppose that Aisha saves for 30 years and then retires. At retirement she wants to withdraw money as an annuity that pays a constant amount every month for 25 years. During the savings phase, the retirement account earns 6% interest compounded quarterly. During the annuity payout phase, the retirement account earns 4.8% interest compounded monthly. Calculate Aisha\u2019s monthly retirement annuity payout.\n\nOptions: \nA. 2350.60\nB. 1625.33\nC. 1500.50\nD. 1422.75\nE. 1898.27\nF. 1755.45\nG. 2100.35\nH. 2200.00\nI. 1995.10\nJ. 1288.88\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1107, "output_tokens": 771, "total_tokens": 1878}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_761", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: On January 17, the shirt buyer for Wellington's Department Store decided to determine his open-to-buy. The following figures were available: Present inventory at retail (Jan 17) Inventory commitments (Jan 17) Planned end-of-month inventory (Jan 31) Planned sales Actual sales Planned markdowns Actual markdowns $12,000 3,000 15,000 6,000 3,000 500 200 What is the buyer's open-to-buy?\n\nOptions: \nA. $18,300\nB. $12,200\nC. $5,000\nD. $10,800\nE. $3,300\nF. $2,800\nG. $15,000\nH. $6,000\nI. $7,700\nJ. $9,500\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The open-to-buy is calculated as: planned ending inventory plus planned sales minus present inventory minus commitments, with adjustments for markdowns.  \nHere, $15,000 (planned end inventory) + $6,000 (planned sales) \u2212 $12,000 (present inventory) \u2212 $3,000 (commitments) \u2212 ($500 planned markdowns \u2212 $200 actual markdowns) = $5,700? Actually, correct formula: ($15,000 + $6,000) \u2013 ($12,000 + $3,000 + $500 \u2212 $200) = $21,000 \u2013 $15,300 = $5,700, but that is not an option; checking net markdowns: planned $500 vs actual $200 means $300 less markdown taken, so add $300? The standard open-to-buy = (planned EOM + planned sales) \u2013 (present inventory + commitments + planned markdowns \u2013 actual markdowns taken) = (15,000 + 6,000) \u2013 (12,000 + 3,000 + 500 \u2013 200) = 21,000 \u2013 15,300 = $5,700, which matches closest to $5,000? No, $5,700 not listed, but re-evaluating: actual markdowns taken reduce the needed markdown provision, so open-to-buy = 21,000 \u2013 (12,000 + 3,000 + 500) + 200 = 21,000 \u2013 15,500 + 200 = $5,700. Since not an option, likely the intended calculation uses planned markdowns only: 21,000 \u2013 15,500 = $5,500 (not listed). Alternatively, some formulas omit markdowns: 21,000 \u2013 15,000 = $6,000, which is option H.  \n\n\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1336, "output_tokens": 3581, "total_tokens": 4917}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_569", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mr. Green, who is 35 years old, has just purchased a new car. The car is classified as symbol 5, and is kept in 06 territory. He has had one accident in the last three years. If he uses the new car for business, what is the difference in cost between $50-deductible and $100-deductible collision insurance?\n\nOptions: \nA. $65\nB. $60\nC. $50\nD. $45\nE. $25\nF. $40\nG. $55\nH. $35\nI. $30\nJ. $70\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 796, "output_tokens": 362, "total_tokens": 1158}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_577", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: InBrowningtown, water is sold to home owners by the cubic foot at the rate of $15.31 for up to and including 3,600 cubic feet, and $.15 for each 100 cubic feet over 3,600 cubic feet. Local taxes on water usage are 4%. If the Thomas family recently received a bill for 35,700 cubic feet of water, how much were they charged?\n\nOptions: \nA. $64\nB. $58\nC. $70\nD. $80\nE. $66\nF. $60\nG. $78\nH. $74\nI. $72\nJ. $68\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 892, "output_tokens": 577, "total_tokens": 1469}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_400", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: 00 p.m., traveled 540 miles and arrived at its destination at 2:30 p.m. Find the average speed of the plane in miles per hour.\n\nOptions: \nA. 360 mph\nB. 450 mph\nC. 330 mph\nD. 240 mph\nE. 180 mph\nF. 420 mph\nG. 270 mph\nH. 300 mph\nI. 600 mph\nJ. 540 mph\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The plane traveled from 10:00 a.m. to 2:30 p.m., which is 4.5 hours. The distance was 540 miles, so average speed is 540 \u00f7 4.5 = 120 mph, but that is not an option. Rechecking: 540 miles in 4.5 hours gives exactly 120 mph, so none of the given options match, indicating an error in the options. However, if forced to choose the closest typical answer, 180 mph is the smallest option, though still incorrect. \n\n\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 848, "output_tokens": 16849, "total_tokens": 17697}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_506", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose a European call option on a barrel of crude oil with a strike price of $50 and a maturity of one-month, trades for $5. What is the price of the put premium with identical strike price and time until expiration, if the one-month risk-free rate is 2% and the spot price of the underlying asset is $52?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.92\nB. 3.20\nC. 4.80\nD. 1.50\nE. 4.50\nF. 5.00\nG. 1.00\nH. 3.50\nI. 3.75\nJ. 2.00\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 792, "output_tokens": 540, "total_tokens": 1332}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_247", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose we are given the following information. Use this information to calculate abnormal return. Rf: 4%\nRm: 12%\nBeta of the Portfolio: 1.8\nBeginning Value of Portfolio: $50,000\nEnding Value of Portfolio: $60,000\nWhat is the abnormal return?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.025\nB. 0.035\nC. 0.016\nD. 0.012\nE. 0.030\nF. 0.040\nG. 0.008\nH. 0.010\nI. 0.020\nJ. 0.050\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 908, "output_tokens": 534, "total_tokens": 1442}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_17", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: George is seen to place an even-money $100,000 bet on the Bulls to win the NBA Finals. If George has a logarithmic utility-of-wealth function and if his current wealth is $1,000,000, what must he believe is the minimum probability that the Bulls will win?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.525\nB. 0.800\nC. 0.450\nD. 0.575\nE. 0.750\nF. 0.350\nG. 0.650\nH. 0.300\nI. 0.700\nJ. 0.400\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 782, "output_tokens": 576, "total_tokens": 1358}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_625", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the cost of renting a compact car for 2 days and 4 hours, and driving it 364 miles? CAR RENTAL SCHEDULE Local and One-Way Car Rate per Day Rate per Week Rate for Extra Hours Compact $12.00 per day $.14 per mile gas included $60.00 per week $.14 per mile gas included $2.75 per hour over 24 $.14 per mile gas included Standard $16.00 per day $.16 per mile gas included $80.00 per day $.16 per mile gas included $2.75 per hour over 24 $.16 per mile gas included Luxury $20.00 per day $.18 per mile gas included $100.00 per day $.18 per mile gas included $2.75 per hour over 24 $.18 per mile gas included MINIMUM CHARGE: 24-hour rate INSURANCE: (per day or any part thereof): Collision, $1.20; Liability, $1.20\n\nOptions: \nA. $102.30\nB. $78.20\nC. $84.96\nD. $110.48\nE. $69.04\nF. $86.40\nG. $125.72\nH. $99.88\nI. $57.88\nJ. $93.16\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1467, "output_tokens": 637, "total_tokens": 2104}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_438", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An investor has utility function $U(x) = x^{{1/4}}$ for salary. He has a new job offer which pays $80,000 with a bonus. The bonus will be $0, $10000, $20000, $30000, $40000, $50000, or $60000, each with equal probability. What is the certainty equivalent value of this job offer?\n\nOptions: \nA. 100000\nB. 108610\nC. 110000\nD. 105000\nE. 90000\nF. 130000\nG. 120000\nH. 85000\nI. 95000\nJ. 115000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 982, "output_tokens": 485, "total_tokens": 1467}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_620", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For a one-period binomial model for the price of a stock, you are given: (i) The period is one year. (ii) The stock pays no dividends. (iii) u =1.433, where u is one plus the rate of capital gain on the stock if the price goes up.  (iv) d = 0.756 , where d is one plus the rate of capital loss on the stock if the price goes down. (v) The continuously compounded annual expected return on the stock is 10%. What is the true probability of the stock price going up.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.58\nB. 0.75\nC. 0.55\nD. 0.30\nE. 0.40\nF. 0.60\nG. 0.65\nH. 0.70\nI. 0.52\nJ. 0.45\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1036, "output_tokens": 576, "total_tokens": 1612}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_216", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Two power line construction routes are being considered. Route A is 15 miles long and goes around a lake. Each mile will cost $6,000 to build and $2,000 a year to maintain. At the end of fifteen years, each mile will have a salvage value of $3,000. Route B is an underwater line that cuts 5 miles across the lake. Construction costs will be $31,000 per mile and annual maintenance costs, $400 per mile. The salvage value at the end of fifteen years will be $6,000 per mile. Assuming interest is 8% and taxes are 3% of the construction costs of each power line, compare the annual costs of Route A and Route B for the first year.\n\nOptions: \nA. $41,558 for Route A and $23,654 for Route B\nB. $45,000 for Route A and $30,000 for Route B\nC. $100,000 for Route A and $50,000 for Route B\nD. $40,000 for Route A and $20,000 for Route B\nE. $80,000 for Route A and $40,000 for Route B\nF. $35,000 for Route A and $25,000 for Route B\nG. $70,000 for Route A and $35,000 for Route B\nH. $60,000 for Route A and $155,000 for Route B\nI. $90,000 for Route A and $155,000 for Route B\nJ. $120,000 for Route A and $75,000 for Route B\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1900, "output_tokens": 1422, "total_tokens": 3322}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_441", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Assume that the Black-Scholes framework holds. The price of a nondividened-paying stock is $30. The price of a put option on this stock is $4.00. You are given $(i) $\\Delta=-0.28$. (ii) $\\Gamma=0.10$ Using the delta-gamma approximation, determine the price of the put option if the stock price changes to $31.50.\n\nOptions: \nA. 5.5\nB. 2.9\nC. 4.8\nD. 3.0\nE. 3.7\nF. 4.5\nG. 5.0\nH. 2.5\nI. 4.2\nJ. 3.9\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 810, "output_tokens": 592, "total_tokens": 1402}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_413", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Loretta Gould has been offered a position as salesperson for the Houston Oil Company. Her manager estimates that her sales will amount to approximately $80,000 the first year. She may accept one of two pay schedules: (1) a salary of $8,000 plus commission of 1% of sales or (2) a salary of $5,800 plus a commission of 5% of sales over $30,000. Which pay schedule is better? By how much is it better?\n\nOptions: \nA. Both schedules are the same\nB. Schedule (1) is better by $300\nC. Both schedules are better by different amounts depending on sales\nD. Schedule (1) is better by $1,200\nE. Schedule (2) is better by $1,200\nF. Schedule (2) is better by $700\nG. Schedule (1) is better by $700\nH. Schedule (1) is better by $500\nI. Schedule (2) is better by $500\nJ. Schedule (2) is better by $300\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1220, "output_tokens": 505, "total_tokens": 1725}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_635", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many 9-inch-by-9-inch tiles are needed to cover a floor which is 9 feet long and 6 feet wide? Find the cost if each tile costs 75 cents.\n\nOptions: \nA. 98 tiles, $73.50\nB. 90 tiles, $67.50\nC. 104 tiles, $78.00\nD. 88 tiles, $66.00\nE. 96 tiles, $72.00\nF. 92 tiles, $69.00\nG. 100 tiles, $75.00\nH. 110 tiles, $82.50\nI. 102 tiles, $76.50\nJ. 94 tiles, $70.50\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1000, "output_tokens": 588, "total_tokens": 1588}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_140", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose there is a 50-50 chance that an individual with logarithmic utility from wealth and with a current wealth of $20,000 will suffer a loss of $10,000 from a car accident. Insurance is competitively provided at actuarially fair rates. Compute the utility if the individual buys full insurance.\n\nOptions: \nA. 8.954\nB. 9.616\nC. 9.000\nD. 9.300\nE. 9.850\nF. 10.000\nG. 8.500\nH. 8.000\nI. 9.700\nJ. 9.210\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 814, "output_tokens": 518, "total_tokens": 1332}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_573", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: JamesTaggertwishes to paint the walls of his storage room. The room's dimensions are 14' by 10' by 8(1/2)' . One quart of paint costing $9.80 will cover 36 sq. ft. Labor costs is $5 per quart or fractionthere of. Find his cost for painting the room.\n\nOptions: \nA. $210.70\nB. $143.20\nC. $158.40\nD. $177.60\nE. $220.50\nF. $185.90\nG. $192.80\nH. $199.50\nI. $165.30\nJ. $205.00\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 900, "output_tokens": 581, "total_tokens": 1481}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_91", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: On September 1, Mr. Blake received a statement for his checking account. The closing balance on the statement was $1,810.50. Mr. Blake's checkbook shows a balance of $1,685.75. In comparing his check stubs to the statement, he notices that checks for amounts of $60.80, $40.30, and $25.00 did not appear on the statement. Also, the statement lists a service charge of $1.35 which does not appear on his checkbook stubs. Prepare a reconciliation statement for. Mr. Blake.\n\nOptions: \nA. $1,748.60\nB. $1810.50\nC. $1,773.00\nD. $126.10\nE. $1,729.55\nF. $1,823.85\nG. $1684.40\nH. $1,710.05\nI. $1685.75\nJ. $1,654.40\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1256, "output_tokens": 795, "total_tokens": 2051}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_516", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: ABC Plumbing has the following current assets and liabilities: Cash, $7,300; Marketable Securities, $14,200, Accounts Receivable, $2,120; Notes Payable, $1,400; Accounts Payable, $1,850. Find the acid-test ratio for ABC, correct to the nearest hundredth.\n\nOptions: \nA. 8.27\nB. 7.77\nC. 7.17\nD. 6.27\nE. 6.77\nF. 5.27\nG. 7.27\nH. 8.77\nI. 4.27\nJ. 9.27\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 