estions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: You can buy a sewing machine selling for $275 net price, or one listed at $320 less a 12(1/2) % discount. Which is the best buy and how much will you save by buying it instead of the other one?\n\nOptions: \nA. $275 machine\nB. $320 machine\nC. $320 machine with a 20% discount\nD. Both are the same price\nE. $300 machine with a 10% discount\nF. $320 machine with a 5% discount\nG. $250 machine with a 15% discount\nH. $280 machine\nI. $310 machine with no discount\nJ. $350 machine with a 15% discount\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 956, "output_tokens": 345, "total_tokens": 1301}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_453", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Express (2 / 5) and [1 / (100)] as a percentage.\n\nOptions: \nA. 40%, 0.25%\nB. 40%, 1%\nC. 35%, 0.75%\nD. 50%, 1%\nE. 40%, 0.5%\nF. 20%, 0.5%\nG. 20%, 0.25%\nH. 50%, 0.5%\nI. 30%, 0.25%\nJ. 20%, 1%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 710, "output_tokens": 368, "total_tokens": 1078}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_232", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nelson's Cycle Shop had a January 1 inventory of $30,156. During the month, new merchandise purchases totaled $28,300, and sales totaled $72,600. If the margin on sales was 45%, estimate the final inventory.\n\nOptions: \nA. $28,300\nB. $45,600\nC. $32,670\nD. $22,150\nE. $20,000\nF. $41,200\nG. $18,526\nH. $39,930\nI. $34,850\nJ. $25,400\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 908, "output_tokens": 550, "total_tokens": 1458}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_720", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the property tax on a house with an assessedvalue of$3,250 if the tax rate charged is 2.351%.\n\nOptions: \nA. $64.12\nB. $83.69\nC. $76.41\nD. $68.24\nE. $74.58\nF. $80.35\nG. $81.23\nH. $78.94\nI. $72.51\nJ. $69.75\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 638, "output_tokens": 206, "total_tokens": 844}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_580", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Owens Company accepted a draft, 90-day sight, amounting to $560 drawn on them by Watts Bros. Watts Bros, had the draft discounted 34 days before the due date at 6%. What were the proceeds?\n\nOptions: \nA. $560\nB. $550.00\nC. $555.00\nD. $558.50\nE. $562.00\nF. $558.00\nG. $563.17\nH. $556.83\nI. $553.83\nJ. $551.67\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 794, "output_tokens": 337, "total_tokens": 1131}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_444", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mr. Griffin, age 22 and single, uses his car strictly for pleasure. His insurance coverage includes 25-and-50 bodily injury liability and $10,000 property damage insurance. If Mr. Griffin lives in 04 territory and has had no accidents, what is the cost of his coverage?\n\nOptions: \nA. $167.45\nB. $99.99\nC. $183.30\nD. $37\nE. $210.75\nF. $125.50\nG. $58.60\nH. $78\nI. $41\nJ. $150.20\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 880, "output_tokens": 385, "total_tokens": 1265}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_483", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mr. Simmons has the choice of buying a 6(1/4), $1,000 bond at 98, or 10 shares of 6% preferred stock, par valued at $100 per share, at 101. Which investment gives the greater effective yield? By how much? Perform all calculations to the nearest (1/10)%.\n\nOptions: \nA. The preferred stock\nB. The bond\nC. Both yield the same\nD. The preferred stock, by 0.7%\nE. The preferred stock, by 1.2%\nF. The bond, by 0.5%\nG. The bond, by 2.0%\nH. Cannot be determined from the information given\nI. The preferred stock, by 0.3%\nJ. The bond, by 1.5%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 980, "output_tokens": 647, "total_tokens": 1627}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_312", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: TheMotorollaElectronics Company is taking inventory. It discovers that it has 30 widgets on hand. Records reveal the following information: Quantity Cost Per Unit Inventory, Dec. 2 6 $2.30 Purchase, Jan. 15 352 $2.50 Purchase, Feb. 4 101 $2.20 Purchase, Feb. 14 645 $2.00 Find the value of widgets in their inventory using the FIFO method of inventory.\n\nOptions: \nA. $120\nB. $45\nC. $55\nD. $30\nE. $85\nF. $60.00\nG. $110\nH. $75\nI. $90\nJ. $100\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 905, "output_tokens": 284, "total_tokens": 1189}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_296", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose that there are two firms in the market facing no costs of production and a demand curve given by Q = 150 - P for their identical products. Suppose the two firms choose prices simultaneously as in the Bertrand model. Compute the prices in the nash equilibrium.\n\nOptions: \nA. 30\nB. 50\nC. 0\nD. 25\nE. 150\nF. 75\nG. 90\nH. 120\nI. 100\nJ. 60\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 715, "output_tokens": 267, "total_tokens": 982}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_244", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which writer was concerned with the reaction of workers to key characteristics of bureaucracies?\n\nOptions: \nA. Marx\nB. Lewin\nC. Mayo\nD. Maslow\nE. Freud\nF. Weber\nG. Durkheim\nH. Gouldner\nI. Merton\nJ. Taylor\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 516, "output_tokens": 321, "total_tokens": 837}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_238", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  _____________is an important element in the communication process. It recognizes that successful communications are more likely to be achieved if the source and the receiver understand each other.\n\nOptions: \nA. The encoding-decoding process.\nB. Personal selling.\nC. The realm of understanding.\nD. The context of the message.\nE. Noise.\nF. The communication channel.\nG. Feedback.\nH. The use of jargon.\nI. The sender-receiver model.\nJ. The use of technology.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 687, "output_tokens": 250, "total_tokens": 937}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_613", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is typically not a result of recognizing the importance of ethnic groups by marketers?\n\nOptions: \nA. Variations in product offerings to suit the wants of a particular group.\nB. Use of an undifferentiated one-size-fits-all marketing strategy.\nC. Promoting only mainstream products without considering ethnic preferences.\nD. Adaptation of the advertising, particularly the use of foreign languages, to the target ethnic market.\nE. Not considering the influence of ethnic backgrounds on purchasing decisions.\nF. Assuming all ethnic groups have the same consumer behavior.\nG. Ignoring the ethnic diversity in the target market.\nH. Study of ethnic buying habits to isolate market segments.\nI. Neglecting to conduct market research on ethnic groups.\nJ. Disregard of cultural sensitivities in advertising campaigns.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 900, "output_tokens": 325, "total_tokens": 1225}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_682", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  If an advertisement shows the interior of a train with comfortable seats and plenty of space yet a customer boards a train only to find a lack of space and hard seating. This is an example of:\n\nOptions: \nA. GAP 9-the gap between service delivery and customer satisfaction.\nB. GAP 2-the gap between management perception and service-quality specification\nC. GAP 4-the gap between service delivery and external communications.\nD. GAP 5-the gap between customer perception and customer expectation.\nE. GAP 7-the gap between service quality and customer perception.\nF. GAP 3-the gap between service-quality specifications and service delivery.\nG. GAP 10-the gap between service quality and service delivery.\nH. GAP1-the gap between the customer's expectations and management perception.\nI. GAP 6-the gap between customer expectation and management perception.\nJ. GAP 8-the gap between external communications and customer expectation.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1061, "output_tokens": 238, "total_tokens": 1299}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_554", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  The train operator understands customer desire for a comfortable seat but fails to specify how many should be provided relative to the anticipated number of travellers on each route. This is an example of:\n\nOptions: \nA. GAP 5-the gap between perceived service and expected service.\nB. GAP1-the gap between the customer's expectations and management perception.\nC. GAP 10-the gap between management perception and customer satisfaction.\nD. GAP 7-the gap between customer expectations and perceived service.\nE. GAP 8-the gap between service delivery and customer satisfaction.\nF. GAP 4-the gap between service delivery and external communications.\nG. GAP 6-the gap between service design and service standards.\nH. GAP 9-the gap between customer perception and service expectation.\nI. GAP 2-the gap between management perception and service-quality specification.\nJ. GAP 3-the gap between service-quality specifications and service delivery.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1054, "output_tokens": 273, "total_tokens": 1327}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_199", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider an arbitrage-free securities market model, in which the risk-free interest rate is constant. There are two nondividend-paying stocks whose price processes are:\n$S_1(t)=S_1(0)e^{{0.1t+0.2Z(t)}}$\n$S_2(t)=S_2(0)e^{{0.125t+0.3Z(t)}}$\nwhere $Z(t)$ is a standard Brownian motion ant $t\\ge0$. What is the continuously compounded risk-free interest rate?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.08\nB. 0.025\nC. 0.02\nD. 0.09\nE. 0.01\nF. 0.03\nG. 0.06\nH. 0.05\nI. 0.07\nJ. 0.04\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1044, "output_tokens": 1092, "total_tokens": 2136}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_293", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is not an assumption underpinning the rational decision making model?\n\nOptions: \nA. Decisions are made in a vacuum, without influence from outside factors\nB. Decisions are always optimal and maximize utility\nC. The decision maker's preferences are stable and consistent\nD. High level of certainty regarding the environment\nE. Unlimited time for making a decision\nF. A structured problem\nG. Perfect knowledge of all possible options and their outcomes\nH. Incomplete information\nI. An agreed goal\nJ. Rationality of the decision maker\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 743, "output_tokens": 320, "total_tokens": 1063}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_609", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Robert is a marketer for a global consumer products company. He is working on the promotional campaign designed to reach a target audience in a new international market. Robert is working hard to make sure that the promotional campaign is clearly understood by the nation's consumers and doesn't offend anyone. By which of the factors in the external environment is he being influenced\n\nOptions: \nA. Economic environment.\nB. Socio-cultural environment.\nC. Geographic environment.\nD. Political environment.\nE. Competitive environment.\nF. Legal environment.\nG. Technological environment.\nH. Natural environment.\nI. International environment.\nJ. Demographic environment.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 756, "output_tokens": 213, "total_tokens": 969}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_289", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The focus on issues, the intended audience extending beyond shareholders and the voluntary nature of ___________ distinguish it from _________.\n\nOptions: \nA. Social accounting, Environmental management initiatives.\nB. Financial accounting, Environmental management initiatives\nC. Social accounting, Annual report publication.\nD. Annual report publication, Social accounting\nE. Environmental management initiatives, Social accounting.\nF. Environmental management initiatives, Financial accounting.\nG. Annual report publication, Financial accounting.\nH. Annual report publication, Environmental management initiatives.\nI. Social accounting, Financial accounting.\nJ. Financial accounting, Social accounting.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 794, "output_tokens": 336, "total_tokens": 1130}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_126", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The primary objective of team-based selling is to\n\nOptions: \nA. equitably manage the sales bonus pool\nB. increase the competitiveness within the sales team\nC. create multiple points of contact between the customer and the company\nD. distribute the work involved in managing an account\nE. reduce the workload of individual salespeople\nF. ensure that every team member gets to interact with the customer\nG. diversify the company's customer base\nH. match various functional areas of the company with customer needs\nI. simplify the process of sales negotiation\nJ. provide a single point of contact for the customer with the company\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 768, "output_tokens": 256, "total_tokens": 1024}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_560", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $P(r,t,T)$ denote the price at time $t$ of $1 to be paid with certainty at time $T, t\\leT$, if the short rate at time $t$ is equal to $r$. For a Vasicek model you are given: $P(0.04, 0, 2)=0.9445$, $P(0.05, 1, 3)=0.9321$, $P(r^*, 2, 4)=0.8960$. What is $r^*$?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.11\nB. 0.06\nC. 0.05\nD. 0.04\nE. 0.08\nF. 0.12\nG. 0.07\nH. 0.09\nI. 0.10\nJ. 0.03\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1084, "output_tokens": 592, "total_tokens": 1676}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_440", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider a strategy of the form $(\\gamma, 0, 0)$ for the investment wheel. Show that the overall factor multiplying your money after $n$ steps is likely to be $(1+2\\gamma)^{{n/2}}(1-\\gamma)^{{n/2}}$. Find the value of $\\gamma$ that maximizes this factor.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.80\nB. 0.25\nC. 0.10\nD. 0.33\nE. 0.50\nF. 0.66\nG. 1.00\nH. 0.20\nI. 0.40\nJ. 0.75\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 768, "output_tokens": 899, "total_tokens": 1667}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_125", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  These objectives are often the most suitable when firms operate in a market dominated by a major competitor and where their financial resources are limited.\n\nOptions: \nA. Hold objectives.\nB. Expansion objectives.\nC. Market objectives.\nD. Competitive objectives.\nE. Niche objectives\nF. Harvest objectives.\nG. Divest objectives.\nH. Growth objectives.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 570, "output_tokens": 304, "total_tokens": 874}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_340", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: JamesParcerdiscounted a customer's $500 note on April 25. The note was dated March 1. and must be paid within 3 months of the day issued. What is the term of discount?\n\nOptions: \nA. 65 days\nB. 37 days\nC. 55 days\nD. 25 days\nE. 60 days\nF. 30 days\nG. 45 days\nH. 92 days\nI. 75 days\nJ. 80 days\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 732, "output_tokens": 322, "total_tokens": 1054}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_583", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mr.Ozaku, age 20 recently took out a $5,000 ordinary life insurance policy. If he pays a semiannual premium until age 75, how much will hepayin premiums? If he dies, how much will his beneficiary receive?\n\nOptions: \nA. $7,000 and $5,000\nB. $6,750 and $5,250\nC. $4,500 and $4,000\nD. $5,500 and $5,000\nE. $5,000 and $4,801.50\nF. $4,500 and $5,500\nG. $6,000 and $6,500\nH. $5,500 and $4,500\nI. $4,801.50 and $5,000\nJ. $5,250 and $5,750\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1152, "output_tokens": 5340, "total_tokens": 6492}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_784", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Assuming that each lived for the term of the policy, compare the cost of a $5,000 20-payment life insurance policy for a young man 25 years of age with a man 45 years of age.\n\nOptions: \nA. $3649 and $2207\nB. $2207 and $5000\nC. $110.35 and $182.45\nD. $5000 and $5000\nE. $1500 and $2500\nF. $182.45 and $110.35\nG. $4250 and $6250\nH. $2207 and $3649\nI. $3649 and $3649\nJ. $2500 and $4500\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 963, "output_tokens": 382, "total_tokens": 1345}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_156", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the difference in annual premiums of a $10,000 20-payment life policy purchased at age 30, as opposed to the same policy purchased at age 20?\n\nOptions: \nA. $48.90\nB. $40.05\nC. $35.50\nD. $75.20\nE. $10.00\nF. $58.30\nG. $19.84\nH. $63.10\nI. $24.73\nJ. $12.65\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 737, "output_tokens": 309, "total_tokens": 1046}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_22", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During a riot, Mr. Winter's car was overturned causing $346.50 in damage.Mr. Winter had $50-deductible col-lision insurance, but no comprehensive coverage. How much will theinsurance company pay Mr. Winter?\n\nOptions: \nA. $296.50\nB. $50\nC. Two-thirds of the cost of the damages\nD. $150\nE. not pay him anything\nF. $200\nG. $346.50\nH. $246.50\nI. full coverage of damage\nJ. Half the cost of the damages\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 812, "output_tokens": 371, "total_tokens": 1183}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_39", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mr. Castle will buy one of two 10-HP motors offered to him. Motor A sells for $169 and has a full-load efficiency of 85.2%. Motor B costs $149 and has a full-load efficiency of 82.1%. The annual inspection and maintenance fee on both motors is 14.5% of the price. If electric energy costs 2.35 cents per kilowatt hour (1 HP = 0.746kw.) find the number of hours per year at which the cost of both motors will be the same.\n\nOptions: \nA. 450 hours\nB. 400 hours\nC. 600 hours\nD. 300 hours\nE. 325 (1 / 3) hours\nF. 275 (1 / 2) hours\nG. 350 hours\nH. 500 hours\nI. 425 hours\nJ. 374 (2 / 3) hours\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1091, "output_tokens": 349, "total_tokens": 1440}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_108", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It has been found that hours of recreation (r) and wages (W) have a direct effect on productivity (P), so that : P =ar+bW. In two surveys it was found that Survey 1P = 170 : r = 51 : W = 136 Survey 2P = 425 : r = 68 : W = 204 What are the values of a and b ?\n\nOptions: \nA. a = 68, b = 204\nB. a = 2, b = 1.25\nC. a = 0, b = 3\nD. a = 170, b = 425\nE. a = 5, b = 2\nF. a = 4, b = 1.5\nG. a = 3, b = 0.5\nH. a = -20, b = 8.75\nI. a = 51, b = 136\nJ. a = 10, b = 0.85\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1220, "output_tokens": 1111, "total_tokens": 2331}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_480", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Compare the costs of a $5,000 20-year endowment policy with a $5,000 20-year limited payment policy if each were to be purchased at age 45.\n\nOptions: \nA. $182.45\nB. $125.75\nC. $233.35\nD. $300.20\nE. $160.65\nF. $99.99\nG. $46.67\nH. $210.10\nI. $75.50\nJ. $50.90\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer depends on the specific premium rates from the insurer's table, which are not provided. Typically, a limited payment policy has higher annual premiums than an endowment because payments are compressed into a shorter period. Without rate data, I would select a moderate value; for example, \\boxed{A} is a plausible answer for a typical difference.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 932, "output_tokens": 555, "total_tokens": 1487}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_177", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Given that the cost of mimeographing x number of copies is C(x) = 0.005x + [(4500) / x], what is the number of copies that will minimize the cost?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2000 copies\nB. 500 copies\nC. 1200 copies\nD. 300 copies\nE. 700 copies\nF. 600 copies\nG. 1500 copies\nH. 949 copies\nI. 800 copies\nJ. 1000 copies\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 741, "output_tokens": 600, "total_tokens": 1341}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_668", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A television manufacturing firm lowered the price of its deluxe portable television set from $350 to $320 per unit, in order to increasetheir revenues and profits. This price change resulted in an increase in sales from 1,000 units per month to 1,080 units per month. Assuming the unit production costs did not change, was their decision to lower prices a good one?\n\nOptions: \nA. The decision was a poor one\nB. The decision had no effect\nC. The decision was a good one\nD. The decision increased profits\nE. The decision increased profits but not revenues\nF. The decision increased revenues but decreased profits\nG. The decision had no effect on revenues but increased profits\nH. The decision decreased both revenues and profits\nI. The decision had no effect on profits but increased revenues\nJ. The decision increased revenues but not profits\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The price drop from $350 to $320 reduced revenue per unit, and the quantity increase from 1,000 to 1,080 was not enough to offset that. Original total revenue was $350,000, while new revenue is $345,600, showing a decrease. Since costs per unit didn\u2019t change, lower revenue means lower profit, so the decision was poor.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1244, "output_tokens": 533, "total_tokens": 1777}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_20", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: (a) Given the two discount series of 30-10-2(1/2) % and 25-15-2%, which is better? (b) Given the discount series 15-15% and the single rate of 30%, which is better?\n\nOptions: \nA. The series 30-10-2(1/2)% and the single rate of 25% are better\nB. The single rate of 25% and the series 15-15% are better\nC. The series 30-10-2(1/2) % and the series 15-15% are better\nD. The series 25-15-2% and the single rate of 30% are better\nE. The series 30-10-2(1/2)% is better, but there is no difference between the series 15-15% and the single rate of 30%\nF. Both discount series are equally beneficial\nG. The series 25-15-2% is better, and the series 15-15% and the single rate of 30% are equally beneficial\nH. The series 25-15-2% and the series 15-15% are better\nI. The series 25-15-2% and the single rate of 25% are better\nJ. The series 30-10-2(1/2) % and the single rate of 30% are better\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1531, "output_tokens": 813, "total_tokens": 2344}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_46", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following would yield the greatest net return to acorporation in the 50% tax bracket A) 5% certificate of deposit B) 5% government bond C) 5% corporate bond D) 5%treasurybond E) 4% municipal bond\n\nOptions: \nA. 4.5% treasury bond with lower liquidity\nB. 3.5% municipal bond with additional state taxes\nC. 5% government bond\nD. 6% corporate bond with a high risk of default\nE. 6% certificate of deposit with a 2% penalty for early withdrawal\nF. 5% corporate bond\nG. 5.5% government bond with additional state taxes\nH. 5% certificate of deposit\nI. 3% corporate bond with tax-deductible expenses\nJ. 4% municipal bond\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 984, "output_tokens": 340, "total_tokens": 1324}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_124", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the following are aimed at providing customers with the peace of mind of knowing that the company they are purchasing from is competitive in price?\n\nOptions: \nA. Price comparison tools.\nB. Price negotiation strategies.\nC. Price competitiveness.\nD. Price discrimination.\nE. Price adjustment policies.\nF. Price skimming strategies.\nG. Price guarantee schemes.\nH. Reference prices.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 598, "output_tokens": 272, "total_tokens": 870}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_129", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of the following political leaders could not be termed a 'transformational' leader?\n\nOptions: \nA. Barack Obama\nB. Winston Churchill\nC. Franklin D. Roosevelt\nD. Martin Luther King Jr.\nE. Mikhail Gorbachov\nF. Nelson Mandela\nG. Mahatma Gandhi\nH. Jawaharlal Nehru\nI. Bill Clinton\nJ. Margaret Thatcher\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 592, "output_tokens": 382, "total_tokens": 974}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_173", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mr. Haskell has decided to buy a rental property. The building costs $50,000 and the land costs $30,000. The annual rent income is estimated to be $10,450 and the annual expense, $3,200. Mr. Haskell plans to depreciate the building by the straight line method over 40 years. Mr. Haskell wants to choose the best of three investment plans. Plan A Pay the full $80,000 from personal account. Plan B Borrow $30,000 and pay $50,000 from personal account. Rate of interest is 4(1/2)%. Plan C Borrow $60,000 and pay $20,000 from personal account. Rate of interest is 5 (1/4)%. If the tax rate is 40%, which investment plan has the highest rate of return?\n\nOptions: \nA. Plan B, if the interest rates drop to 3%\nB. Plan A, if the tax rate decreases to 30%\nC. Plan A\nD. Plan C, assuming rental income increases by 5% annually\nE. Plan C\nF. None of the plans\nG. Plan B\nH. Plan C, if additional tax deductions are available for interest paid\nI. Plan A, with a government grant covering 10% of the initial investment\nJ. Plan B, with an additional private investor contributing $10,000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1532, "output_tokens": 671, "total_tokens": 2203}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_196", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is not an advantage of a hierarchical structure?\n\nOptions: \nA. Clear responsibilities and roles\nB. Discipline and stability\nC. Quick response to change\nD. Clear chain of command\nE. Promotion opportunities\nF. High flexibility\nG. Easy to manage\nH. Small span of control\nI. Enhanced communication\nJ. Improved employee motivation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 596, "output_tokens": 386, "total_tokens": 982}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_221", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Dickenson Company has purchased a hand-operated machine of the following description; after a year, it can purchase an automatic machine of equal capacity and sell the first machine for $1,600. The following data is available: Hand-Operated Machine Automatic Machine Purchase price $4,400 $6,200 Expected Useful life 5 years 4 years Expected salvage value $0 $0 Annual operating costs $2,600 $800 The current interest rate is 8%. Which of the following options should the company chose? Option A - Keep the hand-operated machine 5 years. Option B - Keep the hand-operated machine 1 year, sell it, and purchase the automatic to use for 4 years. Round all calculations to the nearest dollar.\n\nOptions: \nA. Neither options\nB. Keep the hand-operated machine for 4 years, then switch to the automatic machine for 1 year\nC. Purchase the automatic machine immediately without selling the hand-operated machine\nD. Option B\nE. Keep the hand-operated machine for 3 years, then switch to the automatic machine for 2 years\nF. Keep the hand-operated machine for 2 years, then switch to the automatic machine for the remaining 3 years\nG. Option A, but negotiate a higher salvage value for the hand-operated machine after 5 years\nH. Option B, but seek a lower purchase price for the automatic machine\nI. Option A\nJ. Both options\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1508, "output_tokens": 974, "total_tokens": 2482}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_285", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: At the beginning of the 19X1 fiscal year Company X had $28,000 of accounts receivable. At the end of the fiscal year it had $32,000. of accounts receivable. Sales in 19X1 were $850,000. At the end of the 19X2 fiscal year, accounts receivable were $35,000. Sales in 19X2 were $920,000. Using a 360 day year and given that Company X's desired rate of return is 10%, (a) find the average collection period (in days) for 19X1 and 19X2 (b) find the cost (or saving) in extending (or reducing) the credit period during the two periods.\n\nOptions: \nA. 13.52 days, 14.23 days, $5.67\nB. 10.5 days, 11.4 days, $3.50\nC. 11.2 days, 12.1 days, $3.75\nD. 11.9 days, 12.8 days, $3.98\nE. 12.2 days, 12.9 days, $4.15\nF. 14.7 days, 15.6 days, $6.20\nG. 13.3 days, 14.1 days, $5.10\nH. 12.7 days, 13.11 days, $4.45\nI. 15.8 days, 16.7 days, $7.26\nJ. 14.2 days, 15.1 days, $6.78\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1695, "output_tokens": 687, "total_tokens": 2382}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_294", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What type of organisational culture is most likely to deliver stability and efficiency?\n\nOptions: \nA. Power culture\nB. Clan culture\nC. Network culture\nD. Role culture\nE. Task culture\nF. People culture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 444, "output_tokens": 243, "total_tokens": 687}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_325", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Debra Cole wishes to buy a used car worth $720. She can either pay for the car on the installment plan, with 10% down and 12 monthly payments of $65, or borrow the $720 for the same 12 month period at 8% interest. Which method of financing is more economical? By how much?\n\nOptions: \nA. Borrow the $720 at 8% interest with savings of $30\nB. Pay on the installment plan with savings of $74.40\nC. Borrow the $720 at 8% interest with savings of $50\nD. Pay on the installment plan with no savings\nE. Pay on the installment plan with savings of $50\nF. Borrow the $720 with no savings\nG. Pay on the installment plan with savings of $30\nH. Borrow the $720 at 8% interest with savings of $74.40\nI. Borrow the $720 at 8% interest with no savings\nJ. Pay on the installment plan with savings of $100\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1224, "output_tokens": 640, "total_tokens": 1864}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_338", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mr. Johnson, who already has a $20,000 annual salary, has purchased land for $8,000 and a house on the land for $50,000. He expects to sell the property in ten years. For the first 3 years, Johnson expects rent income from the property to be $7,000 and expenses to be $2,700. For the next 7 years, revenue will be $10,000 and expenses, $3,500. Johnson will deduct a 2% depreciation allowance on the building from his taxable incomes. If Johnson sells this property after 10 years for $61,500, what percent of his $58,000 investment will he have gained or lost from the rental and sales incomes? The current interest rate is 7%. The tax rates applied to rental and sales income, above and beyond the $20,000 salary, are: Income Rate On the first $4,00033.44% = 0.3344 On the second $4,00037.84% = 0.3784 On the third $4,00041.36% = 0.4136 On the fourth $4,00044% = 0.44 On the fifth $4,00046.64% = 0.4664\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.9%\nB. 1.84%\nC. -1.5%\nD. 2.5%\nE. 4.2%\nF. 5.7%\nG. -0.3%\nH. 0.89%\nI. 3.1%\nJ. -2.2%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1705, "output_tokens": 563, "total_tokens": 2268}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_391", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Company X desires to acquire either Company A or Company B, but not both. The following data is available and covers last year's operation. Company A Company B Total Assets $1,000,000 $2,000,000 Sales 3,000,000 5,000,000 Gross profit 300,000 750,000 Net income 96,000 272,000 Which company should Company X acquire if the following conditions are present? (a) X has a strong administration but weak sales. (b) X has a strong sales force but a weak administration. (c) X is looking for short-term improvement in its profits.\n\nOptions: \nA. Company A, Company A, Company B\nB. Company A, Company B, Company A\nC. Company A, Company A, Company A\nD. Both Company A and Company B, alternating based on the condition\nE. Company B, Company B, Company B\nF. Company B, Company A, Company B\nG. Company A, Company B, Company B\nH. Company B, Company A, Company A\nI. Neither Company A nor Company B for all conditions\nJ. Company B, Company B, Company A\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Company X should acquire Company A when it has strong administration but weak sales, because Company A has higher asset turnover (sales/assets = 3.0 vs. 2.5 for B). It should acquire Company B when it has a strong sales force but weak administration, because Company B has a much better profit margin (net income/sales = 5.44% vs. 3.2% for A). For short-term profit improvement, Company B has higher net income.  \n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1685, "output_tokens": 582, "total_tokens": 2267}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_421", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Although corporate profit maximization is not directly prescribed by major normative theories to which normative theory is it most similar?\n\nOptions: \nA. ethics of care\nB. preference utilitarianism\nC. Egoism\nD. Deontology\nE. Relativism\nF. The Categorical Imperative\nG. Virtue ethics\nH. Contractarianism\nI. hedonistic utilitarianism\nJ. Consequentialism\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 620, "output_tokens": 238, "total_tokens": 858}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_589", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A drama guild is renovating an old theater, hoping to use it for 15 years. The guild can follow one of two plans to finance the work: Plan A is to use $5,000 collected from guild members to pay for a renovation job which would be done immediately and would last 15 years. Plan B is to borrow $2,000 the year before the theater opens, and then in the 5th and 10th years of the theater's life to renovate it; each job will last five years. Interest is 6% for both plans. (a) Which plan should the guild follow? (b) If, in Plan B, the 2nd and 3rd renovation jobs will cost $3,000 each and the guild will not be able to borrow the money for any of the three jobs (i.e., the members will have to contribute), which plan should the guild follow?\n\nOptions: \nA. Plan A, with the $5,000 invested first to grow at 6% interest before renovating\nB. Plan B, with renovations every 7 years and borrowing at a lower interest rate\nC. Plan A\nD. Plan B, with the guild members contributing an additional $1,000 upfront for future renovations\nE. Plan A, but with an additional loan taken out in the 10th year\nF. Plan A, with a smaller renovation every 5 years using money from fundraising events\nG. Plan B\nH. Both plans\nI. Plan B, with additional renovations every 3 years financed by ticket sales\nJ. Neither plans\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1618, "output_tokens": 797, "total_tokens": 2415}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_590", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mr. Fields is considering selling a property acquired 15 years ago for $65,000; $10,000 was for the land, and $55,000 was for the building. Mr. Fields can now sell the property for $120,000. He can also keep it and continue to collect the annual rent from the building. If Mr. Fields decides to keep the property, he will keep it for another 25 years and will, at that time, sell it for $40,000. The annual rent receipts will be $5,930 for the next twenty-five years. Should Mr. Fields sell the property now or in twenty-five years? Assume that the building, but not the land, has been depreciated using the straight line method at 2%, long term gains are taxable at a rate of 25%, Mr. Fields' income tax rate is 56%, the minimum attractive rate of return after taxes is 2(1/2)%, and taxes will hold for the next 25 years. Make all calculations to the nearest dollar.\n\nOptions: \nA. Mr. Fields should lease the property to a new tenant for a higher annual rent\nB. Mr. Fields should sell the property now for $120,000\nC. Mr. Fields should keep the property for 25 more years\nD. Mr. Fields should convert the building into a personal residence\nE. Mr. Fields should rent the property for another 15 years\nF. Mr. Fields should sell the property after 10 years\nG. Mr. Fields should renovate the property and then decide whether to sell or keep it\nH. Mr. Fields should exchange the property for a similar one to defer taxes\nI. Mr. Fields should hold the property indefinitely for future generations\nJ. Mr. Fields should donate the property to a charitable organization for a tax write-off\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}  \n\nSelling now yields a higher after-tax net present value compared to holding for 25 years, given the low future sale price, depreciation recapture, and the required after-tax return rate. The annual rent does not compensate for the loss in property value and tax disadvantages over the long term. Thus, immediate sale is the better financial choice.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 2336, "output_tokens": 754, "total_tokens": 3090}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_611", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Economic\u2014marketing should encourage long-term economic development as opposed to short-term economic development.\n\nOptions: \nA. Economic, emerging, and evolutionary\nB. Evolutionary, experimental, and economic\nC. Ecological, equitable, and economic\nD. Equitable, evolutionary, and emerging\nE. Evolutionary, equitable, and economic.\nF. Economic, equitable, and experimental\nG. Ecological, experimental, and economic\nH. Ecological, equitable, and emerging.\nI. Economic, ecological, and experimental\nJ. Ecological, evolutionary, and economic\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 724, "output_tokens": 247, "total_tokens": 971}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_616", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Enhancement of job satisfaction and productivity are key characteristics of which theoretical perspective of work design?\n\nOptions: \nA. Human Relations theory\nB. Process improvement\nC. Job enrichment theory\nD. Job enlargement theory\nE. Time and Motion study\nF. Techno-structural change model\nG. Scientific management theory\nH. Socio-technical systems\nI. Motivational theory\nJ. Job characteristics model\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 596, "output_tokens": 250, "total_tokens": 846}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_617", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A young couple has made a non-refundable deposit of the first month's rent (equal to $1, 000) on a 6-month apartment lease. The next day they find a different apartment that they like just as well, but its monthly rent is only $900. They plan to be in the apartment only 6 months. Should they switch to the new apartment?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.0\nB. -200.0\nC. -100.0\nD. 50.0\nE. 100.0\nF. 1.0\nG. -1.0\nH. -50.0\nI. 2.0\nJ. 200.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The couple already paid a $1,000 non-refundable deposit, which is a sunk cost and does not affect the decision. By switching, they would save $100 per month for 6 months, totaling $600 in savings, minus the lost $1,000 deposit, resulting in a net loss of $400; however, the question provides numerical options that compare only the first month's difference in absolute terms, so the immediate loss from forfeiting the deposit to save $100 in first-month rent is $900 vs. $1,000, a net -$100 for the first month.  \n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1122, "output_tokens": 18307, "total_tokens": 19429}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_679", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is the most appropriate pricing strategy to use when introducing a new and unique product to the market?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bundle pricing\nB. Psychological pricing\nC. Price skimming\nD. Cost-plus pricing\nE. Penetration pricing\nF. Economy pricing\nG. Promotional pricing\nH. Competitive pricing\nI. Premium pricing\nJ. Value-based pricing\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 576, "output_tokens": 268, "total_tokens": 844}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_681", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the following is not a useful base for segmenting organizational characteristics?\n\nOptions: \nA. By industry type.\nB. By level of technology adoption.\nC. By geographical location.\nD. By turnover.\nE. By organizational culture.\nF. By employee count.\nG. By type of ownership.\nH. By profitability.\nI. By time of establishment.\nJ. By organizational size.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 600, "output_tokens": 362, "total_tokens": 962}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_683", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  When the analyst reads the data from a critical perspective to determine whether or not this fits with their expectations, this constitutes what is termed a:\n\nOptions: \nA. Control group.\nB. Confirmation bias.\nC. Content validity.\nD. Face validity.\nE. Observational bias.\nF. Criterion validity.\nG. Experimental group.\nH. Focus group.\nI. Construct validity.\nJ. Reliability.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 584, "output_tokens": 218, "total_tokens": 802}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_685", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the following is not an issue that marketers need to consider when using digital resources for marketing activities?\n\nOptions: \nA. Permissions.\nB. Social Media popularity.\nC. Website aesthetics.\nD. Digital literacy.\nE. Ownership.\nF. Disclosure.\nG. Jurisdiction.\nH. Internet connectivity.\nI. Weather conditions.\nJ. Popularity of the product.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 556, "output_tokens": 325, "total_tokens": 881}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_730", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The marketing research firm of Burrows, Heller and Larimer wants to estimate the proportions of men and women who are familiar with a shoe polish. In a sample (random) of 100 men and 200 women it is found that 20 men and 60 women had used this particular shoe polish. Compute a 95% confidence interval for the difference in pro portions between men and women familiar with the product. Use this to test the hypothesis that the proportions are equal.\n\nOptions: \nA. The confidence interval includes zero, indicating no difference in proportions\nB. The proportions are equal\nC. The proportions are not equal\nD. The confidence interval does not include zero, indicating a significant difference in proportions\nE. The proportion of women is higher\nF. The confidence interval is too wide to determine a significant difference\nG. The proportion of men is higher\nH. No conclusion can be drawn without further data\nI. The proportion of men is significantly lower\nJ. The proportion of women is significantly lower\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1108, "output_tokens": 605, "total_tokens": 1713}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_business_783", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A company has a permit to mine for gold in a region of New Mexico for 3 years. Management is trying to decide how to finance the machinery. One option is to rent it for $130 per month over the three years. The deal includes the fuel needed to operate the equipment. The other option is to buy the equipment now and. it after three years. The machinery costs $11,500. There is a down payment of $2,500, so that the balance due will be $11,500 - $2,500 = $9,000. This balance will be covered by a 5(1/2)% loan to be paid in equal annual installments over 15 years. The annual fuel costs for the equipment would be $375. If the minimum attractive rate of return is 5%, at what resale value (end of third year) will both options be equally economical? Make all calculations to the nearest dollar.\n\nOptions: \nA. $8,400\nB. $2,650\nC. $6,825\nD. $5,760\nE. $4,248\nF. $1,987\nG. $7,950\nH. $10,500\nI. $9,937\nJ. $3,500\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1460, "output_tokens": 611, "total_tokens": 2071}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5855", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The cabbages you grow in your summer garden are\n\nOptions: \nA. not counted in either GDP or NDP.\nB. not counted in GDP.\nC. counted in GDP under I.\nD. counted in GDP under X-M.\nE. counted in GDP under G.\nF. counted in GDP under NX.\nG. counted in GDP under C.\nH. counted in NDP but not GDP.\nI. counted in GDP but not NDP.\nJ. counted in both GDP and NDP.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 661, "output_tokens": 251, "total_tokens": 912}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6319", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following estimation techniques are available for the estimation of over-identified systems of simultaneous equations?\n\ni) OLS\n\nii) ILS\n\niii) 2SLS\n\niv) IV\n\nOptions: \nA. (iii) only\nB. (i), (iii) and (iv) only\nC. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nD. (i), (ii) and (iii) only\nE. (i) and (iii) only\nF. (ii) and (iv) only\nG. (i) and (ii) only\nH. (i), (ii), (iii) and (iv)\nI. (i), (ii) and (iv) only\nJ. (iii) and (iv) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "For over-identified systems of simultaneous equations, OLS is generally biased and inconsistent, and ILS only works for exactly identified equations. Both 2SLS and IV methods are appropriate for over-identified cases. Therefore, the correct answer is choice J: (iii) and (iv) only.  \n\n\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1141, "output_tokens": 436, "total_tokens": 1577}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6187", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A white noise process will have\n\n(i) A zero mean\n\n(ii) A constant variance\n\n(iii) Autocovariances that are constant\n\n(iv) Autocovariances that are zero except at lag zero\n\nOptions: \nA. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nB. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv)\nC. (i) and (ii) only\nD. (i), (ii), and (iii) only\nE. (i) and (iii) only\nF. (i), (iii), and (iv) only\nG. (ii) and (iv) only\nH. (i), (ii) and (iv) only\nI. (ii) and (iii) only\nJ. (iii) and (iv) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is 