\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1149, "output_tokens": 253, "total_tokens": 1402}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6251", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a product group?\n\nOptions: \nA. A group of firms producing similar, but not identical, products\nB. A group of identical products\nC. A classification of products based on their manufacturing process rather than their function\nD. A collection of products with different functions that are sold together as a bundle\nE. A set of services offered by a single company\nF. A group of complementary products that are often used together\nG. A group of firms producing identical products\nH. A group of products designed for a specific demographic group\nI. A group of products from different industries categorized under a single label\nJ. A group of unrelated products\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 796, "output_tokens": 237, "total_tokens": 1033}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6397", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the coefficient of elasticity?\n\nOptions: \nA. The sum of the percentage changes in both the dependent and independent variables\nB. The percentage change in the independent variable divided by the percentage change in the dependent variable\nC. The ratio of the percentage change in the independent variable to the absolute change in the dependent variable\nD. The absolute change in the dependent variable divided by the absolute change in the independent variable\nE. The ratio of the change in the dependent variable to the change in the independent variable\nF. The percentage change in the dependent variable divided by the percentage change in the independent variable\nG. The change in the independent variable divided by the change in the dependent variable\nH. The percentage change in the dependent variable divided by the absolute change in the independent variable\nI. The absolute change in the independent variable divided by the percentage change in the dependent variable\nJ. The sum of the changes in the dependent and independent variables\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1107, "output_tokens": 245, "total_tokens": 1352}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6237", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Marginal cost always intersects average variable cost at\n\nOptions: \nA. the minimum of average total cost\nB. the point where average variable cost is equal to marginal cost\nC. the profit-maximizing quantity\nD. the maximum of average variable cost\nE. the point of equilibrium between supply and demand\nF. the point where marginal cost equals average total cost\nG. the minimum of average variable cost\nH. the point where average variable cost is less than marginal cost\nI. the minimum of marginal cost\nJ. the maximum of marginal cost\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 716, "output_tokens": 272, "total_tokens": 988}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5932", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The residual from a standard regression model is defined as\n\nOptions: \nA. The difference between the actual value, y, and the fitted value, y-hat\nB. The square of the difference between the actual value, y, and the fitted value, y-hat\nC. The square of the difference between the fitted value, y-hat, and the mean, y-bar\nD. The difference between the fitted value, y-hat, and the mean, y-bar\nE. The sum of the actual value, y, and the fitted value, y-hat\nF. The difference between the standard deviation, s, and the fitted value, y-hat\nG. The difference between the actual value, y, and the mean, y-bar\nH. The difference between the actual value, y, and the median, m\nI. The square root of the difference between the actual value, y, and the fitted value, y-hat\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1053, "output_tokens": 264, "total_tokens": 1317}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider