 needs as society currently defines those needs.\nE. Poverty is the inability to purchase luxury items and services.\nF. Poverty is the state of living in a rural area without urban amenities.\nG. Poverty is the temporary lack of employment.\nH. Poverty is the state of being inferior in quality or insufficient in amount.\nI. Poverty is the condition of having an income that is less than the median income of a country.\nJ. Poverty is exclusively the state of not having access to education.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 950, "output_tokens": 337, "total_tokens": 1287}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5949", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is meant by the term \"long run\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. A short term investment strategy\nB. A period of time when all factors of production are constant\nC. The time required for a business to fully deplete its resources\nD. A time span where market demand remains unchanged\nE. A duration during which only labor input can be varied\nF. The timeframe in which a company plans its strategic future goals\nG. A time period over which every input in the production process may be considered variable\nH. A period of time when a firm's output is fixed\nI. A time interval in which only technology and innovation drive changes in production\nJ. A period where only capital inputs can be adjusted\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or fe