s given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the purpose of the National Accounts?\n\nOptions: \nA. National Accounts document the financial transactions of a nation\nB. National Accounts provide a detailed demographic breakdown of a nation's population\nC. National Accounts assess the environmental impact of economic activities\nD. National Accounts monitor the national debt\nE. The National Accounts measure the total value of the output of the economy and show where the output originates and how it is allocated.\nF. National Accounts determine the tax rates for different income brackets\nG. National Accounts regulate international trade agreements\nH. National Accounts track the income of individuals\nI. National Accounts calculate the gross domestic product (GDP) per capita only\nJ. National Accounts compile and analyze consumer spending habits only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 915, "output_tokens": 359, "total_tokens": 1274}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5965", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Theo loses his job at the public swimming pool when the pool closes for the winter. This is an example of\n\nOptions: \nA. natural unemployment.\nB. underemployment.\nC. discouraged worker.\nD. structural unemployment.\nE. jobless recovery.\nF. cyclical unemployment.\nG. seasonal unemployment.\nH. frictional unemployment.\nI. long-term unemployment.\nJ. involuntary unemployment.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 594, "output_tokens": 229, "total_tokens": 823}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6183", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of the following is the most appropriate definition of a 99% confidence interval?\n\nOptions: \nA. 99% of the time in repeated samples, the interval would contain the estimated value of the null hypothesis\nB. 99% of the time in repeated samples, the interval would be different from the estimated value of the parameter\nC. 99% of the time in repeated samples, the null hypothesis will not be rejected when it was false\nD. 1% of the time in repeated samples, the interval would not contain the true value of the parameter\nE. 99% of the time in repeated samples, the interval would contain the true value of the null hypothesis\nF. 99% of the time in repeated samples, the null hypothesis will be accepted when it was false\nG. 99% of the time in repeated samples, the null hypothesis will be rejected\nH. 99% of the time in repeated samples, the interval would contain the estimated value of the parameter\nI. 99% of the time in repeated samples, the interval would contain the true value of the parameter\nJ. 99% of the time in repeated samples, the interval would not contain the true value of the null hypothesis\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1312, "output_tokens": 265, "total_tokens": 1577}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5584", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Crowding out\n\nOptions: \nA. occurs when interest rates fall due to government borrowing.\nB. occurs when consumers and firms spend less offsetting expansionary fiscal policy.\nC. occurs when the government reduces its spending in response to inflation.\nD. is a consequence of contractionary fiscal policy.\nE. is one reason fiscal policy is so effective.\nF. is when expansionary fiscal policy leads to a decrease in interest rates.\nG. happens when the government increases taxes to reduce the budget deficit.\nH. causes the aggregate demand curve to shift to the right.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 708, "output_tokens": 231, "total_tokens": 939}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6062", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Note that statistical tables are not necessary to answer this question. For a sample of 1000 observations, the Dickey-Fuller test statistic values are\n\nOptions: \nA. Equal to those in the left hand tail of a normal distribution\nB. Less negative than (i.e. smaller in absolute value than) those in the left hand tail of a normal distribution\nC. Obtained from a standard normal distribution\nD. Obtained from an analytical formula for the density of the Dickey-Fuller distribution\nE. More negative than (i.e. bigger in absolute value than) those in the left hand tail of a normal distribution\nF. More negative (i.e. bigger in absolute value) for a 10% size of test than a 5% test.\nG. Less negative than (i.e. smaller in absolute value than) those in the right hand tail of a normal distribution\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1030, "output_tokens": 287, "total_tokens": 1317}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6197", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the difference between \"caveat emptor\" and \"ceteris paribus\"\n\nOptions: \nA. 'Caveat emptor' is 'Buyer's guarantee' and 'Ceteris paribus' is 'given the circumstances'\nB. 'Caveat emptor' is 'Buyer beware' and 'Ceteris paribus' is 'all things constant'\nC. 'Caveat emptor' is 'Let the buyer beware' and 'Ceteris paribus' is 'all other things being equal'\nD. 'Caveat emptor' is 'Let the buyer choose' and 'Ceteris paribus' is 'other things unchanged'\nE. 'Caveat emptor' is 'Let the seller beware' and 'Ceteris paribus' is 'all things considered'\nF. 'Caveat emptor' means 'Seller's warning' and 'Ceteris paribus' means 'everything else is variable'\nG. 'Caveat emptor' is 'The seller is responsible' and 'Ceteris paribus' is 'all factors constant'\nH. 'Caveat emptor' is 'buyer's choice' and 'Ceteris paribus' is 'equal rights'\nI. 'Caveat emptor' means 'Guarantee for the buyer' and 'Ceteris paribus' means 'considering each part'\nJ. 'Caveat emptor' is 'Let the buyer decide' and 'Ceteris paribus' is 'with all other things'\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1501, "output_tokens": 288, "total_tokens": 1789}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6060", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A Hausman test would be used for\n\nOptions: \nA. Testing for the presence of multicollinearity in a regression model\nB. Checking the validity of the instrumental variables\nC. Determining whether a variable is endogenous or exogenous\nD. Determining whether an equation that is part of a simultaneous system is identified\nE. Determining whether 2SLS or ILS is optimal\nF. Determining whether a simultaneous framework is needed for a particular variable\nG. Determining the order of integration in a time series\nH. Determining whether the structural form equations can be obtained via substitution from the reduced forms\nI. Testing the null hypothesis in a regression model\nJ. Checking the goodness of fit in a multiple regression model\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 872, "