.\nC. Craft unions are for skilled workers while industrial unions are for unskilled workers\nD. Craft unions include workers from multiple industries, while industrial unions are specific to one craft or trade.\nE. Craft unions are found only in the manufacturing sector, while industrial unions can be found in all sectors.\nF. Industrial unions negotiate for individual workers, while craft unions negotiate for all workers within an industry.\nG. Craft unions are smaller than industrial unions\nH. Industrial unions are more powerful than craft unions\nI. Craft unions focus on broad political agendas, while industrial unions focus solely on workplace conditions and pay.\nJ. Industrial unions represent freelance workers, while craft unions represent salaried employees.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1044, "output_tokens": 273, "total_tokens": 1317}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5648", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the main difference between the short-run and long-run Phillips curve?\n\nOptions: \nA. The short-run Phillips curve is downward sloping and the long-run Phillips curve is horizontal.\nB. The short-run Phillips curve is downward sloping and the long-run Phillips curve is vertical.\nC. The short-run Phillips curve is upward sloping and the long-run Phillips curve is vertical.\nD. The short-run Phillips curve is horizontal and the long-run Phillips curve is vertical.\nE. The short-run Phillips curve is vertical and 