 The division of labor refers to the physical division of a company's labor force\nI. The division of labor is a process by which machines are assigned specific tasks to replace human workers\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1027, "output_tokens": 304, "total_tokens": 1331}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5690", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why is the Wagner Act (officially the National Labor Relations Act), considered to be \"labor's Magna Charta\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. It introduced mandatory profit sharing between employers and employees\nB. It obligated employers to bargain in good faith with a union\nC. It outlawed company unions\nD. It created a universal pension system for all workers regardless of employer contributions\nE. It allowed for automatic union membership for all employees in a workplace\nF. It mandated a four-day workweek for all industries\nG. It established a federal minimum wage for all workers\nH. It gave labor the right of self-organization and the right to bargain collectively with employers\nI. It required employers to provide health insurance to all employees\nJ. It prohibited antiunion discrimination by employers\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 900, "output_tokens": 362, "total_tokens": 1262}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6370", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the last 20 years firms that produce cameras have begun to produce fewer 35-mm cameras and more digital cameras. This trend is an example of\n\nOptions: \nA. the market system answering the question of \"what\" cameras should be produced.\nB. the market system answering the question of \"when\" cameras should be produced.\nC. the market system answering the question of \"why\" cameras should be produced.\nD. the influence of government regulation on camera production.\nE. the market system answering the question of \"where\" cameras should be produced.\nF. how central planners dictate which cameras are produced.\nG. the market system answering the question of \"who\" should consume the cameras that are produced.\nH. the market system answering the question of \"how\" cameras should be produced.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 904, "output_tokens": 243, "total_tokens": 1147}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5642", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements is true?\n\nOptions: \nA. The demand for loanable funds consists of savers.\nB. Real GDP is the sum of the money supply and the velocity of money.\nC. The supply of loanable funds is solely determined by the central bank's policies.\nD. Dollars earned today have more purchasing power than dollars earned a year from today.\nE. The velocity of money is the speed at which the stock market indices change.\nF. The demand for loanable funds is entirely driven by government borrowing.\nG. Purchasing power parity ensures that dollars have the same value across all time periods.\nH. The supply of loanable funds consists of investors.\nI. Inflation rates are inversely proportional to the velocity of money at all times.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 876, "output_tokens": 224, "total_tokens": 1100}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5931", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of the following statements is true concerning VARs?\n\nOptions: \nA. The coefficient estimates in VARs are always positive\nB. VARs require all variables to be of the same sign for effective forecasting\nC. The coefficient estimates have intuitive theoretical interpretations\nD. VARs often produce better forecasts than simultaneous equation structural models\nE. All of the components of a VAR must be stationary before it can be used for forecasting\nF. The coefficient estimates have no theoretical interpretations in VARs\nG. VARs cannot be used for forecasting purposes\nH. All components of a VAR must be non-stationary for accurate forecasting\nI. VARs produce poorer forecasts when compared to standalone variable models\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 835, "output_tokens": 323, "total_tokens": 1158}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6241", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If one person has the only original signed copy of The Wealth of Nations by Adam Smith, which of the following would illustrate this situation?\n\nOptions: \nA. A downward sloping supply curve.\nB. An upward sloping demand curve.\nC. An upward sloping supply curve.\nD. An invisible hand.\nE. A perfectly horizontal supply curve.\nF. A perfectly horizontal demand curve.\nG. A perfectly vertical demand curve.\nH. An invisible supply.\nI. A downward sloping demand curve.\nJ. A perfectly vertical supply curve.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 692, "output_tokens": 216, "total_tokens": 908}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5736", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The basis for the 