"output_tokens": 304, "total_tokens": 1220}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5641", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the main contrast between the short-run and long-run Phillips curve?\n\nOptions: \nA. In the short run there is a negative relationship between inflation and unemployment and in the long run the relationship is positive.\nB. In the short run there is a constant relationship between inflation and unemployment and in the long run the relationship is positive.\nC. In the short run there is a constant relationship between inflation and unemployment and in the long run the relationship is negative.\nD. In the short run there is a negative relationship between inflation and unemployment and in the long run the relationship is constant.\nE. In the short run there is a positive relationship between inflation and unemployment, in the long run the relationship is non-existent.\nF. In the short run, inflation and unemployment are unrelated, while in the long run, there is a positive relationship.\nG. In the short run there is a positive relationship between inflation and unemployment and in the long run the relationship is constant.\nH. In the short run there is a positive relationship between inflation and unemployment and in the long run the relationship is negative.\nI. In the short run, inflation and unemployment are unrelated, while in the long run, there is a negative relationship.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1228, "output_tokens": 321, "total_tokens": 1549}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5970", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A negative or contractionary supply shock will\n\nOptions: \nA. shift the Phillips curve to the left.\nB. shift the investment demand curve to the right.\nC. shift the money demand curve to the right.\nD. shift the Phillips curve to the right.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 468, "output_tokens": 205, "total_tokens": 673}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5765", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One aspect of Marxian economics is that some of the pre-dictions of Marx were proven wrong. As a result of this, some radical economists have only adopted the tools of Marxian analysis, without necessarily accepting Marx's con-clusions . In the nineteenth century, other Marxists became 'revisionists'. Explain briefly what distinguishes a re-visionist from a Marxist.\n\nOptions: \nA. Revisionists maintain that capitalism will naturally evolve into socialism without any intervention\nB. Revisionists support the idea of a permanent dictatorship of the proletariat as the path to socialism\nC. Revisionists focus on individual enlightenment and moral reform as the means to achieve socialism\nD. Revisionists argue for immediate abolition of the state to achieve socialism\nE. Revisionists believe in gradual evolution towards socialism through political action and trade unionism, rejecting violent class struggle.\nF. Revisionists emphasize the importance of international trade as a primary tool for achieving socialism\nG. Revisionists adhere strictly to Marx's labor theory of value\nH. Revisionists reject the concept of class struggle entirely and believe in maintaining the status quo\nI. Revisionists fully accept Marx's theories and predictions\nJ. Revisionists believe in achieving socialism through violent revolution\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1232, "output_tokens": 283, "total_tokens": 1515}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6323", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Give the significance of the \"most favored nation clause\" in the Gatt agreement.\n\nOptions: \nA. The 'most favored nation clause' is the agreement that no member of GATT will be treated worse than the 'most favored nation', meaning that no member country's imports can be charged a higher tariff than any other member country, unless special exceptions have been made.\nB. It is a clause that allows for the imposition of high tariffs on certain goods\nC. It is a provision that allows for the exemption of certain countries from tariff reduction\nD. It is an agreement that allows for preferential treatment of a particular country\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 764, "output_tokens": 279, "total_tokens": 1043}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6353", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why is it that the two decades prior to World War Ihave beendubbed \"the golden age of American agriculture\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. The demand for farm products, farm prices, and farm incomes all rose.\nB. Urbanization led to a decrease in the farming workforce.\nC. The federal government imposed high taxes on farm income.\nD. The government introduced significant restrictions on crop exports.\nE. Land grants for farming were abolished.\nF. The industrial revolution started.\nG. The introduction of widespread commercial fertilizer use improved crop yields.\nH. The Great Depression ended.\nI. There was a major decline in agricultural technology.\nJ. The population in the country decreased.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 800, "output_tokens": 271, "total_tokens": 1071}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6122", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is \"indicative planning\"? How does it differfrom socialistcentral planning?\n\nOptions: \nA. Indicative planning is a system practiced only in socialist countries\nB. Indicative planning is a system in which representatives of government and private industries draw up a national economic plan, but unlike socialist enterprises, private firms are not absolutely compelled to cooperate.\nC. Indicative planning is a system where the government sets prices and production quotas for private firms\nD. Indicative planning is a method where only the private sector drafts a national economic plan without government input\nE. Indicative planning is a system where private firms are absolutely compelled to cooperate\nF. Indicative planning is a system where local governments create economic plans that must be strictly followed by both government and private firms\nG. Indicative planning is a system where economic planning is done by international organizations, rather than national governments\nH. Indicative planning is a system in which the government provides suggestions for economic development, but there is no formal plan in place\nI. Indicative planning is a system that relies on market forces alone with no government or private industry planning\nJ. Indicative planning is a system where the government makes all economic decisions\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1271, "output_tokens": 262, "total_tokens": 1533}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5778", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For years you work as a grocery checker at a supermarket and one day you are replaced by self-serve checkout stations. What type of unemployment is this?\n\nOptions: \nA. Seasonal\nB. Structural\nC. Classical\nD. Traditional\nE. Cyclical\nF. Deflationary\nG. Inflationary\nH. Frictional\nI. Voluntary\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 568, "output_tokens": 203, "total_tokens": 771}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5595", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The purpose of \"augmenting\" the Dickey-Fuller test regression is to\n\nOptions: \nA. Ensure that there is no heteroscedasticity in the test regression residuals.\nB. Improve the accuracy of the Dickey-Fuller test\nC. Ensure that the test regression residuals are negatively skewed\nD. Ensure that the test regression residuals are normally distributed\nE. Ensure that all of the non-stationarity is taken into account.\nF. Ensure that the test regression residuals have no outliers\nG. Ensure that the test regression residuals are positively skewed\nH. Ensure that there is no autocorrelation in the test regression residuals\nI. Ensure that the test regression residuals are balanced\nJ. Increase the complexity of the Dickey-Fuller test\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 888, "output_tokens": 306, "total_tokens": 1194}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6344", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Adam Smith's 'invisible hand' operates in the free market system, with active competition, that aligns the self-interests of individuals with the \"public interest\". What exactly is the \"public interest\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Public interest is to control the market\nB. Public interest is to establish monopolies in key industries\nC. Public interest is to distribute wealth equally\nD. Public interest is to prioritize environmental conservation over economic growth\nE. Public interest is to use the scarce resources as efficiently as possible\nF. Public interest is to ensure the government's intervention in all economic activities\nG. Public interest is to maximize individual profits\nH. Public interest is to promote international trade exclusively\nI. Public interest is to provide subsidies to all businesses\nJ. Public interest is to guarantee minimum prices for all products\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 985, "output_tokens": 334, "total_tokens": 1319}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5647", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose yesterday the euro was trading on the foreign exchange market at $1.36 U.S. and today it is trading at $1.40 U.S. Which of the following is true?\n\nOptions: \nA. Interest rates in the United States have decreased.\nB. The U.S. dollar has appreciated.\nC. The U.S. dollar has appreciated and the euro has depreciated.\nD. The exchange rate has remained steady.\nE. The U.S. dollar has stayed the same and the euro has depreciated.\nF. The euro has appreciated.\nG. Interest rates in Europe have increased.\nH. The U.S. dollar has depreciated.\nI. The euro has depreciated.\nJ. Interest rates in the United States have increased.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 868, "output_tokens": 306, "total_tokens": 1174}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5893", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How did Joseph Schumpeter build his theory of the business cycle, and of growth, from the idea of embodied techno- logical progress?\n\nOptions: \nA. The business cycle and growth are driven primarily by traditional industries, with little impact from technological progress.\nB. Without technological progress, there would be no business cycle or growth.\nC. Business cycles and growth are mainly the result of random market fluctuations, with technological progress playing a minor role.\nD. Technological progress and imaginative, risk-taking innovators were the keys to the business cycle, and to growth.\nE. Technological progress is the only factor in the business cycle and growth, with no contribution from entrepreneurs.\nF. Technological progress and growth are unrelated to the business cycle.\nG. Technological progress is solely determined by government policies, which in turn drive the business cycle and growth.\nH. Technological progress hinders the business cycle and growth.\nI. Schumpeter believed that business cycles and growth are perpetuated by consumer demand, not technological progress.\nJ. Technological progress disrupts the business cycle and growth by causing economic downturns.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1152, "output_tokens": 312, "total_tokens": 1464}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6333", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How does labor fit in the circular flowmodel ?\n\nOptions: \nA. Labor is created by businesses and shared among households\nB. Labor is a type of good that households export to other countries\nC. Labor is supplied by businesses and demanded by households\nD. Labor is a finished article demanded by households\nE. Labor is a scarce resource, furnished by households and demanded by businesses\nF. Labor is a renewable resource generated by households for personal use\nG. Labor is an abundant resource, supplied by households\nH. Labor is an unlimited resource that businesses provide to each other\nI. Labor is a service provided by the government to businesses\nJ. Labor is a form of capital that businesses lend to households\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 836, "output_tokens": 211, "total_tokens": 1047}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6266", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Define collective bargaining and give its importance to labor.\n\nOptions: \nA. Collective bargaining is a legal dispute between employees and employers.\nB. Collective bargaining is the system through which employers seek concessions from unions.\nC. Collective bargaining is a form of employment contract.\nD. Collective bargaining is a way for workers to demand higher wages.\nE. Collective bargaining is a process where individual employees negotiate their contracts separately with the employer.\nF. Collective bargaining refers to the governmental intervention in labor disputes.\nG. Collective bargaining is a term used to describe the setting of industry-wide standards by government bodies.\nH. Collective bargaining is the approach used by labor organizations to negotiate with employers or their representatives.\nI. Collective bargaining is a strategy used by employers to dictate terms to employees without negotiation.\nJ. Collective bargaining is the unilateral decision-making process by employers regarding work conditions.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 932, "output_tokens": 278, "total_tokens": 1210}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6054", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is correct concerning logit and probit models?\n\nOptions: \nA. The logit model can result in too many observations falling exactly at the midpoint\nB. They use a different method of transforming the model so that the probabilities lie between zero and one\nC. The logit and probit models are identical in every aspect\nD. For the logit model, the marginal effect of a change in one of the explanatory variables is simply the estimate of the parameter attached to that variable, whereas this is not the case for the probit model\nE. Both logit and probit models fail to account for the possibility of error in the dependent variable.\nF. The logit model can result in too many observations falling at exactly zero or exactly one\nG. The logit model is less flexible in terms of shape and is always symmetric, while the probit model can accommodate asymmetry\nH. For the probit model, the marginal effect of a change in one of the explanatory variables is simply the estimate of the parameter attached to that variable, whereas this is not the case for the logit model\nI. The probit model is based on a cumulative logistic function\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1224, "output_tokens": 397, "total_tokens": 1621}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6154", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The international value of the dollar will appreciate if\n\nOptions: \nA. American income falls relative to the rest of the world.\nB. American interest rates fall relative to interest rates in other countries.\nC. American prices rise.\nD. foreigners boycott American products.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 464, "output_tokens": 476, "total_tokens": 940}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6414", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If a country has a negative value on its current account then it must\n\nOptions: \nA. have a negative value on its financial account.\nB. have a positive value of equal magnitude on its capital account.\nC. decrease its interest rates.\nD. increase its export volume.\nE. take a loan from the International Monetary Fund.\nF. decrease its import volume.\nG. appreciate its currency.\nH. depreciate its currency.\nI. pay that amount to its trading partners.\nJ. increase its interest rates.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In the balance of payments, the current account and the financial/capital account must sum to zero, meaning a negative current account is offset by a positive financial account (or capital account in broader terms). Therefore, the correct answer is that the country must have a positive value of equal magnitude on its capital account.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 836, "output_tokens": 930, "total_tokens": 1766}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6309", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements is positive?\n\nOptions: \nA. The law of increasing costs leads to a downward sloping production possibilities frontier.\nB. Nations should concentrate their resources on producing wholesome consumer goods as opposed to the weapons of war.\nC. The production possibilities frontier is linear due to constant costs.\nD. The production possibilities frontier is convex to the origin because of the law of decreasing costs.\nE. An economy that produces more butter than guns is better off than an economy that produces more guns than butter.\nF. The law of diminishing returns applies to the production of both consumer goods and weapons.\nG. Nations ought to devote at least some of their resources to national defense.\nH. Nations should prioritize military production to ensure their national security.\nI. An economy that produces more guns than butter is worse off than an economy that produces more butter than guns.\nJ. The production possibilities frontier is concave to the origin because of the law of increasing costs.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1108, "output_tokens": 350, "total_tokens": 1458}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5620", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is meant by a bank loan that is called a 7 percent discount?\n\nOptions: \nA. A 7 percent discount loan means the interest is reduced by 7 percent from the standard rate.\nB. A 7 percent discount loan means the borrower doesn't have to pay interest.\nC. A 7 percent discount loan is where the borrower receives $ 93 today and pays back $ 100 in a year.\nD. A 7 percent discount loan is where the borrower receives $107 today and pays back $100 in a year.\nE. A 7 percent discount loan is where the borrower receives $ 100 today and pays back $ 93 in a year.\nF. A 7 percent discount loan means that the lender discounts the total repayable amount by 7 percent as a promotion.\nG. A 7 percent discount loan is where the borrower pays 7 percent interest upfront and then repays the principal after a year.\nH. A 7 percent discount loan means the borrower's repayment amount decreases by 7 percent each year.\nI. A 7 percent discount loan means the borrower pays back 7 percent less than what they borrowed.\nJ. A 7 percent discount loan is where the borrower receives the full amount borrowed and pays back only 93 percent of it.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1348, "output_tokens": 336, "total_tokens": 1684}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5762", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: John Maynard Keynes actively supported direct government intervention in the economy. In particular, he advocated deficit spending as a means to end the Great Depression because he thought business was not investing enough, even with low interest rates to maintain national income and employment at their pre-Depression levels. Why did busi-ness , in the view of Keynes, fail to invest in response to the low interest rates?\n\nOptions: \nA. Businesses were waiting for further reduction in interest rates\nB. Low demand during the Depression made investments unprofitable, regardless of low interest rates.\nC. The government had imposed too many regulations, which discouraged investment\nD. Businesses lacked confidence in the economy\nE. Interest rates were not truly low; there was a misperception about the monetary policy\nF. There was a surplus of goods already, and no need for further production\nG. Businesses were facing internal management issues\nH. Businesses were primarily investing in foreign markets instead of the domestic economy\nI. Businesses were unable to secure loans due to strict banking policies\nJ. High inflation rates were diminishing the real value of potential returns on investments\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1252, "output_tokens": 280, "total_tokens": 1532}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6041", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Lowering reserve requirements would\n\nOptions: \nA. restrict banks from making more loans and buying more investments, thus increasing the money supply.\nB. allow banks to make fewer loans and buy fewer investments, thus increasing the money supply.\nC. restrict banks from making more loans and buying more investments, thus decreasing the money supply.\nD. force banks to hold more reserves and make more loans.\nE. force banks to hold fewer reserves and make fewer loans.\nF. force banks to hold more reserves and decrease their investment capacity.\nG. have no impact on the banks' ability to make loans and buy investments.\nH. allow banks to make more loans and buy more investments thus decreasing the money supply.\nI. allow banks to make more loans and buy more investments thus increasing the money supply.\nJ. allow banks more freedom to merge and acquire other businesses.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 940, "output_tokens": 217, "total_tokens": 1157}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6193", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How is the use of land a cost, not counting the rent onehas topay to use the land?\n\nOptions: \nA. The cost of land is the price one pays to purchase it.\nB. The cost of land refers to the taxes one has to pay for owning it.\nC. The cost of land is the cost of maintaining it.\nD. The use of land also constitutes a cost, in this sense an implicit cost, that is the money payments which the land resource could have earned in their best alternative employments.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 684, "output_tokens": 294, "total_tokens": 978}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6133", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: TheRicardiantheory of land rents led to a movement in the late nineteenth century called the single-tax movement. What was the goal of this movement and what was its economic rationale?\n\nOptions: \nA. To eliminate all taxes but a tax on land\nB. To tax only corporate profits as a means of funding government\nC. To impose a single tax on wealth and capital gains only\nD. To replace all taxes with a single tax on income\nE. To eliminate all taxes\nF. To introduce a single tax on consumption goods and services\nG. To establish a flat tax rate for all forms of income\nH. To levy a single tax on imports and exports to regulate trade\nI. To reduce taxes on land to encourage agriculture\nJ. To increase all taxes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 926, "output_tokens": 322, "total_tokens": 1248}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5724", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For a given level of government spending the federal government usually experiences a budget____during economic____and a budget ______during economic_______.\n\nOptions: \nA. surplus expansion surplus expansion\nB. deficit recession deficit expansion\nC. surplus expansion deficit recession\nD. deficit expansion deficit recession\nE. surplus expansion surplus recession\nF. deficit recession surplus expansion\nG. surplus recession deficit expansion\nH. surplus recession surplus expansion\nI. deficit expansion surplus recession\nJ. surplus recession deficit recession\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 707, "output_tokens": 264, "total_tokens": 971}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6189", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Is it possible for many firms to sell exactly the same product, and still be in monopolistic competition?\n\nOptions: \nA. Only if the products are not identical\nB. Yes, it is entirely possible\nC. Only possible in perfect competition\nD. No, it is not possible\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 492, "output_tokens": 271, "total_tokens": 763}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5746", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Characterize and differentiate capital widening from capi-tal deepening.\n\nOptions: \nA. Capital widening is when more workers are provided with capital goods to increase their productivity, while capital deepening is when each worker is provided with a greater amount of capital goods to be more productive.\nB. Capital widening refers to the increase in technology to boost productivity, while capital deepening is the investment in human capital to improve worker efficiency.\nC. Capital widening is the practice of reducing capital investment to focus on labor-intensive production, while capital deepening involves increasing automation and capital intensity.\nD. Capital widening is when more capital goods are provided to the same number of workers, while capital deepening is when the number of workers is increased without changing the amount of capital goods.\nE. Capital widening occurs when the same amount of capital is spread over a larger workforce, leading to a potential decrease in productivity, while capital deepening is when additional capital is used to upgrade existing workers' tools and machinery.\nF. Capital widening and capital deepening both refer to the addition of more capital goods to increase productivity.\nG. Capital widening is when each worker is provided with a greater amount of capital goods to be more productive, while capital deepening is when more workers are provided with capital goods to increase their productivity.\nH. Capital widening is the process of diversifying investments across different sectors to reduce risk, while capital deepening is the concentration of investments within a particular sector to increase specialization.\nI. Capital widening is the expansion of capital to new geographic regions, while capital deepening is the enhancement of capital within existing production facilities.\nJ. Capital widening is when the overall investment in the economy increases without regard to the labor force, while capital deepening is when investment is focused on innovation rather than on increasing the capital per worker.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1700, "output_tokens": 323, "total_tokens": 2023}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6404", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the difference between money income and real income?\n\nOptions: \nA. Money income is the amount of money earned before taxes, while real income is the amount after taxes.\nB. Money income is the total wealth a person accumulates, while real income is the financial savings a person has.\nC. Money income is the purchasing power, while real income is the amount of dollars a person receives.\nD. Money income is the price index, while real income is the amount of dollars a person receives.\nE. Money income is the amount of dollars a person receives, while real income is the amount of goods and services a person can buy with his money income.\nF. Money income is the number of physical currency units earned, while real income is the value of assets owned.\nG. Money income is the goods a person can buy, while real income is the amount of dollars a person receives.\nH. Money income is the face value of financial investments, while real income is the dividends and interest from those investments.\nI. Money income is the gross domestic product per capita, while real income is the purchasing power parity per capita.\nJ. Money income is the nominal wage rate, while real income is the wage rate adjusted for inflation.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1248, "output_tokens": 244, "total_tokens": 1492}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5938", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How did Joseph Schumpeter distinguish the innovatorfrom the inventor? On which did he base his theory of the business cycle?\n\nOptions: \nA. Innovators invest in inventions and introduce them into industry\nB. Inventors create new products, while innovators improve existing ones\nC. Inventors invest in new inventions\nD. Innovators replicate existing inventions without modification\nE. Innovators make new discoveries\nF. Innovators primarily focus on scientific research\nG. Innovators don't take financial risks\nH. Innovators are solely responsible for funding inventions\nI. Inventors are the ones who commercialize new products\nJ. Inventors develop new ideas, while innovators are responsible for marketing\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 828, "output_tokens": 327, "total_tokens": 1155}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5712", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 2004 the United States had a trade deficit of $603 billion; therefore\n\nOptions: \nA. The value of the dollar increased significantly.\nB. The United States' GDP decreased by $603 billion.\nC. The United States imported exactly $603 billion worth of goods.\nD. The United States had a trade surplus.\nE. Americans consumed more than they produced.\nF. net exports were positive.\nG. America's government spent more than it took in.\nH. The United States exported more goods than it imported.\nI. $603 billion worth of capital flowed out of America.\nJ. The United States was the world's largest exporter.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 845, "output_tokens": 309, "total_tokens": 1154}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6124", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is meant by \"fractional reserve\" banking?\n\nOptions: \nA. Fractional reserve banking is the practice where banks lend out a portion of their deposits while keeping a fraction in the form of gold reserves.\nB. Fractional reserve banking permits banks to keep a varying reserve ratio depending on the size of the deposit.\nC. Fractional reserve banking is when banks are required to keep 100% of their deposits in cash.\nD. Fractional reserve banking means that banks keep all of their deposits in cash.\nE. Fractional reserve banking refers to the practice of banks lending out all their deposits.\nF. Fractional reserve banking is a system where banks are required to keep only a fraction of their deposits in liquid form and can invest the remainder in government bonds only.\nG. Fractional reserve banking means that banks keep less than 100% of their deposits in cash, placing the rest in income-earning investments.\nH. Fractional reserve banking allows banks to lend out exactly 50% of their deposits and requires them to hold the other 50% in reserve.\nI. Fractional reserve banking mandates that banks hold a fixed reserve of 20% of their deposits and are free to use the rest without restrictions.\nJ. Fractional reserve banking is the system in which banks are allowed to issue loans equal to the amount of deposits they have, without maintaining any reserves.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1392, "output_tokens": 349, "total_tokens": 1741}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6014", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the difference between a homogeneous and a differentiated oligopoly?\n\nOptions: \nA. In a homogeneous oligopoly, firms set prices jointly, while in a differentiated oligopoly, each firm sets its own price.\nB. In a homogeneous oligopoly, product differentiation is the key to success, while in a differentiated oligopoly, firms succeed through economies of scale.\nC. In a homogeneous oligopoly, the firms produce similar products, while in differentiated oligopolies, products are completely different.\nD. In a homogeneous oligopoly, there are many producers of identical products, while in a differentiated oligopoly, there are only a few producers with unique products.\nE. In a homogeneous oligopoly, the firms produce standardized products, while in differentiated oligopolies, products are no longer perceived by the consumer as being the same.\nF. In a homogeneous oligopoly, firms rely on marketing strategies to sell their products, while in a differentiated oligopoly, firms compete on product quality alone.\nG. In a homogeneous oligopoly, the firms produce different products, while in differentiated oligopolies, products are identical.\nH. In a homogeneous oligopoly, firms compete on price alone, while in a differentiated oligopoly, firms compete primarily on product features.\nI. In a homogeneous oligopoly, products are differentiated, while in a differentiated oligopoly, products are standardized.\nJ. In a homogeneous oligopoly, the market consists of a single seller, while in a differentiated oligopoly, there are multiple sellers offering similar products.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1472, "output_tokens": 295, "total_tokens": 1767}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5978", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An import quota on foreign automobiles is expected to\n\nOptions: \nA. increase the price of automobiles and protect domestic producers at the expense of consumers.\nB. decrease the price of automobiles and protect foreign producers at the expense of consumers.\nC. increase the price of automobiles and protect foreign producers at the expense of domestic producers.\nD. increase the price of automobiles and protect domestic consumers at the expense of domestic producers.\nE. increase domestic efficiency and protect foreign producers at the expense of domestic consumers.\nF. increase domestic efficiency and protect domestic producers at the expense of foreign producers.\nG. decrease the price of automobiles and protect domestic consumers at the expense of foreign producers.\nH. decrease domestic efficiency and protect domestic consumers at the expense of foreign producers.\nI. decrease domestic efficiency and protect foreign producers at the expense of domestic producers.\nJ. decrease the price of automobiles and protect domestic producers at the expense of consumers.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 980, "output_tokens": 222, "total_tokens": 1202}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6273", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the difference between gross national product and national income?\n\nOptions: \nA. GNP is the total income of a nation, while NI is the total income earned by individuals\nB. GNP is the value of all goods and services produced in a year, while NI is the total income earned by those who contribute to current production, after deductions for indirect taxes, depreciation and the use of capital.\nC. GNP includes only the income earned within a country's borders, while NI includes income from abroad\nD. GNP is the value of all finished products produced by a country, while NI is the value of all raw materials produced by a country\nE. GNP is the total income from domestic and foreign sources, while NI is the total income generated exclusively from foreign investments\nF. GNP is the market value of all final goods and services produced by a country's residents, while NI is the sum of all wages, profits, and rents earned by a country's residents\nG. GNP measures the economic output, while NI measures the economic input\nH. GNP is the sum of all governmental spending, while NI is the sum of all consumer spending\nI. GNP is the total income earned by a nation's corporations, while NI includes only the income earned by its citizens\nJ. GNP is the total export value, while NI is the total import value\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1384, "output_tokens": 350, "total_tokens": 1734}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5627", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Whatare the differencebetween Marginal Fixed Cost (MFC), Marginal Variable Cost (MVC) and Marginal Total Cost (MC)?\n\nOptions: \nA. MFC = 0, MVC = MC\nB. MFC decreases as output increases, MVC = 0\nC. MFC = MVC, MC increases as output decreases\nD. MFC = MC, MVC increases with each additional unit produced\nE. MFC = MC, MVC = 0\nF. MFC increases as output increases, MVC = MC\nG. MFC = MVC = MC\nH. MFC = 0, MVC increases with each additional unit produced, MC = MFC + MVC\nI. MFC > MVC, MC = MFC + MVC\nJ. MFC = MVC, MC = 0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 932, "output_tokens": 308, "total_tokens": 1240}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5909", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Having a fractional reserve banking system means that\n\nOptions: \nA. the central bank holds a certain fraction of the bank's deposits on reserve at all times\nB. a bank cannot lend out all of its deposits\nC. the bank must hold a certain percentage of its deposits in reserve at all times\nD. the central bank holds a certain fraction of GDP on reserve at all times\nE. the central bank reserves the right to set the interest rate on any loan at any time.\nF. a bank can lend out all of its deposits but must maintain a certain level of reserves\nG. all loans must be backed by an equivalent amount of reserves\nH. no single loan can be larger than 20 percent of the bank\u2019s holdings\nI. a bank can only lend out a fixed percentage of its deposits\nJ. the central bank reserves the right to audit any bank at any time\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 984, "output_tokens": 266, "total_tokens": 1250}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6172", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An externality\n\nOptions: \nA. results in a deficit of goods in the market\nB. results in a surplus of goods in the market\nC. exists when the equilibrium price is exactly equal to the market price\nD. exists when markets cannot reach equilibrium\nE. causes the equilibrium price to be artificially low\nF. causes the equilibrium price to be artificially high\nG. results in an equilibrium that does not maximize the total benefit to society\nH. causes a shift in the demand curve to the left\nI. causes the equilibrium quantity to exceed the market quantity\nJ. causes a shift in the supply curve to the right\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 776, "output_tokens": 274, "total_tok