n makes Chris a better worker, voter, parent, and citizen. Because the benefits from education go beyond those that Chris enjoys himself, education provides\n\nOptions: \nA. no externalities and should not be subsidized\nB. decreasing marginal utility and should be taxed\nC. increasing marginal utility and should be subsidized\nD. increasing marginal utility and should not be subsidized\nE. externalities and should be taxed\nF. externalities and should not be subsidized\nG. externalities and should be subsidized\nH. increasing marginal utility and should be taxed\nI. no externalities and should be subsidized\nJ. decreasing marginal utility and should not be taxed\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 788, "output_tokens": 303, "total_tokens": 1091}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6393", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many parameters will be required to be estimated in total for all equations of a standard form, unrestricted, tri-variate VAR(4), ignoring the intercepts?\n\nOptions: \nA. 6\nB. 9\nC. 16\nD. 12\nE. 4\nF. 3\nG. 48\nH. 24\nI. 36\nJ. 18\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 620, "output_tokens": 348, "total_tokens": 968}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6325", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Miss Lane had the following income tax information in 1978 while she worked as a reporter on a large metropolitan news paper: Taxable income $15,000 Exemptions 1,500 Business Expenses 6,000 Non business Expenses 3,000 Find Miss Lane's adjusted gross income and gross income for 1978.\n\nOptions: \nA. Adjusted Gross Income: $19,500, Gross Income: $25,500\nB. Adjusted Gross Income: $8,500, Gross Income: $23,500\nC. Adjusted Gross Income: $20,000, Gross Income: $25,000\nD. Adjusted Gross Income: $9,000, Gross Income: $21,000\nE. Adjusted Gross Income: $16,500, Gross Income: $28,500\nF. Adjusted Gross Income: $12,000, Gross Income: $27,000\nG. Adjusted Gross Income: $11,500, Gross Income: $22,500\nH. Adjusted Gross Income: $10,500, Gross Income: $20,500\nI. Adjusted Gross Income: $19,000, Gross Income: $26,000\nJ. Adjusted Gross Income: $18,500, Gross Income: $24,500\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Miss Lane's taxable income is computed as adjusted gross income (AGI) minus exemptions and non-business deductions, so AGI = $15,000 + $1,500 + $3,000 = $19,500. Gross income is then AGI plus business expenses, giving $19,500 + $6,000 = $25,500. This matches option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1935, "output_tokens": 1431, "total_tokens": 3366}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6247", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider a series that follows an MA(1) with zero mean and a moving average coefficient of 0.4. What is the value of the autocovariance at lag 1?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1\nB. 2\nC. -0.4\nD. The autocovariance at lag 1 is undefined for an MA(1) series.\nE. 0.2\nF. 0.4\nG. The autocovariance at lag 1 is always equal to the moving average coefficient.\nH. 0.34\nI. 0.6\nJ. It is not possible to determine the value of the autocovariances without knowing the disturbance variance.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 844, "output_tokens": 524, "total_tokens": 1368}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5966", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To close an expansionary gap\n\nOptions: \nA. the aggregate demand curve should not be shifted.\nB. the aggregate demand curve should be shifted to the right.\nC. the aggregate supply curve should be shifted to the left.\nD. both the aggregate demand and supply curves should not be shifted.\nE. the aggregate supply curve should be shifted to the right, and the aggregate demand curve to the left.\nF. the aggregate supply curve should be shifted to the right.\nG. the aggregate demand curve should be shifted to the left.\nH. both the aggregate demand and supply curves should be shifted to the left.\nI. the aggregate supply curve should not be shifted.\nJ. both the aggregate demand and supply curves should be shifted to the right.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 860, "output_tokens": 242, "total_tokens": 1102}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5873", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of the following would be a plausible response to a finding of residual non-normality?\n\nOptions: \nA. Use a logarithmic functional form instead of a linear one\nB. Add lags of the variables on the right hand side of the regression model\nC. Estimate the model in first differenced form\nD. Remove any large outliers from the data.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 552, "output_tokens": 328, "total_tokens": 880}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5709", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If XYZ Corporation buys an original Matisse painting to hang in its board room then\n\nOptions: \nA. GDP increases because the painting is considered a luxury good.\nB. GDP is unaffected because it is a second hand sale.\nC. GDP is unaffected because the painting is considered a non-monetary asset.\nD. GI)P decreases because I decreases.\nE. GDP is unaffected because the painting is considered a depreciating asset.\nF. GDP increases because it is considered an investment in art.\nG. GDP decreases by the amount of the purchase because C decreases.\nH. GDP decreases because the painting is considered an unproductive asset.\nI. GDP decreases by the amount of the purchase because G decreases.\nJ. GDP increases by the amount of the purchase because I increases.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 880, "output_tokens": 268, "total_tokens": 1148}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5803", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For a competitive firm, what is the most important thing to consider in deciding whether to shut down in the short run?\n\nOptions: \nA. Do not produce if the TFC is not covered by revenue.\nB. Do not produce if the price is lower than AVC.\nC. Compare AVC to MR.\nD. Compare AFC to MR.\nE. Shut down if the firm is not making a profit.\nF. Do not produce if the TVC is not covered by revenue.\nG. Compare the price of inputs to the price of the product.\nH. Compare TR to TC.\nI. Produce the highest quantity demanded regardless of price.\nJ. Produce as long as the price is higher than AVC.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 838, "output_tokens": 293, "total_tokens": 1131}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5664", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If a series, y, follows a random walk with drift b, what is the optimal one-step ahead forecast of the change in y?\n\nOptions: \nA. The current value of y\nB. The sum of all changes in y over the in-sample period divided by the number of changes\nC. The average value of the change in y over the in-sample period\nD. The current value of y minus the drift b\nE. One\nF. Zero\nG. The median value of the change in y over the in-sample period\nH. The current value of y plus the drift b\nI. The maximum value of the change in y over the in-sample period\nJ. The minimum value of the change in y over the in-sample period\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 876, "output_tokens": 661, "total_tokens": 1537}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5813", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If a series, y, follows a random walk, what is the optimal one-step ahead forecast of y?\n\nOptions: \nA. The current value of y\nB. The median value of y over th