tions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose that we are interested in testing the null hypothesis that a GARCH(2,2) model can be restricted to a process with a constant conditional variance using the likelihood ratio test approach. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nOptions: \nA. The test statistic will follow a chi-squared distribution with 2 degrees of freedom under the null hypothesis\nB. The value of the log-likelihood function will almost always be bigger for the restricted model than for the unrestricted model\nC. If the relevant values of the log-likelihood functions are -112.3 and -118.4, the value of the test statistic is 12.2\nD. The likelihood ratio test compares the slopes of the log-likelihood function at the maximum and at the restricted parameter value.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 900, "output_tokens": 753, "total_tokens": 1653}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6246", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider the following AR(2) process:\n\nyt = 1.5 yt-1 - 0.5 yt-2 + ut\n\nThis is a\n\nOptions: \nA. Non-stationary and unit root process\nB. Unit root process\nC. Explosive process\nD. Unit root and explosive process\nE. Stationary and unit root process\nF. Non-stationary and explosive process\nG. Both stationary and explosive process\nH. Non-stationary process\nI. Neither stationary, unit root, nor explosive process\nJ. Stationary process\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 732, "output_tokens": 847, "total_tokens": 1579}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6058", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements are true concerning the Box-Jenkins approach to diagnostic testing for ARMA models?\n\n(i) The tests will show whether the identified model is either too large or too small\n\n(ii) The tests involve checking the model residuals for autocorrelation, heteroscedasticity, and non-normality\n\n(iii) If the model suggested at the identification stage is appropriate, the acf and pacf for the residuals should show no additional structure\n\n(iv) If the model suggested at the identification stage is appropriate, the coefficients on the additional variables under the overfitting approach will be statistically insignificant\n\nOptions: \nA. (iii) and (iv) only\nB. (i) and (iii) only\nC. (i), (iii), and (iv) only\nD. (i), (ii), and (iii) only\nE. (ii) and (iii) only\nF. (i) and (iv) only\nG. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv)\nH. (ii) and (iv) only\nI. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nJ. (i) and (ii) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1248, "output_tokens": 559, "total_tokens": 1807}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6214", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What were some causes of the stagflation in the early 1970' s?\n\nOptions: \nA. Decrease in unemployment\nB. Rapid acceleration of price level, oil price increases, perversely working tax systems, and macroeconomic policy mistakes\nC. Lowering of oil prices\nD. Expansion of international trade without barriers\nE. Increase in the gold standard value\nF. Excessive production of goods\nG. Advancements in technology reducing costs\nH. Stabilization of currency exchange rates\nI. Economic expansion\nJ. Reduction in government spending\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 728, "output_tokens": 303, "total_tokens": 1031}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6114", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider the following equation and determine the class of model that it best represents\n\n$y_{{it}} = \\alpha + \\beta_{{it}} + \\mu_i + \\nu_{{it}}$\n\nOptions: \nA. A pure time series model\nB. A difference-in-differences model\nC. A random effects model\nD. A pooled OLS model\nE. A mixed effects model\nF. A spatial autocorrelation model\nG. A quantile regression model\nH. A panel data model\nI. An entity fixed effects model\nJ. A time fixed effects model\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 763, "output_tokens": 353, "total_tokens": 1116}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5739", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements are true concerning the standardised residuals (residuals divided by their respective conditional standard deviations) from an estimated GARCH model?\n\ni) They are assumed to be normally distributed\n\n\nii) Their squares will be related to their lagged squared values if the GARCH model is\n\nappropriate\n\n\niii) In practice, they are likely to have fat tails\n\n\niv) If the GARCH model is adequate, the standardised residuals and the raw residuals\n\nwill be identical\n\nOptions: \nA. (i), (ii), and (iii) only\nB. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv)\nC. (iii) and (iv) only\nD. (i) and (iv) only\nE. (i) and (iii) only\nF. (i), (iii), and (iv) only\nG. (ii) and (iv) only\nH. (i) and (ii) only\nI. (ii) and (iii) only\nJ. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1152, "output_tokens": 371, "total_tokens": 1523}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6057", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose that the value of $R^2$ for an estimated regression model is exactly zero. Which of the following are true?\n\ni) All coefficient estimates on the slopes will be zero\n\nii) The fitted line will be horizontal with respect to all of the explanatory variables\n\niii) The regression line has not explained any of the variability of y about its mean value\n\niv) The intercept coefficient estimate must be zero.\n\nOptions: \nA. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv)\nB. (i) and (ii) only\nC. (i) and (iii) only\nD. (iii) and (iv) only\nE. (ii) and (iii) only\nF. (ii) and (iv) only\nG. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nH. (i) and (iv) only\nI. (i), (iii), and (iv) only\nJ. (i), (ii), and (iii) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "When \\( R^2 = 0 \\), the regression model explains none of the variability of \\( y \\) around its mean, so (iii) is true. A zero \\( R^2 \\) implies the fitted values are all equal to the mean of \\( y \\), meaning all slope coefficients are zero and the fitted line is horizontal with respect to every explanatory variable, making (i) and (ii) true. However, the intercept can be nonzero (it equals the mean of \\( y \\)), so (iv) is false.  \n\n\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1361, "output_tokens": 982, "total_tokens": 2343}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5619", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why is it that interest payments on government bonds are not included as income currently earned, particularly, when interest on the bonds of private firms is included in na-tional income as earned income?\n\nOptions: \nA. Interest on government bonds is classified as a loan repayment rather than income\nB. Interest on government bonds is reinvested and not paid out\nC. Interest on government bonds is tax-free\nD. Interest payments are deferred to the maturity of the bonds\nE. Interest paid on such debt does not reflect the generation of any current output or income\nF. Government bonds are typically held by foreign investors, and their interest is not counted in domestic income\nG. The interest on government bonds is counted as part of the budget deficit, not national income\nH. Interest on government bonds is considered a transfer payment within the public sector\nI. Government bonds are not considered as income\nJ. Government bonds are not part of the national income\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1024, "output_tokens": 302, "total_tokens": 1326}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5741", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following assumptions are required to show the consistency, unbiasedness and efficiency of the OLS estimator?\n\ni) $E(u_t) = 0$\n\n\nii) $\\text{{Var}}(u_t) = \\sigma^2$\n\n\niii) $\\text{{Cov}}(u_t, u_{{t-j}}) = 0 \\forall j$\n\n\niv) $u_t \\sim N(0, \\sigma^2)$\n\nOptions: \nA. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv)\nB. (i), (iii), and (iv) only\nC. (ii) and (iv) only\nD. (i), (ii), and (iii) only\nE. (ii) and (iii) only\nF. (i) and (ii) only\nG. (iii) and (iv) only\nH. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nI. (i) and (iv) only\nJ. (i) and (iii) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1140, "output_tokens": 300, "total_tokens": 1440}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6186", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following are plausible approaches to dealing with a model that exhibits heteroscedasticity?\n\ni) Take logarithms of each of the variables\n\nii) Use suitably modified standard errors\n\niii) Use a generalised least squares procedure\n\niv) Add lagged values of the variables to the regression equation.\n\nOptions: \nA. (iii) and (iv) only\nB. (i), (iii), and (iv) only\nC. (i), (ii), and (iv) only\nD. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nE. (i) and (ii) only\nF. (i) and (iv) only\nG. (i) and (iii) only\nH. (ii) and (iv) only\nI. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv)\nJ. (i), (ii), and (iii) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1024, "output_tokens": 359, "total_tokens": 1383}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6327", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How is the federal payroll tax that supports the Social Security program a regressive tax?\n\nOptions: \nA. The tax is regressive because only self-employed individuals are required to pay it.\nB. The tax is regressive because all workers pay the same percentage of their income.\nC. The tax is regressive because higher incomes are taxed at a higher rate.\nD. The tax is regressive because it only applies to the first $10,000 of income.\nE. The tax is regressive because it exempts all investment income.\nF. The tax is regressive because it includes additional deductions for higher income earners.\nG. The tax is regressive because there is a dollar limit on the amount of income, subject to the tax.\nH. The tax is regressive because lower incomes are not taxed to provide relief to lower earners.\nI. The tax is regressive because it is only applied to non-wage forms of income.\nJ. The tax is regressive because it is a flat tax that takes a smaller proportion of income as the income rises.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1120, "output_tokens": 343, "total_tokens": 1463}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5996", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following criticisms of standard (\"plain vanilla\") GARCH models can be overcome by EGARCH models?\n\ni) Estimated coefficient values from GARCH models may be negative\n\nii) GARCH models cannot account for leverage effects\n\niii) The responsiveness of future volatility to positive and negative shocks is symmetric under a GARCH formulation\n\niv) GARCH models cannot allow for a feedback from the volatility to the returns\n\nOptions: \nA. (iii) and (iv) only\nB. (i), (iii), and (iv) only\nC. (i) and (iii) only\nD. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nE. (i), (ii), and (iii) only\nF. (ii) and (iv) only\nG. (ii) and (iii) only\nH. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv)\nI. (i) and (iv) only\nJ. (i) and (ii) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1088, "output_tokens": 414, "total_tokens": 1502}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5593", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What could the government do to most effectively avoid a free rider problem?\n\nOptions: \nA. Supply public goods using tax dollars\nB. Initiate a lottery system for the usage of public goods\nC. Enact stricter antitrust legislation\nD. Increase the prices of public goods\nE. Allow private companies to supply public goods\nF. Tax those creating negative externalities\nG. Ban the use of public goods\nH. Provide more complete information about the relevant goods\nI. Reduce the production of public goods\nJ. Encourage voluntary contributions for public goods\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 716, "output_tokens": 269, "total_tokens": 985}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5594", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements are true concerning information criteria?\n\n(i) Adjusted R-squared is an information criterion\n\n(ii) If the residual sum of squares falls when an additional term is added, the value of the information criterion will fall\n\n(iii) Akaike's information criterion always leads to model orders that are at least as large as those of Schwarz's information criterion\n\n(iv) Akaike's information criterion is consistent\n\nOptions: \nA. (ii) and (iv) only\nB. (ii) and (iii) only\nC. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv)\nD. (i) and (iv) only\nE. (i) and (iii) only\nF. (i), (iii), and (iv) only\nG. (i) and (ii) only\nH. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nI. (iii) and (iv) only\nJ. (i), (ii), and (iii) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1104, "output_tokens": 454, "total_tokens": 1558}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5602", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"Allowing the prices of goods to rise in periods when none of the good is being produced is immoral, because the higher prices do not induce a larger output. They merely give unwarranted profits to those who are lucky enough to own the goods. Either prices should be prevented from rising or the government should take over ownership in order to prevent unjust enrichment quotas.\"Do you agree withthis analysis ?If so, why?If not, why not?\n\nOptions: \nA. Disagree due to higher price permitting a re-allocation of existing goods\nB. Agree due to unjust enrichment\nC. Agree due to unwarranted profits\nD. Disagree due to government interference\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 804, "output_tokens": 264, "total_tokens": 1068}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5663", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of the following factors is likely to lead to a relatively high degree of out-of-sample forecast accuracy?\n\nOptions: \nA. A model that contains many variables\nB. A model that is based on financial theory\nC. A model whose dependent variable has recently exhibited a structural change\nD. A model that heavily relies on subjective judgment\nE. A model that does not consider economic indicators\nF. A model that is entirely statistical in nature with no room for judgmental modification of forecasts\nG. A model that is based on a single variable\nH. A model that predicts based on historical trends only\nI. A model with a high degree of complexity\nJ. A model that ignores market volatility\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 832, "output_tokens": 285, "total_tokens": 1117}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6051", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of the following is a disadvantage of the general to specific or \"LSE\" (\"Hendry\") approach to building econometric models, relative to the specific to general approach?\n\nOptions: \nA. Some variables may be excluded at the first stage leading to coefficient biases\nB. The final model may lack theoretical interpretation\nC. The final model may be statistically inadequate\nD. If the initial model is mis-specified, all subsequent steps will be invalid.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 632, "output_tokens": 362, "total_tokens": 994}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6063", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"Economic theory is applicable only to a capitalist society.\" Evaluate.\n\nOptions: \nA. Economic theory is applicable to any system of competition\nB. Economic theory cannot be applied to socialist societies\nC. Economic theory is irrelevant to communist systems\nD. Economic theory is only applicable to capitalist systems\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 496, "output_tokens": 269, "total_tokens": 765}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6100", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following fiscal policy combinations would be most likely to slowly increase real GDP without putting tremendous upward pressure on the price level?\n\nOptions: \nA. Increase government spending with no change in taxes.\nB. Increase government spending with a matching decrease in taxes.\nC. Increase taxes with a decrease in government spending.\nD. Decrease government spending with no change in taxes.\nE. Decrease taxes with no change in government spending.\nF. No change in taxes with a decrease in government spending.\nG. Decrease government spending with a matching increase in taxes.\nH. No change in government spending with an increase in taxes.\nI. Increase taxes with a matching increase in government spending.\nJ. Decrease taxes with a matching increase in government spending.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 856, "output_tokens": 337, "total_tokens": 1193}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6113", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements are true concerning the acf and pacf?\n\n(i) The acf and pacf are often hard to interpret in practice\n\n(ii) The acf and pacf can be difficult to calculate for some data sets\n\n(iii) Information criteria represent an alternative approach to model order determination\n\n(iv) If applied correctly, the acf and pacf will always deliver unique model selections\n\nOptions: \nA. (i) and (ii) only\nB. (i) and (iii) only\nC. (iii) and (iv) only\nD. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nE. (ii) and (iii) only\nF. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv)\nG. (i), (iii), and (iv) only\nH. (i) and (iv) only\nI. (ii) and (iv) only\nJ. (i), (ii), and (iii) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1084, "output_tokens": 490, "total_tokens": 1574}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6118", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose that 100 separate firms were tested to determine how many of them \"beat the market\" using a Jensen-type regression, and it is found that 3 fund managers significantly do so. Does this suggest prima facie evidence for stock market inefficiency?\n\nOptions: \nA. The results would be different if a different type of regression was used\nB. This suggests evidence for stock market efficiency, not inefficiency\nC. Yes\nD. In order to answer this question, you would need to test every fund manager trading in that market\nE. There is insufficient information given in the question to draw a conclusion about market efficiency.\nF. No\nG. The results are inconclusive without knowing the performance of the market as a whole\nH. It's impossible to draw conclusions based on the performance of only 100 firms\nI. This indicates that the majority of fund managers do not significantly beat the market\nJ. This suggests that only a small percentage of fund managers can beat the market\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1076, "output_tokens": 297, "total_tokens": 1373}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6135", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Adam Smith could count on self-interest to spur businessmen to greater efficiency. Now, with the rise of large corpora-tions , can modern economists also count on self-interest to produce efficiency?\n\nOptions: \nA. Self-interest always leads to efficiency in business\nB. Self-interest is only relevant in small businesses, not in large corporations\nC. Modern economists don't consider self-interest in their analysis\nD. Yes, modern economists can count on self-interest to produce efficiency\nE. Self-interest among modern businessmen is replaced by corporate social responsibility\nF. Modern economists rely solely on government regulation to ensure efficiency\nG. No, modern economists cannot count on self-interest to produce efficiency\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 804, "output_tokens": 275, "total_tokens": 1079}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6249", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If a rich country and a poor country trade with each other, without any restrictions, and the rich country gains $50 million, while the poor country only gains $5 million, is the rich country exploiting the poor country?\n\nOptions: \nA. Exploitation cannot be determined solely based on monetary gains.\nB. The concept of exploitation does not apply to international trade.\nC. The rich country is not exploiting the poor country.\nD. Both countries benefit equally in terms of percentage growth.\nE. The trade terms are fair, and no exploitation occurs.\nF. The poor country is benefiting more, considering the relative size of its economy.\nG. The poor country is exploiting the rich country.\nH. The gain is not significant enough to determine exploitation.\nI. Both countries are exploiting each other.\nJ. The rich country is exploiting the poor country.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 944, "output_tokens": 287, "total_tokens": 1231}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6274", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How can the debt management of the U.S. Treasury contrib-uteto economic stabilization?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Treasury must not issue any debt during a recession or inflation.\nB. The Treasury should only issue debt during periods of economic surplus to prepare for future recessions.\nC. The Treasury must issue short-term debt during a recession and long-term debt during high inflation.\nD. The Treasury must issue more currency rather than debt to manage economic cycles.\nE. The Treasury must issue equal amounts of short-term and long-term debts at all times.\nF. The Treasury must issue long-term debt during a recession and short-term debt during high inflation.\nG. The Treasury must issue inflation-indexed bonds primarily during periods of stable economic growth.\nH. The Treasury must issue debt exclusively to foreign investors during economic downturns.\nI. The Treasury must continuously decrease the national debt to stabilize the economy.\nJ. The Treasury should prioritize foreign debt issuance to manage domestic economic stability.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1032, "output_tokens": 276, "total_tokens": 1308}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6339", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Neoclassical economists developed a production function in which all the factors of production (land, capital, labor) received the value of their marginal product; that is, the interest paid to capital equals the contribution capital makes to the product, wages paid to labor equals the value of the marginal product of labor, etc. Some economists suggested that this result showed that the distribution of free, competitive capitalism is morally right and just. Whatis wrong with this suggestion?\n\nOptions: \nA. Assumes that ownership of resources means the owner is entitled to all the benefits\nB. It underestimates the value of labor\nC. It overlooks the historical and social factors that affect the distribution of resources\nD. It assumes perfect competition and complete information, which are rarely present in real markets\nE. It ignores the potential for market power to influence the distribution of income\nF. It assumes that the market always operates efficiently without any externalities\nG. It overvalues the contribution of capital\nH. It contradicts the socialist view\nI. It does not take into account the role of government intervention in the economy\nJ. It implies that income derived from inheritance or monopolies is also morally justified\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1220, "output_tokens": 354, "total_tokens": 1574}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6395", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Is the achievement of full employment sufficient for the maintenance of growth?\n\nOptions: \nA. Growth only depends on full employment\nB. Yes, full employment guarantees growth\nC. Full employment always leads to increasing per capita output\nD. No, full employment is not sufficient for the maintenance of growth\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 496, "output_tokens": 265, "total_tokens": 761}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6402", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Marx prided himself on his 'scientific' analysis of capital-ism. Through this analysis, he felt he had proved how the problemsfacing the nineteenth century were intimately re-latedto the capitalist mode of production. Modern radical economistshold the similar view that the problems of modernWestern society are inherent in capitalist production. Give the orthodox rebuttal to this viewpoint.\n\nOptions: \nA. Elimination of capitalism can resolve all societal problems.\nB. Many non-capitalist societies suffer from the same problems as Western, capitalist countries.\nC. The capitalist mode of production is the only system that has consistently reduced poverty worldwide.\nD. Problems in Western society are solely due to individual moral failures, not the economic system.\nE. Capitalism naturally corrects any societal problems through market forces without the need for intervention.\nF. Non-Western capitalist societies do not encounter any social or economic problems.\nG. Capitalism is the sole cause of problems in modern Western society.\nH. The problems of modern Western society are a result of technological advancement, not the capitalist production mode.\nI. Only capitalist societies face issues such as exploitation, pollution, and economic inequality.\nJ. Capitalist societies have the best track record for solving social and economic problems.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1248, "output_tokens": 312, "total_tokens": 1560}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_law_1065", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mary, a wealthy St. Petersburg widow, executed her first and only will on May 15, 1990 and died on August 18, 1990. Her will provided that her estate be divided equally between her only child, Joan, and the Salvation Army of Largo. How will Mary's estate actually be distributed?\n\nOptions: \nA. 50% to Joan and the income from the remaining 50% to Joan for life, remainder to the Salvation Army, if Joan files a timely petition protesting the devise to the Salvation Army.\nB. The estate is divided equally between Joan and the Salvation Army, but Joan has the option to reject her share.\nC. 50% to Joan and the income from the remaining 50% to the Salvation Army for life, remainder to Joan.\nD. 100% to Joan if she files a timely petition requesting that the devise to the Salvation Army be avoided.\nE. The estate is held in trust with Joan as the beneficiary during her lifetime, then transferred to the Salvation Army upon her death.\nF. 50% to Joan and 50% to the Salvation Army.\nG. 100% to Joan.\nH. 100% to the Salvation Army.\nI. 75% to Joan and 25% to the Salvation Army.\nJ. 25% to Joan and 75% to the Salvation Army.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1456, "output_tokens": 424, "total_tokens": 1880}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_law_1101", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the meaning of cultural relativism?\n\nOptions: \nA. Cultural relativism posits that the application of human rights is relative to the laws in each nation\nB. Cultural relativism posits that laws in each nation should validate the existence and practice of human rights\nC. Cultural relativism posits that human rights are determined by global consensus\nD. Culture relativism posits that human rights have a cultural origin\nE. Cultural relativism posits that all cultures are objectively equal in value\nF. Cultural relativism posits that human rights should be universally the same in every culture\nG. Cultural relativism posits that human rights are determined by religious beliefs\nH. Culture relativism posits that human rights apply equally to all without restrictions\nI. Cultural relativism posits that the validity of human rights depends on individual beliefs\nJ. Cultural relativism posits that local culture should validate the existence and practice of all human rights\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1028, "output_tokens": 366, "total_tokens": 1394}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_law_813", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Was the use of armed force permitted prior to the United Nations Charter?\n\nOptions: \nA. Armed force was only permitted in self-defense\nB. Armed force was permitted with many restrictions\nC. Armed force was not regulated under international law prior to 1945\nD. Armed force was permitted but required approval from an international body\nE. Armed force was prohibited\nF. Armed force was permitted but required approval from the countries involved\nG. Armed force was permitted subject to few restrictions\nH. Armed force was permitted with no restrictions\nI. Armed force was permitted with the consent of all nations\nJ. Armed force was not permitted under any circumstances\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 796, "output_tokens": 399, "total_tokens": 1195}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_law_1246", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A wedding planner owned a summer cottage on the lake. In order to facilitate the access to the cottage, which is located on a knoll above the lake, the wedding planner entered into an agreement with a neighbor, an adjoining land owner, whereby the neighbor, in writing, granted the wedding planner a right-of-way over a strip of land 30 feet in width and a quarter of a mile in length along the eastern margin of the neighbor's property. Without notif'ing the neighbor, the wedding planner proceeded with his plan to improve the roadbed by having the road asphalted in order to make it more accessible for motor vehicle traffic. Several years later, the neighbor started a sand business, which required him to do heavy hauling that subsequently destroyed the asphalted surface on the road. Ten years after the neighbor started his sand business, the wedding planner sold his lakefront property to an artist. Shortly after the artist took possession of the cottage and property, the neighbor erected wooden barriers across the roadway, thus obstructing the access to the artist's property. The interest that the wedding planner acquired in the access road may best be described as\n\nOptions: \nA. an easement by estoppel.\nB. an easement of light and air.\nC. a prescriptive easement.\nD. an express easement.\nE. a profit a prendre.\nF. an easement by necessity.\nG. an easement implied by prior use.\nH. a license.\nI. an easement of support.\nJ. an easement in gross.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1504, "output_tokens": 314, "total_tokens": 1818}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_law_1186", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Bill purchased a can of Sipep from the Ajax Minimart. After he finished drinking the Sipep, Bill noticed that the can contained dead insects stuck on the inside bottom of the can. In a strict product liability tort action against Ajax, Bill must prove, among other things, that:\n\nOptions: \nA. Ajax is a merchant selling Sipep.\nB. Ajax knew or should have known of the defective condition\nC. Ajax had prior notice of other similar problems with Sipep products.\nD. Ajax actually placed the dead insects into the can.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 716, "output_tokens": 331, "total_tokens": 1047}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_law_1531", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a derogation?\n\nOptions: \nA. A State may suspend particular rights by means of a derogation in circumstances that threaten its existence\nB. A derogation is a process whereby a state can amend a treaty\nC. Derogations are enforcement clauses in human rights treaties\nD. A derogation is a mechanism that allows a state to temporarily suspend its obligations under a treaty in times of peace\nE. A derogation refers to the ability of rights holders to bring a claim against the State for breach of an obligation\nF. Derogations are clauses in human rights treaties that outline the penalties for non-compliance\nG. Derogations refer to the responsibility of a state to ensure the protection of human rights within its territory\nH. Derogations are clauses in treaties that allow a state to withdraw from the treaty\nI. A derogation is a legal term for a state's refusal to comply with a treaty\nJ. Derogations are exemptions from particular human rights obligations contained in a treaty\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1084, "output_tokens": 312, "total_tokens": 1396}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_law_966", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Do third States enjoy any fishing rights within the Exclusive Economic Zone of another State?\n\nOptions: \nA. Third States may never have access to fisheries within another State's EEZ\nB. Third States are free to fish within another EEZ, except from certain designated areas\nC. When the coastal State cannot harvest the 'total allowable catch', the coastal State is to give other State access to that surplus with priority to be given to developing and land-locked States\nD. The coastal State must share all of its fish resources with all other States\nE. Third States have access to fisheries within its EEZ only during a specific season\nF. The coastal State is to give access to fisheries within its EEZ only to States with which it has diplomatic relations\nG. Third States have unlimited fishing rights within the EEZ of any State\nH. Third States can only fish within another State's EEZ with a special permit\nI. The coastal State is to give access to fisheries within its EEZ only to neighbouring States\nJ. Third States can only fish within another State's EEZ if they have a mutual agreement\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1164, "output_tokens": 324, "total_tokens": 1488}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_law_894", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is personal (ratione personae) immunity?\n\nOptions: \nA. Personal immunity is given to individuals for their private conduct, not their public conduct\nB. Personal immunity is afforded to all physical persons\nC. Personal immunity is afforded to all State officials, regardless of their conduct\nD. Personal immunity is only given to individuals who have committed a crime in a public capacity\nE. Personal immunity is afforded only to particular persons irrespective if their conduct was undertaken in a private or public capacity\nF. Personal immunity is given to all individuals, regardless of their conduct\nG. Personal immunity is that which is afforded in a personal capacity and hence does not cover conduct of the State as such\nH. Personal immunity is afforded to State officials for conduct undertaken in a public capacity\nI. Personal immunity is afforded to State officials for conduct undertaken in a private capacity.\nJ. Personal immunity is afforded only to particular persons if their conduct was undertaken in a public capacity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is E. Personal immunity (ratione personae) protects specific high-ranking officials, such as heads of state, from foreign jurisdiction for both private and public acts during their time in office. It attaches to the person due to their status, not the nature of the conduct.\n\n\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1286, "output_tokens": 416, "total_tokens": 1702}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_law_945", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A woman inherited her father's farm when he died testate. Prior to her father's death, the woman had already taken over the operations on the father's farm due to his declining health. Recently, the woman had granted a coal company rights to strip-mine coal from underneath the farm. Their agreement stipulated that the coal company would pay the woman a per-ton royalty for the coal extracted. In addition, the coal company agreed to fill in the excavated area and replace top soil on the surface of the land. After the coal company commenced its strip-mining operations, the woman noticed that the company was not filling in the excavated area as previously agreed. However, because the company paid the woman all the coal royalties from the strip mining, she did not voice any objection regarding its failure to replace the top soil. Two years later, the coal company had now completed its strip-mining operation under its arrangement with the woman. The coal company's right to strip-mine coal from the woman's property would be an example of a (an)\n\nOptions: \nA. constructive trust.\nB. easement appurtenant.\nC. servient estate.\nD. voluntary waste.\nE. license.\nF. easement in gross.\nG. tenancy in common.\nH. profit-a-prendre.\nI. adverse possession.\nJ. easement by necessity.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1360, "output_tokens": 377, "total_tokens": 1737}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_law_1242", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which statement best describes the profit sharing relationship of a general partnership where the partners have agreed only on voting percentage and the voting shares are unequal?\n\nOptions: \nA. Partners share in proportion to their experience and expertise.\nB. Partners share in proportion to their contributions to the capital and assets of the partnership.\nC. Partners share in proportion to their voting percentage.\nD. Partners cannot share until they unanimously agree upon a distribution.\nE. Partners share in proportion to their role in the partnership.\nF. Partners share according to a predetermined ratio agreed upon at the start of the partnership.\nG. Partners share in proportion to the time they spend working for the partnership.\nH. Partners share is determined by a third-party arbitrator.\nI. Partners share equally.\nJ. Partners share in proportion to their individual profits.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 900, "output_tokens": 316, "total_tokens": 1216}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_law_1615", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the 'Lotus principle'?\n\nOptions: \nA. The so-called Lotus principle is that customary law is superior to treaty law\nB. The so-called Lotus principle is that States have the right to intervene in the internal affairs of other States if it concerns their national security\nC. The so-called Lotus principle is that States are permitted to apply their own domestic laws in disputes with other States\nD. The so-called Lotus principle is that international law governs the relations between States and not the relations between individuals.\nE. The so-called Lotus principle is that States have unlimited jurisdiction over their own citizens, regardless of where they are located\nF. The so-called Lotus principle is that States are free to ignore international law as long as they don't infringe on the sovereignty of other States\nG. The so-called Lotus principle is that 'restrictions upon the independence of States cannot therefore be presumed', or, as it has been construed, 'whatever is not prohibited is permitted in international law'\nH. The so-called Lotus principle is that States are not prohibited to assert their enforcement jurisdiction on the high seas\nI. The so-called Lotus principle is that customary law derives from the combination of State practice and opinio juris\nJ. The so-called Lotus principle is that States are free to choose the Court that they will submit their disputes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1340, "output_tokens": 334, "total_tokens": 1674}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_law_1266", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Tom and Jerry entered into a contract whereby Tom agreed to sell Jerry $1,000 worth of heroin, an illegal substance. This is an example of a:\n\nOptions: \nA. quasi contract\nB. unilateral contract\nC. secondary party beneficiary contract\nD. express contract\nE. bilateral contract\nF. implied contract\nG. void contract\nH. voidable contract\nI. unconscionable contract\nJ. contract of adhesion\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 632, "output_tokens": 196, "total_tokens": 828}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_law_1297", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the absence of a provision to the contrary in the articles of incorporation, the directors of a corporation elected for a specified term\n\nOptions: \nA. can be removed from office at a meeting of the shareholders, but only with a 