 within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{class}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 444, "output_tokens": 343, "total_tokens": 787}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_312", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Hotelling's lemma shows this quantity is equal to the derivative of another function.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Hotelling's lemma states that the supply function of a good is equal to the derivative of the profit function with respect to the price of that good. Therefore, the quantity referred to is the profit-maximizing output, and it is equal to the derivative of the profit function. \n\n\\boxed{\\text{profit function}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 300, "output_tokens": 262, "total_tokens": 562}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_339", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A book by William Sumner concludes that different groups defined by this concept owe very little to one another.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{class}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 320, "output_tokens": 267, "total_tokens": 587}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_401", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: William Julius Wilson's book When Work Disappears argues that the disappearance of blue-collar jobs from this country's cities contributes to urban poverty.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{True}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 431, "output_tokens": 337, "total_tokens": 768}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_453", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This phenomenon is efficient in directed search models but may be inefficient in random search.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{Price dispersion}  \n\nPrice dispersion often improves matching in directed search by allowing buyers to choose among different offers, increasing trade efficiency. In random search, however, it can lead to coordination failures or suboptimal matches because agents cannot direct their search toward better opportunities. Thus, the same phenomenon that enhances efficiency in one context may cause inefficiency in another.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 371, 