ok described is Michel Foucault's *The Order of Things*, which explores how human sciences emerged through processes of examination and classification, distinct from the observational methods of natural sciences. Foucault argues that the human sciences developed alongside institutions like prisons, schools, and clinics, where examination became a tool of power and knowledge. This distinction highlights the unique epistemological foundation of the human sciences.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{The Order of Things}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 340, "output_tokens": 394, "total_tokens": 734}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1628", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An essay arguing that the adoption of this practice was bad notes that progressivists seem to believe that this practice led to the creation of the Parthenon and the Mass in B Minor.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The practice referred to is **\"public education\"** or **\"compulsory schooling,\"** as progressivists often credit it with enabling great cultural achievements. The essay mocks this belief by implying it absurdly credits schooling for masterpieces like the Parthenon or Bach's Mass in B Minor.  \n\n\\boxed{\\text{public education}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 481, "output_tokens": 359, "total_tokens": 840}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1655", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a section of a paper titled \"The Problem Illustrated Anew,\" this man used an example from a law case in which a confectioner's mortars and pestles caused vibrations that prevented a doctor from using a stethoscope to examine patients; that paper by this man was published a few weeks before a Guido Calabresi article setting forth similar thoughts about liability rules in automobile accidents and is one of several of his papers that cite the case Sturges v. Bridgman.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{Ronald Coase}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 640, "output_tokens": 375, "total_tokens": 1015}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Social Science_1755", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One economist disputed traditional approaches to this situation by formulating eight design principles, including the use of \"graduated sanctions\"; that economist, Elinor Ostrom, wrote a book that offered governing methods in response to this situation.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{the tragedy of the commons}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 520, "output_tokens": 388, "total_tokens": 908}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality":