l, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4526", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: I tidied up my house.\n\nQuestion: what's the cause for this?\n\nOptions: \nA. I was swamped with work.\nB. I was expecting company.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 376, "output_tokens": 190, "total_tokens": 566}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-CausalReasoning_4439", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: The man drank heavily at the party.\n\nQuestion: what's the effect of this?\n\nOptions: \nA. He had a headache the next day.\nB. He had a runny nose the next day.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 404, "output_tokens": 235, "total_tokens": 639}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_12136", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: George Osborne should spread austerity over a longer period than currently planned to avoid damaging the economy, a leading global watchdog has claimed. The Chancellor looks set to use next month's Budget - the first since the Tories' dramatic election victory last month - to outline plans to balance the books by 2018-19. But the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development suggested that the cuts required in 2016 and 2017 to return Britain to the black may be too harsh. The OECD urged the government to even out austerity over a longer period to 'lower its impact on growth'. Despite the warning, the Paris based think-tank said it again expects Britain to be the fastest growing major economy in the world this year.\n@highlight\nOsborne planning to balance the books by 2018-19 with deep cuts\n@highlight\nOECD warns the spending cuts should be spread over a longer period\n@highlight\nDowngrades\u00a0UK growth to 2.4% \u00a0but still stronger than the rest of the G7\nQuery: 'The Chancellor should heed the @placeholder's warnings that 'continued weak productivity' could lead to 'a higher-than-expected budget deficit'.\n\nOptions : A. Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development\nB. George Osborne\nC. Budget\nD. Downgrades\u00a0UK\nE. Tories\nF. OECD\nG. Britain\nH. Paris\nI. Osborne\nJ. G7\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1795, "output_tokens": 34, "total_tokens": 1829}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_12352", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) -- The small, black-and-white newspaper ad offered a discount: Nine holes of golf for $9.11 -- on September 11. The management of a Wisconsin golf course said the idea was to remember the victims of the September 11, 2001, attacks, but the ad turned into a public relations disaster on social media. By Tuesday, TumbleDown Trails Golf Course was reporting death threats. The golf course in Verona, Wisconsin, placed an advertisement in Monday's Wisconsin State Journal offering to \"commemorate\" the 12th anniversary of the terror attacks with \"9 holes with cart for only $9.11 per person or 18 holes with cart for only $19.11!\"\n@highlight\nSocial media erupts after course offers discount to \"commemorate\" terror attacks\n@highlight\nOffer: $9.11 for nine holes, $19.11 for 18 holes\n@highlight\nManagement apologizes on Facebook, reports death threats\n@highlight\nCourse may be closed on Wednesday due to security concerns\nQuery: By Tuesday afternoon, many @placeholder commenters were defending the course.\n\nOptions : A. Wisconsin\nB. Facebook\nC. Verona\nD. CNN\nE. Wisconsin State Journal\nF. TumbleDown Trails Golf Course\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage mentions \"many @placeholder commenters were defending the course\" but does not specify where; however, the ad was placed in the Wisconsin State Journal, and the context of social media and Facebook is provided in the highlights. The best fit from the options, given the passage and highlights, is \"Facebook.\"\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1684, "output_tokens": 97, "total_tokens": 1781}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_9518", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) It's official -- El Ni\u00f1o is dead. But its demise doesn't necessarily mean we're done with wild weather. The recent climate event -- characterized by warming waters in the eastern Pacific Ocean -- has been one of the strongest ever recorded, and its impact has been felt far and wide. Record smashing temperatures hit Thailand, Laos and Cambodia. In Malaysia, lakes dried up and vegetables withered. Weak monsoons and killer heatwaves left India barren and praying for rain. Storms pounded the Californian coast, leaving apartments teetering on cliff edges as backyards dropped into the ocean. The weather system may even have contributed to the spread of Zika by creating conditions that helped mosquito populations thrive.\n@highlight\nThe temperature of the Pacific has cooled, signaling the end of the El Ni\u00f1o part of the cycle\n@highlight\nExperts say there is a 75% chance of a La Ni\u00f1a pattern forming by the end of 2016\nQuery: According to Dr. Santoso, the risk for a strong @placeholder is enhanced following a strong El Ni\u00f1o, such as the one we just had over the last year.\n\nOptions : A. Malaysia\nB. La Ni\u00f1a\nC. El Ni\u00f1o\nD. Zika\nE. Laos\nF. India\nG. Cambodia\nH. Californian\nI. Thailand\nJ. Pacific\nK. Pacific Ocean\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B. La Ni\u00f1a}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1388, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 1436}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_13287", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) The Force was with Los Angeles. The board of directors for the Lucas Museum of Narrative Art announced Tuesday that the City of Angels will be the site for the $1 billion facility that will house George Lucas' personal art collection. The city's Exposition Park will be the home of the futuristic building, which is sure to be a draw for \"Star Wars\" fans and architecture geeks alike. Los Angeles beat out San Francisco for the site. In a statement, the board said, \"Settling on a location proved to be an extremely difficult decision precisely because of the desirability of both sites and cities.\"\n@highlight\nChicago was the original site for the Lucas Museum of Narrative Art\n@highlight\nFilmmaker George Lucas has a trove of art and \"Star Wars\" memorabilia\nQuery: @placeholder is a magnet for the region and accessible from all parts of the city.\n\nOptions : A. Exposition Park\nB. City of Angels\nC. San Francisco\nD. Star Wars\nE. Lucas Museum of Narrative Art\nF. George Lucas\nG. Force\nH. Chicago\nI. Los Angeles\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A. Exposition Park}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1180, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 1226}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_11207", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) Selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors, known as SSRIs, are the most common type of antidepressants prescribed to pregnant women. Yet a new study indicates that when taken during pregnancy, the drugs are associated with a higher risk of language disorders, including dyslexia, in offspring. The children of women who took SSRIs while pregnant have a 37% greater risk of speech or language disorders compared with the children of depressed but unmedicated mothers, the researchers say. In practical terms, if a depressed mother did not take antidepressants, her child's risk of being diagnosed with a speech or language disorder would be about 1%, but if she took an SSRI, it would increase to 1.37%, explained Dr. Alan Brown, lead author of the study and a professor of psychiatry and epidemiology at Columbia University Medical Center.\n@highlight\nKids of pregnant women who took SSRIs have a higher risk of speech disorders, a study finds\n@highlight\n6% to 10% of pregnant women worldwide are exposed to antidepressants, author says\nQuery: The first \"exposure\" group included 15,596 mothers who purchased @placeholder once or more before or during pregnancy.\n\nOptions : A. Alan Brown\nB. Columbia University Medical Center\nC. SSRI\nD. SSRIs\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D. SSRIs}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1348, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": 1384}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_14224", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) So much for a warm and fuzzy Valentine's Day. About 20 cities across the East endured record-breaking cold Sunday, forecasters say. New York City's temperature plummeted to 1 below zero at Central Park, shattering the record of 2 degrees, set during World War I. Boston reported 9 below. Toronto's temperature reached 16 below over the weekend. And those are just the real temperatures. Factor in strong winds, and states from northern Pennsylvania to Maine felt wind chills well, well below zero. In all, more than 75 million people from the Midwest to the Eastern Seaboard are expected to be affected by snow and freezing rain into Tuesday.\n@highlight\nRecord-low temperatures are reported Sunday in some cities\n@highlight\nPart of Interstate 65 in Indiana is closed after multiple crashes\n@highlight\nSnow and freezing rain are impacting more than 75 million people into Tuesday\nQuery: At least three people died in the pileup on @placeholder 78, Pennsylvania State Police said.\n\nOptions : A. Interstate\nB. Central Park\nC. Valentine's Day\nD. Indiana\nE. New York City\nF. East\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1228, "output_tokens": 24, "total_tokens": 1252}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_14964", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: A million homes in\u00a0Morocco\u00a0could soon be powered by a mega solar plant capable of providing energy at all hours of the day and night. Instead of using the standard photovoltaic solar cells, Ouarzazate's power station will use Concentrated Solar Power (CSP) - a technology that harnesses sunlight to melt salt and power a steam turbine. The plant, called Noor1, is expected to open next month and will be the first of four stations to be set up in the region. Once complete, the establishment will be the largest CSP farm in the world. The Ouarzazate plant is part of Morocco's strategy to produce 42 per cent of its energy from renewable sources by 2020 - a goal that has been praised by the UN.\n@highlight\nThe Ouarzazate plant will be the biggest solar thermal plant in the world\n@highlight\nIt will use a technology known as Concentrate Solar Power (CSP)\n@highlight\nCSP harnesses sunlight to melt salt and power a steam turbine\n@highlight\nMorocco plans to get 42 per cent of its energy from renewables by 2020\nQuery: While solar thermal power methods such as @placeholder only work in very hot countries, solar energy at large is experiencing more widespread use worldwide as the photovoltaic panels' price is progressively falling.\n\nOptions : A. Ouarzazate\nB. Concentrate Solar Power\nC. Morocco\nD. UN\nE. Concentrated Solar Power\nF. CSP\nG. Noor1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1548, "output_tokens": 24, "total_tokens": 1572}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_10005", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Britons are by far the biggest adopters of contactless payments in Europe as the use of the system continues to climb across the continent, new figures reveal. More than one billion contactless transactions worth \u20ac12.6billion took place in Europe over the last 12 months \u2013 a three-fold increase when compared to the same period in 2014, according to Visa Europe. Britain is the country with the highest number of contactless transactions, with 52.6million worth more than \u20ac330million made in March alone, followed by Poland and Czech Republic, with 49.7million and 13.9million transactions respectively. This rapid growth in the UK was fuelled in part by the launch of contactless payments on Transport for London services last September, Visa Europe said.\n@highlight\nThe UK issues the highest number of contactless cards\n@highlight\nBritons made 52.6million transactions worth more than \u20ac330million in March\n@highlight\nSome 1.1billion contactless transactions worth \u20ac12.6billion were made by Visa cardholders across Europe in the last 12 months\nQuery: Across the continent, 131million Visa contactless cards are carried in the pockets and purses of consumers, of which 49.6million are in the @placeholder.\n\nOptions : A. Poland\nB. Transport for London\nC. Britons\nD. Visa\nE. Czech Republic\nF. UK\nG. Visa Europe\nH. Britain\nI. Europe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1548, "output_tokens": 24, "total_tokens": 1572}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_11915", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Jenson Button's miserable Formula One season continued in Bahrain after he failed to start the Bahrain Grand Prix. The British driver was set to start from the back of the grid after he broke down in qualifying. But despite frantic work from his McLaren team to get his car ready in time for the race in Sakhir, Button was forced to watch from the sidelines. Jenson Button (left) waves to fans during the drivers parade before the start of the Bahrain Grand Prix 'The engine is not broken,' said McLaren chairman Ron Dennis. 'What we have is the data in the Energy Recovery System is not clean and the chances of it failing are quite high so it is probably best not to run it.'\n@highlight\nJenson Button was set to start from the back of the grid after mechanical\u00a0 failure in\u00a0qualifying\n@highlight\nDespite frantic work from McLaren mechanics, they were unable to get his car on to the grid leaving Button to watch from the sidelines\n@highlight\nIt was only the third race of the last 272 staged that he has missed\nQuery: Button jumps out of his McLaren\u00a0after failing to complete the qualifying session in @placeholder\n\nOptions : A. Sakhir\nB. Energy Recovery System\nC. Bahrain\nD. Bahrain Grand Prix\nE. Jenson Button\nF. Formula One\nG. Button\nH. McLaren\nI. Ron Dennis\nJ. Grand Prix\nK. British\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C. Bahrain}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1412, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 1444}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_18362", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Their wild ways might already be the talk of Newport high society, but don't assume we've seen the best of Lillian and Beatrice Bellacourt quite yet. Because as these wine-swigging, bed-hopping sisters enter the limelight, their scandalous lifestyles are becoming exposed in all their debauched detail. We're talking sex, drugs and buckets of money \u2013 with a touch of incest thrown in for good measure. Not your average society darling, fame-hungry Lady Lillian isn't afraid to let down her perfectly coiffed hair, with her daringly extravagant soir\u00e9es. To keep up with this upper-class party girl, you'll find yourself downing glasses of cocaine-wine, dodging a gun-toting matriarch and quite possibility getting into a fist-fight with a blind and deaf lady.\n@highlight\nFictional content sponsored by Comedy Central\nQuery: Not to be outdone by her sister's escapades, @placeholder indulges in a few exploits of her own, including daring sexual dalliances.\n\nOptions : A. Newport\nB. Lady Lillian\nC. Comedy Central\nD. Lillian\nE. Beatrice Bellacourt\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E. Beatrice Bellacourt}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1220, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 1268}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_10591", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Scientologists hold a 'blackmail file' on John Travolta to stop him leaving the faith, which includes 'damaging material' from his sessions with auditors at the church, it has been claimed. A documentary investigating the religion and its secret California-based headquarters features a number of allegations about how members are threatened and tortured in prison-style camps and cut off from their family if they decide to leave Scientology. Others belonging to the most senior order of the faith have been forced to play musical chairs to the sound of Queen's Bohemian Rhapsody in a fight to secure a chair to stay in the church, it was claimed.\n@highlight\nGoing Clear documentary claims to reveal secrets of Scientology religion\n@highlight\nIt alleges the church has a 'blackmail file' on John Travolta from auditing sessions and\u00a0members are thrown into 'The Hole' to confess their crimes and vie for places by playing musical chairs to Bohemian Rhapsody\n@highlight\nSylvia 'Spanky' Taylor, who once acted as the intermediary between the church and John Travolta, said people were punished with 30 hours labour\n@highlight\nScientologists rejected allegations saying they are from 'admitted liars'\nQuery: The documentary also claimed @placeholder chiefs hold a 'black PR package' on Travolta, with all the disclosures he made during auditing sessions.\n\nOptions : A. Queen\nB. California\nC. John Travolta\nD. Sylvia 'Spanky' Taylor\nE. Scientologists\nF. Clear\nG. The Hole\nH. Bohemian Rhapsody\nI. Scientology\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C. John Travolta}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1560, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 1600}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_13776", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) World leaders touch down in the Chinese city of Hangzhou this week for the G20 summit and Beijing is determined it will proceed without a hitch. Factories are shuttered, skies are clear and security is tight. Local residents have been given seven days extra vacation time and discounted tours to destinations outside the city to ensure Hangzhou is free of crowds and traffic. Meanwhile, thousands of migrant workers have left the city due to the halt in their work lives and the growing inconvenience caused by G20 preparation measures. What will be discussed at the summit? How has China prepared? And why is it in Hangzhou anyway?\n@highlight\nPollution, residents cleared out in preparation for China's big G20 debut in Hangzhou\n@highlight\nChina wants to focus on economic issues, rather than the South China Sea dispute\nQuery: The Hangzhou summit has been called another \"milestone\" for a rising @placeholder, keen to show its growing dominance on the world stage.\n\nOptions : A. Chinese\nB. Beijing\nC. South China Sea\nD. Hangzhou\nE. G20\nF. China\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1172, "output_tokens": 30, "total_tokens": 1202}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_10013", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: In a world where computers are increasingly powerful and are concealed within ever more glossy slabs of aluminum, the Raspberry Pi (RPi) offers surprising proof for the virtue of moderation. Resembling little more than a credit card-sized scrap of exposed circuit board, the RPi is a fully programmable PC that runs a free, open-source Linux operating system, plugs into any TV, can power 3D graphics, connects to the Internet and, with a little ingenuity, be used to create your own personalized robot slave. The computer's miniature frame is crowded with two USB ports, an SD card slot, an Ethernet connection and microchip in the middle -- all powered by a universal USB mobile charger.\n@highlight\nThe Raspberry Pi is a credit-card sized computer that costs little more than a textbook\n@highlight\nOriginally designed to encourage school children to learn programming skills\n@highlight\nThe mini-PC now hugely popular with DIY geeks, who have used it to power their own creations\nQuery: It turned out there was a voracious appetite -- particularly among a growing class of @placeholder geeks -- for a cheap, easily-programmable, open-source piece of hardware that would allow them to let their imaginations run wild.\n\nOptions : A. Raspberry Pi\nB. Ethernet\nC. Internet\nD. USB\nE. Linux\nF. RPi\nG. DIY\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G. DIY}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1372, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 1420}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_11586", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) For several weeks now, city and state officials have traded barbs over who is ultimately responsible for the toxic water that's inundated Flint, Michigan. On Thursday, the feds said they both are. In an emergency administrative order, the Environmental Protection Agency slammed the city of Flint, the Michigan Department of Environmental Quality and the State of Michigan, saying they are all responsible for the lead contamination in the city's water. Their responses to the crisis, the EPA said, were \"inadequate to protect public health.\" EPA administrator resigns \"There are serious, ongoing concerns with delays, lack of adequate transparency, and capacity to safely manage the drinking water system,\" the agency said in a press release.\n@highlight\nThe EPA says the city of Flint and the state of Michigan are among those responsible for the water crisis\n@highlight\nThe agency's regional administrator who oversees Flint has resigned\n@highlight\nCongress may hold a hearing on the incident\nQuery: The emergency order also means the EPA will start doing its own lead testing in @placeholder's water system.\n\nOptions : A. Michigan\nB. EPA\nC. Michigan Department of Environmental Quality\nD. State of Michigan\nE. Flint\nF. Congress\nG. Environmental Protection Agency\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E. Flint}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1264, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 1296}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_16180", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Since the mid-1990s, Rs 1,500 crore has been spent to clean up the dying Yamuna, but it all has gone down the drain. Now the water you drink is expected to give a new lease of life to the once fabled river. For the first time in history, Delhi may get its share of Yamuna water, treated and supplied to households, from the river itself. The Capital has so far been getting water diverted from the river to Western Yamuna Canal (WYC) in Haryana. This meets Delhi\u2019s 70 per cent drinking water needs. A high-powered committee headed by the secretary, ministry of water resources, Shashi Shekhar, has recommended this move to the National Green Tribunal (NGT) to ensure fresh water flow in the river.\n@highlight\nCommittee says Yamuna river will remain a 'sewer' unless action is taken\n@highlight\nIt will take time for the river to revive, but Green Tribunal supports plan\nQuery: Even now the canal water is deposited at Palla in @placeholder and collected at Wazirabad before it is cleaned up and supplied.\n\nOptions : A. Western Yamuna Canal\nB. WYC\nC. Haryana\nD. Shashi Shekhar\nE. National Green Tribunal\nF. Green Tribunal\nG. The Capital\nH. Delhi\nI. Committee\nJ. Rs\nK. Yamuna\nL. NGT\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1453, "output_tokens": 21, "total_tokens": 1474}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_16687", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Users\u00a0of Microsoft's new Windows 10 software were elated to find the firm had brought back solitaire, the famous free game. In its latest incarnation it boasts more features and can even track your stats. However, there is just one problem - to play without ads, users have to pay Microsoft $10 a year, every year. Experts have describe the decision as odd. 'Netflix charges you $7.99 per month for thousands of streaming movies and TV shows, Spotify, Slacker, Rdio and others charge about $10 per month for unlimited music,' said Mark Hachman of PC World. 'And Microsoft? They want you to pay $1.50 per month to remove ads from Solitaire.'\n@highlight\nFree game was a popular part of earlier windows versions\n@highlight\nNew Version charges users $10 a year for ad free\u00a0Solitaire\u00a0games\n@highlight\nExperts say the feature is 'an accident waiting to happen'\nQuery: '@placeholder itself is free, so complaining too much about this might seem ungracious,' said Hachman.\n\nOptions : A. Windows 10\nB. Solitaire\nC. Rdio\nD. Netflix\nE. Microsoft\nF. PC World\nG. Slacker\nH. New Version\nI. Mark Hachman\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B. Solitaire}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1344, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 1400}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_18477", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) People are often surprised to learn that Shelby Payne has type 1 diabetes -- because her identical twin sister, Sydney, does not. \"Everyone's like, 'Wow, how in the world does (my sister) not have it?' \" said Payne, 23, who once played forward on Stanford's soccer team, like her sister. \"They can't really fathom it.\" Though experts agree that genetics influence who gets type 1 diabetes, Payne's story suggests that something other than genes must also be at play. And some researchers are focusing in on one family of viruses in particular. A new study from Finland joins decades of research suggesting that enteroviruses, which include over 100 individual virus types, may play a key role in triggering type 1 diabetes, which has no cure.\n@highlight\nType 1 diabetes is an autoimmune condition, which may be triggered by factors that are not genetic\n@highlight\nEnteroviruses, known to affect the gut, may be a key player in the development of type 1 diabetes\nQuery: @placeholder and her sister have also enrolled in TrialNet, a diabetes research network studying ways to prevent and delay type 1 diabetes.\n\nOptions : A. Enteroviruses\nB. Type 1\nC. Payne\nD. Finland\nE. Sydney\nF. Stanford\nG. Shelby Payne\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The query refers to the individual mentioned in the passage who has an identical twin without diabetes, which is Shelby Payne.\n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1709, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 1769}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_9449", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: She won an Oscar for playing Elizabeth II in the 2006 film The Queen. Now, Helen Mirren has once again scored a major award for playing her Royal Highness - this time for the play The Audience - at the 2015 Tony Awards in New York City on Sunday night. It also marked the 69-year-old's first ever Tony Award win, which is considered to be U.S. theater's highest honor. The Tony Award meant that Mirren was only a Grammy Award away from gaining so-called EGOT status as the winner of an Emmy, Grammy, Oscar and Tony - a distinction shared by only 12 entertainers.\n@highlight\nHelen Mirren wins for Best Leading Actress in a Play for portrayal of Queen Elizabeth II in The Audience\n@highlight\nThe Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time scores five awards including Best Play and Best Leading Actor in a Play\n@highlight\nFun Home ties for lead with five awards including \u00a0Best Musical, Best Book of a Musical, Best Score, Best Director and Best Leading Actor in a Musical\n@highlight\nTommy Tune accepts Lifetime Achievement Award marking his 10th Tony Award\nQuery: 'Your Majesty, you did it again,' @placeholder said as she accepted her first Tony Award.\n\nOptions : A. Best Leading Actress\nB. Best Leading Actor\nC. Tommy Tune\nD. The Queen\nE. Elizabeth II\nF. Lifetime Achievement Award\nG. Grammy Award\nH. Tony Award\nI. Helen Mirren\nJ. New York City\nK. The Audience\nL. Best Book of a Musical\nM. Tony Awards\nN. Best Musical\nO. Tony\nP. Emmy\nQ. Best Score\nR. Oscar\nS. Best Director\nT. U.S.\nU. Best Play\nV. Royal Highness\nW. Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night\nX. EGOT\nY. Grammy\nZ. Mirren\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1884, "output_tokens": 28, "total_tokens": 1912}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_16116", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: When Suleiman the Magnificent died, his heart and body were buried in separate locations. His embalmed body was laid to rest at mosque in Istanbul and the rest was hidden in a secret location. Now, archaeologists believe they have unearthed the tomb that holds the heart and organs from the great ruler of the Ottoman Empire. 'We have data which all points in the same direction,'said Norbet Pap head of the department of Political Geography, Regional and Development Studies at the University of Pecs in Hungary at a presentation of the latest findings. 'That is why we say 'in all certainty,' because there is no sign pointing in another direction.'\n@highlight\nTeam used historical records and archives to search for location of tomb\n@highlight\nDecorative elements resemble those where his body is\n@highlight\nSuleiman's death at Szigetvar was kept secret for 48 days\n@highlight\nExcavation work at the site would restart in April\nQuery: Until his death at age 71, Suleiman was the @placeholder's longest-ruling sultan.\n\nOptions : A. Suleiman\nB. Norbet Pap\nC. Szigetvar\nD. Regional and Development Studies\nE. University of Pecs\nF. Istanbul\nG. Political Geography\nH. Hungary\nI. Magnificent\nJ. Ottoman Empire\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J. Ottoman Empire}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1372, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 1420}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_17691", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Nasa wants to land the first humans on Mars in 2035, and to do that, it needs the world's toughest parachute. Its latest plan is to use a large inflatable 'flying saucer' that will slow a spacecraft down after piercing through the thin Martian atmosphere. Dubbed the density supersonic decelerator (LDSD), the space agency plans to conduct an ambitious test flight of its design on Wednesday at 1:30pm (5:30pm GMT). The LDSD is unique in its design, using a donut-shaped inflatable decelerator to create atmospheric drag. When attached to the exterior of a capsule travelling at Mach 4 it will be capable of slowing it down to Mach 2, where a regular parachute can then deploy.\n@highlight\nThe saucer is known as the low density supersonic decelerator\n@highlight\nThe test flight will take place on Wednesday at 1:30pm ET (5:30 GMT)\n@highlight\nInflatable saucer is 5ft (4.6 metres) wide, weighing 7,000lbs (3.200kg)\n@highlight\nThe parachute was torn apart in when it deployed in a flight last year\nQuery: Last June, to simulate the @placeholder atmosphere on Earth, the LDSD was lifted to a height of 23 miles (37km) by a high-altitude balloon.\n\nOptions : A. Martian\nB. Nasa\nC. LDSD\nD. Inflatable\nE. GMT\nF. Mars\nG. Mach 2\nH. Mach 4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1596, "output_tokens": 24, "total_tokens": 1620}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_14310", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) -- After downloading the latest iPhone, iPod touch and iPad operating system, iOS 6, the fun part is excitedly poking around and hunting for what's new. Find subtle design changes, like the phone's key pad, or set up new features, like Facebook integration. You might even use Siri again for the first time in a while to test its improved sports and restaurant knowledge. If you have an iPhone 3GS, 4 or 4S, a fourth generation iPod touch, or an iPad 2 or the new iPad, you can upgrade to iOS 6. Go to your settings screen, tap General and then Software Update. Keep in mind that some features are limited to the most recent models.\n@highlight\nNew operating system update for the iPhone, iPad and iPod touch has gained and lost features\n@highlight\nApple's new Maps app drops Google data, including public transit directions, adds turn-by-turn\n@highlight\nVoice assistant Siri adds movie, sports and restaurant data\nQuery: Flyover is only available on the iPhone 4S and later, @placeholder 2 and later, and the iPod touch.\n\nOptions : A. iPhone 3GS\nB. General\nC. Software Update\nD. Google\nE. iPhone\nF. Facebook\nG. iOS\nH. iPod touch\nI. iPad\nJ. Apple\nK. Siri\nL. Maps\nM. CNN\nN. 4S\nO. iOS 6\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1456, "output_tokens": 24, "total_tokens": 1480}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_12184", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: The identity of the kissing couple immortalized in the throes of passions in Times Square on VJ Day, 1945 has been thrown into doubt after a new scientific theory disproved all existing accounts. More than a dozen people claimed to be either the the sailor or the nurse shown passionately embracing as the news broke of the end of the Second World War after Japan's surrender. But according to a team of astronomers, none of their accounts can be true. The scientists say they have managed to pinpoint the time of the shot by analyzing the shadows in the image - and their result does not match any of the stories put forward.\n@highlight\nSailor and a nurse were immortalized in photograph from August 14, 1945\n@highlight\nWas published in Life magazine - but photographer didn't get their names\n@highlight\nMore than a dozen people have claimed they were in the image\n@highlight\nScientists have now debunked some stories via astronomy\n@highlight\nSay they have pinned time of image to 5:51pm - which does not match any leading stories\nQuery: He remembers tearing through @placeholder kissing everyone in sight from sheer excitement.\n\nOptions : A. Second World War\nB. Japan\nC. Life\nD. Sailor\nE. Times Square\nF. VJ Day\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1336, "output_tokens": 24, "total_tokens": 1360}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_11394", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Good news has arrived for stranded holidaymakers after Virgin Australia and Jetstar officially announced that conditions were safe to resume flights to and from Bali. Earlier on Saturday, Indonesian officials declared Denpasar Airport safe to reopen as the cloud of ash from the eruption of Mount Raung drifted away. Virgin sent an observation flight to the airport to have visual confirmation and determine whether conditions were suitable for flights to operate before giving the all-clear. The airline said scheduled flights out of Denpasar would go ahead on Saturday evening and it plans to continue operations in and out of the Indonesian island on Sunday.\n@highlight\nVirgin Australia and Jetstar has confirmed it is able to resume flights\n@highlight\nThey announced the conditions were safe to operate to and from Bali\n@highlight\nStrong winds  pushed the ash cloud away from the airport on Saturday\n@highlight\nAn eruption from\u00a0Mount Raung caused the large ash cloud to form\n@highlight\nThe cloud caused visibility issue and can effect engine electronics\n@highlight\nIt caused thousands of Australians to be stranded at Denpasar airport\nQuery: The ash grounded planes from Virgin, @placeholder, Garuda and AirAsia on Friday.\n\nOptions : A. Mount Raung\nB. Denpasar\nC. Virgin Australia\nD. Bali\nE. Virgin\nF. Australians\nG. Indonesian\nH. Jetstar\nI. Denpasar Airport\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1376, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 1408}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_14820", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) There were more reported cases of sexually transmitted diseases last year than ever before in the United States, according to the latest STD surveillance report by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. The annual report, which was released on Wednesday, showed that the rates of chlamydia, gonorrhea, and syphilis -- the three most commonly reported STDs in the nation -- increased between 2014 and 2015, reaching an all-time high. Reported cases of primary and secondary syphilis rose by 19%, gonorrhea cases rose by 12.8%, and chlamydia cases rose by 5.9%, from 2014. All three STDs are curable with antibiotics, but most infections go undiagnosed and untreated, according to the CDC.\n@highlight\nChlamydia, gonorrhea and syphilis rates hit an all-time high last year, new report shows\n@highlight\n\"We have reached a decisive moment for the nation,\" CDC official says\nQuery: Scientists at the @placeholder warned in July that the bacterium that causes gonorrhea, called Neisseria gonorrhoeae, is developing resistance to the antibiotic drugs used to treat it.\n\nOptions : A. United States\nB. STD\nC. CDC\nD. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\nE. Chlamydia\nF. STDs\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1416, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 1468}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_12028", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Banish the tumour and cure the disease. That\u2019s what a Delhi-based think-tank close to the RSS is set to do by posing a serious legal challenge to Kashmir\u2019s \u2018special\u2019 provisions. The Delhi-based Jammu and Kashmir Study Centre (JKSC) is gearing up to target Article 35A, an outgrowth powered by Article 370 of the Constitution, which gives J&K special status. Article 35A allows the state to grant special privileges and rights to its permanent residents, and not to others living there, the think-tank says. To scrap these special provisions, the Jammu and Kashmir Study Centre (JKSC) has decided to approach the Supreme Court. On July 11, the organisation will formally announce at a seminar in Delhi the date for filing the petition.\n@highlight\nThe Jammu and Kashmir Study Centre, based in Delhi, is challenging Article 35A\n@highlight\nThe amendment is powered by Article 370 of the Constitution, which gives J&K special status\n@highlight\nIt lets the state grant privileges and rights to permanent residents, but not others\nQuery: RSS national executive member Arun Kumar is one of the advisers with the petitioner @placeholder.\n\nOptions : A. Jammu and Kashmir Study Centre\nB. JKSC\nC. Article 370\nD. RSS\nE. J&K\nF. Supreme Court\nG. Delhi\nH. Constitution\nI. Article 35A\nJ. Kashmir\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1488, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 1528}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_10093", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Despite complaints that Google Glass was too bulky and nerdy, rumours suggest the tech giant will release a new version with a larger prism display. The Enterprise Edition (EE) is also said to include an Intel Atom processor for improved performance and battery life. Some users of Glass, which was pulled in January following poor sales and mixed reviews, complained of eye strain after prolonged use. This may explain why Google might have decided to include a larger screen in its next design, 9to5Google reported. It\u2019s rumoured that final iterations of the EE include a prism that extends further, allowing wearers to glance upwards and focus on the screen more comfortably than before.\n@highlight\nRumours suggest Google will release a new version of Google Glass, dubbed the Enterprise Edition, with a larger prism display\n@highlight\nImproved screen could help to reduce eye strain for wearers\n@highlight\nSmart specs are also said to include an Intel Atom processor for improved performance and battery life compared to the previous version\n@highlight\nSome users of Glass, which was pulled in January following poor sales and mixed reviews, complained of eye strain after prolonged use\nQuery: The previous @placeholder headset was launched in a beta version under the firm's Explorer programme.\n\nOptions : A. Google\nB. Google Glass\nC. Intel Atom\nD. Smart\nE. Glass\nF. EE\nG. Enterprise Edition\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E. Glass}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1376, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 1408}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_10484", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: In the ancient Inca kingdom, the wheel was yet to be invented, iron was foreign and steel was unheard of. So when the Incas needed to travel across the Andes, they did so on handwoven rope bridges, stretched over gorges and rivers. Five hundred years later, just one of the Inca rope bridges remains: the Keshwa Chaca, which\u00a0spans the Apurimac River near Huinchiri, Peru, in the Province of Canas. Dangerous work: Local villagers work on renewing the Keshwa Chaca - the last Inca rope bridge - in the Andes near Huinchiri, Peru Incredible skill: The 90ft long Keshwa Chaca remains thanks to local villagers who rebuild the bridge each year using the same techniques as their Inca ancestors\n@highlight\nInca kingdom in the Andes was connected via handwoven rope bridges\n@highlight\nToday, only one bridge remains - the Keshwa Chaca near Huinchiri, Peru\n@highlight\nThe 90ft-long bridge is rebuilt by villagers over three days every June, before gradually\u00a0disintegrating\u00a0each time\n@highlight\nLocals use the same techniques to make the rope as their Inca ancestors\nQuery: The last @placeholder disappeared in the early 17th century, and over the years their bridges followed.\n\nOptions : A. Andes\nB. Inca\nC. Peru\nD. Incas\nE. Apurimac River\nF. Keshwa Chaca\nG. Huinchiri\nH. Canas\nI. Province\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1584, "output_tokens": 24, "total_tokens": 1608}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_18766", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Everyone has that friend who instigates a wild night out, encourages you to have one drink too many, but gets you home in one piece. Now there's a 'smart beer mug' that does a similar thing. Fitted with sensors, the ePint lights up when it is empty, keeps track of the number of drinks its user has sunk and can even suggest ordering a cab at the end of the night. Start-up Xtreme Tech, based in Los Angeles, California, is raising money to put the gadget into production on Kickstarter. The firm audaciously describes its invention as 'Vegas in a cup'.\n@highlight\nePint contains sensors, LEDs and a Bluetooth chip to link to a phone\n@highlight\nIt lights up to show when it is empty or when a sports team has scored\n@highlight\nApp features let users play drinking games and even order a cab home\n@highlight\nGadget is available to pre-order via Kickstarter from $30 (\u00a320)\nQuery: The ePint also has a built-in weight sensor to track how much liquid it is holding, accelerometers and @placeholder that flash and change colour, as well as a bottle opener so it can be filled with beer quickly.\n\nOptions : A. App\nB. Kickstarter\nC. Bluetooth\nD. California\nE. LEDs\nF. Gadget\nG. Los Angeles\nH. Vegas\nI. Xtreme Tech\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E. LEDs}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1420, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 1452}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_15366", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: William Tallon was more than just the Queen Mother\u2019s favourite servant. He rose from impoverished beginnings to become her confidant and close friend. As the first part of a remarkable new biography revealed last week, Tallon was also a predatory homosexual who breached Royal security by bringing young men back to Clarence House at night. And he made powerful enemies. Here, in the final extract of Backstairs Billy, we reveal that courtiers took their revenge by banishing him from the Queen Mother\u2019s side, shamefully disregarding her wish that he should be allowed to live at Clarence House for the rest of his life.\n@highlight\nQueen Mother's royal courtier William Tallon was known as Backstairs Billy\n@highlight\nRose from impoverished beginnings to become her confidant and friend\n@highlight\nBut he also breached protocol and brought young men to Clarence House\n@highlight\nOther courtiers took revenge by banishing him from Queen Mother's side\n@highlight\nAlso denied her request that he should be allowed to live at Clarence House for the rest of his life\nQuery: For years he had organised lunches and dinners for the @placeholder, but he had never had to make his own meals.\n\nOptions : A. Royal\nB. Mother\nC. Queen\nD. Queen Mother\nE. Clarence House\nF. Tallon\nG. William Tallon\nH. Backstairs Billy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D. Queen Mother}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1376, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": 1412}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_12613", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: It's the social and health crisis plaguing almost one million Japanese people. The sufferers of 'Hikikomori' \u2013 mostly young men - have such severe social withdrawal they isolate themselves in their bedroom, in some cases for years. One of the few hikikomori experts in Japan, Dr Takahiro Kato, suffered from the condition as a student and is now working to prevent it from having a widespread affect on the next generation. Dr Kato, who is studying hikikomori with a team of experts at Kyushu University in Fukuoka, said he had seen cases so severe that some men in their 50s had been withdrawn from society for more than 30 years.\n@highlight\n'Hikikomori' is a social and health crisis affect almost one million Japanese\n@highlight\nSufferers have such severe social withdrawal they isolate themselves in their bedroom, in some cases for years\n@highlight\nDoctors are working to stop it having a major affect on the next generation\nQuery: 'It\u2019s one reason why @placeholder have many more hikikomori compared to western society.'\n\nOptions : A. Hikikomori\nB. Sufferers\nC. Japan\nD. Kato\nE. Kyushu University\nF. Fukuoka\nG. Japanese\nH. Takahiro Kato\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1380, "output_tokens": 24, "total_tokens": 1404}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_15745", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) You will be able to test yourself at home for a genetic predisposition for certain diseases, thanks to a new ruling from the US Food and Drug Administration. On Thursday, the FDA gave 23andMe permission to market its Personal Genome Service genetic health risk tests for 10 diseases. It is the first direct-to-consumer genetic test the FDA has allowed to provide that information. The tests can look for a genetic predisposition to conditions; the 10 approved Thursday are Parkinson's; late-onset Alzheimer's; celiac disease; a movement disorder called early-onset primary dystonia; a disorder that elevates your risk for lung and liver disease called Alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency; a blood clotting disorder Factor XI deficiency; an organ and tissue disorder called Gaucher disease type 1; a red blood cell condition known as G6PD; hereditary hemochromatosis, an iron overload disorder; and hereditary thrombophilia, a blood clot disorder.\n@highlight\n23andMe gets FDA approval to market its genetic tests for 10 diseases\n@highlight\nThese tests do not give a diagnosis but suggest whether you have a predisposition\nQuery: Environmental factors and lifestyle choices probably influence whether someone will get a disease like late-onset @placeholder's.\n\nOptions : A. US Food and Drug Administration\nB. Alpha-1\nC. Personal Genome Service\nD. G6PD\nE. Alzheimer\nF. Gaucher\nG. FDA\nH. Parkinson\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1496, "output_tokens": 26, "total_tokens": 1522}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_10724", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: In among all the pomp and ceremony surrounding the Apple Music launch, the firm has quietly killed off its Home Sharing feature, outraging many users. Before the iOS 8.4 update, Home Sharing let people share their iTunes music with other iOS devices on the same Wi-Fi network and was a favourite among families. But since Apple rolled out the software the feature has seemingly vanished and there has been no word as to why, leading to angry tweets and forum posts. The iOS 8.4 update was released to add the Apple Music app to phones and tablets. It also redesigned the music player and tweaked the iTunes Store.\n@highlight\nReports about the demise of Home Sharing appeared on Twitter this week\n@highlight\nAlthough Apple hasn't confirmed the change, it is likely to have been removed because it rivalled Apple's Family plan on Apple Music\n@highlight\nFor $14.99 a month, a family of six can share an Apple Music subscription\n@highlight\nThis is similar to what Home Sharing offered for free on any Wi-Fi network\nQuery: Many disgruntled users have also taken to the @placeholder support forums to complain about the changes.\n\nOptions : A. Wi\nB. iTunes Store\nC. Twitter\nD. Fi\nE. Home Sharing\nF. Apple Music\nG. Apple\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage mentions that users expressed their anger on \"Twitter\" and \"forum posts,\" and the query specifies users took to the \"@placeholder support forums,\" which aligns with the forum references in the passage. However, the best option that fits the context of the query about support forums is not directly stated in the passage, but among the options, \"Twitter\" is the only platform explicitly mentioned in the highlights where complaints appeared. The query says \"support forums,\" but the passage mentions \"angry tweets and forum posts,\" so \"Twitter\" is a direct match for the highlighted complaints.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1648, "output_tokens": 152, "total_tokens": 1800}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_18033", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Arkansas' Supreme Court on Friday afternoon stopped any more same-sex marriages in the state, a court spokeswoman said, leaving the legal status of more than 400 gay and lesbian couples who got marriage licenses in limbo. This development stems from 21 couples' legal challenge of Amendment 83 to the Arkansas Constitution, arguing that it violates their federal and state rights of equal protection and privacy. Pulaski County Circuit Judge Chris Piazza ruled in their favor last Friday. But same-sex marriage was back up in the air after the state Supreme Court said Wednesday it couldn't decide whether to grant an emergency stay because Piazza's decision was \"not final.\"\n@highlight\nA state judge in Arkansas earlier struck down same-sex marriage ban\n@highlight\nArkansas Supreme Court grants a stay, thus preventing more such marriages\n@highlight\nStatus of couples who got marriage licenses is unclear\nQuery: @placeholder, at least, was issuing marriage licenses to same-sex couples by Thursday afternoon.\n\nOptions : A. Arkansas Supreme Court\nB. Supreme Court\nC. Arkansas\nD. Chris Piazza\nE. Amendment 83\nF. Piazza\nG. Arkansas Constitution\nH. Pulaski County\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1232, "output_tokens": 26, "total_tokens": 1258}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_13469", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: A solar system including five Earth-sized planets has been discovered which is so ancient it was born not long after the dawn of time - and experts say it could help find life on planets far older than we expected. The system's parent star, named Kepler-444, is 117 light years from Earth and 11.2 billion years old. When the sun-like star was formed out of a primordial cloud of gas and dust, the universe was just a fifth of its current age. Astronomers made the discovery after trawling through four years' worth of data collected by Nasa's Kepler space telescope.\n@highlight\nSolar system's parent star, named Kepler-444, is 117 light years from Earth\n@highlight\n11.2 billion-year-old star formed when the universe was a fifth of its age\n@highlight\nFive Earth-sized planets orbit the star with years equivalent to 10 days\n@highlight\nFind shows Earth-sized planets have formed throughout universe's history\nQuery: However, the chances of an advanced race of beings living on any of the planets are remote, despite @placeholder being\u00a025 per cent smaller and 700 degrees cooler than the sun.\n\nOptions : A. Kepler\nB. Nasa\nC. Astronomers\nD. Solar\nE. Earth\nF. Five Earth\nG. Kepler-444\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G. Kepler-444}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1408, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 1488}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_13086", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) The long awaited La Ni\u00f1a, which was first predicted by the Climate Prediction Center (CPC) back in April, has finally arrived in the Pacific Ocean, NOAA announced Thursday -- and it's expected to stick around through the winter. La Ni\u00f1a conditions, which are characterized by below-normal sea surface temperatures in the tropical Pacific, were observed during October and have persisted into November -- prompting the CPC to raise the ENSO Alert System from a La Ni\u00f1a Watch to a La Ni\u00f1a Advisory. La Ni\u00f1a, much like its warmer counterpart, El Ni\u00f1o, have far reaching global impacts extending beyond the Pacific Ocean.\n@highlight\nLa Ni\u00f1a is characterized by a cooling of ocean waters in the Pacific\n@highlight\nThe climate pattern is likely to worsen drought in the southeastern US\nQuery: It will be interesting to see if this @placeholder can slow down the rapidly rising global temperatures and prevent 2016 from outpacing 2015 and becoming the third consecutive hottest year for the planet.\n\nOptions : A. US\nB. NOAA\nC. Climate Prediction Center\nD. La Ni\u00f1a\nE. El Ni\u00f1o\nF. Pacific\nG. ENSO Alert System\nH. CPC\nI. La Ni\u00f1a Advisory\nJ. Pacific Ocean\nK. La Ni\u00f1a Watch\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage discusses La Ni\u00f1a and its potential to affect global temperatures. The blank refers to something that could \"slow down the rapidly rising global temperatures,\" which aligns with La Ni\u00f1a's cooling effect.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1656, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 1746}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_14200", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Connellsville, PennsylvaniaJudy Keller, 69, has always relied on Highlands Hospital for medical care, just as her parents did before her. When she walks through the halls, she recognizes faces from the community and even from her days working as a school teacher. The 64-bed facility, she says, is a mainstay of this rural Southwest Pennsylvania town. \"This hospital all my life has been here,\" said Keller, now retired. \"[It] helps a lot of people who don't have adequate health care coverage \u2014 and I don't know what they would do without it.\" Aside from providing health care to a largely poor population, it provides hundreds of jobs in a town that locals say never recovered after industries such as coal mining and glass manufacturing disappeared.\n@highlight\nAffordable Care Act helped vital but financially troubled rural hospitals\n@highlight\nA full repeal of the law could signal their death knell\nQuery: Despite that, @placeholder CFO Andursky said he barely noticed the increase \u2014 the threat of closure is a \"daily concern,\" he said.\n\nOptions : A. Southwest Pennsylvania\nB. Affordable Care Act\nC. PennsylvaniaJudy Keller\nD. Connellsville\nE. Keller\nF. Highlands Hospital\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1256, "output_tokens": 27, "total_tokens": 1283}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_11037", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Fast food giant Domino\u2019s is selling \u2018Frankenfood\u2019 pizzas to customers while claiming to be \u2018GM-free\u2019 on its website. It has emerged that their \u2018thin and crispy\u2019 pizza bases have been made using genetically modified soya bean oil and maize flour since February. Waitrose has also been selling imported American confectionery which contains GM sugar beet and a soya derivative and Marks & Spencer has been stocking American sauces and cookies containing GM soya and corn \u2013 even though the firm has previously boasted about not using GM ingredients. Fast food giant Domino\u2019s is selling \u2018Frankenfood\u2019 pizzas to customers while claiming to be \u2018GM-free\u2019 on its website\n@highlight\n'Thin and crispy' pizza bases made using GM soya bean oil and maize flour since February\n@highlight\nWaitrose selling imported US confectionery containing GM sugar beet and soya derivative\n@highlight\nMarks & Spencer has been stocking American sauces and cookies that contain GM soya and corn\n@highlight\nThe double-dealing has been identified by the campaign group GM Freeze\nQuery: And a Waitrose spokesman insisted that any GM ingredients in @placeholder chocolate stocked by the store were \u2018clearly labelled\u2019.\n\nOptions : A. US\nB. Thin\nC. Domino\nD. Domino\u2019s\nE. GM\nF. Waitrose\nG. Marks & Spencer\nH. Frankenfood\nI. American\nJ. GM Freeze\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1400, "output_tokens": 24, "total_tokens": 1424}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_17965", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) Long-term use of acetaminophen during pregnancy was associated with twice the risk of attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder in children, according to a study published Monday in the journal Pediatrics. However, two experts believe that the data do not support these findings. Acetaminophen, also known as paracetamol, is the active ingredient in Tylenol and hundreds of over-the-counter and prescription medicines, according to the US Food and Drug Administration. It is commonly prescribed during pregnancy to relieve pain and fever, with an estimated 65% of pregnant women in America using the drug, according to the US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention.\n@highlight\nResearchers collected data from about 95,000 mothers with children born between 1999 and 2009\n@highlight\nLong-term acetaminophen use in pregnancy is related to more than a twofold increase in risk for ADHD in children\n@highlight\nThe data does not support their conclusions, other experts say\nQuery: No evidence of a cause-effect relationship between the drug and @placeholder was found, Ystr\u00f8m and his colleagues concluded.\n\nOptions : A. US Food and Drug Administration\nB. Acetaminophen\nC. Long\nD. Pediatrics\nE. America\nF. Tylenol\nG. ADHD\nH. US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The passage states that the study found an association between long-term acetaminophen use during pregnancy and ADHD in children, but other experts say the data do not support these findings. The query mentions \"no evidence of a cause-effect relationship between the drug and @placeholder,\" so the placeholder refers to the condition studied, which is ADHD.\n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1732, "output_tokens": 111, "total_tokens": 1843}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_12215", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: George Osborne today refused to match Labour's pledge not to increase VAT as a row erupted over how to balance the books after the election. The Chancellor declined to give a 'cast-iron guarantee'\u00a0to match Labour's pledge not to increase VAT over the five years of the next Parliament. It came after Labour's shadow chancellor Ed Balls that Conservatives had a history of raising VAT after elections despite saying they had no plans to do so during the campaign. Scroll down for video Chancellor George Osborne declined to give a 'cast-iron guarantee' to match Labour's pledge not to increase VAT from 20 per cent over the five years of the next Parliament\n@highlight\nLabour's Ed Balls unveils poster warning Tories will hike VAT again\n@highlight\nOsborne used first Budget in 2010 to increase rate from 17.5% to 20%\n@highlight\nChancellor insists his plans to balance books do not require new increase\n@highlight\nBut he\u00a0repeatedly\u00a0refused to match Labour's promise ahead of election\nQuery: Mr Balls claimed the @placeholder 'have a secret plan to raise VAT again'\n\nOptions : A. George Osborne\nB. Budget\nC. Ed Balls\nD. Tories\nE. Parliament\nF. Osborne\nG. Labour\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D. Tories}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1304, "output_tokens": 30, "total_tokens": 1334}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_11580", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: The EU's migration chief has urged European leaders to stop thinking about whether accepting refugees into their country will affect the next election. Dimitris Avramopoulos hinted that EU heads of state is letting their worry about how their actions in response to the migration crisis will be seen by voters cloud their humanitarian judgement. The 62-year-old said EU leaders should think more like the Commission, which does not need to be re-elected and therefore does not take into account how their actions might change public opinion. Avramopoulois is European Commissioner for Migration, Home Affairs and Citizenship and has served as both Defence and Foreign Minister in Greece as well as Mayor of Athens.\n@highlight\nDimitris Avramopoulos said EU leaders must stop thinking of next election\n@highlight\nEU Migration chief said to stop thinking about 'political cost' of refugees\n@highlight\nSaid reason for delay in action on crisis was that EU was taken by surprise\nQuery: 'The @placeholder is here for five years to do its job and we did it with vision, responsibility and commitment.\n\nOptions : A. Greece\nB. EU Migration\nC. Said\nD. EU\nE. Dimitris Avramopoulos\nF. Commission\nG. Citizenship\nH. European\nI. Athens\nJ. Avramopoulois\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1316, "output_tokens": 24, "total_tokens": 1340}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_13747", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) \"Yessssss!\" was my reaction to hearing the news that the U.S. Food and Drug Administration intends to regulate e-cigarettes, hookahs, vape pens, e-pipes and other electronic nicotine delivery products. As a family physician, I often have patients ask me about e-cigarettes. Some have seen advertisements and are wondering what they are; some have simply heard that e-cigarettes are safer than traditional cigarettes and want to know if this is true. E-cigarettes are included in the category of ENDS -- Electronic Nicotine Delivery Systems -- products that use a liquid containing nicotine and varying amounts of flavor, glycerin, propylene glycol and other ingredients. This liquid is heated into an aerosol that users then smoke. It is often referred to as \"vaping.\"\n@highlight\nJennifer Caudle says FDA regulation of electronic nicotine delivery systems is overdue\n@highlight\nMore research needed on long-term effects, especially as youth use skyrockets, she says\nQuery: The effect of e-cigarettes and @placeholder on children is also an issue -- especially given the growth of e-cigarette use among teens in recent years.\n\nOptions : A. Yessssss!\nB. Electronic Nicotine Delivery Systems\nC. FDA\nD. Jennifer Caudle\nE. CNN\nF. U.S. Food and Drug Administration\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B. Electronic Nicotine Delivery Systems}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1340, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 1388}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_14974", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: One way or another, Chile's Copa America semi-final with Peru will be settled in Santiago on Monday night, but the two nations will continue to bicker long after the full-time whistle. Whether the debate centres on cocktails or overhead kicks, agreeing to disagree is the only thing these two rivals will concede to one another. And the clash  - the most important in almost 20 years - will re-open old wounds in what is one of football's fiercest yet little-known rivalries. The animosity dates back to the four-year War of the Pacific at the end of the nineteenth century, hence its tag as the 'Pacific Clasico'. The 1879-1883 conflict, which also involved Bolivia, was fought over the supply of nitrates and ended with Chile annexing large parts of its neighbours' territory.\n@highlight\nChile and Peru meet in the semi-finals of the Copa America\n@highlight\nThe two nations have had animosity ever since the War of the Pacific\n@highlight\nThey also disagree on where the local spirit Pisco\u00a0originates\u00a0from\n@highlight\nChile are favourites for the clash after impressing during the tournament\nQuery: Perhaps not, but don't expect the respective fans to come together for a glass of @placeholder afterwards, either.\n\nOptions : A. Copa America\nB. War of the Pacific\nC. Santiago\nD. Peru\nE. Bolivia\nF. Chile\nG. Pisco\nH. Pacific Clasico\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G. Pisco}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1484, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 1527}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_11849", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Airlines have been forced to cancel another day of flights to Denpasar as volcanic ash continues to make its way over Bali's airspace. By 1pm, Jetstar had announced all of Thursday's flights to the holiday island had been stopped, assuring it would resume them as soon as the Volcanic Ash Advisory Centre deemed it safe to do so. Virgin has meanwhile cancelled all flights bound for Bali from Australia for both Thursday and Friday. The carrier said it would make a decision about resuming the flights headed to Australia from Denpasar midday Friday. 'Unfavourable winds have pushed the ash cloud close to Denpasar Airport over the last day and we're not satisfied it is safe to operate services in these conditions,' a statement from Jetstar said.\n@highlight\nJetstar has called off all of Thursday's flights to the holiday island\n@highlight\nVirgin has  cancelled all flights bound for Bali  for both Thursday and Friday\n@highlight\nThey will\u00a0resume flights when Volcanic Ash Advisory Centre deems it safe\n@highlight\nIt comes as winds bring ash from the Mount Raung volcano over Denpasar\nQuery: Jestar customers have been urged to check the status of their flight on Jetstar.com before travelling to airports while @placeholder is directing passengers to change their booking to another flight, which can be made at no extra charge in the next 14 days unless they prefer a full travel credit.\n\nOptions : A. Mount Raung\nB. Denpasar\nC. Australia\nD. Bali\nE. Virgin\nF. Jetstar\nG. Volcanic Ash Advisory Centre\nH. Denpasar Airport\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E. Virgin}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1604, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 1652}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_11950", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (ArsTechnica) -- The Federal Communications Commission is releasing the details of its new net neutrality Order in stages. Although the FCC's new ban on \"unreasonable discrimination\" for wired ISPs allows certain kinds of traffic discrimination (not all bits need be equal), the agency made clear after Tuesday's meeting that \"paid prioritization\" deals with Internet companies are unlikely to be allowed. Critics had worried that the new Order would only affect outright website blocking, leaving paid prioritization untouched (or even implicitly sanctioned). \"Pay for Priority Unlikely to Satisfy 'No Unreasonable Discrimination' Rule,\" advises one subheading of the new net neutrality rules. Ed Whitacre's dream of directly charging Google and Yahoo to \"use his pipes\" -- a key event in starting the entire net neutrality debate -- appears to be dashed.\n@highlight\nThe FCC's new rules forbid Internet providers from blocking lawful content\n@highlight\nCritics worried that the new Order would leave paid prioritization untouched\n@highlight\nFCC: Reasonable network management shall not constitute unreasonable discrimination\nQuery: \"Even open Internet skeptics acknowledge that pay for priority may disadvantage non-commercial uses of the network, which are typically less able to pay for priority, and for which the @placeholder is a uniquely important platform.\"\n\nOptions : A. Google\nB. Internet\nC. ISPs\nD. Yahoo\nE. new Order\nF. Ed Whitacre\nG. FCC\nH. Unreasonable Discrimination' Rule\nI. ArsTechnica\nJ. Federal Communications Commission\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1492, "output_tokens": 24, "total_tokens": 1516}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_17584", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: America's largest internet providers have been accused off ripping off customers and 'throttling' their internet connections. Major providers, including AT&T, Time Warner and Verizon, are all slowing users, many slowing to the speed of a dial up connection at times - despite recent net neutrality rulings which outlaw such practices. Researchers analysed online tests taken by 300,00 people in major cities. This test measures whether interconnection points are experiencing problems. It runs speed measurements from your (the test user\u2019s) ISP, across multiple interconnection points, detecting degraded performance. They says the evidence collected points to slowdowns for users on the networks of five of the largest Internet access providers \u2014 AT&T, CenturyLink, Comcast, Time Warner Cable and Verizon \u2014 which represent 75 percent of all U.S. wireline households\n@highlight\nReport analysed results from 300,000 internet users in major cities\n@highlight\nFound AT&T, Time Warner and Verizon \u00a0all slowed data speeds at times\nQuery: 'In truth, the big phone and cable companies are terrified that so many people are performing the speed tests and compiling data on what ails the @placeholder.,' he said.\n\nOptions : A. Time Warner Cable\nB. AT&T\nC. U.S.\nD. Internet\nE. Verizon\nF. America\nG. Comcast\nH. Time Warner\nI. CenturyLink\nJ. ISP\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D. Internet}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1420, "output_tokens": 42, "total_tokens": 1462}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_15955", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) According to a recent survey, 72% of Americans think coconut oil is a healthy food. But despite popular health claims about coconut oil, a report from the American Heart Association recently advised against its use, stating that it increases LDL cholesterol (a cause of cardiovascular disease) and has no known offsetting effects. \"There are many claims being made about coconut oil being wonderful for lots of different things, but we really don't have any evidence of long-term health benefits,\" said Dr. Walter C. Willett, professor of epidemiology and nutrition at the Harvard T.H. Chan School of Public Health. How exactly, then, does coconut oil rank among oils?\n@highlight\nCoconut oil increases LDL cholesterol, a cause of cardiovascular disease\n@highlight\nBut coconut oil does a particularly nice job of raising HDL, the \"good\" cholesterol\nQuery: Still, though the increase in @placeholder seen with consumption of coconut oil may offset some of the disease risk, it's still not as good as consuming unsaturated oils, which not only raise HDL but lower LDL, according to Willett.\n\nOptions : A. LDL\nB. American Heart Association\nC. Americans\nD. Walter C. Willett\nE. HDL\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1581, "output_tokens": 269, "total_tokens": 1850}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_17871", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) Prepare to say goodbye to Cassini. In the early morning hours of September 15, NASA's 13-year mission exploring Saturn and its moons will come to an end as the spacecraft deliberately dives into Saturn's atmosphere and plunges itself into the planet. Even then, Cassini will transmit new data about the planet's composition as long as its antenna remains pointed toward Earth, with the assist from small thrusters. No spacecraft has ever been so close to Saturn. \"You can think of Cassini as the first Saturn probe,\" said Linda Spilker, Cassini project scientist. The Ion and Neutral Mass Spectrometer will act as the \"nose\" of the spacecraft, directly sampling the composition and structure of the atmosphere -- something that can't be done from orbit, said Hunter Waite, team lead for the spectrometer.\n@highlight\nThe NASA Cassini mission ends Friday after 13 years observing the Saturn system\n@highlight\nCassini data has revealed groundbreaking discoveries about Saturn and its moons\nQuery: While many other options were considered -- such as \"parking\" the spacecraft in orbit around @placeholder -- they didn't want to risk Cassini colliding with any of Saturn's moons.\n\nOptions : A. Saturn\nB. NASA Cassini\nC. Cassini\nD. Ion and Neutral Mass Spectrometer\nE. Linda Spilker\nF. Hunter Waite\nG. NASA\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C. Cassini}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1412, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": 1448}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_16546", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: After months of speculation Microsoft has officially announced its Windows 10 software will launch globally on 29 July. The Washington-based firm said Windows 7 and Windows 8.1 users will have one year from this date to take advantage of the free upgrade. And once a device is upgraded to Windows 10, Microsoft said it will continue to keep it up-to-date for the supported lifetime of the device at no cost. For other Windows users, or people who don't currently run a version of the firm's operating system, they will need to pay for the software. Microsoft hasn't announced pricing but details leaked on a reseller over the weekend suggest it will start at $109.99 for the Home edition, and $149.99 for the Professional version.\n@highlight\nMicrosoft said software will launch across all 190 regions on the same day\n@highlight\nIt will power PCs, phones and connected devices such as bank machines and medical equipment, along with the firm's Xbox One console\n@highlight\nWindows 7 and 8.1 users will have a year from 29 July to get free upgrade\n@highlight\nAnd Microsoft will support the software for the lifetime of the device\nQuery: Although the new software won't be formally released until next year, analysts already consider its success crucial for @placeholder and Satya Nadella.\n\nOptions : A. Xbox One\nB. Windows 8.1\nC. Windows 7\nD. Windows 10\nE. Microsoft\nF. PCs\nG. Windows\nH. Washington\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1552, "output_tokens": 24, "total_tokens": 1576}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_18633", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: The Earth experienced its hottest month of March since record-keeping began in 1880. There's been no break from the globe's record heat - the first three months of 2015 have all set new high temperature marks. Last month's average temperature soared to 56.4\u00b0F (13.6\u00b0C), which is 1.5\u00b0F (0.85\u00b0C) above the average for the 20th century. Last month's average temperature of 56.4\u00b0F (13.6\u00b0C) was the hottest March on record, averaging 1.5\u00b0F (0.85\u00b0C) above the average for the 20th century. This was the highest for March in the 1880\u20132015 record, surpassing the previous record of 2010 by 0.09\u00b0F (0.05\u00b0C). Pictured is how the high temperatures affected different regions of the world\n@highlight\nWorld experience average temperatures of 56.4\u00b0F (13.6\u00b0C) last month - 1.5\u00b0F above average for the 20th century\n@highlight\nFirst 3 months of 2015 have set new high temperature marks, and the trend could continue throughout the year\n@highlight\nScientists warn fossil fuels are pushing greenhouse gas into the atmosphere, leading to increased temperatures\n@highlight\nBut El Ni\u00f1o, a blob of record hot water in the Northeast Pacific Ocean, could also be driving up temperatures\nQuery: 'Many climate prediction models show this weak @placeholder continuing into summer.'\n\nOptions : A. 56.4\u00b0F\nB. F (13.6\u00b0C\nC. Earth\nD. Northeast Pacific Ocean\nE. El Ni\u00f1o\nF. 0.09\u00b0F\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E. El Ni\u00f1o}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1768, "output_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 1808}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_16736", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Nasa has selected a variety of companies to work on projects to create advanced space technologies, including faster methods of propulsion. Other projects to be worked on include improved habitats for humans, and small satellites to explore deep space. And one of the companies in the 12 Next Space Technologies for Exploration Partnerships (NextStep) says they have an engine that could get humans to Mars in just 39 days. Scroll down for video Nasa has selected a variety of companies to work on projects to create advanced space technologies, including a faster method of propulsion known as Vasimr (illustrated), which could apparently get to Mars in a matter of weeks, not months\n@highlight\nCompany in Texas has been asked to develop its revolutionary engine\n@highlight\nAd Astra's Vasimr engine could apparently get to Mars in 39 days\n@highlight\nIt is one of 12 advanced technology projects to be funded by Nasa\n@highlight\nOthers include new types of habitation and small deep space satellites\nQuery: Whether an engine such as @placeholder could shorten the time it would take to cover the distance, though, remains to be seen.\n\nOptions : A. Nasa\nB. Ad Astra\nC. NextStep\nD. Texas\nE. Mars\nF. Next Space Technologies for Exploration Partnerships\nG. Vasimr\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G. Vasimr}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1356, "output_tokens": 36, "total_tokens": 1392}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_12469", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: At the end of last year Apple overtook sales of Android devices for the first time since 2012. And in a bid to fuel this trend further, the Californian tech giant is reportedly planning to extend its\u00a0recycling\u00a0and trade-in scheme to include rival handsets. Reports claim Android, as well as BlackBerry and potentially Windows Phone customers, will be able to exchange their handsets for gift cards and credit towards Apple products. Apple is reportedly planning to extend the recycling and trade-in scheme it launched in 2013 (pictured) to include rival handsets. Reports claim Android, as well as BlackBerry and potentially Windows Phone customers, will be able to exchange their handsets for gift cards and credit towards an Apple product\n@highlight\nApple launched its iPhone Reuse and Recycle trade-in scheme in 2013\n@highlight\nIt gives Apple credit to put towards the purchase of a new device\n@highlight\nSources said Apple will soon accept non-iOS devices on this program\n@highlight\nThis includes Android, Windows Phone and BlackBerry handsets\n@highlight\nEmployees are being trained in the changes now and the scheme is expected to launch 'in the coming weeks'\nQuery: The amount of credit depends on the device and its condition, and its likely that figures for Android handsets, which are typically much cheaper than @placeholder phones, will be low under the scheme.\n\nOptions : A. Android\nB. Windows Phone\nC. Californian\nD. BlackBerry\nE. Recycle\nF. iPhone Reuse\nG. non-iOS\nH. Apple\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1552, "output_tokens": 26, "total_tokens": 1578}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_13409", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: A group of Belgian holidaymakers who were heading to the French Alps for a few days of skiing wound up being taken on a major detour thanks to their coach driver\u2019s sat-nav mistake. The driver wasn\u2019t familiar with the route to La Plagne, a popular destination for ski tourists, and mistakenly drove the tour group to the South of France after selecting the wrong destination on his GPS. Instead of entering La Plagne into his sat-nav, the driver entered Plagne, located in the French Pyrenees, putting the group of 50 holidaymakers on a nearly 800-mile detour, Belgian media reported. The tourists were travelling to La Plagne in the French Alps, but were driven towards the South of France\n@highlight\nGroup of 50 holidaymakers were travelling to La Plagne in the French Alps\n@highlight\nTheir coach driver selected Plagne, in the French Pyrenees, as destination\n@highlight\nThe driver turned around in Toulouse after realising his error\n@highlight\nTour group arrived at La Plagne nearly 24 hours behind schedule\nQuery: By the time the driver realised his mistake the group was already in Toulouse, nearly 425 miles south-west of @placeholder.\n\nOptions : A. French\nB. Alps\nC. French Pyrenees\nD. Toulouse\nE. Plagne\nF. La Plagne\nG. French Alps\nH. Belgian\nI. South of France\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H. Belgian}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1827, "output_tokens": 39, "total_tokens": 1866}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_14349", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: (CNN) With just two weeks until Congress is expected to leave town, the fate of roughly 700,000 young immigrants still hangs in the balance. And, it could be up to Senate Democrats now to decide whether they will make protections for the Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals (DACA) program recipients a condition of their support for a must-pass spending bill or punt the issue to next year when they still have months to work it out. There's a whole host of issues that must be dealt with by the end of the year including reauthorizing a spying program, funding disaster relief and paying for the Children's Health Insurance Program, which has all sparked questions about whether Democrats will insist DACA also be included in that list of year-end spending priorities.\n@highlight\nDemocrats have repeatedly called for a fix to the ending of the DACA program\n@highlight\nThe party may have the most leverage as part of their year-end negotiations\nQuery: The President had spoken favorably in September about DACA recipients and pushed @placeholder to reach a deal, but in recent weeks ne has taken to hardline rhetoric on illegal immigration and blaming Democrats for crime.\n\nOptions : A. Children's Health Insurance Program\nB. Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals\nC. Democrats\nD. DACA\nE. Congress\nF. Senate\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D. DACA}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1320, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 1368}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_16724", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Apple promised it would offer an Android version of its music service in autumn. And it seems it is on track, if leaked images spotted by German website Mobile Geeks are anything to go by. Screenshots seem to show Apple Music features including Beats 1 Radio and the built-in social network Apple Music Connect, as well as Android hallmarks such as sliding sidebars. Shots of the beta version of the app show the 'For Me' recommendations page as well as features not currently available on the iOS version, such as the ability to change the size of the cache used to store music offline, 9to5Mac reported.\n@highlight\nLeaked screenshots were spotted by German website Mobile Geeks\n@highlight\nSeem to show standard Apple Music features including Beats 1 Radio and the built-in social network Apple Music Connect with Android functionality\n@highlight\nApple has previously said the service will launch on Android this autumn\nQuery: It noted the design still looks like an @placeholder product, but the functions are geared towards Android, rather than iPhone users.\n\nOptions : A. For Me\nB. Beats 1 Radio\nC. German\nD. Android\nE. Apple Music Connect\nF. Apple Music\nG. Mobile Geeks\nH. Apple\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D. Android}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1268, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 1300}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_12315", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: NASA has given the people of Earth a rare treat: A color mosaic that captures not only Saturn, but also the tiny dots of Earth and other planets in the background. The panorama, released Tuesday, was captured by the Cassini spacecraft on July 19, when the sun slipped behind the ringed planet. Earth appears as a bright blue dot to Saturn's lower right, just above Saturn's outer, halo-like E-ring. Venus is a dot to the upper left, with Mars appearing as a faint red dot above and to the left of Venus. This is the first image in which Saturn, its moons and rings, and Earth, Venus and Mars are all visible, NASA said. The image -- a panorama of 141 wide-angle pictures -- covers 404,880 miles across Saturn and its ring system.\n@highlight\nImage is Cassini's first showing Saturn, rings, moons, Earth, Venus and Mars at same time\n@highlight\nThe collage is panorama of 141 wide-angle pictures taken July 19\n@highlight\nImage was possible that day because Saturn obstructed spacecraft's view of sun\nQuery: Cassini images showing both Saturn and Earth are rare because the sun is so close to Earth, that targeting the blue planet would damage @placeholder's sensors, NASA says.\n\nOptions : A. Saturn\nB. Venus\nC. Cassini\nD. Earth\nE. NASA\nF. Cassini spacecraft\nG. Mars\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1806, "output_tokens": 45, "total_tokens": 1851}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_9693", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Marking one of England\u2019s most stunning military victories always takes something special. The Battle of Agincourt, where Henry V\u2019s outnumbered army defeated the French against the odds, got just that at a rousing service to commemorate its 600th anniversary yesterday. Henry\u2019s sword, normally kept safely in a museum, was back in the thick of the action, solemnly carried through Westminster Abbey at the start before being placed on the High Altar. Later came high drama as an armour-clad thespian, his forehead spattered with stage-blood, delivered the English king\u2019s inspiring \u2018We few, we happy few, we band of brothers\u2019 speech from Shakespeare\u2019s Henry the Fifth, the play which immortalised the battle.\n@highlight\nCommemoration took place in central London in remembrance of clash\n@highlight\nBattle took place in a farmer's field in northern France on October 25, 1415\n@highlight\nSmall band of English and Welsh archers beat vast French army in one day\n@highlight\nYesterday's service included\u00a0re-enactment and  King Henry V's sword\nQuery: Yesterday was chosen for the service because it took four days for the news of victory to arrive back in @placeholder.\n\nOptions : A. Henry V\nB. French\nC. England\nD. High Altar\nE. Westminster Abbey\nF. Battle of Agincourt\nG. English\nH. Henry\nI. Shakespeare\nJ. Henry\u2019s\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C. England}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1472, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 1504}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_12894", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: Microsoft's Windows 10 software has only been available in its final form for a few hours - but experts have already warned of a major security risk in the software. The feature is designed to easily let people share wifi passwords with friends. However, experts say the feature actually automatically shares your wifi passwords with all Outlook, Skype and Facebook contacts who also use Windows 10. To change your settings, go to Network settings then Manage Wi-Fi settings (Settings > Network & Internet > Wi-Fi > Manage Wi-Fi Settings). There, you can choose which contacts you share Wi-Fi settings with.\n@highlight\nFeature designed to easily let people share wifi passwords with friends.\n@highlight\nExperts say the feature is 'an accident waiting to happen'\nQuery: 'In practice \u2013 @placeholder have, somewhere, an enormous database full of people's passwords.\n\nOptions : A. Windows 10\nB. Facebook\nC. Wi\nD. Skype\nE. Microsoft\nF. Fi\nG. Fi Settings\nH. Outlook\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1076, "output_tokens": 21, "total_tokens": 1097}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "SuperGLUE-ClozeTest_9533", "prompt": "Read the following passage and answer the question by choosing the best option. Provide only the text of the correct option as your answer.\n\nPassage: If Jenson Button has competed in a British Grand Prix for the last time, it can conclusively be said that his association with it was jinxed. He has never so much as had a podium in 16 attempts, and his brief participation in yesterday\u2019s race was fittingly disastrous. He crashed out on the first lap. \u2018I am disappointed, obviously,\u2019 said the 2009 world champion. \u2018In front of your home crowd you want to put on a good show and I wasn\u2019t able to do that after a turn-three incident and that is a shame.\u2019 Button started 18th on the grid, as McLaren-Honda continue to struggle for speed and reliability, and was ensnared in a collision involving the two Lotus cars.\n@highlight\nJenson Button's 16th British Grand Prix lasted less than 20 seconds\n@highlight\nButton's\u00a0miserable\u00a0luck at the race continued in a pile up at turn three\n@highlight\nIt is the first time since 2002 that Button has failed to finish three races\nQuery: But it was not total doom and gloom at @placeholder, with Alonso scoring his first point of the season.\n\nOptions : A. Honda\nB. British Grand Prix\nC. Jenson Button\nD. Button\nE. McLaren\nF. Lotus\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the contetn of the correct option. ", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The placeholder refers to \"British Grand Prix\" as the event where Alonso scored his first point, contrasting with Button's misfortune.\n\n\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1684, "output_tokens"