\n\nContext: Because of the decision, Sofia asked the students to suggest specific types of food. If 279 students suggested adding mashed potatoes while 234 suggested adding bacon to the menu,\n\nQuestion: how many students participated in the suggestion of new food items?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{513}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 560, "output_tokens": 327, "total_tokens": 887}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1962", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: While organizing her files, Bianca deleted 2 pictures, 8 songs and 7 text files.\n\nQuestion: What is the total number of files she deleted? \n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{17}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 440, "output_tokens": 155, "total_tokens": 595}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_241", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Their next destination is Lake Erie. Still in a contest, Hazel caught 48 different fishes while her father caught 46.\n\nQuestion: How many fishes did they catch in Lake Erie?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{94}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 465, "output_tokens": 232, "total_tokens": 697}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1846", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: There were nine kinds of sandwiches on the menu. Unfortunately, five of them had been sold out,\n\nQuestion: how many kinds of sandwiches do they actually provide now?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{4}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 468, "output_tokens": 222, "total_tokens": 690}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1835", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: John threw a Halloween party where 13 people showed up. If only 6 dressed up,\n\nQuestion: how many people didn't wear costumes?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{7}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 407, "output_tokens": 240, "total_tokens": 647}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_159", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Mrs. Hilt saw 21 snakes, 11 alligators, 36 frogs, and 57 bears.\n\nQuestion: How many reptiles did Mrs. Hilt see?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{32}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 412, "output_tokens": 193, "total_tokens": 605}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_238", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Rangers from Flora Natural Park and Wildlife Reserve also joined the activities on that day. They planted 75 redwood trees and 25 cypress trees to replace the trees that were destroyed during a recent forest fire.\n\nQuestion: How many trees did the rangers plant?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{100}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 564, "output_tokens": 172, "total_tokens": 736}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_224", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Last stop in their field trip was the aquarium. Penny identified 35 species of sharks, 15 species of eels and 5 different species of whales.\n\nQuestion: How many species was Penny able to identify?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{55}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 500, "output_tokens": 185, "total_tokens": 685}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1767", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: At the school Halloween party 2 girls and 9 boys dressed as ghosts.\n\nQuestion: How many people total dressed as a ghost?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{11}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 414, "output_tokens": 173, "total_tokens": 587}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_743", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Savant has 3 jars. He puts in 34 coins in the first jar, 29 coins in the second jar and 13 coins in the third jar.\n\nQuestion: How many coins does Savant save together?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{76}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 468, "output_tokens": 195, "total_tokens": 663}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_181", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: There are 43 dogs, 72 fish, and 34 cats at my farm.\n\nQuestion: How many pets do I have at my farm?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{149}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 400, "output_tokens": 187, "total_tokens": 587}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_245", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: It is Buddy's first day at a new school and he is feeling very nervous. His day begins with some bacon and egg prepared by his mother. After eating and preparing, Buddy headed out to catch the school bus from the nearest bus stop. Including Buddy, there were 39 students that got on the bus during the first stop. If 29 more students got on the bus at the second stop,\n\nQuestion: how many students are riding the bus?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{68}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 720, "output_tokens": 192, "total_tokens": 912}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_472", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Allen, Shiela's brother, likes to play with blocks. Shiela repainted Allen's old blocks in different colors. If Allen has 49 identical blocks and there are 7 blocks for every color of paint used,\n\nQuestion: how many colors did Shiela use?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{7}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 511, "output_tokens": 287, "total_tokens": 798}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_747", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: There are some rooms in a building. 35 of them are classrooms, 10 of them are office and the remaining 6 are reading rooms.\n\nQuestion: How many rooms are in the building?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{51}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 472, "output_tokens": 187, "total_tokens": 659}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_825", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Harry's magic wand is 34 cm long. Hermione's magic wand is 3 cm shorter than Harry's.\n\nQuestion: Who has the longer magic wand?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{Harry}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 428, "output_tokens": 194, "total_tokens": 622}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_829", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Emily's bed is 200 cm long. Jimmy's bed is 20 cm longer than Emily's.\n\nQuestion: Whose bed is longer?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Emily's bed is 200 cm long. Jimmy's bed is 20 cm longer, so Jimmy's bed is $200 + 20 = 220$ cm long. Therefore, Jimmy's bed is longer.\n\n\\boxed{{\\text{Jimmy's bed}}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 404, "output_tokens": 184, "total_tokens": 588}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_849", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Diana bought 12 guavas and 16 apples.\n\nQuestion: What is the ratio of guavas to apples?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{3:4}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 388, "output_tokens": 233, "total_tokens": 621}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1135", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A bakery made 19 muffins that contained nuts and 31 muffins that did not contain nuts.\n\nQuestion: What is the ratio of the number of muffins with nuts to the number of muffins without nuts?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The number of muffins with nuts is 19, and the number without nuts is 31. The ratio is therefore 19 to 31. In simplest form, the ratio is \\(\\frac{19}{31}\\).\n\n\\boxed{\\frac{19}{31}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 589, "output_tokens": 337, "total_tokens": 926}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1139", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A movie theater sold 9 child tickets. The other 41 tickets it sold were adult tickets.\n\nQuestion: What is the ratio of the number of child tickets to the number of adult tickets?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The movie theater sold 9 child tickets and 41 adult tickets.  \nThe ratio of child tickets to adult tickets is $ \\frac{9}{41} $.  \nThis ratio cannot be simplified further, so the answer is \\boxed{{\\frac{9}{41}}}.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 469, "output_tokens": 214, "total_tokens": 683}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1141", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: The students in Elise's class got to choose whether to visit the zoo or the aquarium. 15 students went to the zoo and 22 students went to the aquarium.\n\nQuestion: What is the ratio of the number of students who went to the aquarium to the number of students who went to the zoo?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "To find the ratio of the number of students who went to the aquarium to those who went to the zoo, divide the number of aquarium students by the number of zoo students: $ \\frac{22}{15} $. This ratio cannot be simplified further, so the final answer is $ \\boxed{\\left\\{\\frac{22}{15}\\right\\}} $.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 544, "output_tokens": 305, "total_tokens": 849}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1145", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: 17 students want lemonade and 11 students want iced tea.\n\nQuestion: What is the ratio of the number of students who want iced tea to the number of students who want lemonade?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "We are given that 17 students want lemonade and 11 students want iced tea.  \nThe ratio of the number of students who want iced tea to those who want lemonade is $ \\frac{11}{17} $.  \nThis ratio is already in simplest form since 11 and 17 have no common factors other than 1.\n\n\\boxed{\\frac{11}{17}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 448, "output_tokens": 350, "total_tokens": 798}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1146", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Dalton's Ice Cream Shop sold 27 sundaes with nuts and 2 sundaes without nuts.\n\nQuestion: What is the ratio of the number of sundaes with nuts to the number of sundaes without nuts?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{27:2}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 484, "output_tokens": 220, "total_tokens": 704}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1147", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Jacob's Pizzeria made 3 thin-crust pizzas and 14 thick-crust pizzas.\n\nQuestion: What is the ratio of the number of thin-crust pizzas to the number of thick-crust pizzas?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The number of thin-crust pizzas is 3, and the number of thick-crust pizzas is 14.  \nThe ratio of thin-crust to thick-crust pizzas is therefore $ \\frac{3}{14} $.  \nThis ratio cannot be simplified further, so the final answer is:\n\n\\boxed{{\\frac{3}{14}}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 472, "output_tokens": 249, "total_tokens": 721}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1148", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Alexa's Pizzeria made 13 pizzas with pepperoni and 2 pizzas without pepperoni.\n\nQuestion: What is the ratio of the number of pizzas without pepperoni to the number of pizzas with pepperoni?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "We are given that Alexa's Pizzeria made 13 pizzas with pepperoni and 2 pizzas without pepperoni.  \nThe ratio of pizzas without pepperoni to pizzas with pepperoni is $ \\frac{2}{13} $.  \nThus, the answer is \\boxed{{\\frac{2}{13}}}.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 482, "output_tokens": 223, "total_tokens": 705}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1249", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Audrey has 26 peaches. Paul has 48 peaches.\n\nQuestion: What's the difference of the number of Audrey's peaches and Paul's peaches?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{22}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 429, "output_tokens": 189, "total_tokens": 618}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1360", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Last week Howard had 26 dollars. He washed windows over the weekend and now has 52 dollars.\n\nQuestion: How much money did he make washing windows?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{26}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 439, "output_tokens": 135, "total_tokens": 574}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1751", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Will went to the state fair and rode the Ferris wheel thirteen times. If he rode it seven times during the day,\n\nQuestion: how many times did he ride it at night?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{6}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 464, "output_tokens": 170, "total_tokens": 634}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1788", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Janet's dad took the family out to eat for her birthday. There were 10 people total. There were 8 kids and everyone else was an adult.\n\nQuestion: How many adults were there?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{2}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 467, "output_tokens": 169, "total_tokens": 636}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_314", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Lastly, Rob compared Canada's CN Tower and Seattle's Space Needle.\n\nQuestion: How tall is the Space Needle if the CN Tower stands at 553 m high and it is taller than the Space Needle by 369 m?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{184}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 490, "output_tokens": 262, "total_tokens": 752}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1985", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Nancy was counting the number of people on different toys on the playground. She counted: 6, 12, 1, 12, 7, 3 and 8.\n\nQuestion: What is the mean of the people?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{7}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 464, "output_tokens": 221, "total_tokens": 685}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1425", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A boat goes 30 km upstream and 44 km downstream in 10 hours. In 13 hours, it can go 40 km upstream and 55 km downstream.\n\nQuestion: Determine the speed of the stream and that of boat in still water.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{3}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 501, "output_tokens": 1139, "total_tokens": 1640}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1466", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: The sum of the first, two times the second, and three times the third is 70.\n\nQuestion: Find three consecutive odd integers.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{9, 11, 13}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 419, "output_tokens": 382, "total_tokens": 801}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1133", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Aarav cleans 6 apartments in 2.5 hours. If Aarav cleans 30 apartments at this same rate,\n\nQuestion: how long will it take him?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{12.5}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 428, "output_tokens": 212, "total_tokens": 640}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1344", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: The base of the parallelogram is 11 inches and its area is 132 Sq. inches.\n\nQuestion: Find the height of the parallelogram.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{12}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 418, "output_tokens": 399, "total_tokens": 817}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1427", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A sailor goes 8 km downstream in 40 minutes and comes back in 1 hour.\n\nQuestion: Determine the speed of the sailor in still water and the speed of current.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{10, 2}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 424, "output_tokens": 665, "total_tokens": 1089}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_312", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Having been to Paris, Rob also remembered the Eiffel Tower which was the tallest structure in the world at the time it was built. If the height of Eiffel Tower is 324 m,\n\nQuestion: how much lower is it compared to 830m height, today\u2019s tallest man-made structure, the Burj Khalifa?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{506}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 579, "output_tokens": 328, "total_tokens": 907}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1347", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: The perimeter of two squares ABCD and PQRS are 3:2 respectively. The sums of the perimeters of the squares are 30.\n\nQuestion: Find the perimeter of ABCD and PQRS.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{12}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 448, "output_tokens": 438, "total_tokens": 886}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1981", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Amy was doing a classroom survey. She asked the girls in the class how many siblings they had and recorded the results: 1, 6, 10, 4, 3, 3, 11, 3 and 10.\n\nQuestion: What is the mean of the results?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "To find the mean, add all the numbers and divide by the total count. The sum of the results is $1 + 6 + 10 + 4 + 3 + 3 + 11 + 3 + 10 = 51$, and there are 9 results. So, the mean is $51 \\div 9 = 5.\\overline{6}$.\n\n\\boxed{{5.\\overline{6}}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 516, "output_tokens": 317, "total_tokens": 833}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1348", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A field is in the shape of an equilateral triangle attached to the width of the rectangular region where width of the rectangle and side of the triangle measures the same. The length of rectangular region is 76 ft and the side of triangular region measures 42 ft.\n\nQuestion: Find the perimeter of the field.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{278}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 608, "output_tokens": 552, "total_tokens": 1160}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1437", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: If you were to travel by metro the fare for the first kilometer is different from the rate per kilometer for the remaining distance. The total fare for a distance of 20 km is $37.70 and that for a distance of 26 km is $48.50.\n\nQuestion: Find the auto fare for the first kilometer and for each successive kilometer.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{3.50, 1.80}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 612, "output_tokens": 544, "total_tokens": 1156}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1341", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: In an isosceles triangle one of the angles of a triangle is 54 degrees.\n\nQuestion: Find the base angles of the triangle.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{63^\\circ}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 417, "output_tokens": 816, "total_tokens": 1233}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1708", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: At the store Brand A potato chips were $10.40 for 4 bags. Brand B potato chips were $17.78 for 7 bags.\n\nQuestion: Which brand has the cheaper price?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 452, "output_tokens": 254, "total_tokens": 706}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_311", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Rob also compared the Empire State Building and the Petronas Towers.\n\nQuestion: What is the height difference between the two if the Empire State Building is 443 m tall and the Petronas Towers is 452 m tall?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{9}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 508, "output_tokens": 252, "total_tokens": 760}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1516", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Mika measures the lens on a magnifying glass and calculates that it has a circumference of 31.4 centimeters.\n\nQuestion: What is the lens's diameter?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{10}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 443, "output_tokens": 290, "total_tokens": 733}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_843", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Three cleaners, A, B, and C are cleaning the windows of a building. Person A cleans a window every 8 min, person B every 12 min and person C every 14 min. If they start cleaning three windows at the same time at 14:15,\n\nQuestion: at what time will start cleaning windows at the same time again?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{17:03}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 580, "output_tokens": 528, "total_tokens": 1108}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_845", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Three carpenters are installing some doors for a building. Carpenter A installs a door every 40 min, Carpenter B installs a door every 1 h 20 min and Carpenter C installs a door every 1 h 40 min. If they start installing three doors at the same time at 9:15,\n\nQuestion: at what time will they install doors at the same again?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{15:55}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 628, "output_tokens": 407, "total_tokens": 1035}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1433", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A man walks certain distance with certain speed. If he walks 1/2 km/hr faster, he takes 1 hr less. But if he walks 1 km/hr slower, he takes 3 more hours.\n\nQuestion: Find the distance covered by the man and his original rate of walking.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Let the original speed be \\(v\\) km/hr and the distance be \\(d\\) km, with original time \\(t = \\frac{d}{v}\\).\n\nFrom the first condition:  \n\\[\n\\frac{d}{v + 0.5} = t - 1 = \\frac{d}{v} - 1\n\\]  \nFrom the second:  \n\\[\n\\frac{d}{v - 1} = t + 3 = \\frac{d}{v} + 3\n\\]\n\nSolving these gives \\(v = 4\\) km/hr and \\(d = 36\\) km.\n\n\\boxed{36 \\text{ km and } 4 \\text{ km/hr}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 661, "output_tokens": 853, "total_tokens": 1514}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1428", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Points A and B are 70 km apart on a highway. A car starts from A and another car starts from B at the same time. If they travel in the same direction, they meet in 7 hours, but if they travel towards each other they meet in one hour.\n\nQuestion: What are their respective speeds?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Let the speeds of the cars starting from A and B be $ x $ km/h and $ y $ km/h respectively.  \nWhen they travel in the same direction, the relative speed is $ |x - y| $, and they meet in 7 hours: $ 7(x - y) = 70 $ \u2192 $ x - y = 10 $.  \nWhen they travel toward each other, the relative speed is $ x + y $, and they meet in 1 hour: $ x + y = 70 $.  \nSolving the system: $ x - y = 10 $, $ x + y = 70 $, we add the equations to get $ 2x = 80 $ \u2192 $ x = 40 $, then $ y = 30 $.  \n\n\\boxed{{40 \\text{ km/h and } 30 \\text{ km/h}}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 560, "output_tokens": 633, "total_tokens": 1193}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1334", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: The area of trapezium is 84 Sq.cm and height is 8 cm. The parallel sides are in the ratio 2:5.\n\nQuestion: Find the length of the bases.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The area of a trapezium is given by the formula:  \n$$\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (a + b) \\times h\n$$  \nwhere $ a $ and $ b $ are the lengths of the parallel sides (bases), and $ h $ is the height.  \nGiven the area is 84 cm\u00b2, height is 8 cm, and the ratio of the bases is $ 2:5 $, let the sides be $ 2x $ and $ 5x $.  \nSubstitute into the formula:  \n$$\n84 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (2x + 5x) \\times 8 = 4 \\times 7x = 28x\n$$  \nSolving for $ x $:  \n$$\nx = \\frac{84}{28} = 3\n$$  \nThus, the lengths of the bases are $ 2x = 6 $ cm and $ 5x = 15 $ cm.  \nFinal answer:  \n\\boxed{{6 \\text{ cm and } 15 \\text{ cm}}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 436, "output_tokens": 619, "total_tokens": 1055}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_2241", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A new building needed 14 windows. The builder had already installed 5 of them. If it takes 4 hours to install each window,\n\nQuestion: how long will it take him to install the rest?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{36}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 484, "output_tokens": 161, "total_tokens": 645}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1445", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: The larger of two supplementary angles exceeds the smaller by 18 degrees.\n\nQuestion: Find them.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Let the smaller angle be $ x $ degrees. Then the larger angle is $ x + 18 $ degrees. Since the angles are supplementary, their sum is $ 180^\\circ $:  \n$$\nx + (x + 18) = 180\n$$  \nSolving: $ 2x + 18 = 180 $ \u2192 $ 2x = 162 $ \u2192 $ x = 81 $. So, the angles are $ 81^\\circ $ and $ 99^\\circ $.  \n\\boxed{{81^\\circ \\text{ and } 99^\\circ}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 386, "output_tokens": 392, "total_tokens": 778}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_859", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: An alloy is made up of 240 grams Nickel and 320 grams Copper.\n\nQuestion: Find the ratio of nickel to copper.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{3:4}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 404, "output_tokens": 339, "total_tokens": 743}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_163", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A game spinner has 5 equal parts. Two parts are blue and three parts are purple.\n\nQuestion: Which color would you most likely spin?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The spinner has 5 equal parts: 2 blue and 3 purple. Since 3 out of 5 parts are purple, the probability of spinning purple is higher than spinning blue. Therefore, you are most likely to spin purple.\n\n\\boxed{{\\text{purple}}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 422, "output_tokens": 258, "total_tokens": 680}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1054", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Last year, Jefferson County's event hall was used for 18 wedding receptions and 12 anniversary parties. This year it was used for 17 wedding receptions and 14 anniversary parties.\n\nQuestion: During which year was the event hall used for a lower ratio of wedding receptions to anniversary parties?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{this\\:year}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 600, "output_tokens": 252, "total_tokens": 852}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1509", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A length of wire is cut into several smaller pieces. Each of the smaller pieces are bent into squares. Each square has a side that measures 2 centimeters. The total area of the smaller squares is 92 square centimeters.\n\nQuestion: What was the original length of wire?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{184}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 568, "output_tokens": 301, "total_tokens": 869}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_2086", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Fabric is sold in stores from bolts that are 45 or 60 inches wide.\n\nQuestion: What is the width of the widest strips of fabric you can cut from either bolt without wasting any of the fabric if each strip has the same width?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{15}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 513, "output_tokens": 299, "total_tokens": 812}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_170", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Two dimes and 3 pennies,\n\nQuestion: does the former equal the latter?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{20 \\ne 3}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 366, "output_tokens": 171, "total_tokens": 537}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1432", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A railway half ticket costs half the full fare and the reservation charge is the same on half ticket as on full ticket. One reserved first class from Michigan to Massachusetts costs $216 and one full and one half reserved first class tickets cost $327.\n\nQuestion: What is the basic first class full fare and what is the reservation charge?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F = 210,\\ R = 6}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 640, "output_tokens": 534, "total_tokens": 1174}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1045", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: In the fall, Ian's catering company catered 10 small-scale events and 16 large-scale events. In the winter, they catered 7 small-scale events and 12 large-scale ones.\n\nQuestion: During which season did Ian's catering company cater a higher ratio of small-scale to large-scale events?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In the fall, the ratio of small-scale to large-scale events is $ \\frac{10}{16} = 0.625 $.  \nIn the winter, the ratio is $ \\frac{7}{12} \\approx 0.583 $.  \nSince $ 0.625 > 0.583 $, the company catered a higher ratio of small-scale to large-scale events in the fall.  \n\\boxed{{\\text{fall}}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 562, "output_tokens": 344, "total_tokens": 906}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1441", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Fraction becomes 4/5 , if one is added to both numerator and denominator. If however, 5 is subtracted from both, the fraction becomes 1/2.\n\nQuestion: Find the fraction.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Let the fraction be $\\frac{x}{y}$. According to the problem, when 1 is added to both numerator and denominator, the fraction becomes $\\frac{4}{5}$:  \n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{y+1} = \\frac{4}{5} \\quad \\text{(1)}\n$$\nWhen 5 is subtracted from both, the fraction becomes $\\frac{1}{2}$:  \n$$\n\\frac{x-5}{y-5} = \\frac{1}{2} \\quad \\text{(2)}\n$$\nCross-multiplying equation (1): $5(x+1) = 4(y+1)$ \u2192 $5x + 5 = 4y + 4$ \u2192 $5x - 4y = -1$.  \nCross-multiplying equation (2): $2(x-5) = 1(y-5)$ \u2192 $2x - 10 = y - 5$ \u2192 $2x - y = 5$.  \nNow solve the system:  \nFrom $2x - y = 5$, we get $y = 2x - 5$. Substitute into $5x - 4y = -1$:  \n$5x - 4(2x - 5) = -1$ \u2192 $5x - 8x + 20 = -1$ \u2192 $-3x = -21$ \u2192 $x = 7$. Then $y = 2(7) - 5 = 9$.  \nThus, the original fraction is $\\frac{7}{9}$.\n\n\\boxed{\\frac{7}{9}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 472, "output_tokens": 810, "total_tokens": 1282}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1165", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A restaurant critic reviewed restaurants in Richmond and Yardley. In Richmond, the critic gave 14 positive reviews and 20 negative reviews. In Yardley, 12 of the reviews were positive and 17 were negative.\n\nQuestion: In which city did the restaurant critic give a higher ratio of positive to negative reviews?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The ratio of positive to negative reviews in Richmond is \\(\\frac{14}{20} = 0.7\\), while in Yardley it is \\(\\frac{12}{17} \\approx 0.7059\\). Since \\(0.7059 > 0.7\\), Yardley has a higher ratio.\n\n\\boxed{Yardley}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 672, "output_tokens": 823, "total_tokens": 1495}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_881", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Mr. Bradley gave his class a math problem to solve. He said, \"Begin with the number 28. Add 12 to it. Then add 7 more.\" Ned followed the instructions perfectly but Billy subtracted 7.\n\nQuestion: What is the difference between the boys' answers?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{14}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 548, "output_tokens": 188, "total_tokens": 736}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1060", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Tori went on a two-day fishing trip. On the first day, she caught 5 catfish and 6 trout. On the second day, she caught 10 catfish and 12 trout.\n\nQuestion: On which day of the fishing trip did Tori catch a higher ratio of catfish to trout?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "On the first day, the ratio of catfish to trout is $ \\frac{5}{6} $. On the second day, the ratio is $ \\frac{10}{12} = \\frac{5}{6} $. Since both ratios are equal, Tori caught the same ratio of catfish to trout on both days.\n\n\\boxed{{\\text{neither}}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 540, "output_tokens": 283, "total_tokens": 823}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1412", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Ten years ago, the sum of the ages of two sons was one-third of their father's age. One son is two years older than the other and sum of their present ages is 14 years less than the father's present age.\n\nQuestion: Find the present ages of all.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{15, 17, 46}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 548, "output_tokens": 684, "total_tokens": 1232}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_833", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: The weight of 3 glass bottles is 600 g. The total weight of 4 glass bottles and 5 plastic bottles is 1 kg 50 g.\n\nQuestion: How much heavier is a glass bottle than a plastic bottle?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{150}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 484, "output_tokens": 427, "total_tokens": 911}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1407", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A is two years older than B. A's father D is twice as old as A and B is twice old as his sister C. The ages of D and C differ by 40 years.\n\nQuestion: Find the ages of A and B.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{26, 24}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 478, "output_tokens": 608, "total_tokens": 1086}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1473", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: The perimeter of a college basketball court is 96 meters and the length is 14 meters more than the width.\n\nQuestion: What are the dimensions?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Let the width be $ w $ meters. Then the length is $ w + 14 $ meters. The perimeter of a rectangle is given by $ 2(\\text{length} + \\text{width}) $, so:  \n$$\n2(w + (w + 14)) = 96\n$$  \nSimplifying: $ 2(2w + 14) = 96 $ \u2192 $ 4w + 28 = 96 $ \u2192 $ 4w = 68 $ \u2192 $ w = 17 $.  \nThus, the width is 17 meters and the length is $ 17 + 14 = 31 $ meters.  \n\n\\boxed{{17 \\text{ meters (width)}, 31 \\text{ meters (length)}}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 444, "output_tokens": 414, "total_tokens": 858}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1162", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: When Jenna works out, she spends 18 minutes doing cardio and 20 minutes doing resistance training. Leon's workout consists of 17 minutes of cardio and 18 minutes of resistance training.\n\nQuestion: Who does a higher ratio of cardio to resistance training?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{Leon}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 541, "output_tokens": 233, "total_tokens": 774}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1044", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: At Newberry High School, 14 of the members of the women's track team compete in long-distance events and 20 compete in short-distance events. On the men's track team, 10 run in long-distance events and 16 run in short-distance events.\n\nQuestion: Which team has a lower ratio of long-distance to short-distance runners?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "For the women's team, the ratio of long-distance to short-distance runners is $ \\frac{14}{20} = 0.7 $. For the men's team, the ratio is $ \\frac{10}{16} = 0.625 $. Since $ 0.625 < 0.7 $, the men's team has a lower ratio.\n\n\\boxed{{\\text{men's team}}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 572, "output_tokens": 397, "total_tokens": 969}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1159", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Felix and Clara are lawyers. Felix averages 20 civil cases and 10 criminal cases annually. Meanwhile, Clara averages 16 civil cases and 15 criminal ones.\n\nQuestion: Which lawyer has a lower ratio of civil to criminal cases?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Felix's ratio of civil to criminal cases is $ \\frac{20}{10} = 2 $.  \nClara's ratio is $ \\frac{16}{15} \\approx 1.07 $.  \nSince $ 1.07 < 2 $, Clara has a lower ratio.  \n\\boxed{\\text{Clara}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 524, "output_tokens": 219, "total_tokens": 743}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_303", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: With the win streak that they have, Chuck's team was able to get into the playoffs. They reached the semi-finals where they played against the Black Team. If they finished the game with 83 points and won it by 18 points,\n\nQuestion: what is the Black Team's final score?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{65}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 560, "output_tokens": 199, "total_tokens": 759}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1168", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Last month, Ivan spent 20 hours watching TV and 14 hours reading. The same month, Brenna spent 11 hours watching TV and 10 hours reading.\n\nQuestion: Who had a higher ratio of time spent watching TV to time spent reading?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Ivan's ratio is 20:14, which simplifies to 10:7 or approximately 1.4286. Brenna's ratio is 11:10, which equals 1.1. Since 1.4286 is greater than 1.1, Ivan had the higher ratio.\n\n\\boxed{Ivan}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 633, "output_tokens": 334, "total_tokens": 967}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1161", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: While researching colleges, Kendall learns that a typical class at Greenpoint Technical College has 5 men and 6 women, and a typical class at Adams County College has 15 men and 19 women.\n\nQuestion: Which college has classes with a lower ratio of men to women?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "To compare the ratios of men to women, we compute the ratio for each college. At Greenpoint Technical College, the ratio is $ \\frac{5}{6} \\approx 0.833 $, and at Adams County College, the ratio is $ \\frac{15}{19} \\approx 0.789 $. Since $ 0.789 < 0.833 $, Adams County College has a lower ratio of men to women.\n\n\\boxed{{\\text{Adams County College}}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 550, "output_tokens": 366, "total_tokens": 916}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1046", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Last season, Lisa's soccer team won 8 games and lost 6 games. Her cousin Susan's team won 17 games and lost 14 games.\n\nQuestion: Which team had a higher ratio of wins to losses?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Lisa's team won 8 games and lost 6 games, so their win-to-loss ratio is $ \\frac{8}{6} = \\frac{4}{3} \\approx 1.33 $.  \nSusan's team won 17 games and lost 14 games, so their win-to-loss ratio is $ \\frac{17}{14} \\approx 1.21 $.  \nSince $ \\frac{4}{3} > \\frac{17}{14} $, Lisa's team had a higher win-to-loss ratio.  \n\n\\boxed{\\text{Lisa's team}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 480, "output_tokens": 349, "total_tokens": 829}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1443", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A person invested some amount at 12% simple interest and some amount at 10% simple interest. He received an annual interest of $130. But, if he had interchanged and invested he would have received $4 more.\n\nQuestion: How much amount did he invest at the two rates?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{700}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 550, "output_tokens": 917, "total_tokens": 1467}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "AsDiv_1270", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Oliver was weighing boxes for moving. The first was 2 pounds, the second was 3 pounds and the last was 13 pounds.\n\nQuestion: What's the difference between the weight of the first box and the third box?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exac