re X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 574, "output_tokens": 256, "total_tokens": 830}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_605", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following requires a lot of labor, focuses on a small plot of land, or both?\n\nOptions: \nA. Extensive agriculture\nB. Pastoralism\nC. Hunting and gathering\nD. Nomadic herding\nE. Intensive agriculture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 505, "output_tokens": 265, "total_tokens": 770}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_615", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One advantage of the sector model over other models of urban structure is that\n\nOptions: \nA. it portrays a decentralized vision of urban life\nB. it incorporates both industrial corridors and ethnic neighborhoods\nC. it implies that there are multiple nodes of business\nD. it explores the concept of public religiosity\nE. it relies upon the certainties of mathematical modelling\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 648, "output_tokens": 373, "total_tokens": 1021}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_619", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the bid-rent curve, it is expected that as the distance from the PLVI decreases\n\nOptions: \nA. the crime rate increases\nB. the crime rate decreases\nC. the cost of transportation increases\nD. the price of land increases\nE. the price of land decreases\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is D. The bid-rent curve illustrates that land prices are highest near the PLVI (peak land value intersection) due to greater accessibility and demand. As distance from this center decreases, competition for the more desirable land increases, driving up its price. Therefore, moving closer to the PLVI results in higher land costs.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 676, "output_tokens": 470, "total_tokens": 1146}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_624", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to Wallerstein's world systems theory, which of the following would be true?\n\nOptions: \nA. Core countries primarily export raw materials to other countries.\nB. Semi-peripheral countries are located between the core and periphery.\nC. Peripheral countries have mostly service-based economies.\nD. Core countries are the most economically developed and powerful.\nE. Semi-peripheral countries primarily export goods to core countries and import goods from peripheral countries.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 788, "output_tokens": 371, "total_tokens": 1159}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_625", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The most important reason for the rising use of alternative energy crops such as ethanol and biodiesel has been\n\nOptions: \nA. the rapid increase in the price of oil\nB. the public relations efforts of alternative energy advocates\nC. the large amount of waste oil from deep fryers\nD. the slash and burn agriculture occurring in Brazil that has seen the growth of millions of acres of new sugar cane\nE. the improvement in irrigation techniques\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 744, "output_tokens": 420, "total_tokens": 1164}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_629", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of the problems with using the terms First World, Second World, and Third World to describe countries is that\n\nOptions: \nA. First-World countries are sometimes lacking free markets and a high level of productivity value per person\nB. the terms are slightly misleading, since Second-World countries are not necessarily between First- and Third-World countries, but instead are communist centrally planned economies\nC. Third-World countries have agricultural or resourced-based economies but a high quality of life\nD. some First-World countries, such as Argentina, actually resemble Second-World countries\nE. some countries, such as Japan, can't be categorized in this schema\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 984, "output_tokens": 541, "total_tokens": 1525}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_633", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The difference between GDP (gross domestic product) and GNI (gross national income) is\n\nOptions: \nA. GDP measures collective wealth or productivity, but GNI measures general well-being\nB. GDP considers goods and services, but GNI also considers exports and imports\nC. GDP absorbs only data from the service economy, but GNI takes into account data from both service and manufacturing economies\nD. GDP is a measure of inflation, but GNI indicates a standard of living\nE. GDP measures the personal income of an average worker, while GNI measures the purchasing power of that worker\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 884, "output_tokens": 428, "total_tokens": 1312}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_657", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A negative rate of natural increase can often be seen in societies that\n\nOptions: \nA. have banned or greatly restricted immigration\nB. do not take censuses\nC. are developing nations and do not recognize modern methods of measurement\nD. feature an aging population\nE. have suffered a devastating war\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 556, "output_tokens": 290, "total_tokens": 846}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_659", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An example of a fuzzy cultural border would be\n\nOptions: \nA. where Dixie ends and the American Northeast or Midwest begins\nB. between the epicenter of Jainist belief and the region where African Voodoun is mainstream\nC. where the Wailing Wall ends and the Temple of Solomon begins\nD. the transition from modern to contemporary architecture\nE. between the Kurgan hearth and the Anatolian hearth\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 700, "output_tokens": 481, "total_tokens": 1181}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_683", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The workers who survived the Black Plague, which killed nearly a third of European population, ironically saw their wages rise in later years. This phenomenon is best explained by\n\nOptions: \nA. natural resource depletion\nB. national choice theory\nC. Marx's theory of surplus value\nD. Keynesian economics\nE. the iron law of wages\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 632, "output_tokens": 408, "total_tokens": 1040}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_689", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to Figure 2, the majority of the world's population is\n\