societies differ from stage 2 societies primarily in that\n\nOptions: \nA. a stage 3 economy is agricultural, not manufacturing\nB. a stage 3 birth rate is decreasing, not increasing\nC. a stage 3 death rate is increasing, not decreasing\nD. a stage 3 total population has leveled off\nE. a stage 3 gender imbalance has rebalanced itself\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 669, "output_tokens": 453, "total_tokens": 1122}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_702", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Countries that are near or below zero population growth will often\n\nOptions: \nA. eliminate guest worker programs\nB. elect nativist or authoritarian leaders\nC. experience reduced levels of manufacturing\nD. offer incentives to citizens to have more children\nE. exhibit an increased death rate\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 596, "output_tokens": 322, "total_tokens": 918}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_704", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An example of cyclic movement is\n\nOptions: \nA. a Polish woman working as a housekeeper in Ireland each summer\nB. a Chinese software entrepreneur opening a branch of his business in Ethiopia\nC. a French woman with dual citizenship retiring to her parents' homeland of Tunisia\nD. a Syrian refugee seeking refuge with his family in Germany\nE. a young Colombian moving from the countryside to Bogot\u00e1 to attend university\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 724, "output_tokens": 304, "total_tokens": 1028}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_719", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The concept of sequent occupance is best illustrated by which of the following situations?\n\nOptions: \nA. The arrival of a Somali family into a white Minnesota neighborhood\nB. The discovery by construction workers in Rome of previously unknown ancient ruins\nC. A young girl who is sharing an apartment with her parents and two sets of grandparents\nD. The laws that allow squatters legal rights to a property after a set period of time has elapsed\nE. The construction of Las Vegas on flat, untouched desert\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 808, "output_tokens": 459, "total_tokens": 1267}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_720", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The perception of Mexicans as wearing large sombreros and eating tacos is an example of Mexico as a(n)\n\nOptions: \nA. political region\nB. environmental region\nC. absolute location\nD. relative location\nE. vernacular region\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 524, "output_tokens": 325, "total_tokens": 849}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_732", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The \"tragedy of the commons\" is best exemplified by which of the following situations?\n\nOptions: \nA. Deteriorating language because of poor formal instruction\nB. The Malthusian idea of population limited by its food production\nC. Neighboring ethnic groups that have coexisted peacefully devolving into warfare\nD. Degrading land as a result of too many individuals grazing their livestock on publicly held pasture\nE. Declining resistance to viruses as a result of more densely packed populations\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 770, "output_tokens": 381, "total_tokens": 1151}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_736", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The primary economic difference between urban and rural areas is that\n\nOptions: \nA. urban areas feature higher levels of education, while rural areas feature higher levels of experience\nB. urban areas offer more entertainment options, while rural areas offer more outdoor activities\nC. urban areas are built upon services, while rural communities are built upon resources\nD. urban areas promote free-market policies, while rural areas promote big-government policies\nE. urban areas contain elite residential neighborhoods, while rural areas contain housing for the poor\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 876, "output_tokens": 474, "total_tokens": 1350}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_743", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the field of high-tech services, the primary advantage that India enjoys over other nations is\n\nOptions: \nA. its population of nearly one billion\nB. its tradition of hosting many diverse religions\nC. its traditional caste system\nD. its inability to manufacture textiles and other goods\nE. its English language heritage owing to its colonial past\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 623, "output_tokens": 389, "total_tokens": 1012}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_747", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The difference between buying a single hot dog at the corner convenience store, a pack of six hot dogs at the nearest grocery store, and a case of forty-eight hot dogs at a faraway big-box retail outlet is the difference in\n\nOptions: \nA. comparative advantage\nB. distance elastic\nC. supply chain\nD. peak land value intersection\nE. urban hierarchy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The scenario illustrates different purchasing options based on quantity and location, which relates to the structure and distribution of retail outlets. This concept is best described by the **urban hierarchy**, where larger, more distant stores offer bulk discounts while smaller, closer stores charge higher prices for convenience. Therefore, the correct answer is E.\n\n\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 742, "output_tokens": 420, "total_tokens": 1162}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_749", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A diamond-cutting company that employs four different workers, and whose only physical need is four machines on a table, can be regarded as part of\n\nOptions: \nA. a special economic zone\nB. a decentralized network\nC. a supply chain\nD. a footloose industry\nE. a high-benefit service\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 554, "output_tokens": 294, "total_tokens": 848}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_751", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Unlike other models of urban structure, the multiple-nuclei model\n\nOptions: \nA. analyzes the different areas of a city from a scientific standpoint\nB. can be applied to all urban environments around the world\nC. explains the growth at the periphery of cities\nD. admits that there is often more than one commercial center in a city\nE. defines zones more loosely than other theories do\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 662, "output_tokens": 404, "total_tokens": 1066}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_759", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A person who takes a bus to a subway to an airport for a flight has experienced several\n\nOptions: \nA. examples of rapid transit\nB. convergence zones\nC. vertical integrations\nD. intermodal connections\nE. spatial fixes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 520, "output_tokens": 260, "total_tokens": 780}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_766", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The precise location of retail services is spatially dependent on the relationship between\n\nOptions: \nA. potential cost-overruns and projected revenue\nB. consumer demand and local supply\nC. variable cost and revenue surfaces\nD. infrastructure costs and recaptured revenue\nE. local consumer demand and geographic viability\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 500, "output_tokens": 265, "total_tokens": 765}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_769", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Furniture requires parts to be assembled into components that are then assembled together to create a larger finished product. In this regard, furniture is an example of a\n\nOptions: \nA. footloose industry\nB. high-benefit service\nC. supply chain\nD. bulk-losing industry\nE. deglomeration\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 556, "output_tokens": 426, "total_tokens": 982}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_780", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The primary reason that humanity has been able to escape the Malthusian trap is\n\nOptions: \nA. changing weather patterns\nB. improvements in human digestion\nC. increased government intervention\nD. reduced open-border policies\nE. improved agricultural technology\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 539, "output_tokens": 379, "total_tokens": 918}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_817", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The point at which the lines of food production and human population cross would best be described as the point at which\n\nOptions: \nA. rapid migration to North America leads to a decline in the world economy\nB. a former communist economy completes the transition from a Second World country to a Third World country\nC. technological innovations will eliminate global food shortages\nD. a former agrarian economy completes the transition into an industrialized economy\nE. the population exceeds its ability to feed itself\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 780, "output_tokens": 281, "total_tokens": 1061}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_828", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The movement of West African voodoo religion occurred via relocation diffusion, which itself was a result of\n\nOptions: \nA. religious oppression from the landed aristocracy in Africa\nB. a slowly dying cultural hearth\nC. an evangelical tradition among its adherents\nD. european-directed slavery \nE. a social custom that favors inclusion of outsiders\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 652, "output_tokens": 321, "total_tokens": 973}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_829", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The reason that people of Latin America are often absent from the discussion of racial group physiology is that\n\nOptions: \nA. there are too many racial groups to consider within the Latin race\nB. experts consider the indigenous people of South America to be racially unclassifiable\nC. they contain a blend of Mongoloid, Negroid, and Caucasoid races but are not considered a separate race\nD. the field of ethnology suffers from systematic prejudice\nE. mestizos are found primarily within the Caucasian race but not the Mongoloid race\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 803, "output_tokens": 448, "total_tokens": 1251}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_830", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A Chinese man working in Africa meets another Chinese man and begins the conversation by asking which city he comes from. This is an example of an expression of\n\nOptions: \nA. internal identity\nB. external identity\nC. xenophobia\nD. possibilism\nE. racism\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "succe