timality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1116", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A geographer who supports the theory of environmental determinism would most likely agree with which of the following statements?\n\nOptions: \nA. Humans are not entirely a product of their environment, and they possess the skills to adapt their environment to fit their needs.\nB. A society\u2019s physical and intellectual attributes are shaped by the location and climate in which they develop.\nC. Human activity has resulted in global climate change and increasingly severe weather patterns.\nD. Most societies can control their environment to their benefit, resulting in higher levels of economic development.\nE. Societies are not influenced by their environments, instead developing independently of environmental factors.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 960, "output_tokens": 333, "total_tokens": 1293}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1122", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following best describes a primary purpose for why state and local political boundaries were defined, delimited, and demarcated in the United States?\n\nOptions: \nA. To establish the authority of the federal government\nB. To set the limits of political sovereignty\nC. To prevent gerrymandering from taking place\nD. To encourage the development of regional identity\nE. To establish political voting districts\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 724, "output_tokens": 480, "total_tokens": 1204}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1123", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After decades of Soviet rule and control of Eastern Europe, in 1989, the Berlin Wall and the Iron Curtain fell, precipitating the end of the Soviet Union. This is best described as an example of which of the following?\n\nOptions: \nA. Devolution\nB. Heartland theory\nC. Imperialism\nD. Balkanization\nE. Annexation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 579, "output_tokens": 295, "total_tokens": 874}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1126", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A family of immigrants learns the language of their new country, with each generation becoming more fluent. This process is an example of which of the following?\n\nOptions: \nA. Irredentism\nB. Acculturation\nC. Centrifugal force\nD. Cultural shatterbelt\nE. Chain migration\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 557, "output_tokens": 352, "total_tokens": 909}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1133", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following would best describe the type of political entity that an American Indian reservation would be classified as?\n\nOptions: \nA. Nation-state\nB. Multinational state\nC. Independent state\nD. City-state\nE. Semiautonomous region\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 548, "output_tokens": 341, "total_tokens": 889}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1136", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the late 1940s, tensions between India and Pakistan escalated into armed conflict. The tensions were fueled, in part, by religious differences. Such differences are best described by which of the following?\n\nOptions: \nA. National iconography\nB. Devolution\nC. Colonialism\nD. Centrifugal forces\nE. Centripetal forces\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 607, "output_tokens": 341, "total_tokens": 948}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1141", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The majority of African states entered the United Nations after 1960 because\n\nOptions: \nA. the United Nations excluded all African states before 1960\nB. the United States vetoed several African states\u2019 requests to join\nC. a majority of African states were under the control of the Soviet Union\nD. most African states sought to form the Organisation of African Unity (OAU)\nE. the majority of the states hadn\u2019t become independent until the 1960s\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 734, "output_tokens": 289, "total_tokens": 1023}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1142", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: San Marino and Vatican City are countries that are located within Italy. Lesotho is a country that is located within South Africa. Which of the following best describes the political geography of these three