tences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 940, "output_tokens": 380, "total_tokens": 1320}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1167", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A group of farmers decide to grow crops in tropical areas for sale in more developed countries. Which of the following best describes this type of farming?\n\nOptions: \nA. Slash-and-burn farming\nB. Plantation agriculture\nC. Intensive subsistence agriculture\nD. Shifting cultivation\nE. Commercial agriculture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 612, "output_tokens": 372, "total_tokens": 984}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1172", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following best explains why Ullman and Harris developed the multiple nuclei model?\n\nOptions: \nA. To demonstrate the effects of decreased car ownership\nB. To support the concentric zone model\nC. To describe the complex development of urban areas\nD. To standardize urban studies terminology\nE. To explain the consolidation of cities' central business districts\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 645, "output_tokens": 380, "total_tokens": 1025}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1174", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements best explains the bid-rent theory?\n\nOptions: \nA. Land value is highest in the central business district, and land value decreases with distance from the CBD.\nB. Land value is highest in the suburbs, resulting in larger houses.\nC. More space is available in the urban core because most growth is upward.\nD. Land value is higher in the suburbs due to a greater demand for land there.\nE. Land value is constant throughout the metropolitan area due to the high demand for residential space in general.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 836, "output_tokens": 393, "total_tokens": 1229}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1176", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is an example of a basic industry?\n\nOptions: \nA. A hotel in San Francisco\nB. A restaurant in Atlanta\nC. A car factory in Detroit\nD. A convenience store in Dallas\nE. A movie theater in Tampa\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 516, "output_tokens": 438, "total_tokens": 954}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1186", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following best explains the basis for Walter Christaller's central place theory?\n\nOptions: \nA. Social structure is based on transportation systems rather than on the distance from the central business district.\nB. Growth independent of the central business district is connected to the central city by a highway or an interstate.\nC. People will travel the least distance possible to meet their service needs.\nD. Zones are randomly placed in the city and are separated from each other by walls.\nE. Lower classes will likely live closest to the central business district, while the upper classes will likely live farther out.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 887, "output_tokens": 359, "total_tokens": 1246}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1188", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following best describes a significant position in Weber's least cost theory?\n\nOptions: \nA. People will travel the least possible distance for services.\nB. The greater influence a city has, the more migration to that city.\nC. The cost to transport raw materials is more important than the cost of the raw materials themselves.\nD. Birth rate, death rate, and total population are the only factors relevant to population growth.\nE. Farmers sell all of their agricultural harvest.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 757, "output_tokens": 361, "total_tokens": 1118}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1189", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is an example of a weight-gaining industry?\n\nOptions: \nA. Automobile manufacturing\nB. Potato chip making\nC. Sugar processing\nD. Pharmaceutical manufacturing\nE. Fresh produce shipping\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is C. Sugar processing, as raw sugar beets or cane are heavy and bulky, while the refined sugar product is lighter, making it a weight-reducing industry\u2014not weight-gaining. For a weight-gaining industry, the final product is heavier than the inputs, but none of these clearly fit that description. Potato chip making (B) might seem plausible, but since most such manufacturing involves removing water weight from potatoes, it is typically weight-reducing.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 616, "output_tokens": 1052, "total_tokens": 1668}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1192", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The transfer of a shipment of blue jeans from a train to a truck at a distribution point is an example of\n\nOptions: \nA. gross domestic product\nB. a growth pole\nC. outsourcing\nD. a break-of-bulk point\nE. carrier efficiency\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 515, "output_tokens": 277, "total_tokens": 792}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1193", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following exemplifies why Shanghai is considered one of China's special economic zones (SEZs)?\n\nOptions: \nA. The workforce in Shanghai equates personal and professional value with how the company performs.\nB. Foreign car makers including Ford, General Motors, and Volkswagen have located plants near Shanghai.\nC. The Huang River serves as a major transportation route for the manufacturing industries in Shanghai.\nD. Shanghai is a treaty port that efficiently exports goods made in China.\nE. Kaohsiung, one of the busiest ports in the world, is an exportation hub that has given rise to Shanghai\u2019s rapid economic growth.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 895, "output_tokens": 462, "total_tokens": 1357}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1196", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to the core-periphery model, as shown in the map below, the Canadian northern territories would be classified as\n\nOptions: \nA. an industrial core\nB. an upward transition\nC. a downward transition\nD. a semi-periphery\nE. a resource frontier\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 552, "output_tokens": 426, "total_tokens": 978}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1197", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A large corporation looking to lower labor costs would most likely seek which of the following?\n\nOptions: \nA. Outsourcing\nB. Agglomeration\nC. Carrier efficiency\nD. Basic industries\nE. Sustainable development\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 494, "output_tokens": 300, "total_tokens": 794}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1205", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why was the Gender Development Index (GDI) developed by the United Nations?\n\nOptions: \nA. The GDI was created to measure the ratio of female to male children.\nB. The GDI was created to measure the percentage of women employed in manufacturing industries.\nC. The GDI was created to determine the disparities between men\u2019s and women\u2019s relative overall human development.\nD. The GDI was created to measure the three dimensions of human development.\nE. The GDI was created to determine the differences in educational attainment for men and women.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 813, "output_tokens": 324, "total_tokens": 1137}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1212", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Almost 99 percent of the people in Denmark are Danes, follow the Lutheran religion, and speak Danish. Denmark is thus an exemplar of which of the following?\n\nOptions: \nA. City-state\nB. Microstate\nC. Stateless nation\nD. Political boundary\nE. Nation-state\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 546, "output_tokens": 313, "total_tokens": 859}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1213", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to the demographic transition model, a country enters stage 3 when\n\nOptions: \nA. the birth rate sharply increases\nB. the birth rate decreases\nC. the birth and death rates are nearly equal, stabilizing the population\nD. the fertility rate falls below two children per family\nE. the introduction of medicine causes the death rate to decrease\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 629, "output_tokens": 361, "total_tokens": 990}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1220", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A family plans to move from Los Angeles, California, to New Orleans, Louisiana, but stops and stays in Albuquerque, New Mexico, because of the positive amenities. This is an example of\n\nOptions: \nA. distance decay\nB. an environmental pull factor\nC. an environmental push factor\nD. intervening opportunity\nE. intervening obstacle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 608, "output_tokens": 328, "total_tokens": 936}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1227", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Farming in the United States is in a transition period best characterized by\n\nOptions: \nA. the increase in farms located in the Midwest\nB. the movement toward industrial farming\nC. the movement from hunting and gathering to planting and sustaining\nD. the movement of population to rural areas\nE. the use of less genetic engineering to modify plants and animals\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 664, "output_tokens": 378, "total_tokens": 1042}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1235", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following describes the spread of religion as a result of Bhutanese refugees migrating to North Carolina?\n\nOptions: \nA. Expansion diffusion\nB. Stimulus diffusion\nC. Sun Belt migration\nD. Relocation diffusion\nE. Distribution\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 520, "output_tokens": 325, "total_tokens": 845}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1243", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Central Park in New York City is a public recreation space that hosts outdoor events. This is a good example of which of the following features?\n\nOptions: \nA. A central business district\nB. A greenbelt\nC. A festival landscape\nD. Urban development\nE. An ethnic landscape\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 496, "output_tokens": 249, "total_tokens": 745}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1255", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is presupposed in von Th\u00fcnen's model of agricultural land use?\n\nOptions: \nA. The farmers sell all of their farm production to a market.\nB. The higher-end commodities are located farther from the market.\nC. The lighter commodities are closer to the market to ensure profitability.\nD. The heavier commodities are around the market because they need irrigation.\nE. The market is based on subsistence farming practices in less developed countries.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 700, "output_tokens": 322, "total_tokens": 1022}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1256", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following best explains an aspect of von Th\u00fcnen's model of agricultural land use?\n\nOptions: \nA. The cost of transportation from livestock fattening is more than the cost of livestock ranching.\nB. While the cost of transporting vegetables is low, they belong in the first zone because the cost of spoilage is very high.\nC. Although dairy byproducts do not spoil easily, the dairy industry is close to the market because milk does spoil easily.\nD. Livestock ranching is a higher zone because the animals weigh much less compared to those raised by livestock fattening.\nE. Because the cost to produce and transport grain is low, commercial grain farming can be far from the market.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1000, "output_tokens": 389, "total_tokens": 1389}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1261", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Los Angeles receives goods from Asia via ships. In the ports, the goods are put on trains for distribution around the United States. Which of the following terms best describes Los Angeles in this scenario?\n\nOptions: \nA. Break-of-bulk point\nB. Variable-cost provider\nC. Fixed-cost provider\nD. Basic industry site\nE. Trade alternative partner\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 648, "output_tokens": 265, "total_tokens": 913}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1268", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is a common negative consequence of gentrification?\n\nOptions: \nA. Older neighborhoods are revitalized.\nB. New development creates urban sprawl.\nC. Property taxes are increased.\nD. New transportation systems replace older ones.\nE. More restaurants and shops move into the gentrified area.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 589, "output_tokens": 296, "total_tokens": 885}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1277", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following best represents a potential centrifugal force?\n\nOptions: \nA. Religious diversity\nB. Homogeneous population\nC. A common language\nD. Government-supported education\nE. National anthem\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 508, "output_tokens": 266, "total_tokens": 774}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1280", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following best describes the outsourcing of labor from more developed countries to less developed countries in order to take advantage of cheaper labor costs?\n\nOptions: \nA. The new international division of labor\nB. The core/periphery relationship\nC. Economic factors of development\nD. Standards of industrial development\nE. Inadequate debt financing of employment\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 648, "output_tokens": 357, "total_tokens": 1005}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1281", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Recent immigrants from China have established commercial activities in Chinatown in Washington, D.C. Their cultural imprint has given this neighborhood a distinctive flair, creating\n\nOptions: \nA. an ethnic neighborhood\nB. a gated community\nC. a blockbusted neighborhood\nD. a redlined area\nE. an adaptive strategy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 591, "output_tokens": 339, "total_tokens": 930}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1288", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following most accurately explains why the North Atlantic Treaty Organization was created?\n\nOptions: \nA. To start the process of creating the European Union\nB. To replace the League of Nations\nC. To oppose the Warsaw Pact\nD. To counter the spread of communism\nE. To bring an end to World War II\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 612, "output_tokens": 421, "total_tokens": 1033}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1289", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The movement of Mexicans from farmland to Mexico City is best described by which migration pattern?\n\nOptions: \nA. Cyclical movement\nB. Intercontinental\nC. Interregional\nD. Urban to rural\nE. Transhumance\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 494, "output_tokens": 296, "total_tokens": 790}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1295", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following best describes the relationship between core and periphery countries according to the world systems theory?\n\nOptions: \nA. Core countries usually engage in free and fair trade practices when dealing with periphery countries.\nB. Core countries invest very little foreign capital in periphery countries.\nC. Core countries transfer natural resources to periphery countries.\nD. Core countries help the workers in periphery countries by providing them with higher-paying jobs.\nE. Core countries refuse to give humanitarian assistance to periphery countries.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer according to world systems theory is that core countries exploit periphery countries, typically through unequal trade and resource extraction, not through fair practices or substantial aid. Option A is incorrect because trade is generally exploitative rather than free and fair. Option C is the closest to the actual dynamic, as core countries extract resources from periphery countries, not transfer them, but no option perfectly captures the exploitative relationship; however, given the choices, none are fully accurate, and all are misleading, but the theory emphasizes that core countries do not provide higher-paying jobs (D) or significant foreign investment (B) that truly benefits the periphery. \n\n\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1035, "output_tokens": 20947, "total_tokens": 21982}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1296", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For the last 10 years, a medium-sized city in the Midwest has suffered from an increase in crime, pollution, traffic congestion, and housing costs. Because of these issues, a significant number of people have left the city. This process is best described as\n\nOptions: \nA. blockbusting\nB. redlining\nC. counterurbanization\nD. decentralization\nE. pull factor migration\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "tok