here longitude was accurately calculated at sea\nE. a historical fact that has been woven into the multicultural identity of the United States\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 944, "output_tokens": 500, "total_tokens": 1444}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_944", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is the most plausible explanation for the trends seen in the Mediterranean region of the map?\n\nOptions: \nA. Conservative traditions that encourage moderate family size \nB. A repressive political climate \nC. Environmental disasters such as heat waves\nD. Religious prohibition of contraception\nE. Severe national debt and consistently high unemployment\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 539, "output_tokens": 270, "total_tokens": 809}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_951", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following would indicate sustainable resource utilization?\n\nOptions: \nA. Disposal of solid municipal waste in an open landfill at a rural location\nB. Commercial fishing only in open oceans beyond the continental shelf\nC. Paving roads and highways with recycled automobile tire and glass waste\nD. Heating and cooking in Third-World homes with wood from local forests \nE. Increased cattle farming in dry grasslands where commercial crops will not grow\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 768, "output_tokens": 341, "total_tokens": 1109}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_997", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Carl Sauer would most strongly agree with which of the following statements?\n\nOptions: \nA. Environmental determinism means humans possess the skills necessary to modify their environment to fit their needs.\nB. Environmental determinism is both factually incorrect and a prejudicial tool of Western colonialism.\nC. Neo-environmental determinism means humans possess the skills necessary to modify their environment to fit their needs.\nD. Neo-environmental determinism is both factually incorrect and a prejudicial tool of Western colonialism.\nE. The possibilist approach to geographic study concludes that cultures are a direct result of where they exist.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 960, "output_tokens": 404, "total_tokens": 1364}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1008", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A geographer who supports the human capital model of migration would most strongly agree with which of the following statements?\n\nOptions: \nA. People's odds of migrating must be evaluated by looking at their social and cultural perspectives.\nB. Migration occurs in conjunction with a demographic transition, which encourages migration to areas of economic opportunity.\nC. As people age, their personal wealth allows them greater freedom to relocate long distances, thus spurring migration.\nD. Economic downturns force people to leave an area in search of new employment.\nE. People primarily seek to improve their incomes over the course of their lives.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 956, "output_tokens": 440, "total_tokens": 1396}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1047", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following would most likely minimize pollution and congestion in urban areas?\n\nOptions: \nA. Building more roads\nB. Enforcing restrictive covenants\nC. Transitioning to a walkable city\nD. Increasing the urban heat island effect\nE. Redeveloping brownfields\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 532, "output_tokens": 280, "total_tokens": 812}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1057", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A geographer committed to the preservationist land use model would agree with which of the following statements?\n\nOptions: \nA. The land can be developed as long as the ecosystem is preserved.\nB. The landscape is worth more in its natural state than in any type of developed state.\nC. The landscape can be altered if the majority of the land is preserved\nD. Developed land must prioritize preservation of animals and forests.\nE. If developers use the land, they should not alter the overall natural state of the landscape.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 828, "output_tokens": 310, "total_tokens": 1138}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "GeoBench_1074", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To an average American, who has never traveled outside of the United States, what does \"We