ed{202}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 556, "output_tokens": 1184, "total_tokens": 1740}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MATH_232", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem and provide the final answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If $\\omega^{{1997}} = 1$ and $\\omega \\neq 1,$ then evaluate\n\\[\\frac{{1}}{{1 + \\omega}} + \\frac{{1}}{{1 + \\omega^2}} + \\dots + \\frac{{1}}{{1 + \\omega^{{1997}}.\\]\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "We are summing over all \\(1997\\)th roots of unity except \\(\\omega = 1\\).  \nThe sum  \n\\[\nS = \\sum_{k=1}^{1996} \\frac{1}{1+\\omega^k}\n\\]  \ncan be symmetrically paired: for each \\(\\omega^k\\), its complex conjugate \\(\\omega^{-k}\\) appears, and  \n\\[\n\\frac{1}{1+\\omega^k} + \\frac{1}{1+\\omega^{-k}} = 1.\n\\]  \nSince the sum has an even number of terms (1996 terms = 998 pairs), each pair sums to 1, giving  \n\\[\nS = 998.\n\\]  \nThus the evaluation yields \\(\\mathbf{998}\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{998}\n\\]", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 653, "output_tokens": 5497, "total_tokens": 6150}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MATH_251", "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem and provide the final answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Six cars pull up to a red light, one at a time. At the light, there are three lanes, one left-turn lane, one straight-going lane, and one right-turn lane. How many ways can the cars stack up