\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1580, "output_tokens": 285, "total_tokens": 1865}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3307", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Charles Darwin was the first person to propose\n\nOptions: \nA. that humans evolved from apes.\nB. that evolution occurs.\nC. that evolution occurs through a process of gradual change.\nD. that the Earth is older than a few thousand years.\nE. a mechanism for how evolution occurs.\nF. a mechanism for evolution that was supported by evidence.\nG. a complete taxonomy of all known species.\nH. the idea of natural selection.\nI. the theory of relativity.\nJ. the concept of genetic inheritance.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 796, "output_tokens": 351, "total_tokens": 1147}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2676", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Those being hunted adopt a coloring scheme that allows them to blend in to the colors of the environment.\n\nOptions: \nA. Mimetic coloration\nB. Aposomatic coloration\nC. Deceptive markings\nD. Batesian mimicry\nE. Flash coloration\nF. Protective coloration\nG. Warning coloration\nH. Cryptic coloration\nI. Disruptive coloration\nJ. Counter shading\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 641, "output_tokens": 228, "total_tokens": 869}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3106", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the heat shock response ?\n\nOptions: \nA. Heat shock is a response where cells decrease the overall transcription rate and maintain only vital functions at high temperatures\nB. Heat shock is a response where cells increase the transcription of all genes uniformly in response to high temperatures\nC. Heat shock is a response to cold temperatures\nD. Heat shock is a response where cells only transcribe heat shock genes under normal temperature conditions\nE. Heat shock is a response where cells stop transcribing the previously active genes and instead transcribe a new set of genes called heat shock genes when the temperature is raised.\nF. Heat shock is a state where cells rapidly divide in response to high temperatures\nG. Heat shock is a response where cells continue to transcribe the same genes despite high temperatures\nH. Heat shock is a response where cells primarily transcribe heat shock genes in extremely low temperatures\nI. Heat shock is a cellular process that repairs DNA damage caused by high temperatures without altering gene transcription\nJ. Heat shock is a gene mutation caused by 