ons given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the prevailing notion prior to the time of Lyell and Darwin?\n\nOptions: \nA. Earth is millions of years old, and populations are unchanging.\nB. Earth is millions of years old, and populations gradually change.\nC. Earth is a few thousand years old, and populations rapidly change.\nD. Earth is a few thousand years old, and populations are unchanging.\nE. Earth is billions of years old, and populations gradually change.\nF. Earth is a few hundred years old, and populations are unchanging.\nG. Earth is billions of years old, and populations are unchanging.\nH. Earth is a few thousand years old, and populations gradually change.\nI. Earth is millions of years old, and populations rapidly change.\nJ. Earth is a few hundred years old, and populations gradually change.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1084, "output_tokens": 318, "total_tokens": 1402}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2763", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The skin is much more than merely an outer wrapping for an animal; it is an important organ system and performs many diverse functions. What are some of the primary functions of the skin in man?\n\nOptions: \nA. The skin primarily serves as a storage site for fat-soluble vitamins\nB. The skin's primary function is to enhance physical appearance\nC. The primary function of the skin is to provide an outer covering for the body\nD. The main function of the skin is to produce sweat and keep the body cool\nE. The skin's main function is to regulate the level of oxygen entering the body\nF. The main function of the skin is to produce pigments that give color to the hair and eyes\nG. The skin's primary function is to absorb nutrients from the external environment\nH. The primary role of the skin is to act as a secondary respiratory organ\nI. The primary functions of the skin are to protect the body against external agents, maintain a constant internal environment, thermoregulation, and excretion of metabolic wastes.\nJ. The primary function of the skin is to facilitate the sense of touch only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1404, "output_tokens": 344, "total_tokens": 1748}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3323", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is meant by arteriosclerosis and what is the cause of thiscondition?\n\nOptions: \nA. Arteriosclerosis is an inflammation of the arterial walls caused primarily by bacterial infections.\nB. Arteriosclerosis is caused by high blood pressure.\nC. Arteriosclerosis is a disease characterized by a thickening of the arterial wall with connective tissue and deposits of cholesterol. It is caused by factors like smoking, obesity, high-fat diet, and nervous tension.\nD. Arteriosclerosis is a disease caused by a virus.\nE. Arteriosclerosis is a condition where veins harden due to calcium deposits.\nF. Arteriosclerosis is a disease where the arterial walls thin and weaken, often due t