tomatically trains animals to perform complex tasks without reinforcement\nB. Skinner box is a tool for enhancing the cognitive abilities of animals through exposure to various puzzles\nC. Skinner box is used for memory exercises\nD. Skinner box is used in operant conditioning to reward or punish a behavior, thereby increasing or decreasing the probability of its occurrence.\nE. Skinner box is a punishment device\nF. Skinner box is a tool for sensory deprivation\nG. Skinner box is primarily used for classical conditioning involving involuntary behaviors\nH. Skinner box is designed to study the natural habitat behaviors of animals\nI. Skinner box is a device that measures the intelligence quotient (IQ) of animals\nJ. Skinner box is used to observe the effects of different drugs on behavior without any reinforcement contingencies\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1168, "output_tokens": 401, "total_tokens": 1569}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2702", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is meant by the termtransgressivesegregation? How can it be explained?\n\nOptions: \nA. Transgressive segregation is when there is no variability in the F_2 generation.\nB. Transgressive segregation results from the combination of recessive alleles from both parents.\nC. Transgressive segregation is the consistent expression of only dominant alleles in the F_2 generation.\nD. Transgressive segregation is a process where the F_2 generation remains identical to the parent generation.\nE. Transgressive segregation is a process where the F_2 generation shows a reversal of traits compared to the F_1 generation.\nF. Transgressive segregation is seen when the variability of an F_2 generation is so great that some individuals show more extreme development than either parental type.\nG. Transgressive segregation occurs when the F_2 generation shows less variability than the F_1 generation.\nH. Transgressive segregation happens when the F_2 generation shows traits that are intermediate between the two parental types.\nI. Transgressive segregation only occurs when all active alleles are equal.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1404, "output_tokens": 376, "total_tokens": 1780}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3264", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A women feeds her new cat daily with canned cat food. As she opens the cans with a noisy electric can opener, she calls the cat. The cat comes in response, to its name, and the woman feeds it. Why does the cat eventually come running when it hears the electric can opener?\n\nOptions: \nA. The cat believes that the can opener itself is a toy.\nB. The cat has learned that the can opener noise means someone is in the kitchen.\nC. The cat recognizes the can opener as a signal that its owner is nearby.\nD. The cat enjoys the routine of the feeding process and the sound signifies the start.\nE. The cat is trained to respond to the sound of the can opener.\nF. The cat is attracted by the noise of the can opener.\nG. The cat likes the sound of the can opener.\nH. The cat has associated the sound of the can opener with the presentation of food.\nI. The cat is curious about the source of the noise and comes to investigate.\nJ. The cat has been conditioned to come for a treat whenever it hears any electrical appliance.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1324, "output_tokens": 387, "total_tokens": 1711}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3299", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Distinguish between covalent and ionic bonds.\n\nOptions: \nA. A covalent bond is the attraction between two atoms sharing multiple protons, whereas an ionic bond is the attraction between two neutrally charged atoms.\nB. A covalent bond is a bond in which two atoms are held together by a shared pair of electrons. An ionic bond is a bond in which oppositely charged ions are held together by electrical attraction.\nC. A covalent bond is created when one atom donates both electrons in a pair, and an ionic bond occurs when two positively charged ions attract each other.\nD. A covalent bond is a bond formed when two atoms share a neutron. An ionic bond is a bond formed when two ions of different charges form a magnetic attraction.\nE. A covalent bond involves the transfer of electrons from one atom to another, while an ionic bond involves sharing a pair of neutrons between two atoms.\nF. A covalent bond is a bond where two atoms share a pair of protons. An ionic bond is a bond where two ions of the same charge are held together by their magnetic field.\nG. A covalent bond is formed when two atoms share a pair of electrons. An ionic bond is formed when two atoms of the same charge are held together by electrical repulsion.\nH. A covalent bond is formed by the attraction between ions of the same charge, and an ionic bond is formed when atoms share pairs of protons.\nI. A covalent bond is a bond where two atoms share a pair of electrons unevenly, and an ionic bond is a bond where two atoms of opposite charges share a neutron.\nJ. A covalent bond occurs when two atoms share a pair of electrons with identical charges, while an ionic bond is the result of two atoms with similar electronegativities transferring electrons.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 2040, "output_tokens": 426, "total_tokens": 2466}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2958", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why are organ transplants generally unsuccessful?\n\nOptions: \nA. Lack of available organs\nB. Graft rejection due to immunological reaction\nC. Incompatibility of blood types\nD. Allergic reactions to anesthesia\nE. Insufficient surgical expertise\nF. Inadequate post-operative care\nG. Genetic mutations in the donor organ\nH. Infection due to non-sterile surgical environment\nI. Organ malfunction post-transplant\nJ. Poor surgical procedures\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 644, "output_tokens": 287, "total_tokens": 931}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3066", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is meant by the term \"renal threshold\"?\"renal clearance\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. The renal threshold is the blood pressure level above which the kidneys start to increase urine production.\nB. Renal threshold and renal clearance refer to the same concept.\nC. Renal clearance is the rate at which a particular substance is introduced into the renal tubules.\nD. Renal threshold is the amount of substance that can be absorbed by the kidney.\nE. Renal threshold is the minimum plasma concentration of a substance required to trigger kidney disease.\nF. Renal clearance is the process by which the kidneys filter out cellular waste products from the blood into the urine, without considering the concentration of substances.\nG. Renal threshold refers to the maximum volume of urine that can be produced by the kidneys.\nH. Renal clearance measures the ability of the kidneys to recover a substance from the urine and return it to the blood.\nI. The renal threshold is the concentration in the plasma of a substance such as glucose at the point where it just begins to appear in the urine. The renal clearance expresses quantitatively the kidneys' ability to eliminate a given substance from the blood.\nJ. Renal clearance refers to the quantity of substance that can be filtered by the kidney.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1511, "output_tokens": 397, "total_tokens": 1908}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2904", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Differentiate between an isometric and an isotonic contraction.\n\nOptions: \nA. Isotonic contractions are used for maintaining posture and isometric contractions are used for movement\nB. An isotonic contraction is when the muscle length remains constant and an isometric contraction is when the muscle length changes\nC. An isotonic contraction is when a muscle maintains the same tension as it lengthens, while an isometric contraction is when a muscle shortens without any load.\nD. An isotonic contraction is when a muscle lengthens and an isometric contraction is when a muscle shortens\nE. An isotonic contraction is when a muscle shortens and lifts a load, with the load remaining constant. An isometric contraction is the development of muscle tension at a constant muscle length, typically used for maintaining posture.\nF. Isometric contractions result in muscle lengthening under tension, while isotonic contractions maintain a constant muscle length without tension.\nG. An isotonic contraction results in a change in muscle tension but no movement or change in muscle length.\nH. Isometric contractions involve dynamic movements that change muscle length, while isotonic contractions are static and involve no movement.\nI. Isotonic contractions occur without any external load, while isometric contractions involve lifting varying weights.\nJ. An isometric contraction occurs when a muscle both shortens and lengthens simultaneously while lifting a load.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1674, "output_tokens": 315, "total_tokens": 1989}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3182", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An inexperienced nurse measures the blood pressure in the artery of the upper arm of a man. She then measures the blood pressure in the artery of the man's leg. The nurse obtains a different value. Why?\n\nOptions: \nA. The man's leg has a different heart rate\nB. The arm and leg measurements differ because of a temporary blockage in the leg artery\nC. The blood pressure decreases as the blood moves further away from the heart\nD. The different readings are due to the man's varying stress levels\nE. The man was standing during the leg measurement, affecting the result\nF. The leg artery was constricted, leading to a higher reading\nG. The blood pressure is always the same in all parts of the body\nH. The nurse made a measurement error\nI. The blood pressure is higher in the leg due to increased muscle activity\nJ. The leg artery naturally has higher pressure due to gravity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1184, "output_tokens": 372, "total_tokens": 1556}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2784", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What components of the plasma can affect the blood pressure? Explain how they affect it. What other solutes are present in the plasma?\n\nOptions: \nA. The concentration of inorganic salts has no effect on blood pressure.\nB. The presence of white blood cells is the main determinant of blood pressure.\nC. Only red blood cells affect the blood pressure.\nD. Only the concentration of oxygen and carbon dioxide in plasma affects blood pressure.\nE. Plasma proteins have no influence on blood pressure; plasma is primarily composed of vitamins and minerals.\nF. The viscosity of plasma, unrelated to its solute content, is the sole factor influencing blood pressure.\nG. Plasma contains only water and no solutes.\nH. The concentrations of inorganic salts and plasma proteins can affect the blood pressure. Plasma also contains organic nutrients, nitrogenous waste products, hormones and dissolved gases.\nI. Blood pressure is unaffected by plasma composition; plasma contains only immune system factors.\nJ. The concentration of glucose in plasma is the only factor affecting blood pressure.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1392, "output_tokens": 362, "total_tokens": 1754}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3099", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The predominant cell type infected by HIV is CD4^+ cells. The mostimportant of these are the T-helper cells. (Review the immunogeneticschapter for a description of T_H-cells.) As the diseaseprogresses through latency into AIDS-related complexand finally full-blown AIDS, the absolute number of CD4^+ cells (i.e., T_H-cells) decreases.The rate of T_H-cell deletionincreases as the patient enters ARC. As the number ofT_H-cells decreases, the ratio of CD4^+ to CD8^+ cells inverts, goingfrom about 2:1 to less than 1:2. Why is the T_H-cell sucha devastating target ?\n\nOptions: \nA. T_H-cells are auxiliary cells that enhance the phagocytic function of macrophages without affecting lymphocytes.\nB. T_H-cells are necessary for the proper functioning of the specific immune system, that is, for cytotoxic T-cells (T_c) and most B-cells.\nC. T_H-cells are necessary for the functioning of only B-cells\nD. T_H-cells are primarily involved in the production of mucus as a barrier against pathogens.\nE. T_H-cells are the primary cell type that produces histamine in response to allergens.\nF. T_H-cells are necessary for the maintenance of the skin's barrier function.\nG. T_H-cells are only involved in the initial recognition of pathogens, without influencing the adaptive immune response.\nH. T_H-cells are necessary for the functioning of non-specific immune system\nI. T_H-cells are responsible for the production of antibodies against only non-pathogenic antigens.\nJ. T_H-cells are not necessary for the immune system\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1791, "output_tokens": 394, "total_tokens": 2185}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3155", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Vinegar is classified as an acid. What does this tell you about the concentration of the hydrogen ions and the hydroxide ions?\n\nOptions: \nA. Vinegar has a lower concentration of hydrogen ions than hydroxide ions\nB. Vinegar has an excess of hydrogen ions with respect to hydroxide ions\nC. Vinegar has a higher concentration of hydroxide ions than water\nD. Vinegar has no hydroxide ions\nE. Vinegar does not contain hydrogen ions\nF. Vinegar has an excess of hydroxide ions with respect to hydrogen ions\nG. Vinegar has an equal concentration of hydrogen ions to water\nH. Vinegar has a fluctuating concentration of hydrogen and hydroxide ions\nI. Vinegar's hydrogen and hydroxide ion concentrations are not measurable\nJ. Vinegar has an equal concentration of hydrogen and hydroxide ions\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1092, "output_tokens": 239, "total_tokens": 1331}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3153", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a chemical reaction? What is meant by the rate- limiting step of a chemical reaction?\n\nOptions: \nA. A chemical reaction occurs when there is no change in the bonds of the reactants\nB. A chemical reaction is the process of combining elements to form new compounds\nC. Chemical reactions are changes where new substances are formed by changing the location of electrons only, while the rate-limiting step is the one that involves the least number of molecules.\nD. A chemical reaction is the process of heating substances to create a new product, and the rate-limiting step is the initial step that starts the reaction.\nE. Chemical reactions involve the breakdown of compounds into their elemental parts, and the rate-limiting step is the final step that completes the reaction.\nF. A chemical reaction is a process that only involves the exchange of ions between two compounds, with the rate-limiting step being the one that releases the most energy.\nG. The rate-determining step is the fastest step in a reaction\nH. A chemical reaction is a physical change that alters the state of matter of the reactants without changing their chemical composition, and the rate-limiting step is the step that occurs more frequently than others.\nI. A chemical reaction is an interaction where reactants remain chemically the same but change in physical form, and the rate-determining step is the step with the lowest concentration of reactants.\nJ. A chemical reaction is one in which bonds are broken and/or formed, with products being chemically different from the reactants. The rate-determining (or limiting) step of a reaction is the step that requires the highest activation energy and thus determines the rate of the entire reaction.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1938, "output_tokens": 342, "total_tokens": 2280}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3220", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Are there comparable changes, in the male, to female menopause?\n\nOptions: \nA. Males experience a temporary pause in reproductive function, which fully recovers after a few years\nB. Males undergo a sudden increase in fertility at an age comparable to female menopause\nC. No complete cessation of reproductive function in males analogous to female menopause\nD. Testosterone levels in males increase to peak levels in their later life, similar to a reverse menopause\nE. Males face a complete and permanent stop in the production of all reproductive hormones at a certain age\nF. Testosterone levels sharply drop in males in their later life\nG. Dramatic changes occur in males similar to female menopause\nH. Males have a gradual increase in reproductive hormones during middle age\nI. Males experience a well-defined period known as andropause, which is identical to menopause\nJ. Males also experience menopause\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1216, "output_tokens": 461, "total_tokens": 1677}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2695", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In humans, the liver is one of the largest and most active organsin the body. Describe its functions.\n\nOptions: \nA. The liver only detoxifies harmful substances.\nB. The liver filters out red blood cells, produces urine, and regulates body temperature.\nC. The liver produces insulin and glucagon, regulates carbohydrate metabolism, and stores vitamins.\nD. The liver is mainly responsible for the production of bile.\nE. The liver regulates the level of glucose in the blood, converts glucose into fat, produces bile, detoxifies ammonia, produces cholesterol, plays roles in blood clotting, and is involved in the activation of vitamin D.\nF. The liver synthesizes proteins for muscle development and stores excess glucose as glycogen.\nG. The liver's main function is the regulation of glucose levels.\nH. The liver is involved in the synthesis of growth hormones and the regulation of the body's immune response.\nI. The liver is responsible for the production of digestive enzymes and the absorption of nutrients.\nJ. The liver's primary role is to break down muscle tissue and recycle red blood cells.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1408, "output_tokens": 359, "total_tokens": 1767}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3039", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is mutualism? Give three examples of this type of relationship.\n\nOptions: \nA. Mutualism is a relationship where one species benefits and the other is harmed. Examples include: the clownfish and sea anemone, oxpeckers and rhinos, and honeybees and flowers.\nB. Mutualism is a relationship where one species benefits and the other is unaffected. Examples include: barnacles on whales, remoras on sharks, and orchids growing on trees.\nC. In the mutualistic type of relationship, both species benefit from each other. Examples include: Nitrogen-fixing bacteria of the genus Rhizobium and legumes, lichens which are a combination of fungi and algae, and ants and aphids or scale insects.\nD. Only one species benefits in mutualism\nE. Mutualism is a relationship where both species are harmed. Examples include: parasitic wasps and caterpillars, mistletoe and trees, and tapeworms and mammals.\nF. Mutualism is a type of relationship where both species compete for resources. Examples include: different tree species in a forest, coral and algae, and various species of scavengers on a carcass.\nG. Mutualism does not occur in plants\nH. Mutualism refers to the relationship between predator and prey. Examples include: cheetahs and gazelles, wolves and deer, and hawks and rodents.\nI. Examples of mutualism include lion and gazelle, cat and mouse, wolf and rabbit\nJ. Examples of mutualism include sharks and remoras, crocodiles and plover birds, and humans and domesticated animals.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1741, "output_tokens": 363, "total_tokens": 2104}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3171", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If antibodies can be brought into contact with a virus before it attaches itself to the host cell, the virus will be inactivated. Once infection has occurred, the production of interferon may protect the host from extensive tissue destruction. Explain.\n\nOptions: \nA. Interferon kills the virus directly\nB. Interferon enhances the attachment of viruses to host cells, facilitating the infection process.\nC. Interferon is a broad-spectrum antiviral drug that is administered to patients to cure viral infections.\nD. Interferon strengthens the virus, making it more difficult for the immune system to eliminate it.\nE. Interferon is a type of virus that fights other viruses\nF. Interferon is a protein produced by virus-infected cells, which spreads to uninfected cells and makes them more resistant to viral infection. This prevents synthesis of viral proteins which are essential for viral production.\nG. Antibodies produce interferon in response to a viral infection, which then inactivates the virus.\nH. Interferon is a chemical signal that increases the permeability of cells, allowing antibodies to enter and attack the virus.\nI. Interferon triggers the immediate destruction of the host cell to prevent the spread of the virus.\nJ. Interferon is produced by the virus to weaken the host cell\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1604, "output_tokens": 400, "total_tokens": 2004}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2773", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Explain how an estimate of the age of a rock is made on the basisof the radioactive elements present.\n\nOptions: \nA. By assessing the fossil content found within the rock layers\nB. By comparing the density of the rock to a known age database\nC. By examining the color and texture of the rock\nD. By counting the layers of the rock\nE. By measuring the amount of carbon-14 remaining in the rock\nF. By observing the size and weight of the rock\nG. By measuring the proportion of uranium and lead in a given rock, we can estimate with a high degree of accuracy the absolute age of the rock.\nH. By calculating the rate of sediment deposition on the rock\nI. By determining the magnetic properties of the rock\nJ. By analyzing the chemical composition of minerals within the rock for wear and degradation patterns\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1075, "output_tokens": 377, "total_tokens": 1452}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2727", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It is observed that the chemical transmission occurring at a synapse is unidirectional that is, the neurotransmitter always travels from thepresynapticaxon to the post-synaptic dendrite . Explain why.\n\nOptions: \nA. Neurotransmitter release is stimulated by electrical signals traveling towards the dendrites only.\nB. The receptors for neurotransmitters are only found on the axonal terminals.\nC. The neurotransmitter is present in the axonal end of a neuron only.\nD. The synaptic vesicle is present inside the dendrites of a neuron.\nE. The axonal terminals do not possess the machinery to release neurotransmitters.\nF. The neurotransmitter degrades immediately upon release and cannot travel to the axon.\nG. The dendrites actively pump the neurotransmitter back to the axon after it has been received.\nH. The neurotransmitter is present in the dendritic end of a neuron only.\nI. The dendrites release a different neurotransmitter that negates the effect of the axonal neurotransmitter.\nJ. The neurotransmitter can travel in both directions.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1352, "output_tokens": 395, "total_tokens": 1747}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3316", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is implied by the theory ofuniformitarianism?\n\nOptions: \nA. Uniformitarianism indicates that human activity is the primary driver of geological change.\nB. Uniformitarianism posits that the earth is static and unchanging over time.\nC. Uniformitarianism implies rapid geological changes.\nD. Uniformitarianism suggests that the same geological processes observed today did not operate in the past.\nE. Uniformitarianism infers that geological processes occur exclusively during catastrophic events.\nF. Uniformitarianism asserts that the earth's geological features were formed in a single, divine creation event.\nG. Uniformitarianism implies that animals and plants continually undergo a process of organic evolution and that the earth must be much older than a few thousand years.\nH. Uniformitarianism assumes that the rate of geological change is unpredictable and chaotic.\nI. Uniformitarianism states that geological forces have changed over time.\nJ. Uniformitarianism suggests the earth is only a few thousand years old.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1260, "output_tokens": 487, "total_tokens": 1747}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3033", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the presence of alcohol dehydrogenase, the rate of reduction of acetaldehyde to ethanol increases as the concentration of acetaldehyde is increased. Eventually, the rate of the reaction reaches a maximum, after which point further increases in the concentration of acetaldehyde have no effect. Which of the following is true at the maximal rate of reaction?\n\nOptions: \nA. The enzyme's catalytic activity has been reduced.\nB. The change in free energy of the reaction decreases.\nC. The concentration of acetaldehyde has surpassed the enzyme's affinity for it.\nD. The enzyme starts interacting with other molecules instead of acetaldehyde.\nE. The enzyme is no longer specific for acetaldehyde.\nF. The enzyme has been denatured.\nG. Nearly all of the enzyme molecules are interacting with acetaldehyde molecules.\nH. The enzyme molecules are completely saturated with ethanol.\nI. The activation energy of the reaction decreases.\nJ. The reaction has reached a state of equilibrium.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1233, "output_tokens": 355, "total_tokens": 1588}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3025", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An eager AP Biology student interested in studying osmosis and the movement of water in solutions took a dialysis bag containing a 0.5 M solution and placed it into a beaker containing a 0.6 M solution. Which of the following is true about water potential?\n\nOptions: \nA. An eager AP Biology student interested in studying osmosis and the movement of water in solutions took a dialysis bag containing a 0.5 M solution and placed it into a beaker containing a 0.6 M solution. It drives the movement of water from a region of lower water potential to a region of higher water potential.\nB. Solute potential is the only factor that determines the water potential.\nC. Pressure potential combines with solute potential to determine the water potential.\nD. Water potential always drives water from an area of lower pressure potential to an area of higher pressure potential.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1172, "output_tokens": 455, "total_tokens": 1627}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2780", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The kangaroo rat never drinks water, yet it survives in some of the hottest and driest regions of the world. Explain how it obtains and conserves water.\n\nOptions: \nA. The kangaroo rat has a symbiotic relationship with a plant that provides it with water\nB. The kangaroo rat consumes small pebbles that help it extract moisture from the food it eats\nC. The kangaroo rat relies on a slow metabolism to minimize water loss\nD. The kangaroo rat extracts water from the insects it eats\nE. The kangaroo rat obtains all of its water from carbohydrate metabolism and its kidneys are modified to conserve as much water as possible.\nF. The kangaroo rat drinks dew drops from plants\nG. The kangaroo rat collects water in its fur during the night and licks it off\nH. The kangaroo rat burrows deep underground to access moisture in the soil\nI. The kangaroo rat has a special organ to absorb water from the air\nJ. The kangaroo rat stores water in its tail\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1215, "output_tokens": 344, "total_tokens": 1559}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2822", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Are the daughter nuclei formed during cleavage exactly equivalent , or is there some sort of parceling out of potentialities during cleavage?\n\nOptions: \nA. Partial segregation of genetic potentialities during cleavage\nB. Partial segregation of genetic potentialities, influenced by environmental factors during cleavage\nC. Random parceling out of genetic potentialities independent of cleavage\nD. Segregation of genetic potentialities occurs, but only in specific cell lineages\nE. Segregation of genetic potentialities only in later stages\nF. Segregation of genetic potentialities with bias toward cellular location\nG. No segregation of genetic potentialities during cleavage\nH. Segregation of genetic potentialities based on maternal and paternal origin\nI. Segregation of genetic potentialities during cleavage\nJ. Equal segregation of genetic potentialities, but differential activation during cleavage\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The daughter nuclei formed during cleavage are genetically identical due to mitosis, so no segregation of genetic potentialities occurs at that stage. While cytoplasmic determinants may be partitioned, the nuclei themselves remain equivalent. Therefore, the correct choice is G.\n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1183, "output_tokens": 719, "total_tokens": 1902}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3213", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: I nsulin , interferon, and growth hormone have been successfully manufactured in large quantities by the pharmaceutical industries. Explain the importance of genetic engineering in this process.\n\nOptions: \nA. Genetic engineering facilitates the mass production of these proteins by enhancing the animals' ability to produce them in their milk.\nB. Genetic engineering assists in the development of new pharmaceutical drugs.\nC. Genetic engineering is primarily used for cloning organisms, which increases the yield of insulin, interferon, and growth hormone.\nD. Genetic engineering enables the creation of completely synthetic substitutes for insulin, interferon, and growth hormone that do not rely on biological processes.\nE. Genetic engineering improves the nutritional value of food which indirectly helps in the production of these proteins.\nF. Genetic engineering allows for the direct extraction of insulin, interferon, and growth hormone from genetically modified plants.\nG. Genetic engineering is used to modify the human genome to produce insulin, interferon, and growth hormone naturally in the body.\nH. Genetic engineering allows for the large scale production of proteins such as insulin, interferon, and growth hormone through recombinant DNA techniques, lowering their prices and making them more accessible.\nI. Genetic engineering helps in understanding the genetic basis of diseases.\nJ. Genetic engineering aids in the diagnosis of diseases.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1768, "output_tokens": 425, "total_tokens": 2193}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3115", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One group of compounds that may become quite important in birth control is the prostaglandins. What are the advantages of prostaglandins in birth control?\n\nOptions: \nA. Prostaglandins are used to enhance mood and have no effect on birth control.\nB. Prostaglandins increase fertility by promoting ovulation.\nC. Prostaglandins are able to prevent pregnancy by altering the DNA of the sperm and egg.\nD. Prostaglandins are known to mediate hormonal action\nE. Prostaglandins are non-hormonal, reducing the risk of hormonal side effects.\nF. Prostaglandins can be taken orally once a month, providing long-term birth control.\nG. Prostaglandins are cyclic, oxygenated, 20-carbon fatty acids\nH. Prostaglandins induce strong contractions in the uterus, prevent the fertilized ovum from being implanted, and can be introduced directly into the uterus, making them potentially safer contraceptives than oral chemical agents.\nI. Prostaglandins improve skin condition and are used as a beauty supplement.\nJ. Prostaglandins are efficient in treating nasal congestion\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1323, "output_tokens": 350, "total_tokens": 1673}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2885", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why is the organism that causes smallpox not used in the vaccine against smallpox?\n\nOptions: \nA. The organism is extinct in the wild and cannot be harvested for vaccine production\nB. The organism that causes smallpox is too costly to use in vaccine production\nC. The use of the actual virulent variola virus may be dangerous if too much is administered\nD. Smallpox virus is confined to research laboratories\nE. There is no specific treatment for smallpox\nF. The smallpox virus mutates too rapidly to be effective in a vaccine\nG. There are ethical concerns about using a live pathogen in vaccines\nH. Vaccinia virus, a less dangerous relative, provides immunity without the risk of causing disease\nI. The smallpox organism cannot be weakened or inactivated for safe vaccine use\nJ. Smallpox is never produced with the vaccinia virus\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1140, "output_tokens": 339, "total_tokens": 1479}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2909", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A newborn infant is examined by a doctor, who determines that the child has syphilis. Explain how the child con-tracted syphilis .\n\nOptions: \nA. The baby contracted it from a contaminated surface.\nB. The baby acquired the infection through kissing or close contact with an infected person.\nC. The infant contracted the disease from another infant.\nD. The child inherited the disease as an autosomal recessive trait from the parents.\nE. The child contracted the disease from a blood transfusion shortly after birth.\nF. The infant was vaccinated with a contaminated needle.\nG. An infected mother can transmit the organism by placental transfer to the fetus during the first four months of pregnancy or as the fetus passes through the infected vagina during birth.\nH. The infant developed the disease due to exposure to the bacterium in the hospital environment after birth.\nI. The baby contracted it through breastfeeding from an infected mother.\nJ. The baby was born with it due to a genetic mutation.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1312, "output_tokens": 344, "total_tokens": 1656}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3230", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: All of the algae have the green pigment chlorophyll, yet the different phyla of algae show a great variety of colors. Explain.\n\nOptions: \nA. Different algae phyla contain a variety of pigments, including accessory pigments, in varying concentrations resulting in different colors. These pigments absorb different light wavelengths and play roles in photosynthesis.\nB. Algal colors change with the seasons, similar to leaves on a tree.\nC. All algae only have green pigments\nD. The color of algae is due to the surrounding environment\nE. Algae can camouflage their color to match their surroundings, leading to diversity in appearance.\nF. Different colors in algae are a result of different water temperatures they live in.\nG. The intensity of sunlight exposure alters the green pigment, causing variations in color.\nH. Different colors in algae are due to genetic mutations\nI. The presence of various minerals in the water contributes to the color differences in algae.\nJ. Color variations in algae are due to the depth at which they are found in the water, as different colors penetrate water to different depths.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1354, "output_tokens": 397, "total_tokens": 1751}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2799", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Describe the differences between an element and a compound.\n\nOptions: \nA. Compounds are formed from elements through physical changes, such as freezing and melting.\nB. An element's properties are the result of the combination of the properties of the compounds it contains.\nC. Elements are always liquid at room temperature, while compounds are always solid.\nD. Compounds are substances that consist of identical molecules. Elements are made of two or more types of molecules combined randomly.\nE. Compounds consist of identical atoms.\nF. Elements are composed of multiple types of atoms.\nG. Elements can be broken down into compounds through nuclear reactions, while compounds are indivisible.\nH. Elements can be separated into simpler substances by chemical means, while compounds cannot.\nI. Elements are substances that consist of identical atoms. A compound is a substance that is composed of two or more different kinds of atoms combined in a definite weight ratio.\nJ. Elements and compounds have the same atomic structure\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1262, "output_tokens": 299, "total_tokens": 1561}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2728", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How can radioactive isotopes be used in biological research such as tracing the pathways of compounds synthesized in the living cell?\n\nOptions: \nA. Labeling substance with radioactive isotopes is a powerful method for studying specific metabolic pathways, as well as being applicable to many other areas of biological research.\nB. Radioactive isotopes are used for improving the flavor and texture of food products.\nC. Radioactive isotopes are used to stimulate the immune system in organisms.\nD. Radioactive isotopes are used to increase the oxygen-carrying capacity of blood.\nE. Radioactive isotopes are used to enhance the growth of agricultural crops.\nF. Radioactive isotopes are used as a direct nutrient supplement in animal diets.\nG. Radioactive isotopes are primarily used to create glow-in-the-dark materials for scientific equipment.\nH. Radioactive isotopes are used to provide energy for spacecrafts.\nI. Radioactive isotopes are used to kill cancer cells.\nJ. Radioactive isotopes are used for dating archaeological samples.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1348, "output_tokens": 321, "total_tokens": 1669}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2994", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the physiological basis of allergies? What measures can be taken to decrease the effect of allergies?\n\nOptions: \nA. Allergies are adverse immunological responses to antigens. Antihistamines and desensitization therapy can help decrease the effect of allergies.\nB. Allergies are triggered by the body's overproduction of white blood cells. Avoiding allergens and taking vitamin supplements can decrease the effect of allergies.\nC. Allergies are caused by genetic mutations and can be minimized by regular exercise and a healthy diet.\nD. Allergies can be fully cured with antihistamines.\nE. Allergies are caused by exposure to pathogens.\nF. Allergies develop due to an overactive nervous system. Beta-blockers and nerve-calming medications can help mitigate the effects of allergies.\nG. Allergies are a result of lack of immune response.\nH. Allergies are psychosomatic and can be managed through stress reduction techniques and meditation.\nI. Allergies result from the body's inability to produce sufficient antibodies. Immunoglobulin therapy can help decrease the effect of allergies.\nJ. Allergies are the body's natural response to environmental pollutants. Using air purifiers and avoiding outdoor activities can reduce allergy symptoms.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1560, "output_tokens": 383, "total_tokens": 1943}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2765", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the physiological purpose of shivering?\n\nOptions: \nA. Shivering is a method the body uses to relieve pain.\nB. Shivering is a tactic to ward off predators by appearing agitated.\nC. Shivering is a way to burn excess calories\nD. Shivering is a response to fear or anxiety\nE. Shivering is an involuntary action to prepare muscles for physical activity.\nF. Shivering is a means by which the body maintains its normal temperature when the ambient temperature is cold.\nG. Shivering is a strategy to reduce body temperature in hot environments.\nH. Shivering is a side effect of the body's immune response to infections.\nI. Shivering is a reaction to high body temperature\nJ. Shivering is a reflex that helps to increase oxygen intake.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1010, "output_tokens": 324, "total_tokens": 1334}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2997", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How has the action of reverse transcriptase been exploited by biologists?\n\nOptions: \nA. Reverse transcriptase is employed to directly replicate DNA in PCR amplifications.\nB. Reverse transcriptase is applied in the creation of vaccines by altering DNA sequences.\nC. Reverse transcriptase catalyzes the synthesis of DNA from RNA and is a necessary reagent for genetic engineering with recombinant DNA.\nD. Reverse transcriptase is used to transcribe DNA from proteins\nE. Reverse transcriptase is used to convert lipids into DNA for genome mapping.\nF. Reverse transcriptase is utilized to enhance the mutation rate in organisms for evolutionary studies.\nG. Reverse transcriptase is used to transcribe proteins from DNA\nH. Reverse transcriptase is used for converting mRNA into proteins in vitro.\nI. Reverse transcriptase is used in the manufacturing of synthetic RNA for therapeutic purposes.\nJ. Reverse transcriptase is primarily used in the study of retroviruses\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1207, "output_tokens": 398, "total_tokens": 1605}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3086", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements concerning a sarcomere of a striated muscle (such as skeletal muscle) is correct?\n\nOptions: \nA. The A band shortens during muscle contraction.\nB. During contraction H zones become elongated.\nC. The proteins troponin and tropomyosin constitute the thick and thin filaments, respectively.\nD. Myosin filaments are found in the I band.\nE. Troponin and tropomyosin are located in the H zone.\nF. Tropomyosin binds to myosin, blocking the actin-binding site.\nG. The thin filaments are composed entirely of myosin.\nH. In the relaxed position tropomyosin impedes myosin's access to the binding site of actin.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 944, "output_tokens": 522, "total_tokens": 1466}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2830", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Distinguish betweenpenetranceand expressivity.\n\nOptions: \nA. Penetrance refers to how widespread a trait is within a population, while expressivity measures the intensity of the trait.\nB. Penetrance is the physical appearance resulting from a genotype, while expressivity is the genetic makeup of an organism.\nC. Penetrance is the measure of the strength of a gene's effect, while expressivity is the measure of the stability of a gene's expression across generations.\nD. Penetrance is the percentage of individuals who carry a gene and express it phenotypically, while expressivity is the degree of effect or the extent to which a gene expresses itself in different individuals.\nE. Expressivity is the proportion of individuals in a population who show a particular trait, whereas penetrance is the range of manifestations of a gene in different tissues.\nF. Penetrance and expressivity are the same.\nG. Penetrance is the consistency of a gene's expression across different environments, while expressivity is the ability of a gene to be suppressed by other genes.\nH. Penetrance is the likelihood that a trait will appear in the offspring, whereas expressivity is the range of phenotypes resulting from a given genotype.\nI. Penetrance is the degree of effect or the extent to which a gene expresses itself in different individuals, while expressivity is the percentage of individuals who carry a gene and express it phenotypically.\nJ. Expressivity is the probability of a gene being inherited, and penetrance is the variability of a trait's expression among individuals.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1884, "output_tokens": 360, "total_tokens": 2244}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2818", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A competitive inhibitor of an enzyme exerts its effect by\n\nOptions: \nA. reversibly modifying some of the amino acid residues that help to comprise the enzyme's active site\nB. irreversibly forming covalent links with the enzyme, effectively preventing the enzyme's dissociation from it\nC. irreversibly modifying some of the amino acid residues that help to comprise the enzyme's active site\nD. reversibly increasing the number of enzyme molecules that are available to bind substrates\nE. irreversibly decreasing the number of enzyme molecules that are available to bind substrates\nF. competing with the product molecule for the same enzyme but a different binding site than the product binding site\nG. competing with the substrate molecule for the same enzyme but a different binding site than the substrate binding site\nH. irreversibly forming covalent links with the substrate, effectively preventing the enzyme's dissociation from it\nI. reversibly decreasing the number of enzyme molecules that are available to bind substrates\nJ. competing with the substrate molecule for the same enzyme and the same binding site as the substrate binding site\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1460, "output_tokens": 278, "total_tokens": 1738}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2914", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Both food and air pass through the pharynx. Explain how these are channeled into the proper tubes so that the food goes into the stomach and the air goes to the lungs.\n\nOptions: \nA. Food and air take turns entering the pharynx based on the body's breathing and digestive rhythm\nB. Food and air are separated by a valve in the esophagus\nC. The trachea has a filter mechanism that directs food to the stomach and air to the lungs\nD. A series of small cilia in the pharynx sorts food and air into their respective tubes\nE. The epiglottis closes the entrance to the trachea during breathing, ensuring air goes to the lungs and food to the stomach\nF. Food and air are channeled by distinct muscular contractions that guide them to the correct passages\nG. The esophagus expands to receive food while the trachea contracts to guide air\nH. The pharynx separates food and air based on their weight\nI. The larynx moves up so that the glottis is closed by the epiglottis during swallowing, directing food into the esophagus and air into the lungs.\nJ. The lungs filter out food particles from the air\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"inp