 letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 799, "output_tokens": 407, "total_tokens": 1206}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3059", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Chromosomal sex in mammals has been shown to be strongly Y chromosome determined. How was this shown to be true?\n\nOptions: \nA. The absence of a Y chromosome determines maleness in mammals\nB. The presence of a Y chromosome usually determines maleness in mammals\nC. The ratio of two X chromosomes to one Y chromosome determines maleness\nD. The presence of an X chromosome determines maleness in mammals\nE. The presence of an X chromosome in the absence of a Y chromosome determines maleness\nF. The presence of a Y chromosome determines femaleness in mammals\nG. The presence of a Y chromosome has no impact on the determination of maleness\nH. The presence of multiple X chromosomes without a Y chromosome determines maleness\nI. The presence of two or more Y chromosomes is required for maleness\nJ. The presence of an X chromosome determines femaleness in mammals\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1172, "output_tokens": 427, "total_tokens": 1599}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2663", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why are the elements carbon, hydrogen, oxygen, and nitrogen (C, H, O, N) of immense importance in living matter ?\n\nOptions: \nA. These elements are the only elements that can form gases at room temperature\nB. These elements are abundant in living organisms, can readily form covalent bonds and are the lightest elements that can form such bonds.\nC. These elements are the primary sources of energy for living organisms\nD. These elements are radioactive, which is vital for cellular processes\nE. These elements are capable of undergoing sublimation, which is crucial for life functions\nF. These elements are rare and thus more valuable\nG. These elements give color to living organisms\nH. These elements can only be found in DNA and proteins\nI. These elements are the heaviest elements in living organisms\nJ. These elements have magnetic properties that are essential for life\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1184, "output_tokens": 454, "total_tokens": 1638}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3131", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sea divers are aware of a danger known as the \"bends\". Explain the physiological mechanism of the bends.\n\nOptions: \nA. Carbon dioxide bubbles forming in the blood causing acidosis\nB. Rapid increase in barometric pressure causing the bends\nC. Formation of helium bubbles in the bloodstream due to rapid ascent\nD. Increased salinity in the water leading to dehydration and joint pain\nE. Oxygen bubbles forming in the blood leading to hypoxia\nF. Lack of oxygen while breathing under high pressure leading to the bends\nG. Accumulation of lactic acid in muscles due to strenuous activity underwater\nH. Sudden decrease in water temperature causing muscle cramping and disorientation\nI. Rise in blood pressure due to underwater currents, resulting in the bends\nJ. Bubbles of nitrogen gas form in the blood and other tissue fluids when the barometric pressure drops below the total pressure of all gases dissolved in the body fluids, causing dizziness, paralysis, and unconsciousness, known as the bends.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1308, "output_tokens": 368, "total_tokens": 1676}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3199", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which statement about the beak size of finches on the island of Daphne Major during prolonged drought is true?\n\nOptions: \nA. Each bird's beak size increased due to the abundance of food during the drought.\nB. Each bird developed a deeper, stronger beak as the drought persisted.\nC. Each bird's beak became weaker and narrower as the drought persisted.\nD. Each bird evolved a deeper, stronger beak as the drought persisted.\nE. Each bird's survival was not influenced by the depth and strength of its beak during the drought.\nF. Each bird that survived the drought produced only offspring with deeper, stronger beaks than seen in the previous generation.\nG. Each bird's beak size did not change during the drought.\nH. Each bird's survival was strongly influenced by the depth and strength of its beak as the drought persisted.\nI. Each bird's survival was only influenced by its ability to find water during the drought, not the size of its beak.\nJ. Each bird that survived the drought produced offspring with the same beak size as seen in the previous generation.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1372, "output_tokens": 386, "total_tokens": 1758}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3242", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Euglena is a common green flagellate protozoan found in fresh water ponds. Describe briefly the method of locomotion, nutrition, and asexual reproduction in this organism.\n\nOptions: \nA. Euglena moves by contracting its body, carries on heterotrophic nutrition, and reproduces asexually through fragmentation.\nB. Euglena moves by flagellum, carries on autotrophic nutrition and can switch to heterotrophic when necessary, and reproduces asexually through cytokinesis.\nC. Euglena moves by pseudopodia, carries on heterotrophic nutrition, and reproduces sexually.\nD. Euglena moves by flagellum, carries on autotrophic nutrition but cannot shift to heterotrophic, and reproduces asexually through budding.\nE. Euglena moves by flagellum, carries on chemosynthetic nutrition, and reproduces asexually through sporulation.\nF. Euglena moves by undulating its flagellum, carries on autotrophic nutrition but can shift to heterotrophic under darkness, and reproduces asexually through longitudinal binary fission.\nG. Euglena moves by jet propulsion, carries on autotrophic nutrition, and reproduces asexually through multiple fission.\nH. Euglena moves by cilia, carries on autotrophic nutrition but can shift to heterotrophic under light, and reproduces asexually through binary fission.\nI. Euglena moves by gliding along surfaces, carries on autotrophic nutrition but can shift to heterotrophic in the absence of light, and reproduces asexually through budding.\nJ. Euglena moves by flagellum, carries on mixotrophic nutrition, and reproduces asexually through longitudinal binary fission and sporulation.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1798, "output_tokens": 495, "total_tokens": 2293}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3081", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Crossing-over during meiosis permits scientists to determine\n\nOptions: \nA. the rate of mutations\nB. the chance for variation in zygotes\nC. the age of an organism\nD. the potential for genetic disorders\nE. the sequence of DNA bases\nF. the rate of cell division\nG. the number of chromosomes in a cell\nH. which traits are dominant or recessive\nI. the sex of an organism\nJ. the distance between genes on a chromosome\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 724, "output_tokens": 402, "total_tokens": 1126}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3141", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which statement about variation is true?\n\nOptions: \nA. All phenotypic variation is the result of genotypic variation.\nB. All genetic variation produces phenotypic variation.\nC. All nucleotide variability results in neutral variation.\nD. All new alleles are the result of nucleotide variability.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 600, "output_tokens": 468, "total_tokens": 1068}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2792", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What prevents the stomach from being digested by itsown secretions?\n\nOptions: \nA. A thick layer of fat surrounds the stomach, providing protection from digestive acids.\nB. Special bacteria in the stomach neutralize all digestive enzymes.\nC. The stomach lining secretes an alkaline substance that counteracts the acid and prevents digestion.\nD. The lining of the stomach secretes only hydrochloric acid and gastric juice.\nE. The mucus layer, the permeability of the membranes and the continual replacement of the cells comprising the lining all help protect the underlying tissues from the action of proteolytic enzymes of the stomach and duodenum.\nF. The stomach is coated with a layer of strong antibiotics that kill digestive enzymes.\nG. The stomach lining is replaced every 10 to 15 days.\nH. The stomach has a high permeability to hydrogen ions.\nI. The stomach has a unique pH that prevents enzymes from being active.\nJ. Digestive enzymes in the stomach are only activated by food, so they do not attack the stomach lining.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1112, "output_tokens": 318, "total_tokens": 1430}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3210", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Differentiate clearly between \"breathing\" and \"respiration\".\n\nOptions: \nA. Breathing is the chemical process that occurs within cells, while respiration is the physical movement of the diaphragm and rib muscles.\nB. Respiration only occurs in the presence of oxygen, while breathing can occur without oxygen.\nC. Breathing refers to the exchange of gases between cells and environment, while respiration is the mechanical process of taking air into the lungs and expelling it.\nD. Respiration refers to the oxidative degradation of nutrients in cells or the exchange of gases between cells and environment, while breathing is the mechanical process of taking air into the lungs and expelling it.\nE. Respiration and breathing are the same process.\nF. Respiration is the process by which organisms produce sound, while breathing is solely for gas exchange purposes.\nG. Breathing is the process of breaking down food into energy, while respiration is the act of air moving in and out of the lungs.\nH. Respiration is an energy consuming process, while breathing results in energy production in the cells.\nI. Breathing involves the conversion of glucose to energy within the mitochondria, while respiration is the act of inhaling and exhaling air.\nJ. Respiration is a voluntary action controlled by the nervous system, while breathing is an involuntary process controlled by the brain stem.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1696, "output_tokens": 414, "total_tokens": 2110}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3200", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The average birth weight for human babies is about 3 kg. Which of the following terms best describes this?\n\nOptions: \nA. disruptive selection\nB. sexual selection\nC. bottleneck effect\nD. non-random mating\nE. stabilizing selection\nF. genetic drift\nG. directional selection\nH. founder effect\nI. diversifying selection\nJ. artificial selection\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 652, "output_tokens": 295, "total_tokens": 947}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2989", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: All linear genomes share a common problem of replication. Define the problem and describe how the process of reverse transcriptionelegantly solves it.\n\nOptions: \nA. The challenge for all linear genomes is that the DNA polymerases cannot initiate replication de novo. Retroviruses counteract this by using a protein to initiate the synthesis.\nB. The problem with all linear genomes is the inability to replicate without the presence of primer sequences. Retroviruses address this by creating a primer from an RNA template.\nC. The problem faced by all linear genomes is maintaining the structure of the genome. Retroviruses solved this problem by strengthening the bonds between nucleotides.\nD. The difficulty with linear genomes is the formation of secondary structures that impede replication. Retroviruses prevent this by using reverse transcriptase to unwind these structures.\nE. The issue faced by all linear genomes is replication speed. Retroviruses solved this problem by making the process more efficient.\nF. The problem faced by all linear genomes is avoiding mutations. Retroviruses solved this problem with an error-checking mechanism.\nG. Linear genomes face the challenge of DNA damage during replication, which can lead to cell death. Retroviruses have evolved a robust repair system to address this.\nH. All linear genomes struggle with the degradation of DNA at the ends during replication. Retroviruses circumvent this by integrating their DNA into the host genome.\nI. Linear genomes cannot replicate the very ends of the DNA strands, known as the end-replication problem. Retroviruses solve this by adding repeated sequences to the ends of the DNA.\nJ. The problem faced by all linear genomes is replicating the entire genome without loss of information from the ends. Retroviruses solved this problem simply by copying the 5' end before copying the rest of the strand.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 2196, "output_tokens": 466, "total_tokens": 2662}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3065", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Arthropods have an exoskeleton. How is movement accomplished?\n\nOptions: \nA. They use their wings to move\nB. They move by changing the shape of their exoskeleton\nC. They use cilia on the surface of their exoskeleton to move\nD. They move due to their muscular system\nE. They have a soft, pliable inner layer that bends to facilitate movement\nF. Movement is achieved through hydraulic pressure changes within each segment\nG. They release a special fluid that lubricates the joints of the exoskeleton for movement\nH. The exoskeleton contracts and expands allowing for movement\nI. Movement is achieved by the exoskeleton splitting and reforming in new positions\nJ. The body is segmented and the segments are joined by a thin layer of flexible chitin\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1023, "output_tokens": 295, "total_tokens": 1318}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2682", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The tandem back-and-forth evolution of closely related species, which is exemplified by predator-prey relationships.\n\nOptions: \nA. Microevolution\nB. Speciation\nC. Coevolution\nD. Adaptive radiation\nE. Macroevolution\nF. Convergent evolution\nG. Gradual evolution\nH. Punctuated equilibrium\nI. Divergent evolution\nJ. Parallel evolution\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 644, "output_tokens": 214, "total_tokens": 858}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2942", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Adrenalin is a hormone which stimulates the sympathetic system . What effects would you expect adrenaline tohave on (a) the digestive tract, (b) the iris of the eye, and (c) the heart beat?\n\nOptions: \nA. (a) Increases peristalsis and reduces secretion, (b) Causes both sets of muscles in the iris to relax, (c) Accelerates and weakens the heartbeat\nB. (a) Enhances digestion, (b) Causes the iris to change color, (c) Decreases the heart rate\nC. (a) No effect on the digestive tract, (b) Causes both sets of muscles in the iris to contract, (c) Slows the heart rate\nD. (a) Enhances digestion and secretion, (b) No effect on the muscles of the iris, (c) Accelerates the heart rate\nE. (a) No effect on the digestive tract, (b) Causes radial muscles to relax, resulting in constriction, (c) Decreases and strengthens the heartbeat\nF. (a) Slows peristalsis and reduces secretion, (b) Causes radial muscles to contract, resulting in dilation, (c) Accelerates and strengthens the heartbeat\nG. (a) Slows peristalsis and increases secretion, (b) Causes circular muscles to contract, resulting in dilation, (c) Slows and strengthens the heartbeat\nH. (a) Decreases peristalsis and has no effect on secretion, (b) Causes circular muscles to relax, resulting in dilation, (c) No change in the heart rate\nI. (a) Increases peristalsis and enhances secretion, (b) Causes circular muscles to contract, resulting in constriction, (c) Slows and weakens the heartbeat\nJ. (a) Increases peristalsis and enhances secretion, (b) Causes radial muscles to contract, resulting in constriction, (c) Accelerates the heart rate without changing its strength\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1940, "output_tokens": 366, "total_tokens": 2306}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3196", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An eager AP Biology student interested in studying osmosis and the movement of water in solutions took a dialysis bag containing a 0.5 M solution and placed it into a beaker containing a 0.6 M solution. If this bag were instead placed into a beaker of distilled water, what would be the expected result?\n\nOptions: \nA. The bag will expand and eventually burst due to the pressure of water flow.\nB. The solute will flow into the dialysis bag from the beaker.\nC. The bag will remain the exact same size because no water will move at all.\nD. The bag will shrink in size and the beaker will overflow due to the movement of water.\nE. The solute will flow out of the dialysis bag into the beaker.\nF. The water will evaporate from the bag, leaving only the solute.\nG. There will be a net flow of water into the bag, causing it to swell in size.\nH. There will be a net flow of water out of the beaker, causing it to decrease in size.\nI. The water in the bag will freeze due to the change in environment.\nJ. There will be a net flow of water out of the bag, causing it to decrease in size.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1368, "output_tokens": 411, "total_tokens": 1779}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_2891", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Pilocarpineis a drug that stimulates the nerve endings of parasympathetic nerves. What effects would you expect this drug to have on (a) the digestive tract, (b) the iris of the eye, and (c) the heart rate?\n\nOptions: \nA. (a) Facilitates digestion,