Standard deviation: 0.093, Mean deviation about the median: 0.075, Coefficient of Variation: 0.044\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1876, "output_tokens": 340, "total_tokens": 2216}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3049", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Miniature poodles are thought to have a mean height of 12 inches and a standard deviation of 1.8 inches. If height is measured to the nearest inch, find the percentage of poodles having a height exceeding 14 inches.\n\nOptions: \nA. 45 percent\nB. 2.5 percent\nC. 5 percent\nD. 30 percent\nE. 20 percent\nF. 10 percent\nG. 15 percent\nH. 35 percent\nI. 40 percent\nJ. 25 percent\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The z-score for a height of 14 inches is \\( \\frac{14 - 12}{1.8} \\approx 1.11 \\). The area to the right of this z-score in a standard normal distribution is about 0.1335, or roughly 13%, and the closest given option is 10 percent due to measurement rounding. Therefore, the most likely correct answer is F.  \n\n\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 870, "output_tokens": 746, "total_tokens": 1616}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3101", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Three hundred college freshmen are observed to have grad point averages that are approximately normally distributed with mean 2.1 and a standard deviation of 1.2. How many of these freshmen would you expect to have grade point averages between 2.5 and 3.5 if the averages are recorded to the nearest tenth?\n\nOptions: \nA. 103 students\nB. 50 students\nC. 90 students\nD. 110 students\nE. 82 students\nF. 95 students\nG. 120 students\nH. 75 students\nI. 68 students\nJ. 57 students\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 784, "output_tokens": 376, "total_tokens": 1160}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3204", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In chloroplasts, a certain protein is found in the lumen of the thylakoid (thylakoid space). It is transcribed in the nucleus and synthesized on cytoplasmic ribosomes. How many membrane bilayers must this protein cross to reach its final location?\n\nOptions: \nA. Four\nB. Nine\nC. Three\nD. Eight\nE. One\nF. Zero\nG. Five\nH. Two\nI. Seven\nJ. Six\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 