reater cognitive abilities. While other options highlight valid differences, the combination of modern appearance, refined culture, and increased intelligence best encapsulates why they are seen as a more advanced evolutionary stage.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1313, "output_tokens": 553, "total_tokens": 1866}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4308", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Hund's rule requires that\n\nOptions: \nA. all electrons must have opposite spins in an orbital\nB. no two electrons can have the same four quantum numbers\nC. no two electrons can occupy the same orbital\nD. no two electrons with the same spin can occupy an orbital\nE. all electrons must occupy the highest energy level first\nF. no two electrons can have opposite spins in an orbital\nG. no two electrons can occupy separate orbitals\nH. all electrons must fill the lowest energy level first\nI. no two electrons can pair up if there is an empty orbital at the same energy level available\nJ. no three electrons can occupy the same orbital\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 944, "output_tokens": 345, "total_tokens": 1289}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3793", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: London dispersion forces are caused by\n\nOptions: \nA. temporary dipoles created by the position of electrons around the nuclei in a molecule\nB. the strong nuclear forces within atomic nuclei\nC. the permanent dipoles created by the shape of the molecule\nD. the intermolecular bonding between ions in an ionic compound\nE. the three-dimensional intermolecular bonding present in all covalent substances\nF. the transfer of electrons in an ionic bond\nG. the electronegativity differences between the different atoms in a molecule\nH. the uneven electron-to-proton ratio found on individual atoms of a molecule\nI. the sharing of electrons in a covalent bond\nJ. the polar covalent bonds within a molecule\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 975, "output_tokens": 303, "total_tokens": 1278}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3757", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Determine the number of cubic centimeter in one cubic inch.\n\nOptions: \nA. 39.37 cc\nB. 100 cc\nC. 50 cc\nD. 2.54 cc\nE. 5 cc\nF. 16.4 cc\nG. 10 cc\nH. 12 cc\nI. 25.4 cc\nJ. 30 cc\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 480, "output_tokens": 236, "total_tokens": 716}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a2