y removed when ground-state aluminum is ionized?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5\nB. 2\nC. -1\nD. 4\nE. 6\nF. 3\nG. 7\nH. 1\nI. 0\nJ. 8\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 512, "output_tokens": 246, "total_tokens": 758}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4206", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: There are some 25,000ribosomesin an E. coli cell. If the structucalproteins of theseribosomeswere stretched out end to end as fully extended polypeptide chains, how many times could they encircle the E. coli cell?Assume that theribosomesare 180 \\AA in diameter, with a specific gravity of 1.0, and that they contain 40% protein. Assume that the E. coli cell is a sphere 1\\mu in diameter.\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.10 \u00d7 10^4 times\nB. 1.26 \u00d7 10^4 times\nC. 0.80 \u00d7 10^4 times\nD. 3.50 \u00d7 10^4 times\nE. 1.76 \u00d7 10^4 times\nF. 3.00 \u00d7 10^4 times\nG. 4.00 \u00d7 10^4 times\nH. 2.54 \u00d7 10^4 times\nI. 1.00 \u00d7 10^4 times\nJ. 2.00 \u00d7 10^4 times\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "We can estimate the total length of all ribosomal protein chains by first calculating the mass and number of amino acid residues. A single ribosome (180 \u00c5 diameter, 40% protein) has a volume of about \\(3.05 \\times 10^6 \\, \\text{\u00c5}^3\\), mass ~\\(3.05 \\times 10^{-18} \\, \\text{g}\\), protein mass ~\\(1.22 \\times 10^{-18} \\, \\text{g}\\), corresponding to ~\\(7.3 \\times 10^3\\) residues per ribosome. With 25,000 ribosomes, total residues \u2248 \\(1.83 \\times 10^8\\), and at 3.5 \u00c5 per residue, total chain length \u2248 \\(6.4 \\times 10^8 \\, \\text{\u00c5}\\) = 0.064 m. The E. coli circumference is \\(\\pi \\times 1\\,\\mu\\text{m} \\approx 3.14 \\times 10^4 \\, \\text{\u00c5}\\), so dividing gives about 2.04 \u00d7 10\u2074 times, closest to option **E**.\n\n\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1320, "output_tokens": 1709, "total_tokens": 3029}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3463", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Two narrow slits separated by $0.10 \\mathrm{{~mm}}$ are illuminated by light of wavelength $600 \\mathrm{{~nm}}$. What is the angular position of the first maximum in the interference pattern? If a detector is located $2.00 \\mathrm{{~m}}$ beyond the slits, what is the distance between the central maximum and the first maximum?\n\nOptions: \nA. 4 mm\nB. 18 mm\nC. 14 mm\nD. 24 mm\nE. 8 mm\nF.  12 mm\nG. 6 mm\nH. 20 mm\nI. 10 mm\nJ. 16 mm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 740, "output_tokens": 493, "total_tokens": 1233}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3567", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-c