ase read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An excellent method of making alcohols is the reaction of an aldehydeon a Grignard reagent. If you perform this reaction, you must scrupulously dry thealdehydebefore adding it to the Grignard reagent. Why?\n\nOptions: \nA. The aldehyde's structure is altered by the presence of water\nB. The aldehyde can react with other components if not dried\nC. Water increases the viscosity of the reaction mixture, reducing the efficiency\nD. Water can initiate a side reaction with the Grignard reagent, forming an unwanted byproduct\nE. Water can cause the Grignard reagent to decompose into a hydrocarbon\nF. The dry aldehyde can absorb moisture from the air, which can slow down the reaction\nG. The Grignard reagent is sensitive to temperature changes\nH. The aldehyde will polymerize if not dried\nI. The aldehyde needs to be in a dry state for the reaction to occur\nJ. The presence of water reduces or eliminates the Grignard reagent from solution\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1217, "output_tokens": 373, "total_tokens": 1590}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3963", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If one increases the angle away from the Z axis, how does the wave function for a 2P_Z electron change?\n\nOptions: \nA. The wave function increases.\nB. The wave function inverts in phase.\nC. The wave function and the electron density for a 2P_Z electron decreases.\nD. The wave function becomes constant throughout all angles.\nE. There is no change in the wave function or electron density.\nF. The electron density spreads out uniformly in all directions.\nG. The electron density becomes more spherically symmetric.\nH. The electron density concentrates on the equatorial plane.\nI. The electron density increases.\nJ. The wave function decreases only along the Z axis.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 938, "output_tokens": 382, "total_tokens": 1320}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3847", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 1932, many cities showed higher sunlight levels than in the previous year. Explain this observation.\n\nOptions: \nA. The Earth's magnetic field weakened, allowing more solar radiation to reach the surface.\nB. Improved measurement techniques provided more accurate readings of sunlight levels.\nC. Fewer particles were released that could scatter or absorb the sunlight due to reduced industrial activity.\nD. A change in Earth's orbit resulted in longer days and more sunlight during the year.\nE. There were fewer tall buildings blocking the sunlight in 1932.\nF. The Earth's atmosphere had an unusually low amount of ozone, allowing more sunlight to pass through.\nG. There was a large-scale removal of forests, which previously blocked sunlight in many cities.\nH. The sun was closer to the Earth in 1932.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1066, "output_tokens": 285, "total_tokens": 1351}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3953", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The number average and weight average molecular-weights are defined as M_n= [(\\sumN_i M_i) / (\\sumN_i)] = [1 / {{\\sum(w_i/ M_i)}}] and M_w = [(\\sumW_iM_i) / (\\sumW_i)] = [(\\sumN_i M^2_i) / (\\sumN_i M_i)] = \\sumw_iM_i respectively, where M_i = molecular weight of theithspecies N_i = moles of molecules with molecular weight M_i W_i= weight of material with molecular weight M_i w_i= weight fraction of molecules of theithspecies. Derive equations analogous to the ones above for the number average,X_n, and weight average,X_w, degree of polymerization.\n\nOptions: \nA. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X^2_i) / (\\sumN_i X_i)]\nB. X_n= [(\\sumW_i X_i) / (\\sumW_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i^3) / (\\sumW_i X_i)]\nC. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i X_i^0.5)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i^1.5) / (\\sumN_i)]\nD. X_n= [(\\sumw_i X_i) / (\\sumw_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i^0.5) / (\\sumN_i)]\nE. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i X_i^2)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X^2_i) / (\\sumN_i X_i^2)]\nF. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X_i^2) / (\\sumN_i^2 X_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i^2)]\nG. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X_i^3) / (\\sumN_i X_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i X_i^3)]\nH. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X^2_i) / (\\sumN_i X_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i)]\nI. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X_i^2) / (\\sumN_i X_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i)]\nJ. X_n= [(\\sumW_i X_i^2) / (\\sumN_i X_i)], X_w= [(\\sumW_i X_i) / (\\sumW_i X_i^2)]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1664, "output_tokens": 430, "total_tokens": 2094}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4175", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Although all electrons spin, only molecules containing unpairedelectrons - only free radicals - giveesrspectra. Why is this? (Hint: Consider the possibility (a)thatone electron of a pair has its spin reversed, or (b)thatboth electrons of a pair have their spins reversed.)\n\nOptions: \nA. Electron pairs have a net magnetic moment\nB. Only electrons in the outermost shell contribute to the magnetic moment, regardless of pairing\nC. Each electron of a pair has a unique magnetic moment\nD. Free radicals lack electron pairs, which is why they cannot generate a magnetic moment\nE. Electron pairs always spin in the same direction, enhancing the magnetic moment\nF. Electron pairs generate a magnetic moment of the same magnitude\nG. Electron pairs have spins that cancel only in the presence of an external magnetic field\nH. Each electron of an electron pair generates a magnetic moment but of equal and opposite magnitude; the electron pair therefore has no net magnetic moment.\nI. Electron pairs generate magnetic moments only at high temperatures\nJ. The magnetic moments of electron pairs reinforce each other, resulting in a double magnetic moment\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1389, "output_tokens": 347, "total_tokens": 1736}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3475", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Would you expect He_2^\\oplus to be more stable than He_2? Than He?\n\nOptions: \nA. He_2^\\oplus is the most stable among He, He_2, and He_2^\\oplus\nB. He_2^\\oplus is more stable than He_2 but less stable than He\nC. He, He_2, and He_2^\\oplus have the same stability\nD. He_2^\\oplus is the least stable among He, He_2, and He_2^\\oplus\nE. He and He_2 have the same stability, both more stable than He_2^\\oplus\nF. He_2^\\oplus is more stable than He but less stable than He_2\nG. He_2^\\oplus is less stable than both He_2 and He\nH. He_2^\\oplus and He_2 have the same stability, both more stable than He\nI. He_2^\\oplus and He have the same stability, both less stable than He_2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 976, "output_tokens": 477, "total_tokens": 1453}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4259", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Even though 1, 3, 5-trinitrobenzene (TNB) has more shattering power (more brisance) and is no more dangerous to handle, 2, 4, 6-trinitrotoluene (TNT) has always been the high ex-plosive in more general use. Can you suggest a reason (connected with manufacture) for the popularity of TNT? (Benzene and toluene are both readily available materials; for many years benzene was cheaper.)\n\nOptions: \nA. Toluene is more easily nitrated, and therefore more easily polynitrated than benzene.\nB. The nitrating agents required for TNB are less readily available than those needed for TNT.\nC. The production of TNB generates more harmful byproducts compared to TNT.\nD. TNT is more stable than TNB.\nE. Benzene is more easily nitrated than toluene.\nF. The cost of manufacturing TNT is lower.\nG. TNB is more sensitive to friction and shock, making it less safe to manufacture.\nH. The purification process for TNB is more costly and time-consuming than that for TNT.\nI. The chemical process for synthesizing TNB is more complex and requires higher temperatures than TNT.\nJ. TNB has a shorter shelf life than TNT, making it less suitable for long-term storage.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1441, "output_tokens": 407, "total_tokens": 1848}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4407", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 2.0 L flask holds 0.40 g of helium gas. If the helium is evacuated into a larger container while the temperature is held constant, what will the effect on the entropy of the helium be?\n\nOptions: \nA. It will increase as the gas molecules will be more dispersed in the larger flask.\nB. It will remain constant as the helium is simply transferred to a larger container.\nC. It will remain constant because the volume of the flask does not affect entropy.\nD. It will remain constant as the number of helium molecules does not change.\nE. It will increase as the temperature is held constant.\nF. It will decrease as the pressure of the gas will decrease in the larger flask.\nG. It will decrease as there will be fewer collisions between the helium molecules in the larger flask.\nH. It will decrease as the gas will be more ordered in the larger flask.\nI. It will decrease because the molecules will collide with the sides of the larger flask less often than they did in the smaller flask.\nJ. It will increase because the molecules will collide with the sides of the larger flask more often than they did in the smaller flask.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1204, "output_tokens": 244, "total_tokens": 1448}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3785", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following operators isHermitian; d/dx,id/dx, d^2/dx^2?\n\nOptions: \nA. none are Hermitian\nB. b and c are Hermitan\nC. only a is Hermitian\nD. all are Hermitian\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 483, "output_tokens": 364, "total_tokens": 847}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3679", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: There exists a carbohydrate that is slightly soluble in water, does not have a sweet taste, but does dissolve slowly when heated with diluteHCl. To what class of carbohydrates does it probably belong?\n\nOptions: \nA. Pentoses\nB. Disaccharides\nC. Polysaccharides\nD. Lipids\nE. Oligosaccharides\nF. Amino acids\nG. Proteins\nH. Mono-saccharides\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 648, "output_tokens": 332, "total_tokens": 980}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4421", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suggest a reason why liquid hydrogen fluoride is preferable to concentrated, aqueoushydrobromicacid in inducing propeneto react with benzene to produceisopropylbenzene.\n\nOptions: \nA. Hydrogen fluoride reacts more selectively with propene\nB. Hydrogen fluoride provides a better solvent environment for the reaction\nC. Hydrogen fluoride is less acidic\nD. Hydrogen fluoride has lower molecular weight, which speeds up the reaction\nE. Hydrogen fluoride will give a greater yield of product\nF. Hydrogen fluoride can be recycled more easily in the process\nG. Hydrogen fluoride is a stronger oxidizing agent\nH. Hydrogen fluoride is less reactive\nI. Hydrogen fluoride is more stable\nJ. Hydrogen fluoride has a higher boiling point, which aids in the reaction\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Liquid hydrogen fluoride acts as both a catalyst and a solvent in the Friedel-Crafts alkylation of benzene with propene, promoting the formation of the more stable isopropyl carbocation intermediate with high selectivity. Concentrated hydrobromic acid, in contrast, is less effective as a Lewis acid catalyst and can lead to unwanted side reactions like polymerization or rearrangement. This selective catalysis by HF is key to efficiently producing isopropylbenzene over other possible products.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1272, "output_tokens": 608, "total_tokens": 1880}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3349", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is incorrectly named?\n\nOptions: \nA. MgO   magnesium oxide\nB. AgNO3   silver nitrate\nC. CuCl2   copper(II) chloride\nD. H2SO4   sulfuric acid\nE. K2Cr2O7   potassium dichromate\nF. Na2SO4   sodium sulfate\nG. Fe(NO3)3   iron(III) nitrate\nH. CaCl2   calcium chloride\nI. AlBr3   aluminum tribromide\nJ. Zn(NO3)2   zinc nitrate\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 652, "output_tokens": 346, "total_tokens": 998}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4320", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A buffer is made from equal concentrations of a weak acid and its conjugate base. Doubling the volume of the buffer solution by adding water has what effect on its pH?\n\nOptions: \nA. It causes the pH to fluctuate unpredictably.\nB. It causes the pH to equalize with the water's pH.\nC. It causes the pH to become extremely basic.\nD. It neutralizes the pH completely.\nE. It significantly decreases the pH.\nF. It has little effect.\nG. It significantly increases the pH.\nH. It doubles the pH value.\nI. It changes the pH asymptotically to the pKa of the acid.\nJ. It causes the pH to become extremely acidic.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 891, "output_tokens": 376, "total_tokens": 1267}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3855", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: From the following five statements, indicate which ones are correct when an ideal gas is allowed to escape rever-sibly and isothermally into a vacuum. [Hint: What is the average kinetic energy of an ideal gas?] 1. W = 0, \\DeltaE = q = a positive number 2. w = P\\DeltaV + V\\DeltaP 3. w = P\\DeltaV, \\DeltaE = 0, q = - P\\DeltaV and is a negative number 4. \\DeltaE = 0, q = - w = a positive number 5. w = 0, q = 0, \\DeltaE = 0\n\nOptions: \nA. All statements are correct\nB. Statements 3 and 4 are correct\nC. Statements 2 and 5 are correct\nD. Statement 1 is correct\nE. Statement 2 is correct\nF. Statements 2, 4, and 5 are correct\nG. Statements 1, 3, and 5 are correct\nH. Statement 4 is correct\nI. Statement 5 is correct\nJ. Statements 1 and 2 are correct\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1056, "output_tokens": 383, "total_tokens": 1439}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3622", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nitrous acid, HNO2, has a pKa value of 3.3. If a solution of nitrous acid is found to have a pH of 4.2, what can be said about the concentration of the conjugate acid/base pair found in solution?\n\nOptions: \nA. [HNO2] > [NO2-]\nB. [H2NO2+] < [NO2-]\nC. [NO2-] < [H2NO2+]\nD. [H2NO2+] > [NO2-]\nE. [NO2-] > [HNO2]\nF. [NO2-] = [HNO2]\nG. [H2NO2+] > [HNO2]\nH. [HNO2] = [H2NO2+]\nI. [HNO2] > [H2NO2+]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 700, "output_tokens": 442, "total_tokens": 1142}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4187", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: You have two 1-liter containers connected to each other by a valve which is closed. In one container, you have liquid water in equilibrium with water vapor at 25\u00b0C. The other container contains a vacuum. Suddenly, you open the valve. Discuss the changes that take place, assuming temperature is constant with regard to (a) the vapor pressure, (b) the concentration of the water molecules in the vapor, (c) the number of molecules in the vapor state.\n\nOptions: \nA. Vapor pressure is halved, the concentration of the gaseous molecules is doubled, and the number of molecules is doubled\nB. Vapor pressure is unchanged, the concentration of the gaseous molecules is halved, and the number of molecules is doubled\nC. Vapor pressure, the concentration of the gaseous molecules and the number of molecules are all unchanged\nD. Vapor pressure is doubled, the concentration of the gaseous molecules is doubled, and the number of molecules is halved\nE. Vapor pressure is doubled, the concentration of the gaseous molecules is halved, and the number of molecules is unchanged\nF. Vapor pressure and the concentration of the gaseous molecules are halved, the number of molecules remains unchanged\nG. Vapor pressure is halved, the concentration of the gaseous molecules remains unchanged, and the number of molecules is doubled\nH. Vapor pressure and the concentration of the gaseous molecules remain unchanged, the number of molecules is doubled\nI. Vapor pressure and the concentration of the gaseous molecules are doubled, the number of molecules remains unchanged\nJ. Vapor pressure is doubled, the concentration of the gaseous molecules and the number of molecules remain unchanged\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1652, "output_tokens": 351, "total_tokens": 2003}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3976", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During the study of the reaction A \u2192 2B, a chemist constructs several graphs. The graph of [A] versus time and the graph of ln [A] versus time both give a curved line; however, the graph of 1/[A] versus time and gives a straight line. This implies the rate law is\n\nOptions: \nA. Rate = k[A]^4\nB. Rate = k[A]^-1\nC. Rate = k[A]^2\nD. Rate = k[A]\nE. Rate = k[A]^-2\nF. Rate = k[A]^0\nG. Rate = k[A]^1/2\nH. Rate = k[A]^-3\nI. Rate = 2k[A]\nJ. Rate = k[A]^3\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 797, "output_tokens": 290, "total_tokens": 1087}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4193", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \\rho/P, g/liter-atm 10 11 10 (\\rho = density) P,atm: 1 10 20 The critical pressure of this gas must then be (greater than 10atm, greater than 20atm, between 1 and 20atm, between 1 and 10atm, less than 20atm, can't tell).\n\nOptions: \nA. less than 20 atm\nB. greater than 10 atm\nC. between 1 and 10 atm\nD. exactly 20 atm\nE. cannot be determined without additional information\nF. greater than 20 atm\nG. greater than 1 atm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 766, "output_tokens": 319, "total_tokens": 1085}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3888", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An experiment was performed to determine the moles of carbon dioxide gas formed (collected over water) when an acid reacts with limestone. To do this, a piece of dry limestone was weighed. Then carbon dioxide was collected until the limestone disappeared. The atmospheric pressure was measured at 0.965 atm. The temperature was 295 K. The volume of CO2 was measured to the nearest mL and corrected for the vapor pressure of water. The student continuously got low results from what was expected. Can you suggest why?\n\nOptions: \nA. Perhaps there was too much acid, which interfered with the results.\nB. The measurement of atmospheric pressure was incorrect.\nC. Carbon dioxide is rather soluble in water.\nD. The temperature might have affected the reaction.\nE. Limestone is Ca(HCO3)2.\nF. The limestone did not fully disappear.\nG. Limestone is never pure CaCO3.\nH. Perhaps there was not enough acid to dissolve all the limestone.\nI. The volume of CO2 was not measured correctly.\nJ. The vapor pressure of water was not correctly accounted for.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1352, "output_tokens": 313, "total_tokens": 1665}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4311", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Formation of a solution can often be visualized as a three-step process. Step 1. Solvent molecules are separated from each other to make space for the solute. Step 2. Solute molecules are separated so they fit into spaces in the solvent. Step 3. Separated solute and solvent are brought together, filling in the spaces. Which of the following statements about the energy involved in the above is correct?\n\nOptions: \nA. Step 1 is endothermic, steps 2 and 3 are exothermic.\nB. All three steps are endothermic.\nC. Steps 1 and 3 are exothermic, and step 2 is endothermic.\nD. All three steps are exothermic.\nE. Steps 1 and 3 are endothermic, and step 2 is exothermic.\nF. Step 1 is exothermic, steps 2 and 3 are endothermic.\nG. Step 3 is exothermic, steps 1 and 2 are neither exothermic nor endothermic.\nH. Step 1 and 2 are exothermic, step 3 is neither exothermic nor endothermic.\nI. Steps 1 and 2 are exothermic, and step 3 is endothermic.\nJ. Steps 1 and 2 are endothermic, and step 3 is exothermic.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1336, "output_tokens": 319, "total_tokens": 1655}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3729", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What do the differences in properties between lithium acetyl acetone (m.p. very high, insoluble in chloroform) and beryllium acetyl acetone (m.p. 108\u00b0,b.p. 270\u00b0, soluble in chloroform) suggest about their structures?\n\nOptions: \nA. Both are non-ionic compounds\nB. Lithium acetylacetonate is non-ionic and beryllium acetylacetonate is ionic\nC. Both are ionic compounds\nD. Lithium acetylacetonate is soluble in chloroform due to its polar nature, while beryllium acetylacetonate is not\nE. Beryllium acetylacetonate is polymeric due to hydrogen bonding, whereas lithium acetylacetonate is not\nF. Both exhibit similar degrees of ionic character and solubility properties\nG. Beryllium acetylacetonate is a volatile liquid at room temperature, while lithium acetylacetonate is a high melting solid\nH. Lithium acetylacetonate is ionic or salt-like and beryllium acetylacetonate is non-ionic or covalent\nI. Lithium acetylacetonate is a polymeric compound, while beryllium acetylacetonate is monomeric\nJ. Both are polymeric in nature with extensive hydrogen bonding\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1368, "output_tokens": 444, "total_tokens": 1812}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3534", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A proposed mechanism for a reaction is as follows: NO2 + F2 \u2192NO2F + F Slow step. F + NO2 \u2192 NO2F Fast step. What is the order of the overall reaction?\n\nOptions: \nA. Fourth order\nB. Second order\nC. First order\nD. Zero order\nE. Third order in NO2 and zero order in F2\nF. Second order in F2 and third order in NO2\nG. First order in NO2 and second order in F2\nH. Fifth order\nI. Third order\nJ. Second order in NO2 and first order in F2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 748, "output_tokens": 344, "total_tokens": 1092}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3447", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Examining data obtained from mass spectrometry supports which of the following?\n\nOptions: \nA. The smell of elements\nB. The common oxidation states of elements\nC. The feel of elements\nD. The temperature at which elements melt\nE. Ionization energy trends within the periodic table\nF. The color of elements\nG. The sound produced when elements react\nH. Atomic size trends within the periodic table\nI. The taste of elements\nJ. The existence of isotopes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 735, "output_tokens": 296, "total_tokens": 1031}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3837", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An equation of state due to Dieterici is P(V - nb')exp [(na') / (RTV)] = nRT(1) Evaluate the constants a' and b' in terms of the critical constants P_c, V_c, and T_c of a gas.\n\nOptions: \nA. a' = 2RT_cV_c, b' = (V_c / 2)\nB. a' = 2RT_cV_c, b' = V_c\nC. a' = RT_cV_c, b' = (V_c / 3)\nD. a' = 4RT_cV_c, b' = (V_c / 8)\nE. a' = RT_cV_c / P_c, b' = V_c / P_c\nF. a' = (RT_cV_c) / 2, b' = 2V_c\nG. a' = (RT_cV_c) / 4, b' = 3V_c\nH. a' = P_cV_c^2 / T_c, b' = (V_c / P_c)\nI. a' = 3RT_cV_c, b' = (V_c / 4)\nJ. a' = RT_cV_c, b' = V_c\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "To find the constants, we use the conditions at the critical point:  \n\\(\\left( \\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial V} \\right)_T = 0\\) and \\(\\left( \\frac{\\partial^2 P}{\\partial V^2} \\right)_T = 0\\), applied to the Dieterici equation.  \nSolving these gives \\(V_c = 2b'\\) and \\(T_c = \\frac{a'}{4Rb'}\\), which leads to \\(a' = \\frac{2RT_cV_c}{?}\\) \u2014 careful solving yields \\(a' = 2RT_c V_c\\) and \\(b' = \\frac{V_c}{2}\\).  \n\nThus the correct answer is \\boxed{A}.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1687, "output_tokens": 1113, "total_tokens": 2800}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4070", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The vibrational wavenumber of $\\mathrm{{Br}}_2$ is $323.2 \\mathrm{{~cm}}^{{-1}}$. Evaluate the vibrational partition function explicitly (without approximation) and plot its value as a function of temperature. At what temperature is the value within 5 per cent of the value calculated from the approximate formula?\n\nOptions: \nA. 7000 K\nB. 2500 K\nC. 3500$\\mathrm{{~K}}$\nD. 6000 K\nE. 2000 K\nF.  4500$\\mathrm{{~K}}$\nG. 4000$\\mathrm{{~K}}$\nH. 5500 K\nI. 5000$\\mathrm{{~K}}$\nJ. 3000 K\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The vibrational partition function is given explicitly by \\( q_\\text{vib} = \\frac{1}{1 - e^{-\\Theta_\\text{vib}/T}} \\) and, for high temperature, by the approximation \\( q_\\text{vib} \\approx \\frac{T}{\\Theta_\\text{vib}} \\).  \nThe characteristic temperature \\( \\Theta_\\text{vib} \\) for Br\u2082 is \\( 323.2 \\ \\text{cm}^{-1} \\times 1.4388 \\ \\text{K\u00b7cm} \\approx 465 \\ \\text{K} \\), and the approximation is within 5% when the temperature is high enough that the exponential correction term is small.  \nThis occurs near \\( T \\approx 10\\, \\Theta_\\text{vib} \\), which is about 4650\u202fK; among the choices, 4500\u202fK is closest.\n\n\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1013, "output_tokens": 710, "total_tokens": 1723}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4318", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A student performs five titrations and obtains a mean result of 0.110 M, with a standard deviation of 0.001 M. If the actual concentration of the titrated solution is 0.100 M, which of the following is true about the titration results?\n\nOptions: \nA. Moderately accurate and precise\nB. Accurate but not precise\nC. Precise but not accurate\nD. Both accurate and precise\nE. Neither precise nor slightly accurate\nF. Neither accurate nor precise\nG. Highly accurate but imprecise\nH. Accurate but imprecise\nI. Precise and slightly accurate\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 832, "output_tokens": 274, "total_tokens": 1106}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7149", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose $\\Omega$ is a bounded open area in $\\mathbb{{R}}^n$. For any $f\\in L^2(\\Omega)$, the Laplace equation (with respect to a real function $u$), $\\Delta u = f$ with boundary condition $u\\mid_{{\\partial \\Omega}}=0$, has a unique weak solution. This can be proved by: 1. Poincare inequality and Riesz representation theorem; 2. Cauchy-Schwartz inequality and Hahn-Banach theorem. 3. None of the above. Return the answer as a number\n\nOptions: \nA. 2. Arzel\u00e0-Ascoli theorem and Banach fixed-point theorem\nB. 1. Arzel\u00e0-Ascoli theorem and Riesz representation theorem\nC. 1.0\nD. 3.0\nE. 2. Sobolev embedding theorem and Riesz representation theorem\nF. 1. Poincare inequality and Banach fixed-point theorem\nG. 2. Poincare inequality and Hahn-Banach theorem\nH. 2.0\nI. 1. Sobolev embedding theorem and Lax-Milgram theorem\nJ. All of the above\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1148, "output_tokens": 538, "total_tokens": 1686}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6590", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose C is a compact convex set in a linear normed space, and let T: C \u2192 C be a continuous mapping. Then, there exists a fixed point of T in C. Is this correct? Answer 1 for yes and 0 for no.\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.0\nB. 2.5\nC. -0.5\nD. 1.5\nE. -1.0\nF. 0.5\nG. 0.0\nH. 2.0\nI. -2.0\nJ. 3.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 633, "output_tokens": 266, "total_tokens": 899}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6428", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A subset H of a group (G,*) is a group if\n\nOptions: \nA. a,b in H => a / b in H\nB. a,b in H => a + b in H\nC. a,b in H=> a - b^-1 in H\nD. H contains the identity element\nE. a in H => a^-1 in H\nF. a,b in H=> a * b in H\nG. a in H => a^2 in H\nH. a in H => a * a^-1 in H\nI. H contains the zero element\nJ. a,b in H=> a * b^-1 in H\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 681, "output_tokens": 327, "total_tokens": 1008}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6846", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A company is interested in comparing the mean sales revenue per salesperson at two different locations. The manager takes a random sample of 10 salespeople from each location independently and records the sales revenue generated by each person during the last four weeks. He decides to use a t-test to compare the mean sales revenue at the two locations. Which of the following assumptions is necessary for the validity of the t-test?\n\nOptions: \nA. The population of the sales records at each location is not normally distributed.\nB. The population of the sales records at each location is normally distributed.\nC. The sample size at both locations is less than 30\nD. The population standard deviations at both locations are equal.\nE. The sales revenue is measured on an interval or ratio scale.\nF. The population of the sales records at each location follows a uniform distribution.\nG. The population standard deviations at both locations are not equal.\nH. The population standard deviations at both locations are known.\nI. The population mean sales revenue at both locations are not equal.\nJ. The population mean sales revenue at both locations are equal.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1468, "output_tokens": 479, "total_tokens": 1947}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7746", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If $f(x) = 2$ for all real numbers $x$, what is the value of $f(x + 2)$?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0\nB. $x^2 + 2$\nC. 4\nD. $2x$\nE. $x + 2$\nF. Undefined\nG. 1\nH. $2x + 2$\nI. 2\nJ. $4x$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 519, "output_tokens": 209, "total_tokens": 728}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6934", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A symmetric random walk on the three-dimensional cubic lattice Z^3 is transient or persistent? Return 1 for persistent and 0 for transient.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.0\nB. -1.0\nC. 4.0\nD. 0.5\nE. 2.5\nF. 2.0\nG. 1.5\nH. -0.5\nI. 1.0\nJ. 3.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 536, "output_tokens": 288, "total_tokens": 824}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6962", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An outlier is an observation that\n\nOptions: \nA. is the mode of the data set\nB. is the mean of the data set\nC. is seen more frequently than the other observations in the data set\nD. is always larger than the other observations in the data set\nE. is always smaller than the other observations in the data set\nF. is seen less frequently than the other observations in the data set\nG. is significantly different from the other observations in the data set\nH. is an error in the data set\nI. is the median of the data set\nJ. is exactly the same as the other observations in the data set\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 892, "output_tokens": 376, "total_tokens": 1268}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6821", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What are the generators of the additive cyclic group Z?\n\nOptions: \nA. [1, -1]\nB. [1, 0]\nC. [0, 2]\nD. [-1, 1]\nE. [0, 1]\nF. [2, 0]\nG. [0, -1]\nH. [3, -3]\nI. [2, -2]\nJ. [1, 2]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 484, "output_tokens": 336, "total_tokens": 820}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6623", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Draw one card at random from a standard deck of cards. The sample space $S$ is the collection of the 52 cards. Assume that the probability set function assigns $1 / 52$ to each of the 52 outcomes. Let\n$$\n\\begin{{aligned}}\nA & =\\{{x: x \\text {{ is a jack, queen, or king }}\\}}, \\\\\nB & =\\{{x: x \\text {{ is a }} 9,10, \\text {{ or jack and }} x \\text {{ is red }}\\}}, \\\\\nC & =\\{{x: x \\text {{ is a club }}\\}}, \\\\\nD & =\\{{x: x \\text {{ is a diamond, a heart, or a spade }}\\}} .\n\\end{{aligned}}\n$$\nFind $P(A)$\n\nOptions: \nA. $\\frac{{14}}{{52}}$\nB. $\\frac{{12}}{{52}}$\nC. $\\frac{{13}}{{52}}$\nD. $\\frac{{15}}{{52}}$\nE. $\\frac{{10}}{{52}}$\nF. $\\frac{{7}}{{52}}$\nG. $\\frac{{11}}{{52}}$\nH. $\\frac{{9}}{{52}}$\nI. $\\frac{{8}}{{52}}$\nJ. $\\frac{{16}}{{52}}$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1444, "output_tokens": 371, "total_tokens": 1815}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen