one\n\nQuestion: You need to construct a 94% confidence interval for a population proportion. What is the upper critical value of z to be used in constructing this interval?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.645\nB. 1.282\nC. 0.9699\nD. 1.88\nE. 2.81\nF. 1.40\nG. 2.33\nH. 1.96\nI. 1.555\nJ. 2.576\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 650, "output_tokens": 290, "total_tokens": 940}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7399", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is the central limit theorem?\n\nOptions: \nA. The central limit theorem states that the mean of a large number of independent and identically distributed random variables, each with finite mean and variance, will approximately follow a normal distribution.\nB. If the population is uniformly distributed, then as the sample size increases, the sampling distribution of the sample mean becomes closer to a normal distribution.\nC. No matter how the population is distributed, as the sample size increases, the standard deviation of the sample means becomes closer to the standard deviation of the population divided by the square root of the sample size.\nD. If the population is normally distributed, then as the sample size increases, the sampling distribution of the sample mean becomes closer to a normal distribution.\nE. The central limit theorem states that the median of a large number of independent and identically distributed random variables, each with finite mean and variance, will approximately follow a normal distribution.\nF. The central limit theorem refers to something else.\nG. The central limit theorem states that as the sample size increases, the median of the sample means becomes closer to the median of the population.\nH. No matter how the population is distributed, as the sample size increases, the mean of the sample means becomes closer to the mean of the population.\nI. Regardless of the distribution of the population, the variance of the sample means will converge to the variance of the population as the sample size increases.\nJ. The central limit theorem states that the sum of a large number of independent and identically distributed random variables, each with finite mean and variance, will approximately follow a normal distribution, regardless of the shape of the original measurement distribution.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 2026, "output_tokens": 559, "total_tokens": 2585}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6832", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  A typical roulette wheel used in a casino has 38 slots that are numbered $1,2,3, \\ldots, 36,0,00$, respectively. The 0 and 00 slots are colored green. Half of the remaining slots are red and half are black. Also, half of the integers between 1 and 36 inclusive are odd, half are even, and 0 and 00 are defined to be neither odd nor even. A ball is rolled around the wheel and ends up in one of the slots; we assume that each slot has equal probability of $1 / 38$, and we are interested in the number of the slot into which the ball falls. Let $A=\\{{0,00\\}}$. Give the value of $P(A)$.\n\nOptions: \nA. $\\frac{{1}}{{19}}$\nB. $\\frac{{1}}{{76}}$\nC. $\\frac{{20}}{{38}}$\nD. $\\frac{{2}}{{38}}$\nE. $\\frac{{3}}{{38}}$\nF. $\\frac{{4}}{{38}}$\nG. $\\frac{{36}}{{38}}$\nH. $\\frac{{1}}{{38}}$\nI. $\\frac{{1}}{{2}}$\nJ. $\\frac{{18}}{{38}}$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1132, "output_tokens": 384, "total_tokens": 1516}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7594", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: 5.5-15. Let the distribution of $T$ be $t(17)$. Find\n(a) $t_{{0.01}}(17)$.\n\n\nOptions: \nA. $1.789$\nB. $3.456$\nC. $4.025$\nD. $3.745$\nE. $2.110$\nF. $1.740$\nG. $2.567$\nH. $3.921$\nI. $2.898$\nJ. $2.897$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 512, "output_tokens": 372, "total_tokens": 884}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6560", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Use the list of numbers: 22, 25, 14,