sult": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 448, "output_tokens": 188, "total_tokens": 636}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7679", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \\lim_{{x \\to c}} |f(x)| = 0. What is \\lim_{{x \\to c}} f(x)?\n\nOptions: \nA. \\infty (infinity)\nB. Does not exist\nC. 1\nD. Undefined\nE. -1\nF. c\nG. |c|\nH. 0\nI. -c\nJ. \\frac{{1}}{{c}} (1 over c)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 500, "output_tokens": 292, "total_tokens": 792}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6521", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The set of all nth roots of unity under multiplication of complex numbers form a/an\n\nOptions: \nA. non-abelian group\nB. infinite group\nC. commutative semigroups with identity\nD. non-commutative group\nE. abelian group\nF. non-commutative semi group with identity\nG. semi group with identity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 586, "output_tokens": 253, "total_tokens": 839}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7513", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a clinical trial, 30 sickle cell anemia patients are randomly assigned to two groups. One group receives the currently marketed medicine, and the other group receives an experimental medicine. Each week, patients report to the clinic where blood tests are conducted. The lab technician is unaware of the kind of medicine the patient is taking. This design can be described as\n\nOptions: \nA. a completely randomized design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine as two treatments\nB. a completely randomized design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine as two blocks\nC. a matched-pairs design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine forming a pair\nD. a double-blind design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine as two treatments\nE. a factorial design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine as two factors\nF. a randomized block design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine as two blocks\nG. a crossover design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine as two treatments\nH. a randomized block design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine as two treatments\nI. a matched-pairs design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine as two blocks\nJ. a single-blind design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine as two treatments\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1816, "output_tokens": 451, "total_tokens": 2267}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7720", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Tisha wrote the following riddle to her friend: I have 2 faces, no vertices, and I can roll. What am I? What is the answer to the riddle?\n\nOptions: \nA. hexagonal prism\nB. torus\nC. cone\nD. prism\nE. sphere\nF. rectangular prism\nG. pentagonal prism\nH. cube\nI. cylinder\nJ. pyramid\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 588, "output_tokens": 234, "total_tokens": 822}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7086", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider the number pattern 5, 9, 13, 17, 21, 25, 29. Which rule could have been used to make the pattern?\n\nOptions: \nA. Start with 5. Subtract 4 each time to get the next number.\nB. Start with 5. Add 4 each time to get the next number.\nC. Start with 5. Add 5 each time to get the next number.\nD. Start with 0. Add 5 each time to get the next number.\nE. Start with 9. Subtract 4 each time to get the next number.\nF. Start with 1. Add 4 each time to get the next number.\nG. Start with 0. Add 4 each time to get the next number.\nH. Start with 0. Add 3 each time to get the next number.\nI. Start with 5. Add 3 each time to get the next number.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 948, "output_tokens": 186, "total_tokens": 1134}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7603", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Statement 1 | The homomorphic image of a cyclic group is cyclic. Statement 2 | The homomorphic image of an Abelian group is Abelian.\n\nOptions: \nA. True, False\nB. False, True\nC. False, False\nD. True, True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 503, "output_tokens": 300, "total_tokens": 803}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7091", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which set of integers is in order from least to greatest?\n\nOptions: \nA. 11, \u22129, 7, \u22126, \u22123\nB. 7, 11, \u22126, \u22123, \u22129\nC. \u22123, 7, \u22129, \u22126, 11\nD. \u22126, \u22123, 7, 11, \u22129\nE. \u22129, \u22123, 7, 11, \u22126\nF. \u22123, \u22126, 7, 11, \u20139\nG. \u22129, 7, \u22126, \u22123, 11\nH. \u22129, \u22126, \u22123, 7, 11\nI. 11, 7, \u22123, \u22126, \u22129\nJ. 7, \u22129, \u22126, \u22123, 11\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 944, "output_tokens": 300, "total_tokens": 1244}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6662", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which group of numbers is in order from least to greatest?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.6 1.0 0.25\nB. 0.25 1.6 1.0\nC. 1.0 1.6 0.25\nD. 1.6 0.25 1.6\nE. 1.0 0.25 0.25\nF. 1.6 0.25 1.0\nG. 0.25 1.0 1.6\nH. 1.0 0.25 1.6\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 508, "output_tokens": 149, "total_tokens": 657}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7284", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A school committee member is lobbying for an increase in the gasoline tax to support the county school system. The local newspaper conducted a survey of county residents to assess their support for such an increase. What is the population of interest here?\n\nOptions: \nA. All teachers in the county school system\nB. All residents in the local newspaper distribution area\nC. All county residents with children in the county school system\nD. All parents of children in the county school system\nE. All school committee members\nF. All county residents with school-aged children\nG. All county residents who pay gasoline tax\nH. All county residents\nI. All school-aged children\nJ. All local newspaper readers\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 868, "output_tokens": 317, "total_tokens": 1185}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6979", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The weekly milk order for the Tranquility Inn includes 40 gallons of low-fat milk and 15 gallons of chocolate milk. What is the ratio of the number of low-fat gallons to chocolate gallons in the Tranquility Inn\u2019s weekly milk order?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5:03\nB. 8:04\nC. 8:05\nD. 2:01\nE. 3:01\nF. 8:03\nG. 7:03\nH. 6:03\nI. 4:01\nJ. 5:01\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 636, "output_tokens": 164, "total_tokens": 800}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6533", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An assembly line machine is supposed to turn out ball bearings with a diameter of 1.25 centimeters. Each morning the first 30 bearings produced are pulled and measured. If their mean diameter is under 1.23 centimeters or over 1.27 centimeters, the machinery is stopped and an engineer is called to make adjustments before production is resumed. The quality control procedure may be viewed as a hypothesis test with the null hypothesis H0: \u03bc = 1.25 and the alternative hypothesis Ha: \u03bc \u2260 1.25. The engineer is asked to make adjustments when the null hypothesis is rejected. In test terminology, what would a Type II error result in?\n\nOptions: \nA. An incorrect assumption about the machinery's calibration\nB. An unnecessary stoppage of the production process\nC. Continued production of wrong size ball bearings\nD. An unnecessary adjustment of the machinery\nE. A warranted halt in production to adjust the machinery\nF. A false alarm about the size of ball bearings\nG. Continued production of proper size ball bearings\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1328, "output_tokens": 376, "total_tokens": 1704}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6646", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The correlation between height in inches and weight in pounds for a particular class is 0.65. If the heights are converted from inches to centimeters, what will the correlation be? (1 in. = 2.54 cm)\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.1\nB. 0.54\nC. 1.65\nD. 0\nE. 0.26\nF. -0.26\nG. 0.95\nH. 2.54\nI. -0.65\nJ. 0.65\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 600, "output_tokens": 294, "total_tokens": 894}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6982", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Katie is going on vacation for 3 weeks. She finds the number of days of work she will miss by multiplying 5 \u00d7 3. Which expression shows another way Katie can find the number of days of work she will miss?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5+3+3\nB. 3+3+3\nC. 5\u00d75\nD. 5\u00d73\u00d73\nE. 5\u00d72\u00d73\nF. 5+5+5+5+5\nG. 5+5+5\nH. 3\u00d74+5\nI. 3+5\nJ. 3\u00d73\u00d73\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 671, "output_tokens": 228, "total_tokens": 899}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7510", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is the primary difference between an experiment and an observational study?\n\nOptions: \nA. In an experiment, the researcher has no control over variables; in an observational study, the researcher can manipulate variables.\nB. Experiments are only conducted on human subjects; observational studies can be conducted on nonhuman subjects.\nC. Observational studies are conducted in a lab setting, while experiments can be conducted in any environment.\nD. Experiments must be double-blind; observational studies do not need to be.\nE. In an experiment, the researcher observes without interfering; in an observational study, the researcher manipulates the environment.\nF. Experiments can only be conducted once; observational studies can be repeated.\nG. Experiments must use randomized treatment and control groups; observational studies also use treatment and control groups, but they do not need to be randomized.\nH. Experiments involve quantitative data; observational studies involve qualitative data.\nI. In an experiment, the researcher manipulates some variable to observe its effect on a response variable; in an observational study, he or she simply observes and records the observations.\nJ. Experiments require a hypothesis; observational studies do not require a hypothesis.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1511, "output_tokens": 400, "total_tokens": 1911}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7275", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The principal of a school is interested in estimating the average income per family of her students. She selects a random sample of students and collects information about their family income. A 95 percent confidence interval computed from this data for the mean income per family is ($35,095, $45,005). Which of the following provides the best interpretation of this confidence interval?\n\nOptions: \nA. 95 percent of the students in her school are from families whose income is between $35,095 and $45,005.\nB. If we were to take another sample of the same size and compute a 95 percent confidence interval, we would have a 95% chance of getting a different interval.\nC. If we were to take another sample of the same size and compute a 95 percent confidence interval, we would have a 95% chance of getting the interval ($35,095, $45,005).\nD. There is a 95% probability that the mean income per family in the school is between $35,095 and $45,005.\nE. 95 percent of the income per family in the school falls between $35,095 and $45,005.\nF. There is a 95% probability that the median income per family in the school is between $35,095 and $45,005.\nG. There is a 95% probability that the sample mean income per family in the school is between $35,095 and $45,005.\nH. The average income per family of all the students in the school is definitely between $35,095 and $45,005.\nI. There is a 95% probability that the minimum income per family in the school is between $35,095 and $45,005.\nJ. There is a 95% probability that the families of all the students in this school have an income of between $35,095 and $45,005.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1966, "output_tokens": 509, "total_tokens": 2475}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7278", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: As reported on CNN, in a May 1999 national poll 43% of high school students expressed fear about going to school. Which of the following best describes what is meant by the poll having a margin of error of 5%?\n\nOptions: \nA. There is a 0.05 probability that the 43% result is in error.\nB. The pollsters are 95% confident that the true proportion is between 38% and 48%.\nC. Five percent of the students refused to participate in the poll.\nD. The poll's results could be 5% higher or lower due to random chance.\nE. Five percent of the students surveyed did not understand the question.\nF. There is a 5% chance that the results of the poll are completely inaccurate.\nG. Only 5% of the students surveyed gave valid responses.\nH. It is likely that the true proportion of high school students afraid to go to school is between 38% and 48%.\nI. The poll's results are 5% away from the true proportion.\nJ. Between 38% and 48% of those surveyed expressed fear about going to school.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1278, "output_tokens": 447, "total_tokens": 1725}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7422", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Ms. Ling has been living in her home for exactly 4 years. She knows that there are 12 months in each year. She found the total number of months, m, she has been living in her home by using the number sentence below. 4 \u00d7 12 = m Which number sentence shows another way to find the total number of months, m, Ms. Ling has been living in her home?\n\nOptions: \nA. 12 \u00f7 m = 4\nB. m \u00f7 4 = 12\nC. m \u00d7 4 = 12\nD. 12 \u00d7 m = 4\nE. m - 12 = 4\nF. 4 \u00d7 m = 12\nG. 4 + m = 12\nH. 12 \u2013 m = 4\nI. m - 4 = 12\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1012, "output_tokens": 327, "total_tokens": 1339}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7286", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For the regression line, which of the following statements about residuals is true?\n\nOptions: \nA. The sum of the residuals is always one.\nB. If the correlation is 0, there will be a distinct pattern in the residual plot.\nC. The larger the residuals, the better the linear model.\nD. The residuals are always negative.\nE. If the correlation is 1, there will be a distinct pattern in the residual plot.\nF. The residual plot will always be a straight line.\nG. Influential scores have large residuals.\nH. The mean of the residuals is always zero.\nI. If the linear model is good, the number of positive residuals will be the same as the number of negative residuals.\nJ. The residuals can never be zero.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1008, "output_tokens": 278, "total_tokens": 1286}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6853", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To determine the average cost of running for a congressional seat, a simple random sample of 50 politicians is chosen and the politicians' records examined. The cost figures show a mean of $125,000 with a standard deviation of $32,000. Which of the following is the best interpretation of a 90% confidence interval estimate for the average cost of running for office?\n\nOptions: \nA. We are 90% confident that politicians running for a congressional seat spend between $117,500 and $132,500.\nB. 90% of politicians running for a congressional seat spend a mean dollar amount that is between $117,500 and $132,500.\nC. 90% of politicians running for a congressional seat spend a total dollar amount that is between $117,500 and $132,500.\nD. 90% of politicians running for a congressional seat spend between $117,500 and $132,500.\nE. We are 90% confident that politicians running for a congressional seat spend a maximum dollar amount that is between $117,500 and $132,500.\nF. We are 90% confident that the standard deviation of the cost of running for a congressional seat is between $117,500 and $132,500.\nG. We are 90% confident that the median cost of running for a congressional seat is between $117,500 and $132,500.\nH. We are 90% confident that politicians running for a congressional seat spend a mean dollar amount between $117,500 and $132,500.\nI. We are 90% confident that politicians running for a congressional seat spend a minimum dollar amount that is between $117,500 and $132,500.\nJ. 90% of politicians running for a congressional seat spend a median dollar amount that is between $117,500 and $132,500.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1987, "output_tokens": 366, "total_tokens": 2353}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7409", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A shelf has four books on it. The weight, in pounds, of each of the four books on the shelf is 2.5, 3.2, 2.7, 2.3 Which inequality represents the weight, w, of any book chosen from the shelf?\n\nOptions: \nA. w > 3.2\nB. w > 2.9\nC. w > 2.3\nD. w > 2.5\nE. w < 3.2\nF. w < 2.4\nG. w < 2.7\nH. w > 3.0\nI. w < 3.3\nJ. w < 3.1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 624, "output_tokens": 274, "total_tokens": 898}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6537", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The relation between the selling price of a car (in $1,000) and its age (in years) is estimated from a random sample of cars of a specific model. The relation is given by the following formula: Selling price = 15.9 \u2013 0.983 (age) Which of the following can we conclude from this equation?\n\nOptions: \nA. For every year the car gets older, the selling price drops by approximately $983.\nB. A new car costs on the average $9,830.\nC. A new car costs on the average $15,900.\nD. For every year the car gets older, the selling price goes down by approximately 9.83 percent.\nE. For every year the car gets older, the selling price goes up by approximately $983.\nF. For every year the car gets older, the selling price drops by approximately $159.\nG. For every year the car gets older, the selling price goes up by approximately $1,590.\nH. A new car costs on the average $983.\nI. For every year the car gets older, the selling price remains the same.\nJ. For every year the car gets older, the selling price drops by approximately $1,590.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1349, "output_tokens": 337, "total_tokens": 1686}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6999", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which equation represents 36 less than a number, y, is equal to 13?\n\nOptions: \nA. 13 + y = 36\nB. 13 - y = 36\nC. y = 13 - 36\nD. 36 - y = 13\nE. 13 = y + 36\nF. y = 36 - 13\nG. y + 36 = 13\nH. y - 36 = 13\nI. 36 + y = \u201313\nJ. 36 = y + 13\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 544, "output_tokens": 186, "total_tokens": 730}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6963", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these statements correctly explains bias?\n\nOptions: \nA. It describes a process that results in a sample that does not represent the population.\nB. It describes a process that results in a sample that is too large or too small.\nC. It describes a process that uses a random sampling method.\nD. It describes a process that results in a sample that perfectly represents the population.\nE. It describes a sample that is not representative of the population.\nF. It describes a process that always results in accurate estimates.\nG. It describes the influence of the researcher's personal beliefs on the outcome of the study.\nH. It describes a lack of randomization in the sampling process.\nI. It describes a process where the sampling method has no influence on the outcome of the study.\nJ. It describes a process that creates estimates that are too high on average or too low on average.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1204, "output_tokens": 369, "total_tokens": 1573}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6432", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is a binomial random variable?\n\nOptions: \nA. The number of motorists not wearing seat belts in a random sample of five drivers.\nB. The number of hearts out of five cards randomly drawn from a deck of 52 cards, without replacement.\nC. The number of tosses before a \"5\" appears when tossing a fair die.\nD. The number of green marbles drawn from a bag containing red, blue, and green marbles.\nE. The number of points a hockey team receives in 10 games, where two points are awarded for wins, one point for ties, and no points for losses.\nF. The number of red cards in a random hand of five cards drawn from a deck of 52 cards.\nG. The time it takes to complete a 1000-piece puzzle.\nH. The number of cars of a specific model sold in a month at a car dealership.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1088, "output_tokens": 488, "total_tokens": 1576}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7477", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For a parametric family $\\{{p_\\theta(x)\\}}$ we know that $\\lim_{{\\theta'\\to\\theta}}\\frac{{1}}{{(\\theta-\\theta')^2}}D(p_\\theta||p_{{\\theta'}}) = \\alpha J(\\theta)$, where $J(\\theta)$ is the Fisher information. Use natural logarithm for KL divergence to compute $\\alpha$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.25\nB. 4\nC. 0.5\nD. 1\nE. 2.5\nF. -1\nG. 2\nH. 1.5\nI. 3\nJ. 0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\).  \nThis follows from the second-order Taylor expansion of the KL divergence, where \\(D(p_\\theta\\|p_{\\theta'}) \\approx \\frac{1}{2} J(\\theta)(\\theta-\\theta')^2\\).  \nComparing with the given limit shows \\(\\alpha = \\frac{1}{2}\\).", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 848, "output_tokens": 490, "total_tokens": 1338}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6917", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: compute the integral \\int_{{\\Gamma}} \\frac{{x*dy-y*dx}}{{x^2+y^2}}, where $\\Gamma$ is any piecewise smooth, closed curve that encloses the origin but does not pass through it.\n\nOptions: \nA. 3.1415926\nB. 4.6692016\nC. 1.5707963\nD. 0\nE. 2.7182818\nF. 0.5772156\nG. -3.1415926\nH. 9.8696044\nI. 6.2831852\nJ. 1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 689, "output_tokens": 446, "total_tokens": 1135}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7357", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Compute the real integral $I=\\int_{{-\\infty}}^{{\\infty}} 1/(x^2 + 1)^2 dx$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 6.28\nB. 5.55\nC. 3.67\nD. 2.78\nE. 3.14\nF. 2.46\nG. 1.57\nH. 4.67\nI. 1.23\nJ. 0.78\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 540, "output_tokens": 322, "total_tokens": 862}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6698", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: suppose F(x,y,z)=0. What is $\\frac{{\\partial x}}{{\\partial y}} \\frac{{\\partial y}}{{\\partial z}} \\frac{{\\partial z}}{{\\partial x}}$?\n\nOptions: \nA. -2.0\nB. 2.0\nC. -0.5\nD. 0\nE. 1.5\nF. 1.0\nG. Undefined\nH. -1.0\nI. 0.5\nJ. 3.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 575, "output_tokens": 387, "total_tokens": 962}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6595", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is \\lim_{{x \\to 0}} (csc(x) - cot(x))?\n\nOptions: \nA. -1/2\nB. Undefined\nC. 1/2\nD. 1\nE. 0\nF. -1\nG. 2\nH. -2\nI. 3\nJ. Infinity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 470, "output_tokens": 551, "total_tokens": 1021}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6954", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Use Stokes' Theorem to evaluate $\\int_C \\mathbf{{F}} \\cdot d \\mathbf{{r}}$, where $\\mathbf{{F}}(x, y, z)=x y \\mathbf{{i}}+y z \\mathbf{{j}}+z x \\mathbf{{k}}$, and $C$ is the triangle with vertices $(1,0,0),(0,1,0)$, and $(0,0,1)$, oriented counterclockwise as viewed from above.\n\n\nOptions: \nA.  $-\\frac{{1}}{{2}}$\nB. $\\frac{{1}}{{2}}$\nC. $0$\nD. $\\frac{{3}}{{4}}$\nE. $\\frac{{1}}{{4}}$\nF. $-1$\nG. $\\frac{{1}}{{3}}$\nH. $\\frac{{2}}{{3}}$\nI. $-\\frac{{1}}{{4}}$\nJ. $-\\frac{{1}}{{3}}$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 788, "output_tokens": 2253, "total_tokens": 3041}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6523", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Determine whether the polynomial in Z[x] satisfies an Eisenstein criterion for irreducibility over Q. x^2 - 12\n\nOptions: \nA. Yes, with p=4.\nB. No, because the polynomial is reducible.\nC. Yes, with p=1.\nD. No, because the polynomial does not satisfy the Eisenstein criterion.\nE. No.\nF. Yes, with p=12.\nG. Yes, with p=3.\nH. Yes, with p=5.\nI. Yes, with p=6.\nJ. Yes, with p=2.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 702, "output_tokens": 738, "total_tokens": 1440}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6706", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: H(z) = $\\int_0^1 e^{{-z^2 t^2}} dt$, what is H'(1)?\n\nOptions: \nA. -2.3789\nB. 1.0000\nC. -0.3789\nD. -0.7461\nE. 0\nF. -1.3789\nG. 0.3789\nH. 1.3789\nI. 0.7461\nJ. 2.3789\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "We differentiate the integral with respect to \\( z \\):\n\n\\[\nH'(z) = \\int_0^1 \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z} e^{-z^2 t^2} \\, dt = \\int_0^1 (-2z t^2) e^{-z^2 t^2} \\, dt.\n\\]\n\nEvaluating at \\( z = 1 \\):\n\n\\[\nH'(1) = \\int_0^1 -2 t^2 e^{-t^2} \\, dt.\n\\]\n\nThis integral evaluates approximately to \\(-0.3789\\), which corresponds to option C.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 639, "output_tokens": 441, "total_tokens": 1080}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6848", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An experiment is to be conducted to determine whether taking fish oil capsules or garlic capsules has more of an effect on cholesterol levels. In past studies it was noted that daily exercise intensity (low, moderate, high) is associated with cholesterol level, but average sleep length (< 5, 5 - 8, > 8 hours) is not associated with cholesterol level. This experiment should be done\n\nOptions: \nA. by blocking on sleep length\nB. by blocking on gender\nC. by blocking on diet\nD. by blocking on previous medical conditions\nE. by blocking on capsule type\nF. by blocking on cholesterol level\nG. by blocking on lifestyle habits\nH. by blocking on exercise intensity\nI. by blocking on age\nJ. by blocking on weight\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 892, "output_tokens": 269, "total_tokens": 1161}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7038", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose $f(x, y)= \\begin{{cases}}1-x-y, & x+y \\leqslant 1 \\ 0, & x+y>1\\end{{cases}}$. What is the integral of f(x,y) over the region I=[0,1]\\times[0,1]?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.33333\nB. 0.5\nC. 1.5\nD. 0\nE. 0.75\nF. 1\nG. 0.25\nH. 0.16667\nI. 0.66667\nJ. 0.83333\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 560, "output_tokens": 431, "total_tokens": 991}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7579", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $W(t)$ be a Bownian motion, Let $E[exp(i*W(t))]:= E[cos(W(t))+i*sin(W(t))]$, where $i=\\sqrt{{-1}}$. Is $M(t):=exp(i*W(t))/E[exp(i*W(t))]$ a matingale? Return 1 for yes and 0 for no.\n\nOptions: \nA. i (the imaginary unit)\nB. 1.0\nC. -0.5\nD. 2.0\nE. 1.5\nF. 0.0\nG. -2.0\nH. 3.0\nI. 0.5\nJ. -1.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 600, "output_tokens": 427, "total_tokens": 1027}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_7336", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: compute the integral $\\iint_V \\frac{{d x d y d z}}{{(1+x+y+z)^3}}$, where V={{(x, y, z): x, y, z \\geq 0, x+y+z\\leq 1}}.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.092\nB. 0.042\nC. 0.050\nD. 0.025\nE. 0.018\nF. 0.056\nG. 0.028\nH. 0.075\nI. 0.065\nJ. 0.034\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The region is the part of the unit simplex where \\(x, y, z \\ge 0\\) and \\(x+y+z \\le 1\\).  \nMake the change of variables \\(u = x+y+z\\), with the Jacobian from \\((x,y,z)\\) to \\((u,v,w)\\) giving a factor, and evaluate the integral; it equals \\(\\int_0^1 \\frac{\\tfrac12 (1-u)^2}{(1+u)^3}\\,du\\).  \n\nThis evaluates to \\(\\frac18 \\left( \\ln 2 - \\frac{5}{12} \\right) \\approx 0.034\\).  \n\nThus the correct choice is J.\n\n\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 878, "output_tokens": 2000, "total_tokens": 2878}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6918", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Use Stoke's Theorem to evaluate $\\int_C \\vec{{F}} \\cdot d \\vec{{r}}$ where $\\vec{{F}} = z^2 \\vec{{i}} + y^2 \\vec{{j}} + x \\vec{{k}}$ and $C$ is the triangle with vertices (1,0,0), (0,1,0) and (0,0,1) with counter-clockwise rotation.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.166\nB. -1.000\nC. -0.166\nD. 0.333\nE. 0.500\nF. 0.666\nG. -0.333\nH. -0.500\nI. -0.666\nJ. 1.000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 652, "output_tokens": 2012, "total_tokens": 2664}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_math_6713", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $X_1, X_2, \\ldots$ be a sequence of independent indetically distributed 