. an average of 10 times, with an rms deviation of about 0.1\nD. an average of 10 times, with an rms deviation of about 1\nE. an average of 10 times, with an rms deviation of about 6\nF. an average of 5 times, with an rms deviation of about 2\nG. an average of 20 times, with an rms deviation of about 3\nH. an average of 10 times, with an rms deviation of about 4\nI. an average of 15 times, with an rms deviation of about 4\nJ. an average of 10 times, with an rms deviation of about 2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1172, "output_tokens": 537, "total_tokens": 1709}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_physics_7903", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What equal positive charges would have to be placed on Earth and on the Moon to neutralize their gravitational attraction?\n\nOptions: \nA. $3.3 \\times 10^{{13}} \\mathrm{{C}}$\nB. $3.5$$10^{{13}} \\mathrm{{C}}$\nC. $4.2$$10^{{13}} \\mathrm{{C}}$\nD. $1.2 \\times 10^{{14}} \\mathrm{{C}}$\nE. $7.8 \\times 10^{{13}} \\mathrm{{C}}$\nF. $2.5 \\times 10^{{13}} \\mathrm{{C}}$\nG. $8.3 \\times 10^{{12}} \\mathrm{{C}}$\nH.  $5.7$$10^{{13}} \\mathrm{{C}}$\nI. $9.4 \\times 10^{{13}} \\mathrm{{C}}$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 776, "output_tokens": 412, "tota