 the surface defined by the paraboloid $z=1-x^2-y^2$, where $z \\geq 0$.\n\nOptions: \nA. $2\\pi$\nB. $\\pi$\nC. $\\frac{{\\pi}}{{2}}$\nD. $4\\pi$\nE. $-\\frac{{\\pi}}{{2}}$\nF. $-2\\pi$\nG. $3\\pi$\nH. $0$\nI. $-\\pi$\nJ. $-3\\pi$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 692, "output_tokens": 805, "total_tokens": 1497}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_physics_8155", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If the frequency of one source of sound is 500 Hz and a second sound source is 504 Hz, then when the two waves interfere with each other, the beat frequency will be\n\nOptions: \nA. 2 Hz\nB. 504 Hz\nC. 500 Hz\nD. 12 Hz\nE. 1,004 Hz\nF. 4 Hz\nG. 8 Hz\nH. 10 Hz\nI. 16 Hz\nJ. 6 Hz\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 580, "output_tokens": 211, "total_tokens": 791}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_physics_8452", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Optometrists use a linear scale of lens power, measured in diopters, to prescribe corrective lenses. Sufferers of myopia, or nearsightedness, have difficulty resolving distant objects because the lenses in their eyes are too strong. If a myopic person has a prescription of -5 diopters, what image do her corrective lenses create for distant objects?\n\nOptions: \nA. An upright, real image about 20 cm behind her eyes\nB. An upright, virtual image about 5 cm behind her eyes\nC. An inverted, virtual image about 20 cm in front of her eyes\nD. An inverted, real image about 20 cm behind her eyes\nE. An inverted, real image about 20 cm in front of her eyes\nF. An inverted, virtual image 5 cm behind her eyes\nG. An upright, real image about 5 cm in front of her eyes\nH. An upright, virtual image about 20 cm in front of her eyes\nI. An upright, real image about 20 cm in front of her eyes\nJ. An inverted, real image about 5 cm in front of her eyes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1248, "output_tokens": 423, "total_tokens": 1671}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_physics_8602", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If you lived on Venus what phases of the Earth would you see? (Assume your telescope can see through Venus\u2019s thick clouds\u2026)\n\nOptions: \nA. Waning crescent New Waxing crescent\nB. New Waxing crescent First quarter\nC. Full Waning crescent New\nD. Full moon only\nE. First quarter Waxing gibbous Full\nF. New only\nG. Waning gibbous New Waxing gibbous\nH. Waxing gibbous Full Waning gibbous\nI. Third quarter Waning crescent New\nJ. New first quarter full third quarter\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is J. Observed from inside Venus's orbit, Earth would show a complete cycle of phases just like the Moon does from Earth, because Venus is closer to the Sun. As Venus orbits the Sun, Earth would go through all phases from new to first quarter to full to third quarter. Thus, from Venus, you would see new, first quarter, full, and third quarter phases over time.\n\n\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 961, "output_tokens": 587, "total_tokens": 1548}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_physics_8059", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: All walking animals, including humans, have a natural walking pace\u2014a number of steps per minute that is more comfortable than a faster or slower pace. Suppose that this pace corresponds to the oscillation of the leg as a physical pendulum.  Fossil evidence shows that T. rex, a two-legged dinosaur that lived about 65 million years ago, had a leg length L = 3.1 m and a stride length S = 4.0 m (the distance from one footprint to the next print of the same foot).  Estimate the walking speed of T. rex. (Unit: m/s)\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.6\nB. 0.7\nC. 1.4\nD. 1.8\nE. 1.1\nF. 0.9\nG. 2.2\nH. 2.5\nI. 3.0\nJ. 2.8\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_token