e options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why are the season's in Mars' southern hemisphere so extreme?\n\nOptions: \nA. because Mars' axis is less tilted than the Earth's\nB. because Mars has a smaller size than the Earth\nC. because Mars has a slower rotation speed than the Earth\nD. because Mars has more carbon dioxide in its atmosphere than the Earth\nE. because Mars has a shorter year than the Earth\nF. because Mars has more water vapor in its atmosphere than the Earth\nG. because Mars has a more eccentric orbit than the Earth\nH. because Mars is closer to the sun than the Earth\nI. because Mars is farther from the sun than the Earth\nJ. because Mars' axis is more tilted than the Earth's\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 960, "output_tokens": 432, "total_tokens": 1392}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_physics_8924", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Jupiter and the other jovian planets are sometimes called \"gas giants.\" In what sense is this term misleading?\n\nOptions: \nA. They actually contain a significant fraction of non-gaseous matter.\nB. The materials they are made of are not normally gaseous in everyday experience.\nC. They are not giant in size compared to other celestial bodies.\nD. The term 'gas' suggests they are entirely gaseous, but they have solid cores.\nE. Actually it's a great description because these worlds are big and gaseous throughout.\nF. The term 'giant' implies they are the largest planets, which is not always 