ess than the wavelength of the original standing waves?\n\nOptions: \nA. The wavelength will be greater, because the tension in the string varies inversely with the wave speed, which varies inversely with the wavelength.\nB. Less, because the tension in the string varies directly with the wave speed, which varies directly with the wavelength.\nC. The wavelength cannot be determined without more information about the properties of the string and the wave generator.\nD. Greater, because the tension in the string varies directly with the wave speed, which varies inversely with the wavelength.\nE. Less, because the tension in the string varies directly with the wave speed, which varies inversely with the wavelength.\nF. Greater, because the tension in the string varies directly with the wave speed, which varies directly with the wavelength.\nG. The wavelength will be less, because the tension in the string varies inversely with the wave speed, which varies directly with the wavelength.\nH. The wavelength will be greater, because the increased tension in the string will cause an increase in the wave speed, resulting in a longer wavelength.\nI. The wavelength will remain the same, because the tension in the string does not affect the wavelength.\nJ. The wavelength will be less, because the increased tension in the string will cause a decrease in the wave speed, resulting in a shorter wavelength.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1842, "output_tokens": 486, "total_tokens": 2328}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_physics_8267", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What happens to the image formed by a concave mirror as the object is moved from far away to near the focal point?\n\nOptions: \nA. The image disappears as it moves toward the mirror.\nB. The image moves away from the mirror and gets taller.\nC. The image stays at the same distance from the mirror and gets shorter.\nD. The image moves toward the mirror and gets shorter.\nE. The image moves toward the mirror and gets taller.\nF. The image stays at the same distance from the mirror and gets taller.\nG. The image moves toward the mirror and stays the same height.\nH. The image flips upside down as it moves toward the mirror.\nI. The image moves away from the mirror and stays the same height.\nJ. The image moves away from the mirror and gets shorter.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1056, "output_tokens": 334, "total_tokens": 1390}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_physics_8853", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A barge of mass 15,000 kg, made from metal of density 7500 kg\\bulletm^-3, is being loaded in a closed dock of sur-face area 6633 m^2 with ore of density 3 g\\bulletcm^-3. When 80,000 kg of ore are aboard, the barge sinks. How does the water level in the dock alter? The area of the barge is assumed negligible in comparison with the area of the dock.\n\nOptions: \nA. 3.5 cm\nB. 2 cm\nC. 0.2 cm\nD. 2.5 cm\nE. 0.8 cm\nF. 1.5 cm\nG. 3 cm\nH. 1 cm\nI. 0.5 cm\nJ. 4 cm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The barge sinks when the ore weight and its own weight displace water equal to the total weight.  \nThe water level change depends only on the volume of the barge and ore that become submerged after sinking, not on the floating displacement.  \nThe barge\u2019s metal volume is \\(15,000 / 7500 = 2 \\, \\text{m}^3\\), and the ore volume is \\(80,000 / 3000 = 26.67 \\, \\text{m}^3\\), totaling \\(28.67 \\, \\text{m}^3\\), which spread over the dock area of \\(6633 \\, \\text{m}^2\\) gives a rise of about \\(0.00432 \\, \\text{m}\\) or \\(0.43 \\, \\text{cm}\\), closest to 0.5 cm.  \n\n\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 998, "output_tokens": 642, "total_tokens": 1640}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_physics_8883", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A spherical charge distribution varies with the radius r by the equation \u03c1 = ar, where \u03c1 is the volume charge density and a is a positive constant. The distribution goes out to a radius R. Which of the following is true of the electric field strength due to this charge distribution at a distance r from the center?\n\nOptions: \nA. It increases as r approaches infinity.\nB. It increases exponentially for r > R.\nC. It increases linearly for r > R.\nD. It decreases non-linearly for r < R.\nE. It decreases exponentially for r < R.\nF. It increases non-linearly for r < R.\nG. It decreases linearly for r > R.\nH. It remains constant for r < R.\nI. It remains constant for r > R.\n