ithin 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 564, "output_tokens": 175, "total_tokens": 739}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MathQA_2052", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: a courtyard is 21 meter long and 14 meter board is to be paved with bricks of dimensions 14 cm by 8 cm . the total number of bricks required is :\n\nOptions: \nA. 16000\nB. 18000\nC. 20000\nD. 26250\nE. none of these\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 516, "output_tokens": 300, "total_tokens": 816}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MathQA_1072", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: in township k each property is taxed at 12 percent of its assessed value . if the assessed value of a property in township k is increased from $ 20,000 to $ 24,000 , by how much will the property tax increase ?\n\nOptions: \nA. $ 32\nB. $ 50\nC. $ 320\nD. $ 400\nE. $ 480\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 568, "output_tokens": 218, "total_tokens": 786}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MathQA_662", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: if x , y , and z are positive integers and 2 x = 3 y = 4 z , then the least possible value of x + y + z is\n\nOptions: \nA. 40\nB. 50\nC. 60\nD. 70\nE. 31\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "We have \\(2x = 3y = 4z = k\\), so \\(x = \\frac{k}{2}\\), \\(y = \\frac{k}{3}\\), \\(z = \\frac{k}{4}\\).  \nFor \\(x, y, z\\) to be positive integers, \\(k\\) must be a common multiple of 2, 3, and 4; the least is 12.  \nThen \\(x = 6, y = 4, z = 3\\), giving \\(x + y + z = 13\\), but 13 isn\u2019t among the options, so \\(k\\) must be the LCM of 2,3,4 multiplied to match the given numbers \u2014 actually the correct minimum sum from the choices comes from taking \\(k = 60\\) to get integers, giving \\(x = 30, y = 20, z = 15\\) and sum \\(65\\), but since that's not an option, checking the LCM approach leads to the sum 13, which is not listed, meaning the intended interpretation yields sum 13, but the least given option is 31 (E).\n\n\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 575, "output_tokens": 14344, "total_tokens": 14919}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MathQA_1421", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: according to the directions on the can of frozen orange juice concentrate , 1 can of concentrate is to be mixed with 3 cans of water to make orange juice . how many 12 ounces cans of the concentrate are required to prepare 240 6 ounces servings of orange juice ?\n\nOptions: \nA. a ) 25\nB. b ) 34\nC. c ) 50\nD. d ) 67\nE. e ) 30\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 628, "output_tokens": 344, "total_tokens": 972}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MathQA_324", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: find the constant k so that : - x 2 - ( k + 8 ) x - 8 = - ( x - 2 ) ( x - 4 )\n\nOptions: \nA. 11\nB. 12\nC. 14\nD. 19\nE. 15\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 450, "output_tokens": 15300, "total_tokens": 15750}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MathQA_360", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: n = 1 ! + 2 ! + 3 ! . . . . . + 10 ! . what is the last digit of n ^ n ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 4\nC. 5\nD. 6\nE. 7\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The sum from 5! onward ends in zero, so n\u2019s last digit comes from 1!+2!+3!+4! = 1+2+6+24 = 33, giving last digit 3.  \nNumbers ending in 3 cycle through 3, 9, 7, 1 when raised to powers; since n ends in 3, the exponent n also ends in 3, which corresponds to the third position in the cycle (3\u00b9\u21923, 3\u00b2\u21929, 3\u00b3\u21927).  \nThus the last digit of n^n is 7.  \n\n\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 532, "output_tokens": 663, "total_tokens": 1195}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MathQA_305", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: suzie \u2019 s discount footwear sells all pairs of shoes for one price and all pairs of boots for another price . on monday the store sold 22 pairs of shoes and 16 pairs of boots for $ 540 . on tuesday the store sold 8 pairs of shoes and 32 pairs of boots for $ 720 . how much more do pairs of boots cost than pairs of shoes at suzie \u2019 s discount footwear ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 12\nB. 11\nC. 10\nD. 15\nE. 16\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 704, "output_tokens": 399, "total_tokens": 1103}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MathQA_1373", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions 