": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_90", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The real line under the K-topology is Hausdorff and has this property, but is neither regular nor normal.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The property is that the real line with the K-topology is Hausdorff and **second countable**, but neither regular nor normal.  \n\n\\boxed{\\text{second countable}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 439, "output_tokens": 923, "total_tokens": 1362}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_640", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This theorem is the m-equals-one case of the empire problem.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The theorem referred to is the Four Color Theorem. It is the case when m = 1 in the empire problem, where each \"empire\" consists of a single country. The Four Color Theorem states that any planar map can be colored with no more than four colors such that no two adjacent regions share the same color.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{Four Color Theorem}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 324, "output_tokens": 336, "total_tokens": 660}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_126", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 2002, Duke University lost the right to use one of these devices after losing a patent case against its inventor, former Duke professor John Madey.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{free-electron laser}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 412, "output_tokens": 329, "total_tokens": 741}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_283", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The moment-generating function of a random variable X is defined as the expectation value of this function of X times t.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The moment-generating function of a random variable $ X $ is defined as $ M_X(t) = \\mathbb{E}[e^{tX}] $. It is the expected value of $ e^{tX} $, where $ t $ is a real number. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{e^{tX}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 384, "output_tokens": 277, "total_tokens": 661}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1858", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of these animals presented to King George II was called the Indian Monster and was reportedly fed hard boiled eggs.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{zebra}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 366, "output_tokens": 317, "total_tokens": 683}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_474", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This planet's shepherd moon Pan is located within this planet's Encke Gap.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{Saturn}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 327, "output_tokens": 209, "total_tokens": 536}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1473", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When Evan Priestley was part of this organization, he developed the Phabricator collaboration tool, which is used for code reviews.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{Facebook}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 340, "output_tokens": 253, "total_tokens": 593}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_918", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This quantity is linearly related to a type of enthalpy in the Evans\u00c2\u2013Polanyi principle.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{activation energy}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 356, "output_tokens": 336, "total_tokens": 692}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1133", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Russell Schaedler names a group of eight common bacterial species that live in this habitat.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The group of eight common bacterial species is known as the \"eight key phyla\" of the human gut microbiome. These include Firmicutes, Bacteroidetes, Actinobacteria, Proteobacteria, Fusobacteria, Verrucomicrobia, Cyanobacteria, and Spirochaetes. Therefore, the habitat is the human gut.\n\n\\boxed{human\\ gut}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 429, "output_tokens": 482, "total_tokens": 911}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1790", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a 1984 book co-written with Ann Druyan, Carl Sagan suggested that Earth is at the heart of over a trillion of these objects.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{galaxies}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 384, "output_tokens": 404, "total_tokens": 788}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_888", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Cancers of this organ are assessed by the RMI score, which depends on the concentration of the biomarker CA-125.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{ovary}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 376, "output_tokens": 337, "total_tokens": 713}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_53", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Hardware-enforced control-flow integrity requires a \"shadow\" version of this structure.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{stack}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 348, "output_tokens": 392, "total_tokens": 740}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_792", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The first element of the signature of a number field is the number of embeddings of the field in this set.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The first element of the signature of a number field refers to the number of real embeddings of the field. This is part of the signature (r\u2081, r\u2082), where r\u2081 is the number of real embeddings and r\u2082 is the number of conjugate pairs of complex embeddings. The real embeddings map the field into the real numbers.\n\n\\boxed{\\mathbb{R}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 368, "output_tokens": 341, "total_tokens": 709}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1063", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Holonomic constraints take a function of the position variables and the time and set it equal to this number.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{0}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 372, "output_tokens": 265, "total_tokens": 637}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_492", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Note to moderator: Take a second to read the pronunciation guides and the answerline.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{Answer}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 304, "output_tokens": 23, "total_tokens": 327}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_607", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of these constructs named for Banach and Mazur can be used to define Baire spaces.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{Banach-Mazur game}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 348, "output_tokens": 417, "total_tokens": 765}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1800", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This scientist is often credited with devising a problem in which a customer either stays in a waiting room or tries to wake up the namesake person if no one else is getting a haircut.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The problem described is the \"sleeping barber\" problem, a classic synchronization issue in computer science. It was devised by Edsger Dijkstra. \n\n\\boxed{Dijkstra}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 542, "output_tokens": 474, "total_tokens": 1016}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_849", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A field that is \"formally [this adjective]\" can be equipped with an ordering to become an ordered field.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The adjective is \"real\". A field that is formally real can be given a total order compatible with its operations, making it an ordered field. \n\n\\boxed{\\text{real}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 426, "output_tokens": 350, "total_tokens": 776}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_71", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Measurements of these particles violated the Leggett inequalities that are implied by nonlocal realism in a 2007 study by Anton Zeilinger's group.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{photons}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 408, "output_tokens": 359, "total_tokens": 767}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_572", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This body contains a so-called \"mountain in a moat\" whose origin is unknown.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The answer is \\boxed{Iapetus}, referring to Saturn's moon Iapetus, which has a unique equatorial ridge that makes it appear like a \"mountain in a moat.\" The origin of this ridge remains uncertain among scientists.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 414, "output_tokens": 370, "total_tokens": 784}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1026", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a 1976 experiment that exactly recapitulated theory, Robert Trivers and Hope Hare found that these individuals weighed almost exactly three times as much as their counterparts.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{queen ants}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 529, "output_tokens": 467, "total_tokens": 996}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_550", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An algorithm for this problem that classifies bases as either witnesses or liars is named for Solovay and Strassen.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question refers to the **Solovay\u2013Strassen primality test**, which uses the Jacobi symbol and Euler's criterion to determine whether a number is composite or probably prime. In this algorithm, numbers that correctly identify a composite are called **Euler witnesses**, and those that incorrectly suggest primality are **Euler liars**.  \n\n\\boxed{Euler}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 446, "output_tokens": 419, "total_tokens": 865}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1710", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Localizing a subset S of a ring gives every element of S this property.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Localizing a subset $ S $ of a ring makes every element of $ S $ invertible (i.e., a unit) in the localized ring. This is the fundamental property achieved by the localization process. \n\n\\boxed{\\text{invertible}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 332, "output_tokens": 216, "total_tokens": 548}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1149", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The power that can be extracted from a windmill depends on this function of the wind speed.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The power that can be extracted from a windmill depends on the cube of the wind speed. This is because the kinetic energy of moving air is proportional to the square of the speed, and the mass flow rate through the turbine is directly proportional to the speed, resulting in a cubic relationship. Thus, doubling the wind speed increases the available power by a factor of eight.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{cube}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 342, "output_tokens": 387, "total_tokens": 729}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1164", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Glucose sensors work by colorimetrically monitoring the formation of this compound when glucose is oxidized.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{hydrogen peroxide}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 445, "output_tokens": 393, "total_tokens": 838}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_643", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Smooth muscle relaxation is thought to be promoted by this hormone in its namesake \"block\" on the myometrium.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{progesterone}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 362, "output_tokens": 260, "total_tokens": 622}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1232", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Electrons in e-sub-g orbitals do not contribute to orbital angular momentum because the e-sub-g orbitals cannot transform between each other under this operation.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The statement is incorrect. Electrons in *eg* orbitals (such as in octahedral complexes) do not contribute to orbital angular momentum not because they cannot transform into each other, but because the orbital angular momentum is quenched due to the symmetry of the ligand field. In an octahedral field, the *eg* orbitals (dz\u00b2 and dx\u00b2\u2212y\u00b2) are symmetrically oriented and experience a crystal field that restricts orbital motion, leading to quenching.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{False}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 424, "output_tokens": 478, "total_tokens": 902}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_804", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Cohn, Kleinberg, Szegedy, and Umans provided a group theoretic approach to this task that re-derives an earlier algorithm for it that Virginia Williams improved upon in 2011.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{matrix multiplication}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 436, "output_tokens": 377, "total_tokens": 813}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_766", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Two ways of measuring this quantity are Lipschitz equivalent if they are bounded between constant multiples of each other.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{metric}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 369, "output_tokens": 258, "total_tokens": 627}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_450", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In these locations, smaller species evolve to get larger and larger species become smaller, according to Foster's rule.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{islands}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 380, "output_tokens": 375, "total_tokens": 755}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_308", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This phenomenon is exhibited by the rotation of a water wheel with leaky buckets.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{Reynolds' dilatancy}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 371, "output_tokens": 287, "total_tokens": 658}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_819", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Haloketones of this type can react upon the addition of an aqueous base to form a cyclopropanone intermediate that subsequently rearranges to form a carboxylic acid.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "This reaction describes the haloform reaction, where a methyl ketone with halogens on the methyl group undergoes base-catalyzed cleavage. Upon treatment with aqueous base, the trihalomethyl ketone forms a cyclopropanone-like intermediate that collapses to yield a carboxylic acid and haloform. The most common product is a carboxylic acid with one fewer carbon than the original ketone.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{carboxylic acid}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 419, "output_tokens": 356, "total_tokens": 775}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_292", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The rate of this process can be measured through the use of an acetylene reduction assay.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{nitrogen fixation}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 352, "output_tokens": 315, "total_tokens": 667}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1222", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Application of sodium amide to a ben\u00c2\u00b7zyl\u00c2\u00b7ic version of these compounds can lead to ortho alkylation in the Sommelet-Hauser rearrangement.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{ammonium salts}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 404, "output_tokens": 377, "total_tokens": 781}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_796", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: BzK photometry is used to classify galaxies by this phenomenon, which, along with redshift, characterizes Lyman-break galaxies.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{Lyman break}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 388, "output_tokens": 460, "total_tokens": 848}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_691", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A group with this name can be represented by Specht modules or by Young tableaux with n boxes and n\u00a0distinct entries.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{S_n}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 373, "output_tokens": 265, "total_tokens": 638}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_634", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The difference in this quantity between two systems can be determined using the Bennett acceptance ratio.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quantity is **free energy**. The Bennett acceptance ratio method is widely used to compute free energy differences between two thermodynamic states, particularly in molecular simulation. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{\\text{free energy}}.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 440, "output_tokens": 324, "total_tokens": 764}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_967", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Like loops, these things are often unrolled such that the items stored within them fit into a single unit of memory to improve cache performance.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{array}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 408, "output_tokens": 301, "total_tokens": 709}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1236", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A normal example of these sequences has an underlying sigma  eld equal to sigma of the sign of the W function; that one named for Azema is subject to Kurtz's theorem, which states that one of these things converges if the \"Z-hat t\" operator for it is self-adjoint.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{martingale}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 492, "output_tokens": 354, "total_tokens": 846}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_354", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Some cells in this structure can become hyperpolarized when the activation of the G-protein transducin triggers phospho-di-ester-ase to cleave cGMP.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{retina}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 412, "output_tokens": 355, "total_tokens": 767}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1095", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Jacobus Kapteyn was the first to use \"statistical\" data from this concept, and not \"secular\" data to gauge the layout of stars in the sky.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{parallax}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 400, "output_tokens": 315, "total_tokens": 715}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1338", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An error-correction scheme that relies on values constructed by using non-singular projective curves defined over one of these constructs is the Goppa code.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{finite\\ fields}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 405, "output_tokens": 334, "total_tokens": 739}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_72", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Any continuous positive definite function that maps 0 to 1 can serve as a function known by this word due to Bochner's theorem.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{characteristic}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 388, "output_tokens": 312, "total_tokens": 700}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1138", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Alfve\u0301n's  (all-VANE's)  theorem uses the idealized form of this law to prove that magnetic field lines exactly coincide with the streamlines in a plasma.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Alfv\u00e9n's theorem relies on the ideal magnetohydrodynamics (MHD) approximation, in which the magnetic field lines are \"frozen-in\" to the plasma flow. This concept is derived from Faraday's law combined with Ohm's law for a perfectly conducting fluid. The law in question is **Faraday's law of induction**.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{Faraday's law}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 420, "output_tokens": 350, "total_tokens": 770}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1145", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A normed space named after these objects defines the notion of these objects' size.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{vectors}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 334, "output_tokens": 244, "total_tokens": 578}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_364", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The relativistic kinetic energy of a photon equals this quantity times the speed of light.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The correct answer is the photon's momentum.  \nIn relativity, the energy of a photon is given by \\( E = pc \\), so the kinetic energy equals momentum times the speed of light.  \nThus, the missing quantity is momentum.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{momentum}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 411, "output_tokens": 481, "total_tokens": 892}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_43", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Treating this operation as an automorphism is the first step in constructing the adjoint representation of a Lie (\"lee\") group.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The operation referred to is the conjugation action of a Lie group on itself, which induces the adjoint representation on its Lie algebra. Treating this conjugation as an automorphism leads to the differential of the map at the identity, giving the adjoint representation Ad: G \u2192 Aut(\ud835\udd24). The key operation is conjugation.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{conjugation}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 388, "output_tokens": 340, "total_tokens": 728}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_168", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For Dirichlet (\"DEE-ree-klet\") boundary conditions, this quantity is given by the volume integral of the charge density times the Green's function.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quantity described is the electrostatic potential, which for Dirichlet boundary conditions can be expressed as the volume integral of the charge density multiplied by the Green's function. This follows from Green's theorem and the properties of the Green's function in electrostatics. \n\n\\boxed{\\text{potential}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 408, "output_tokens": 349, "total_tokens": 757}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_580", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Laughlin wavefunction is used to study this effect for filling factors of one over an odd integer.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Laughlin wavefunction is used to study the fractional quantum Hall effect for filling factors of one over an odd integer. This effect occurs in two-dimensional electron systems under strong magnetic fields and low temperatures. The wavefunction explains the emergence of quasiparticles with fractional charge.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{fractional quantum Hall effect}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 364, "output_tokens": 394, "total_tokens": 758}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_750", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The ylide made by the reaction of this compound with methyl iodide, followed by subsequent deprotonation, is used to cyclopropanate double bonds.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The compound described is trimethylsulfonium iodide, which, upon treatment with a strong base, forms a sulfur ylide (dimethylsulfonium methylide). This ylide is commonly used in the Johnson-Corey-Chaykovsky reaction to convert alkenes into cyclopropanes. The most common and correct answer is trimethylsulfonium iodide.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{trimethylsulfonium iodide}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 408, "output_tokens": 354, "total_tokens": 762}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_843", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Debye\u2013H\u00fcckel equation, the log of the activity coefficient is proportional to this parameter to the negative three-halves power, times the square root of ionic strength.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The parameter is the Debye length. In the Debye\u2013H\u00fcckel theory, the activity coefficient depends on the Debye length raised to the negative three-halves power multiplied by the square root of ionic strength. This relation appears in the limiting law for electrolyte solutions.  \n\n\\boxed{\\text{Debye length}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 537, "output_tokens": 2125, "total_tokens": 2662}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_994", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It has nothing to do with magnetic fields, but the Biot\u00c2\u2013Savart  (byoh-sah-VARR)  law can be used to derive this force in a theory derived by Ludwig Prandtl.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The Biot\u2013Savart law, when applied in aerodynamics, is used to model the velocity induced by vortex filaments, forming a key part of lifting-line theory developed by Ludwig Prandtl. This theory helps calculate the lift distribution over a three-dimensional wing. The force derived in this context is the aerodynamic lift force.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{lift}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 423, "output_tokens": 339, "total_tokens": 762}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1085", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The extent to which this phenomenon is observed is given by \" e  to the negative  d , times sinh  (sinch)  \n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The expression described, \"e to the negative d, times sinh,\" likely refers to the mathematical form $ e^{-d} \\sinh(d) $, which appears in contexts such as physics or engineering (e.g., attenuation in wave propagation or heat transfer). However, without additional context, the most common simplified interpretation of such an expression in standard usage is related to the **Laplace transform** or **exponential decay modulated by hyperbolic sine**. Given the phrasing and typical usage, the intended answer is likely the **attenuation factor** or **decay function**, commonly represented as:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{e^{-d} \\sinh(d)}\n$$\n\nThis expression quantifies the extent of a decaying wave or signal over distance $ d $.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 368, "output_tokens": 574, "total_tokens": 942}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1255", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An algorithm named the \"big O of log n\" algorithm performs this task, and requires that all inputs be written in the form of A x plus B y plus C equals zero.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question appears to conflate concepts: \"big O of log n\" refers to time complexity, typically associated with algorithms like binary search, which do not require inputs in the form $ Ax + By + C = 0 $. That form is standard for linear equations in two variables and is unrelated to logarithmic-time algorithms. Therefore, the premise is flawed, but the most common algorithm with $ O(\\log n) $ complexity is binary search.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{binary search}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 411, "output_tokens": 377, "total_tokens": 788}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1312", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This technique can be used to determine the oxygen environment of hepta\u00c2\u00b7valent neptunium compounds, in particular whether oxygen ligands are bridging or not.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{X-ray absorption spectroscopy}  \n\nThis technique, specifically NEXAFS or EXAFS, probes the local electronic and geometric structure around neptunium, revealing whether oxygen ligands are terminal or bridging. It is sensitive to changes in oxidation state and coordination environment, making it ideal for distinguishing bonding modes. Thus, it is the most common method for analyzing oxygen environments in heptavalent neptunium compounds.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 512, "output_tokens": 612, "total_tokens": 1124}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1360", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Lambda-CDM model, the accelerating expansion of the universe begins at a scale factor equal to this function of omega-sub-matter over two omega-sub-lambda.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "In the Lambda-CDM model, the accelerating expansion of the universe begins when the scale factor $ a = \\left( \\frac{\\Omega_{m,0}}{2\\Omega_{\\Lambda,0}} \\right)^{1/3} $. This occurs when the repulsive effect of dark energy (dominated by the cosmological constant $ \\Lambda $) overcomes the gravitational pull of matter. The most common and correct expression for the scale factor at the onset of acceleration is the cube root of the ratio of matter to twice the dark energy density parameters.\n\n\\boxed{\\left( \\frac{\\Omega_{m,0}}{2\\Omega_{\\Lambda,0}} \\right)^{1/3}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 376, "output_tokens": 491, "total_tokens": 867}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1519", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Determining this quantity for a system can be done using only the core velocity dispersion if one uses King's method, also known as core  tting.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{mass}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 408, "output_tokens": 380, "total_tokens": 788}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1615", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This quantity and the second virial coef\u2734cient can be estimated by extrapolating a Zimm plot to \"theta equals zero.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The quantity referred to is the second virial coefficient, which is obtained from a Zimm plot by extrapolating to zero angle and zero concentration. In a Zimm plot, data are extrapolated to zero scattering angle (\u03b8 = 0) and zero concentration to determine the molar mass and the second virial coefficient. The second virial coefficient itself quantifies solute-solvent interactions and is directly obtained from the concentration extrapolation at \u03b8 = 0.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{second virial coefficient}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 370, "output_tokens": 475, "total_tokens": 845}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1700", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Metallocenes can be synthesized by reacting a cyclo\u00c2\u00b7penta\u00c2\u00b7diene sandwich complex of this element with a metal halide.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{sodium}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 384, "output_tokens": 400, "total_tokens": 784}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1724", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nitrogen  xation is assayed by an experiment in which this compound is reduced.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{acetylene}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 340, "output_tokens": 349, "total_tokens": 689}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_739", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Finding the largest number of rooks on an m-by-n chessboard with k squares removed such that none of the rooks attack each other can be solved by reducing to this problem.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The problem of placing the maximum number of non-attacking rooks on an m-by-n chessboard with k squares removed reduces to finding a maximum matching in a bipartite graph.  \n\nIn this graph, the left vertices represent the rows and the right vertices represent the columns, with an edge missing for each removed square.  \n\nThe largest number of rooks equals the size of the maximum matching in this bipartite graph.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{maximum matching in a bipartite graph}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 524, "output_tokens": 571, "total_tokens": 1095}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_613", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This statement can be derived from Lagrange's identity when the time derivative of the scalar G function is equal to zero.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{Poisson's bracket}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 462, "output_tokens": 346, "total_tokens": 808}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_679", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Chris Freiling argued that this statement is false because it is equivalent to the negation of his axiom of symmetry.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "Chris Freiling argued that the Continuum Hypothesis (CH) is false because it contradicts his intuitive Axiom of Symmetry, which he believed to be a natural probabilistic principle. His argument hinges on the idea that certain intuitive symmetry properties of the real numbers should hold, which are violated if CH is true. Therefore, the statement Freiling claimed to be false is the Continuum Hypothesis.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{Continuum Hypothesis}}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 380, "output_tokens": 401, "total_tokens": 781}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1892", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A form of this property manifests as the destruction of anti-nodal coherence peaks in the local density of states spectra of under-doped cuprate superconductors.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{pseudogap}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 409, "output_tokens": 331, "total_tokens": 740}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1112", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This phenomenon's namesake \"wedge\" appears red in color due to backscattering from a light source whose zenith angle is in between 10 and 20 degrees.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{Belt of Venus}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 412, "output_tokens": 393, "total_tokens": 805}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "QANTA_Science_1826", "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a coordinate system devised by the IAU in 1958, the distribution of neutral hydrogen emissions was used to determine the \"equator\" of this structure.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{Milky Way}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 416, "output_tokens": 323, "total_tokens": 739}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a2