y": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10103", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Obtain the partial-fraction expansion of F(s) = [(s^2 + 3s + 1) / {{(s + 1)^3 (s + 2)^2}}]\n\nOptions: \nA. F(s) = [(- 1) / (s + 1)^3] + [3 / (s + 1)^2] - [4 / (s + 1)] - [1 / (s + 2)^2] + [4 / (s + 2)]\nB. F(s) = [1 / (s + 1)^3] - [2 / (s + 1)^2] + [3 / (s + 1)] - [1 / (s + 2)^2] + [5 / (s + 2)]\nC. F(s) = [2 / (s + 1)^3] + [1 / (s + 1)^2] - [5 / (s + 1)] + [2 / (s + 2)^2] + [3 / (s + 2)]\nD. F(s) = [(- 1) / (s + 1)^3] + [3 / (s + 1)^2] - [4 / (s + 1)] + [1 / (s + 2)^2] + [4 / (s + 2)]\nE. F(s) = [1 / (s + 1)^3] + [3 / (s + 1)^2] - [4 / (s + 1)] + [1 / (s + 2)^2] + [4 / (s + 2)]\nF. F(s) = [(- 2) / (s + 1)^3] + [4 / (s + 1)^2] - [3 / (s + 1)] + [2 / (s + 2)^2] - [6 / (s + 2)]\nG. F(s) = [(- 1) / (s + 1)^3] - [2 / (s + 1)^2] + [4 / (s + 1)] + [2 / (s + 2)^2] - [5 / (s + 2)]\nH. F(s) = [(- 1) / (s + 1)^3] + [3 / (s + 1)^2] + [4 / (s + 1)] + [1 / (s + 2)^2] + [4 / (s + 2)]\nI. F(s) = [1 / (s + 1)^3] + [2 / (s + 1)^2] - [4 / (s + 1)] + [1 / (s + 2)^2] - [3 / (s + 2)]\nJ. F(s) = [(- 1) / (s + 1)^3] + [3 / (s + 1)^2] - [4 / (s + 1)] + [1 / (s + 2)^2] - [4 / (s + 2)]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "We set up the partial fraction decomposition as  \n\n\\[\n\\frac{s^2+3s+1}{(s+1)^3(s+2)^2} = \\frac{A}{(s+1)^3} + \\frac{B}{(s+1)^2} + \\frac{C}{s+1} + \\frac{D}{(s+2)^2} + \\frac{E}{s+2}.\n\\]\n\nSolving for the coefficients (by clearing denominators and equating coefficients, or using appropriate substitution methods) yields  \n\\(A = -1\\), \\(B = 3\\), \\(C = -4\\), \\(D = 1\\), \\(E = 4\\).\n\nThis corresponds exactly to option D.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 3676, "output_tokens": 1959, "total_tokens": 5635}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10882", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For point-to-point communication at higher frequencies, the desiredradiation pattern is a single narrow lobe or beam. To obtainsuch a characteristic (at least approximately) a multi-elementlinear array is usually used. An array is linear whenthe elements of the ar-ray are spaced equally along a straightline. In a uniform linear array the elements are fed withcurrents of equal magnitude and having a uniform progressivephase shift along the line. The pattern of such anarray can be obtained by addingvectoriallythe field strengthsdue to each of the elements. For a uniform array of non-directionalelements the field strength would be E_T = E_0 \\vert1 +e^J\\psi+ e^J2\\psi + e^J3\\psi + ... +e^j^(^n-1)\\psi \\vert(1) where \\psi =\\betadcos\\textphi + \\alpha and\\alpha is the progressive phase shift between elements, (\\alpha is theangle by which the current in any element leads the currentin the preceding element.) Compute the pattern of such a linear array.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.512\nB. 0.612\nC. 0.212\nD. 0.212 (with a different phase shift)\nE. 0.412\nF. 0.312\nG. 0.112\nH. 0.712\nI. 0.912\nJ. 0.112 (with a different element spacing)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question asks for the computed pattern of a uniform linear array, but no numerical parameters (like number of elements, phase shift, or angle) are provided, so a specific numeric value cannot be determined from the information given.\n\nGiven that multiple options are similar but differ only by decimals, the answer requires details that are absent in the prompt.\n\nTherefore, based on the missing data, no single numeric choice is justified, but the most plausible answer in context might be based on a standard result like half-power beamwidth or normalized field value; assuming typical parameters, **F. 0.312** could be a common midpoint.\n\n\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1798, "output_tokens": 916, "total_tokens": 2714}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10219", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Using the definition of the bilateral z transform F (z) = ^\\infty\\sum_n=-\\infty f[n] z^-n, find the z - transform of f[n] = 3\\delta [n+2] + 4\\delta [n-1] + 2\\delta [n-3].\n\nOptions: \nA. 3z^-2 + 4z^-1 + 2z^3\nB. 3z^2+ 4z^-1 + 2z^-3\nC. 2z^3 + 4z^-2 + 3z^-1\nD. 4z^2+ 3z^-1 + 2z^-3\nE. 4z^-3 + 3z^-2 + 2z^-1\nF. 3z^2+ 2z^-1 + 4z^-3\nG. 2z^2+ 4z^-1 + 3z^-3\nH. 3z^3 + 4z + 2z^-2\nI. 4z^3 + 2z + 3z^-2\nJ. 2z^-1 + 3z^-3 + 4z^2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 724, "output_tokens": 444, "total_tokens": 1168}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10350", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A single phase one pulse controlled circuit has a resistance R and counter emf E load 400 sin(314 t) as the source voltage. For a load counter emf of 200 V, the range of firing angle control is\n\nOptions: \nA. 60\u00b0 to 180\u00b0.\nB. 90\u00b0 to 150\u00b0.\nC. 60\u00b0 to 150\u00b0.\nD. 30\u00b0 to 120\u00b0.\nE. 30\u00b0 to 180\u00b0.\nF. 30\u00b0 to 150\u00b0.\nG. 60\u00b0 to 120\u00b0.\nH. 90\u00b0 to 180\u00b0.\nI. 45\u00b0 to 180\u00b0.\nJ. 45\u00b0 to 135\u00b0.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 696, "output_tokens": 517, "total_tokens": 1213}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10322", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A box contains 7 red, 5 white, and 4 black balls. What is the probability of your drawing at random one red ball? One black ball?\n\nOptions: \nA. P(R) = 2/3, P(B) = 1/3\nB. P(R) = 5/14, P(B) = 4/14\nC. P(R) = 1/2, P(B) = 1/4\nD. P(R) = 7/15, P(B) = 4/15\nE. P(R) = 7/16, P(B) = 1/4\nF. P(R) = 5/16, P(B) = 1/4\nG. P(R) = 1/3, P(B) = 1/4\nH. P(R) = 1/4, P(B) = 1/5\nI. P(R) = 7/16, P(B) = 1/2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 692, "output_tokens": 212, "total_tokens": 904}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10345", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The statistical data for a certain community indicate that 25% of all girls are blondes, 50% of all girls and 75% of all blondes have blue eyes. If it is known that a girl has blue eyes, how much additional information is available if one is told that she is also a blonde?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.85 bits\nB. 1 bit\nC. 2 bits\nD. 0.5 bits\nE. 1.25 bits\nF. 0.75 bits\nG. 0.25 bits\nH. 1.75 bits\nI. 1.415 bits\nJ. 1.6 bits\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The question asks for the additional information in bits when learning that a blue-eyed girl is also blonde. This is calculated using the mutual information formula, and given the probabilities, the correct value is 0.415 bits, with the closest option being 0.5 bits. Thus, the answer is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 923, "output_tokens": 3406, "total_tokens": 4329}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10567", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Given the probability distribution of the random variable X in the table below, compute E(X) andVar(X). x_i Pr(X = x_i) 0 (8/27) 1 (12/27) 2 (6/27) 3 (1/27)\n\nOptions: \nA. E(X) = 3/2, Var(X) = 1/4\nB. E(X) = 2, Var(X) = 1/3\nC. E(X) = 5/3, Var(X) = 5/9\nD. E(X) = 1, Var(X) = 2/3\nE. E(X) = 3/4, Var(X) = 3/8\nF. E(X) = 2/3, Var(X) = 1\nG. E(X) = 0.5, Var(X) = 0.5\nH. E(X) = 1.5, Var(X) = 1.5\nI. E(X) = 1/2, Var(X) = 1/2\nJ. E(X) = 1/3, Var(X) = 2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 752, "output_tokens": 566, "total_tokens": 1318}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10122", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the Fourier cosine series over the interval 0 < x < c for the function f(x) = x.\n\nOptions: \nA. f(x) \\sim (1 / 2)c + (2c / \\pi^2)\\infty\\sum_k=1 [{{cos[(2k)\\pix/ c]}} / (2k)^2]\nB. f(x) \\sim (1 / 2)c + (4c / \\pi^2)\\infty\\sum_k=0 [{{cos[(2k + 1)\\pix/ c]}} / (2k + 1)^2]\nC. f(x) \\sim (1 / 2)c - (4c / \\pi^2)\\infty\\sum_n=1 [1 / n^2]cos{{(n\\pix) / c}}\nD. f(x) \\sim (1 / 2)c - (4c / \\pi^2)\\infty\\sum_k=0 [{{cos[(2k + 1)\\pix/ c]}} / (2k + 1)^2]\nE. f(x) \\sim (1 / 2)c - (4c / \\pi^2)\\infty\\sum_k=1 [{{cos[(2k)\\pix/ c]}} / (2k)^2]\nF. f(x) \\sim (1 / 2)c - (2c / \\pi^2)\\infty\\sum_n=0 [{{1 - (-1)^n}} / n^2]cos{{(n\\pix) / c}}\nG. f(x) \\sim (1 / 2)c + (4c / \\pi^2)\\infty\\sum_n=1 [{{(-1)^n}} / n^2]cos{{(n\\pix) / c}}\nH. f(x) \\sim (1 / 2)c + (2c / \\pi^2)\\infty\\sum_n=1 [{{1 - (- 1)^n}} / n^2]cos{{(n\\pix) / c}}\nI. f(x) \\sim (1 / 2)c + (2c / \\pi^2)\\infty\\sum_n=1 [(-1)^n / n^2]cos{{(n\\pix) / c}}\nJ. f(x) \\sim (1 / 2)c - (2c / \\pi^2)\\infty\\sum_n=1 [{{1 - (- 1)^n}} / n^2]cos{{(n\\pix) / c}}\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1284, "output_tokens": 457, "total_tokens": 1741}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10937", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An analog signal is quantized and encoded using pulse code modulation (PCM). (a) If the number of quantization levels M = 16 and the word length is 400 \\musec determine the minimum channel bandwith (f_c) required to transmit the bi-nary PCM signal. (b) If the channel has a bandwidth half of what is found in (a), determine the new number of quantiza-tion levels so that the PCM signal can pass through this channel.\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.26 \u00d7 10^+3Hz and 8\nB. 6.12 x 10^+3Hz and 12\nC. 2.00 x 10^+3Hz and 16\nD. 3.00 x 10^+3Hz and 3\nE. 1.53 x 10^+3Hz and 2\nF. 4.00 x 10^+3Hz and 1\nG. 3.56 x 10^+3Hz and 6\nH. 4.53 x 10^+3Hz and 8\nI. 2.53 \u00d7 10^+3Hz and 4\nJ. 5.06 x 10^+3Hz and 2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "We are told the number of quantization levels \\( M = 16 \\), which corresponds to 4 bits per sample (\\(n = \\log_2 16 = 4\\)).  \nThe word length (sample period) is 400 \u03bcs, so the bit rate is \\( 4 \\text{ bits} / 400 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{ s} = 10,000 \\) bits/s.  \nFor binary PCM, the minimum required bandwidth is half the bit rate: \\( f_c = 10,000 / 2 = 5000 \\) Hz, but careful \u2014 since word length refers to the PCM word duration, that gives actual bit rate as 4 bits per 400 \u03bcs = 10 kbps, so minimum bandwidth = 5 kHz. None of the options near 5 kHz match; the closest in the list is not matching exactly unless we recalculate: if word length is the *total sampling interval*, sample rate = 1/(400 \u03bcs) = 2500 samples/s, with 4 bits/sample \u2192 10 kbps and \\(f_c = 5\\) kHz \u2014 still not among options. Considering slight nuance, let\u2019s try: bit rate = bits per sample / sample period = 4 / (400\u00d710^{-6}) = 10,000 bps \u2192 \\(f_c\\) = 5000 Hz. None fit, but if M=16 then bits=4; checking with possible rounding mismatch leads closest to 5.06\u00d710^3 Hz and for half bandwidth ~2.53 kHz requiring halving bits per sample to 2 bits \u2192 M=4. This matches **I**.\n\n\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1313, "output_tokens": 8814, "total_tokens": 10127}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10627", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Convert the Fourier series f(t) = ^+\\infty\\sum_k=-\\infty {{(1) / (1 +jk)}}e^jkt to trigonometric form.\n\nOptions: \nA. f(t) = 1 + 2 ^\\infty\\sum_k=1 [{{coskt}} / {{1 + k^2}}]\nB. f(t) = ^\\infty\\sum_k=1 [{{coskt+ k sinkt}} / {{1 + k^2}}]\nC. f(t) = 2 ^\\infty\\sum_k=1 [{{coskt+ k sinkt}} / {{1 + k^2}}]\nD. f(t) = 1 + 2 ^\\infty\\sum_k=1 [{{coskt+ k sinkt}} / {{1 + k^2}}]\nE. f(t) = 2 + 2 ^\\infty\\sum_k=1 [{{coskt}} / {{1 + k^2}}]\nF. f(t) = 2 + ^\\infty\\sum_k=1 [{{coskt+ k sinkt}} / {{k^2 - 1}}]\nG. f(t) = 1 + 2 ^\\infty\\sum_k=1 [{{coskt - k sinkt}} / {{1 + k^2}}]\nH. f(t) = 1 + ^\\infty\\sum_k=1 [{{coskt+ k sinkt}} / {{1 + k^2}}]\nI. f(t) = 1 + ^\\infty\\sum_k=1 [{{sinkt}} / {{1 + k^2}}]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 984, "output_tokens": 518, "total_tokens": 1502}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10423", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the variance of the random variable, Z = X + Y if X and Y are not independent.\n\nOptions: \nA. VarZ = VarX + VarY - 2E[{{X - E(X)}}{{Y - E(Y)}}]\nB. VarZ = |VarX - VarY|\nC. VarZ =VarX +VarY\nD. VarZ = VarX + VarY + Cov(X,Y)\nE. VarZ = (VarX + VarY) / 2\nF. VarZ =VarX -VarY + 2E[{{X - E(X)}}{{Y - E(Y)}}]\nG. VarZ = VarX * VarY\nH. VarZ =VarX +VarY + 2E[{{X - E(X)}}{{Y - E(Y)}}]\nI. VarZ =VarX +VarY + 2E[{{X + E(X)}}{{Y + E(Y)}}]\nJ. VarZ = VarX + VarY - 2Cov(X,Y)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 861, "output_tokens": 255, "total_tokens": 1116}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10175", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A sinusoidal signal in the frequency range 0.4 to 4.4 KHz is being sampled at a rate equal to four times theNyquistrate. If this signal is received by a receiver of signal-to-noise ratio {{(s_i) / (\\eta}} = 10^6 after being quantized by a 256 levelquantizer at the transmission end, calculate (a) The time T between samples. (b) The number of bits N and the probability of error if the quantized signal is encoded into a binary PCM waveform. (c) The probability of error,P_e, if the signal is encoded into 1 to 256 orthogonal signals.\n\nOptions: \nA. T = 5.125 microseconds, N = 6 bits, P_e = 10^-3\nB. T = 3.125 microseconds, N = 8 bits, P_e = 10^-5\nC. T = 3.75 microseconds, N = 10 bits, P_e = 10^-5\nD. T = 2.5 microseconds, N = 7 bits, P_e = 10^-4\nE. T = 2.875 microseconds, N = 7 bits, P_e = 10^-2\nF. T = 2.25 microseconds, N = 8 bits, P_e = 10^-6\nG. T = 1.25 microseconds, N = 7 bits, P_e = 10^-7\nH. T = 4.5 microseconds, N = 9 bits, P_e = 10^-4\nI. T = 4.125 microseconds, N = 9 bits, P_e = 10^-6\nJ. T = 3.5 microseconds, N = 8 bits, P_e = 10^-3\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The sinusoidal signal has a maximum frequency of 4.4 kHz, so the Nyquist rate is 8.8 kHz. Sampling at four times the Nyquist rate gives a sampling frequency of 35.2 kHz, so the time between samples is \\( T = 1/35200 \\approx 28.4 \\, \\mu\\text{s} \\), which is not matching any option exactly \u2014 but checking carefully: actually, the Nyquist rate is \\(2 \\times 4.4 = 8.8\\) kHz, and four times that is 35.2 kHz, giving \\( T \\approx 28.4 \\, \\mu\\text{s}\\), so let's re-evaluate.  \n\nA 256-level quantizer requires \\( \\log_2 256 = 8 \\) bits, and with signal-to-noise ratio of \\(10^6\\), the probability of error for binary PCM is very small, typically around \\(10^{-6}\\). Only option F has 8 bits and \\(P_e = 10^{-6}\\), and its \\(T = 2.25 \\, \\mu\\text{s}\\) roughly fits if the maximum frequency were higher, but the calculation discrepancy indicates the closest match by bit count and error probability is F.\n\nThus, \\boxed{F}.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1929, "output_tokens": 15663, "total_tokens": 17592}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10179", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A frequency modulation (FM) receiver with input signal- to- noise ratio (S_i /nf_m) = 40 dB is used to pick- up sig-nals from different FM stations. If the transmitted FM signal is represented by km(t) = \\beta \\bullet \\omega \\bulletcos(\\omega_mt), calcu-late output signal- to- noise ratio for different values of \\beta such as 5, 10 and 105.\n\nOptions: \nA. \u03b2 = 5, 58.7 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 64.7 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 85.185 dB\nB. \u03b2 = 5, 55.7 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 61.7 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 82.185 dB\nC. \u03b2 = 5, 50 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 60 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 80 dB\nD. \u03b2 = 5, 52.5 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 58.5 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 78.685 dB\nE. \u03b2 = 5, 60.1 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 66.1 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 87.285 dB\nF. \u03b2 = 5, 47.2 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 53.2 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 73.385 dB\nG. \u03b2 = 5, 45.7 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 51.7 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 72.185 dB\nH. \u03b2 = 5, 65.7 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 71.7 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 92.185 dB\nI. \u03b2 = 5, 43.6 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 49.6 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 69.785 dB\nJ. \u03b2 = 5, 42 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 48 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 68.185 dB\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 2324, "output_tokens": 594, "total_tokens": 2918}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provid