 3)]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1164, "output_tokens": 1251, "total_tokens": 2415}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10349", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If six messages having probabilities (1 / 4), (1 / 4), (1 / 8), (1 / 8), (1 / 8) and (1 / 8) can be accommodated in a single communication system, determine the entropy.\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.00 bits/message\nB. 2.25 bits/message\nC. 1.75 bits/message\nD. 3.00 bits/message\nE. 2.75 bits/message\nF. 3.25 bits/message\nG. 4.00 bits/message\nH. 3.50 bits/message\nI. 2.50 bits/message\nJ. 1.50 bits/message\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 704, "output_tokens": 398, "total_tokens": 1102}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10111", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Determine the inverse Laplace transform of F(s), where F(s) is given by F(s) = [(3s + 1) / {{(s - 1)(s^2 + 1)}}]\n\nOptions: \nA. 3e^t + sin t - cos t\nB. e^t - cos t + sin t\nC. e^t - sin t - cos t\nD. e^t + cos t - 2 sin t\nE. 3e^t - cos t - 2 sin t\nF. 2e^t + sin t + 2 cos t\nG. 2e^t - 2 cos t + sin t\nH. 2e^t - 2 sin t + cos t\nI. e^t - 2 cos t + 2 sin t\nJ. 2e^t + 2 cos t - sin t\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "We start with partial fraction decomposition:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3s+1}{(s-1)(s^2+1)} = \\frac{A}{s-1} + \\frac{Bs+C}{s^2+1}\n\\]\nMultiplying through gives \\( 3s+1 = A(s^2+1) + (Bs+C)(s-1) \\).\n\nPlugging \\(s=1\\): \\(4 = A(1+1) \\Rightarrow A=2\\).  \nComparing coefficients: \\(A+B=0 \\Rightarrow B=-2\\); and \\(A - C = 1 \\Rightarrow 2 - C = 1 \\Rightarrow C=1\\).\n\nThus  \n\\[\nF(s) = \\frac{2}{s-1} + \\frac{-2s+1}{s^2+1} = \\frac{2}{s-1} - 2\\frac{s}{s^2+1} + \\frac{1}{s^2+1}.\n\\]\n\nTaking the inverse Laplace:  \n\\[\nf(t) = 2e^t - 2\\cos t + \\sin t.\n\\]\n\nThis matches option **G**.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{G}\n\\]", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 942, "output_tokens": 1261, "total_tokens": 2203}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10638", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A punch press has a no. 308 spherical roller bearing. The mainshaft runs at 1600 rpm and the bearing experiences a radialload of 2000 lbs. and a thrust of 1400 lbs. Under steadyloading conditions and for outer bearing ring rotation evaluate (a)bearinglife for 90% reliability (b)bearinglife for 96% reliability.\n\nOptions: \nA. 625.8 hrs. to 315.9 hrs.\nB. 680.3 hrs. to 350.4 hrs.\nC. 697.4 hrs. to 383.6 hrs.\nD. 650.0 hrs. to 325.0 hrs.\nE. 500.0 hrs. to 250.0 hrs.\nF. 750.5 hrs. to 400.7 hrs.\nG. 850.7 hrs. to 450.3 hrs.\nH. 760.2 hrs. to 410.1 hrs.\nI. 800.0 hrs. to 420.0 hrs.\nJ. 720.6 hrs. to 390.8 hrs.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 916, "output_tokens": 655, "total_tokens": 1571}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10013", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Use partial fraction expansion to find the inverse z-transform of F (z) = [{{2z^2 - 2z}} / {{(z - 3) (z - 5)^2}}].\n\nOptions: \nA. f [n] = 4nu[n] + [(5/6)n - 1] 6^n u[n]\nB. f [n] = 6nu[n] + [(2/3)n - 1] 3^n u[n]\nC. f [n] = 3^(n+1)u[n] - 5^n u[n]\nD. f [n] = 3nu[n] + [(4/5)n - 1] 5^n u[n]\nE. f [n] = [(2/3)n + 1] (3/2)^n u[n] - 2^(n-1) u[n]\nF. f [n] = 3nu[n] + [(5/4)n - 1] (4/5)^n u[n]\nG. f [n] = 4nu[n] + [(7/8)n - 2] 8^n u[n]\nH. f [n] = 2nu[n] + [(3/5)n - 1] 4^n u[n]\nI. f [n] = 5nu[n] + [(6/7)n - 1] 7^n u[n]\nJ. f [n] = 2^n u[n] + [(3/4)n + 1] (4/3)^n u[n]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "We first perform partial fraction expansion on \\(F(z)/z\\) because the standard \\(z\\)-transform pairs are typically for \\(F(z)/z\\).  \n\n\\[\n\\frac{F(z)}{z} = \\frac{2z - 2}{(z-3)(z-5)^2}\n\\]  \nUsing partial fractions, this expands to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{A}{z-3} + \\frac{B}{z-5} + \\frac{C}{(z-5)^2}\n\\]  \nSolving gives \\(A = 1\\), \\(B = -1\\), \\(C = 4\\).  \n\nThus  \n\\[\nF(z) = \\frac{z}{z-3} - \\frac{z}{z-5} + \\frac{4z}{(z-5)^2}\n\\]  \nTaking inverse \\(z\\)-transforms:  \n- \\(\\frac{z}{z-3} \\to 3^n u[n]\\)  \n- \\(-\\frac{z}{z-5} \\to -5^n u[n]\\)  \n- \\(\\frac{4z}{(z-5)^2} \\to 4n \\cdot 5^{n-1} u[n] = \\frac{4}{5} n \\cdot 5^n u[n]\\)  \n\nThis gives  \n\\[\nf[n] = 3^n u[n] - 5^n u[n] + \\frac{4}{5} n 5^n u[n] = 3^n u[n] + \\left[\\frac{4}{5} n - 1\\right]5^n u[n]\n\\]  \nThis matches option D.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1265, "output_tokens": 888, "total_tokens": 2153}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10334", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A three input information channel with all three input symbols equally probable, is defined by the channel matrix, \\vert0.50.30.2\\vert \\vert0.20.30.5\\vert \\vert0.30.30.4\\vert Assuming that a maximum-likelihood decision rule is used, determine the error probability, P_E, of the channel.\n\nOptions: \nA. (13) / (30)\nB. (19) / (30)\nC. (15) / (30)\nD. (18) / (30)\nE. (14) / (30)\nF. (17) / (30)\nG. (21) / (30)\nH. (12) / (30)\nI. (16) / (30)\nJ. (20) / (30)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 760, "output_tokens": 1946, "total_tokens": 2706}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10721", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the Fourier sine series of f(x) = x^2 over the interval (0, 1).\n\nOptions: \nA. x^2 \\sim_s ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{[{{(- 1)^n+1}} / (n\\pi)]}} sinn\\pix\nB. x^2 \\sim_s ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{2 / (n\\pi)]}} sinn\\pix\nC. x^2 \\sim_s ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{[{{(- 1)^n}} / (n^3\\pi^3)]}} sinn\\pix\nD. x^2 \\sim_s ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{[{{(- 1)^n+1}} / (n\\pi)] + [{{4}} / (n^3\\pi^3)]}} sinn\\pix\nE. x^2 \\sim_s ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{[{{(- 1)^n}} / (n^2\\pi^2)]}} sinn\\pix\nF. x^2 \\sim_s 2 ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{[{{(- 1)^n+1}} / (n\\pi)] + [{{2[1 - (- 1)^n]}} / (n^3\\pi^3)]}} sinn\\pix\nG. x^2 \\sim_s ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{[{{1}} / (n\\pi)] + [{{(- 1)^n+1}} / (n^2\\pi^2)]}} sinn\\pix\nH. x^2 \\sim_s 2 ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{1 / (n^2\\pi^2)}} sinn\\pix\nI. x^2 \\sim_s 2 ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{[{{(- 1)^n+1}} / (n\\pi)] - [{{2[1 - (- 1)^n]}} / (n^3\\pi^3)]}} sinn\\pix\nJ. x^2 \\sim_s ^\\infty\\sum_n=1 {{[{{(- 1)^n+1}} / (n^2\\pi^2)] - [{{2[1 - (- 1)^n]}} / (n^4\\pi^4)]}} sinn\\pix\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1216, "output_tokens": 458, "total_tokens": 1674}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10877", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider the function, g(x) = (1 + x^2)^-1 Determine a constant k such that f(x) = k(1 + x^2)^-1 is a proper probability density for - \\infty < x < \\infty. Find F(x) = Pr(X \\leq x) if X is distributed with density function f(x).\n\nOptions: \nA. 