}}]\n\nOptions: \nA. - e^-t - e^2t + 2te^2t - (t^2 / 2)e^2t\nB. e^-t - 2e^2t + 3te^2t - (t^3 / 6)e^2t\nC. -e^-t + 3e^2t - t^2e^2t\nD. -e^-t + 2e^2t - 2te^2t + (t^3 / 3)e^2t\nE. e^-t + e^2t - 2te^2t + (t^2 / 2)e^2t\nF. -2e^-t - e^2t + (t^2 / 2)e^2t - te^2t\nG. e^-t + e^2t - (t^2 / 2)e^2t - 3te^2t\nH. 2e^-t + 3e^2t - 4te^2t + (t^3 / 3)e^2t\nI. - e^-t + e^2t + 2te^2t - (t^2 / 2)e^2t\nJ. - e^-t + e^2t - 2te^2t + (t^2 / 2)e^2t\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "We perform partial fraction decomposition of  \n\\[\nF(s) = \\frac{5s^2 - 15s + 7}{(s+1)(s-2)^3}.\n\\]  \nThe form is  \n\\[\n\\frac{A}{s+1} + \\frac{B}{s-2} + \\frac{C}{(s-2)^2} + \\frac{D}{(s-2)^3}.\n\\]  \nSolving gives \\(A = -1\\), \\(B = 1\\), \\(C = 2\\), \\(D = -1\\).  \nTaking the inverse Laplace yields  \n\\[\n- e^{-t} + e^{2t} + 2t e^{2t} - \\frac{t^2}{2} e^{2t},\n\\]  \nwhich matches option I.  \n\n\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1417, "output_tokens": 789, "total_tokens": 2206}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10180", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Use the derivative property of Laplace transforms to solve the differential equation y' - y = e^-x(1) where y(0) = 0 is the initial value of y.\n\nOptions: \nA. sinh x\nB. e^x - e^-x\nC. e^x + x\nD. x^2 e^x\nE. cosh x\nF. (1 / 2)e^x - (1 / 2)e^-x\nG. x*e^x\nH. e^-x\nI. (1 / 2)e^x + (1 / 2)e^-x\nJ. e^x\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "predictio