}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10562", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a factory four machines produce the same product. Machine A produces 10% of the output, machine B, 20%, machine C, 30%, and machine D, 40%. The proportion of defective items produced by these follows: Machine A: .001; Machine B: .0005; Machine C: .005; Machine D: .002. An item selected at random is found to be defective. What is the probability that the item was produced by A? by B? by C? by D?\n\nOptions: \nA. P(M_1|M) = 1/30, P(M_2|M) = 2/30, P(M_3|M) = 1/3, P(M_4|M) = 1/30\nB. P(M_1|M) = 1/15, P(M_2|M) = 1/15, P(M_3|M) = 1/2, P(M_4|M) = 2/15\nC. P(M_1|M) = 1/25, P(M_2|M) = 3/25, P(M_3|M) = 1/5, P(M_4|M) = 5/25\nD. P(M_1|M) = 2/25, P(M_2|M) = 2/25, P(M_3|M) = 1/4, P(M_4|M) = 7/25\nE. P(M_1|M) = 1/25, P(M_2|M) = 1/25, P(M_3|M) = 3/5, P(M_4|M) = 8/25\nF. P(M_1|M) = 1/25, P(M_2|M) = 1/25, P(M_3|M) = 1/5, P(M_4|M) = 1/25\nG. P(M_1|M) = 1/20, P(M_2|M) = 1/20, P(M_3|M) = 2/5, P(M_4|M) = 1/20\nH. P(M_1|M) = 1/50, P(M_2|M) = 1/50, P(M_3|M) = 1/10, P(M_4|M) = 1/50\nI. P(M_1|M) = 2/25, P(M_2|M) = 1/25, P(M_3|M) = 2/5, P(M_4|M) = 6/25\nJ. P(M_1|M) = 3/25, P(M_2|M) = 1/50, P(M_3|M) = 3/10, P(M_4|M) = 9/25\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1778, "output_tokens": 569, "total_tokens": 2347}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10912", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\n