0 \u00d7 10^7t - 1.23 sin (2\u03c0 \u00d7 10^6t) m\nI. 1.50 \u00d7 10^7t - 2.23 cos (2\\pi \u00d7 10^6t) m\nJ. 1.50 \u00d7 10^7t - 2.23 sin (2\\pi \u00d7 10^6t) m\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The electron is released with an initial velocity of \\(10^6\\) m/s in the x-direction.  \nThe applied voltage creates a time-dependent electric field, causing an oscillatory motion superimposed on the constant velocity drift.  \nThe correct expression matching the problem\u2019s parameters is \\(1.50 \\times 10^7 t - 2.23 \\sin (2\\pi \\times 10^6 t)\\) m.\n\n\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1693, "output_tokens": 611, "total_tokens": 2304}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10428", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Use Fouriertransformmethods to find the time-domain responseof a network having a system function [(j2\\omega) / (1 + 2j\\omega)], ifthe input is V(t) =cost (For asinusodialinputcost, the Fourier transform is \\pi[\\delta (\\omega + 1) + \\delta (\\omega - 1)] ).\n\nOptions: \nA. (4/5)cost - (2/5) sin t\nB. (3/4)cost - (1/4)sint\nC. (2/5)cost + (4/5) sin t\nD. cost + sint\nE. (3/5)cost + (1/5)sint\nF. (4/5)cost + (2/5) sin t\nG. (1/5)cost - (3/5)sint\nH. (1/2)cost + (1/2)sint\nI. (1/3)cost - (2/3)sint\nJ. (2/5)cost - (4/5) sin t\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed