/m^3. Find the surface current density at a surface making an angle of 45\u00b0 withM.\n\nOptions: \nA. 6000 A m^-1\nB. 6500 A m^-1\nC. 7070 A m^-1\nD. 5000 A m^-1\nE. 8000 A m^-1\nF. 7500 A m^-1\nG. 4500 A m^-1\nH. 5500 A m^-1\nI. 9000 A m^-1\nJ. 10000 A m^-1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 680, "output_tokens": 392, "total_tokens": 1072}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10925", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 15 hp internal-combustion engine runs at 1400 rpm and rotates a grinding disc at 700 rpm under smooth conditions. If a triple strand no. 50 roller chain is to transmit power, calculate the number of teeth on both sprockets and the kind of lubrication needed for rust-proof operation.\n\nOptions: \nA. Driving sprocket = 11 teeth, Driven sprocket = 22 teeth, Lubrication type = B\nB. Driving sprocket = 7 teeth, Driven sprocket = 14 teeth, Lubrication type = D\nC. Driving sprocket = 6 teeth, Driven sprocket = 12 teeth, Lubrication type = C\nD. Driving sprocket = 14 teeth, Driven sprocket = 28 teeth, Lubrication type = A\nE. Driving sprocket = 15 teeth, Driven sprocket = 30 teeth, Lubrication type = D\nF. Driving sprocket = 12 teeth, Driven sprocket = 24 teeth, Lubrication type = C\nG. Driving sprocket = 9 teeth, Driven sprocket = 18 teeth, Lubrication type = B\nH. Driving sprocket = 13 teeth, Driven sprocket = 26 teeth, Lubrication type = A\nI. Driving sprocket = 8 teeth, Driven sprocket = 16 teeth, Lubrication type = C\nJ. Drivi