017, "total_tokens": 2781}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10298", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 6-pole 3-phase 60-cycle alternator has 12 slots per pole and four conductors per slot. The winding is five-sixths pitch. There are 2,500,000 maxwells (= 0.025 weber) entering the armature from each north pole, and this flux is sinusoidally distributed along the air gap. The armature coils are all connected in series. The winding is Y-connected. Determine the open-circuit emf of the alternator.\n\nOptions: \nA. 296 volts\nB. 480 volts\nC. 425 volts\nD. 350 volts\nE. 550 volts\nF. 600 volts\nG. 513 volts\nH. 250 volts\nI. 275 volts\nJ. 700 volts\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The open-circuit emf of the alternator is approximately 513 volts, which corresponds to option G. This is determined by calculating the phase voltage using the formula \\( E_{\\text{ph}} = 4.44 f \\Phi N_{\\text{ph}} k_w \\), where \\( N_{\\text{ph}} = 48 \\) turns per phase, \\( k_w = 0.9251 \\) (product of pitch and distribution factors), and \\( \\Phi = 0.025 \\) Wb, yielding \\( E_{\\text{ph}} \\approx 296 \\) V, and then converting to line voltage for a Y-connection: \\( E_{\\text{line}} = \\sqrt{3} \\times 296 \\approx 513 \\) V.\n\n\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1251, "output_tokens": 4957, "total_tokens": 6208}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engin