ave of40KHzis radiated by an antenna . Find the time taken by this wave to reach a point 60 km away.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.3 msec\nB. 0.8 msec\nC. 0.6 msec\nD. 0.25 msec\nE. 0.1 msec\nF. 0.2 msec\nG. 1.5 msec\nH. 0.4 msec\nI. 0.05 msec\nJ. 0.9 msec\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 603, "output_tokens": 408, "total_tokens": 1011}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10001", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The drag of a ship in water is assumed to depend on the Reynolds number and the Froude number so that [drag / {{(1/2)(\\rhoV^2A)}}] = f [{{(\\rhoVD) / \\mu}}, (V^2 / gD)] It is proposed that a model one-tenth the size of a full-scale ship be tested in water and the results be used to predict the performance of the full-scale ship. Is this feasible?\n\nOptions: \nA. both Froude and Reynolds numbers need to be greater in the prototype\nB. only Weber numbers need to be equal for model and prototype\nC. the attainment of dynamic similarity in model and prototype is not possible\nD. both Froude and Reynolds numbers need to be smaller in the model\nE. similitude can be achieved by matching the Euler numbers only\nF. the attainment of dynamic similarity in model and prototype is possible\nG. dynamic similarity is irrelevant for predicting performance\nH. the attainment of geometric similarity in model and prototype is sufficient\nI. only Reynolds numbers need to be equal for model and prototype\nJ. only Froude numbers need to be equal for model and prototype\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1364, "output_tokens": 460, "total_tokens": 1824}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10055", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A single phase full bridge inverter can operated in load commutation mode in case load consist of\n\nOptions: \nA. Purely resistive load.\nB. RL.\nC. RLC underdamped with a parallel connection.\nD. RLC critically damped.\nE. RLC underdamped with a series connection.\nF. Capacitive load.\nG. RLC underdamped.\nH. Purely inductive load.\nI. RLC overdamped.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 652, "output_tokens": 423, "total_tokens": 1075}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10064", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Gas a, liters^2 -atm/mole b, liters/mole A 4.0 0.027 B 12.0 0.030 C 6.0 0.032 Which gas has (a) the highest critical temperature, (b) the largest molecular volume, and (c) most ideal general behavior around STP?\n\nOptions: \nA. Gas B has the highest critical temperature, Gas A has the largest molecular volume, Gas C has the most ideal general behavior around STP\nB. Gas B has the highest critical temperature, Gas C has the largest molecular volume, Gas A has the most ideal general behavior around STP\nC. Gas A has the highest critical temperature, Gas B has the largest molecular volume, Gas C has the most ideal general behavior around STP\nD. Gas C has the highest critical temperature, Gas B has the largest molecular volume, Gas A has the most ideal general behavior around STP\nE. Gas A has the highest critical temperature, Gas C has the largest molecular volume, Gas B has the most ideal general behavior around STP\nF. Gas C has the highest critical temperature, Gas A has the largest molecular volume, Gas B has the most ideal general behavior around STP\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1340, "output_tokens": 439, "total_tokens": 1779}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10223", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The \u0475 -irelation of a nonlinear resistor is given by \u0475 (t) = (1/2)i^2 (t) Is this resistor voltage-controlled? Current-controlled?\n\nOptions: \nA. The resistor is controlled by the square root of the current\nB. The resistor is current controlled\nC. The resistor is both voltage and current controlled\nD. The resistor control depends on the frequency of the input signal\nE. The resistor is controlled by the cube of the current\nF. The resistor is voltage