rovide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It has been observed that a reduction in family size and improved sanitary condition have led to an increase in allergic conditions. The 'hygiene hypothesis' suggests that\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Living on a working farm will increase the development of atopic diseases\nB. Particular care must be taken during breast feeding in high risk infants\nC. Living on a working farm will help reducing the development of atopic diseases\nD. Using antibiotics frequently will reduce allergies\nE. Living in urban areas will help reduce the development of atopic diseases\nF. The frequent use of antiseptic swipes will reduce allergies\nG. Exposure to allergens in early childhood will increase the risk of developing allergies\nH. Staying in highly sanitized environments will reduce the development of atopic diseases\nI. Breastfeeding should be avoided in high risk infants to prevent allergies\nJ. The use of probiotics in infants will increase the development of atopic diseases\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1016, "output_tokens": 311, "total_tokens": 1327}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4969", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following could lead to iodine deficiency?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Living at high altitudes\nB. Excessive consumption of fast food\nC. Intake only of locally grown food in central Africa\nD. Low intake of dairy products\nE. Drinking t