ons given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What happens during the 'incubation period'?\n\nOptions: \nA. The virus mutates and becomes more virulent\nB. This period commonly lasts for a few hours\nC. Virus replication happens at an intracellular level\nD. Symptoms of the disease start appearing in the host\nE. The virus is spread to others without any symptoms in the host\nF. The host's body becomes immune to the virus\nG. The virus is cleared from the body by the immune system\nH. This period commonly lasts for a few years\nI. The virus is dormant and does not replicate\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 832, "output_tokens": 277, "total_tokens": 1109}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5497", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Those more likely to experience depression after a loss are those who\n\nOptions: \nA. Have a strong social support network\nB. Have no previous history of mental health issues\nC. Have not previously experienced depression\nD. Have a high income\nE. Have been married less than a year\nF. Are young survivors\nG. Are in good health\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 632, "output_tokens": 352, "total_tokens": 984}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5545", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Older adults are able to improve their memories and reduce their anxiety about declining memory when\n\nOptions: \nA. They engage in social activities and interact with peers\nB. They practice mindfulness and meditation to reduce stress levels\nC. They engage in physical activity regularly\nD. They regularly solve puzzles and engage in brain-stimulating activities\nE. They learn that many aspects of memory do not decline and some even get better\nF. They simply learn a number of memory improvement techniques\nG. They take memory-enhancing medications\nH. They learn about memory and aging and learn some techniques\nI. They consume a diet rich in antioxidants and omega-3 fatty acids\nJ. Older adults cannot do either of these\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 934, "output_tokens": 331, "total_tokens": 1265}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5546", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Loss of stomach lining can lead to symptoms that resemble\n\nOptions: \nA. Diabetes\nB. Dementia\nC. Osteoporosis\nD. Tuberculosis\nE. Hepatitis\nF. Senescence\nG. Leukemia\nH. Anorexia\nI. Parkinson's disease\nJ. Hypertension\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}  \n\nLoss of stomach lining impairs digestion and absorption of nutrients, often leading to severe weight loss and appetite suppression that mimics anorexia. It does not directly cause the metabolic, neurological, or bone disorders listed in the other options. Anorexia nervosa shares similar symptomatic features with the malnutrition resulting from advanced gastric atrophy.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 648, "output_tokens": 458, "total_tokens": 1106}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5572", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements about the protein requirement is correct\n\n\nOptions: \nA. The protein requirement can be less than the demand.\nB. The protein requirement is equal to the demand minus the efficiency of utilization.\nC. The protein requirement is equal to the demand divided by the efficiency of utilization.\nD. The protein requirement is always higher than the demand.\nE. The protein requirement is the same for all individuals regardless of age or health status.\nF. The protein requirement is equal to the demand multiplied by the efficiency of utilization.\nG. The protein requirement is always the same as the demand.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 944, "output_tokens": 346, "total_tokens": 1290}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5574", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The effects of iron on certain aspects of socio-emotional development (shyness, orientation/engagement and response to unfamiliar pictures) is due to:\n\n\nOptions: \nA. The role of iron in serotonin production\nB. None of the above\nC. The role of iron in neurochemistry\nD. The role of iron in maintaining blood sugar levels\nE. The role of iron in muscle function\nF. The role of iron in energy metabolism\nG. The role of iron in dopamine production\nH. The role of iron in myelination\nI. The role of iron in cognitive development\nJ. The role of iron in red blood cell production\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 884, "output_tokens": 461, "total_tokens": 1345}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4977", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A team of engineers constructing signal lights for airplanes that they can use to guide them to runways are attempting to determine the brightness needed for the pilot to be able to detect the tower at 1 mile away. They set the light to a test brightness and establish communication with an inbound pilot. When the pilot is 1 mile away from the tower, he says he cannot see the 