g cannot be a substrate for gluconeogenesis?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Palmitic acid\nB. Pyruvate\nC. Galactose\nD. Glycerol\nE. Propionic acid\nF. Lactic acid\nG. Aspartic acid\nH. Alanine\nI. Glutamic acid\nJ. Oxaloacetate\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 536, "output_tokens": 418, "total_tokens": 954}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4912", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Newborn infants in countries with limited access to safe water and low levels of education should be:\n\nOptions: \nA. Exclusively formula fed for six months\nB. Exclusively breast fed for six months\nC. Should receive both breast milk and other foods as tolerated in the first 6\nD. months\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 592, "output_tokens": 452, "total_tokens": 1044}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5421", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A race car attempting to jump a series of 8 buses is set up on a flat track with a ramp at the end. Engineers assigned to the project have determined that, in order to jump the buses, the car must reach a velocity of 130 km/h. If the distance of the track is 50m, at what rate must the car accelerate to reach this velocity?\n\nOptions: \nA. 26 m/s^2\nB. 22 m/s^2\nC. 10 m/s^2\nD. 20 m/s^2\nE. 17 m/s^2\nF. 15 m/s^2\nG. 7 m/s^2\nH. 13 m/s^2\nI. 18 m/s^2\nJ. 30 m/s^2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 821, "output_tokens": 492, "total_tokens": 1313}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5253", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: On an average daily basis, the gross energy intake of a healthy woman is 9279 kJ, the energy content of her faeces and urine are 647 kJ and 318 kJ, respectively. Her average daily digestible energy intake and metabolisable energy intake would be, respectively,:\n\n\nOptions: \nA. 9279-318 kJ and 9279-647 kJ\nB. 9279-318 kJ and 9279-318 kJ\nC. 9279-(318+647) kJ and 9279-647 kJ\nD. 9279+647 kJ and 9279-(318+647) kJ\nE. 9279+318 kJ and 9279-(318+318) kJ\nF. 9279-647 kJ and 9279-(647+318) kJ\nG. 9279-318 kJ and 9279-(318+318) kJ\nH. 9279+318 kJ and 9279+647 kJ\nI. 9279 kJ and 9279-(318+318) kJ\nJ. 647 kJ and 318 kJ\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 916, "output_tokens": 321, "total_tokens": 1237}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5423", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Walking down a street late at night, an adult male pedestrian notices a young female on the ground, not moving. The female is on the opposite side of the street. Crossing the street, the pedestrian notices that the young woman appears both much wealthier than he is and is of a different ethnicity. Seeing no one else present, the pedestrian renders aid. According to the bystander effect, which of the following would change how the pedestrian reacts?\n\nOptions: \nA. The presence of a security camera on the street\nB. The presence of one other person who is already approaching the girl\nC. The person requiring aid appearing to be of a lower socioeconomic class rather than a higher one\nD. The presence of a large, intimidating dog near the girl\nE. The person requiring aid appearing to be the same ethnicity rather than a different one\nF. The person requiring aid appearing to be less wealthy than initially thought\nG. The person requiring aid appearing to be older rather than younger\nH. The person requiring aid appearing to be of the same gender rather than a different one\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1323, "output_tokens": 430, "total_tokens": 1753}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4997", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The likelihood of an individual in a population carrying two specific alleles of a human DNA marker, each of which has a frequency of 0.2, will be:\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.24\nB. 0.4\nC. 0.32\nD. 0.1\nE. 0.16\nF. 0.12\nG. 0.02\nH. 0.04\nI. 0.08\nJ. 0.06\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 548, "output_tokens": 279, "total_tokens": 827}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4921", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A segment of DNA from a lab mouse is determined to be 5\u2019 \u2013 GGATCCTCATG \u2013 3\u2019. Which of the following DNA segments would be the result of this original DNA sequence experiencing both a point mutation and a deletion?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5' - GGATCCTCA - 3'\nB. 5\u2019 \u2013 TGATCCCAG \u2013 3\u2019\nC. 5\u2019 \u2013 GGATCCATG \u2013 3\u2019\nD. 5' - GGATCCTCGT - 3'\nE. 5\u2019 \u2013 GGTCCTCATC \u2013 3\u2019\nF. 5' - GGATCCGCATG - 3'\nG. 5' - GGATCTCATG - 3'\nH. 5' - GGATCCTCAT - 3'\nI. 5' - GGATCCTCAG - 3'\nJ. 5\u2019 \u2013 GCATCCTCATG \u2013 3\u2019\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The original sequence is 5\u2019 \u2013 GGATCCTCATG \u2013 3\u2019. A deletion removes one or more bases, and a point mutation changes a single base.  \nOption C, 5\u2019 \u2013 GGATCCATG \u2013 3\u2019, has two bases deleted (the \"TC\" after GGATCC) and no point mutation, so it does not include both changes.  \nOption D, 5' - GGATCCTCGT - 3', has a deletion of the last \"G\" and a point mutation (T\u2192G in the \"TG\" region), fulfilling both conditions.  \n\n\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1092, "output_tokens": 10390, "total_tokens": 11482}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5258", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If the mean rate of oxygen consumption of a male athlete during a training session is 2 l/min, then his rate of energy expenditure is approximately:\n\nOptions: \nA. 20 kJ/min.\nB. 500 kJ/min.\nC. 30 kJ/min.\nD. 40 kJ/min.\nE. 400 kJ/min.\nF. 60 kJ/min.\nG. 200 kJ/min.\nH. 100 kJ/min.\nI. 80 kJ/min.\nJ. 120 kJ/min.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 616, "output_tokens": 292, "total_tokens": 908}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5203", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Under which circumstances would you not use a catheter valve?\n\nOptions: \nA. If the patient chooses it.\nB. If the patient is bedridden.\nC. If urine does not need to be meas