f Society EXCEPT:\n\nOptions: \nA. The extensive use of technology in everyday life\nB. Rationalization of decisions into cost/benefit analysis structures and away from traditional modes of thinking\nC. A focus on efficiency and predictability in all aspects of society\nD. An intense effort on achieving sameness across diverse markets\nE. Increased emphasis on quantity over quality\nF. The prioritization of profit over societal well-being\nG. Bureaucratic organization that formalizes well-establish division of labor and impersonal structures\nH. The standardization of societal norms and practices\nI. A shift from individual craftsmanship to mass production\nJ. A dissolution of hierarchical modes of authority into collaborative teambased decision protocols\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1124, "output_tokens": 474, "total_tokens": 1598}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5198", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why do vigorous CD8 cell responses in chronically infected HIV-positive individuals fail to eliminate the virus?\n\nOptions: \nA. Inadequate MHC Class I presentation\nB. Suboptimal CTL\nC. Overproduction of interferon gamma\nD. Overactive T-helper cells\nE. Absence of dendritic cells\nF. CTL exhaustion\nG. Presence of neutralizing antibodies\nH. Epitope escape\nI. Insufficient natural killer cell activity\nJ. Lack of B cell response\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 719, "output_tokens": 359, "total_tokens": 1078}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4923", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A certain molecule acts by binding to cytochrome oxidase A3, the final enzyme in the electron transport chain. Administration of a large dose of this substance to a human would likely:\n\nOptions: \nA. Decrease the rate of glycolysis, leading to a drop in ATP production.\nB. Have no effect as cells would switch which macronutrient they metabolize to circumvent the blocked biochemical pathway.\nC. Stimulate the cell to increase its production of cytochrome oxidase A3 to compensate for the blocked enzyme.\nD. Lead to the overproduction of NADH, causing a buildup of toxic metabolites in the cell.\nE. Increase the cell\u2019s ATP production as negative feedback would cause the cell to up-regulate anaerobic pathways.\nF. Increase the efficiency of the electron transport chain by providing an alternative pathway for electron transfer.\nG. Have no effect as the cells would increase their reliance on fatty acid oxidation for energy production.\nH. Lead to death due to an inability of the cell to pass electrons to oxygen, thus stopping aerobic respiration and asphyxiating the cells.\nI. Lead to death due to an inadequate supply of ADP to accept a phosphate group at the ATP synthase enzyme.\nJ. Cause a rapid increase in the production of reactive oxygen species, leading to oxidative stress and cell death.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1348, "output_tokens": 311, "total_tokens": 1659}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4873", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A problem for immune system theories of senescence is\n\nOptions: \nA. Determining what first causes the senescence in the immune system\nB. The immune system theories do not explain the role of lifestyle in senescence\nC. Immune system theories do not explain the role of genetic factors in senescence\nD. Immune system theories are too complex to test effectively\nE. The lack of information about senescence in general\nF. That the immune system improves with age\nG. Immune system theories cannot account for the environmental factors in senescence\nH. That the immune system does not decline with age\nI. The difficulty of isolating the immune system from other bodily systems\nJ. Auto-immune disorders are far too rare\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 990, "output_tokens": 382, "total_tokens": 1372}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4955", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A phase 2, multicenter trial was conducted to determine the efficacy of a new vaccine for prevention of HIV infection. The study enrolled 4000 subjects, aged 20 to 65 years. Of these subjects, 2100 were men and 1900 were women; 2500 were white, 1000 were African American, 300 were Hispanic, and 200 were Asian/Pacific Islanders. Results of the trial showed no overall benefit of the vaccine. However, post hoc analysis disclosed a small but statistically significant vaccine protection among African American subjects. Which of the following is the most accurate rationale for questioning the validity of efficacy analysis of the HIV vaccine among the African American study subjects?\n\nOptions: \nA. HIV infection is more prevalent among African American populations\nB. The vaccine had no overall benefit\nC. The study was not blinded\nD. The age of the subjects could have affected the results\nE. The study did not disclose the number of subjects who were actually infected with HIV\nF. There was a Type II error\nG. Vaccine response among African American subjects was not the primary outcome measure\nH. The vaccine response varied across different ethnicities\nI. There was a Type I error\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1496, "output_tokens": 445, "total_tokens": 1941}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5141", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If the human norovirus cannot be cultured in cell cultures how can it best be studied?\n\nOptions: \nA. Volunteer studies\nB. Animal studies using non-human primates\nC. Through computer simulation models of the virus\nD. By studying the virus's effect on plant cells\nE. In cells using replicon systems\nF. Animal models\nG. By isolating the virus in a laboratory setting\nH. In cells using non-replicon systems\nI. Deductions from the 3 human ORF's of the virus genome\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 708, "output_tokens": 259, "total_tokens": 967}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5212", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which level of personality description appears to show the most change with age?\n\nOptions: \nA. Values\nB. Communication skills\nC. Identity\nD. Traits\nE. Self-esteem\nF. Interests\nG. Social roles\nH. Emotional responses\nI. Coping strategies\nJ. Personal concerns\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 554, "output_tokens": 458, "total_tokens": 1012}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4954", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Over 1 year, a study is conducted to assess the antileukemic activity of a new tyrosine kinase inhibitor in patients with chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis. All patients enrolled in the study are informed that they would be treated with the tyrosine kinase inhibitor. They are assigned to successive dose cohorts of 300 to 1000 mg/day of the drug. Six to eight patients are assigned to each dose. Treatment efficacy is determined based on the results of complete blood counts and bone marrow assessments conducted regularly throughout the study. This study is best described as which of the following?\n\nOptions: \nA. Prospective observational study\nB. Randomized clinical trial\nC. Quasi-experimental study\nD. Retrospective study\nE. Cohort study\nF. Open-labeled clinical trial\nG. Case-control study\nH. Crossover study\nI. Double-blind clinical trial\nJ. Longitudinal study\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1151, "output_tokens": 397, "total_tokens": 1548}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5412", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For Binge Eating Disorder it is incorrect that:\n\n\nOptions: \nA. BED patients have higher odds of developing obesity\nB. Binge Eating episodes in BED are usually richer in calories than those of BN, leading patients to obesity\nC. Spontaneous remission is a possible outcome\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 488, "output_tokens": 347, "total_tokens": 835}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5093", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The best available evidence for an association between amount of sugars and risk of dental caries comes from which type of study design?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Case-control study\nB. Longitudinal study\nC. Non-randomised controlled\nD. Cross sectional observational\nE. Experimental study\nF. Meta-analysis\nG. Qualitative study\nH. Randomised controlled\nI. Cohort\nJ. Ecological study\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The strongest evidence for a causal association typically comes from experimental studies, specifically randomized controlled trials (RCTs). However, for ethical and practical reasons regarding dental caries and sugar intake, the best available evidence often derives from longitudinal or cohort studies that track sugar consumption and caries development over time. Among the options, a cohort study (I) is the most appropriate for providing robust evidence on this association. \n\n\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 761, "output_tokens": 464, "total_tokens": 1225}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5570", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Inviduals suffering from inhalant allergies may also react to cross- reacting food allergens. A person suffering from a natural latex allergy might not react to one of the following allergens\n\n\nOptions: \nA. peanuts\nB. figs\nC. tomato\nD. avocado\nE. peach\nF. kiwi\nG. strawberries\nH. mango\nI. chestnuts\nJ. banana\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 620, "output_tokens": 420, "total_tokens": 1040}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4906", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Vitamin D deficiency can often be found as a single nutrient deficiency, that is, in an otherwise well-nourished person. The main reason this can happen is because:\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Vitamin D is not essential for the body, therefore, its deficiency doesn't affect the overall nourishment.\nB. Vitamin D is a rare nutrient and can only be found in a few expensive food items.\nC. Vitamin D absorption is not affected by the presence of other nutrients in the body.\nD. The content of vitamin D in foods depends on the soil in which the food was grown so is not related to wealth or age.\nE. Overconsumption of Vitamin D can lead to its deficiency.\nF. Diets containing sufficient other nutrients to promote growth can increase the requirement of vitamin D so that it becomes limiting.\nG. Most vitamin D in the body does not come from food so access to food is not an important determinant of vitamin D status.\nH. Foods containing large amounts of vitamin D are eaten by both poor and wealthy people according to various cultural reasons.\nI. Vitamin D is present in all types of food, therefore, its deficiency is usually accompanied by other nutrient deficiencies.\nJ. Vitamin D is only produced in the body during certain times of the year.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1544, "output_tokens": 320, "total_tokens": 1864}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5312", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A new enzyme is found in a transgenic mice that participates in synthesis of an unknown product using two reactants. When using radiolabeled compounds to study the enzyme, it is found that the enzyme catalyzes a process that switches a nitrogen group on one reactant to the other reactant. Which of the following categories would this new enzyme fall under?\n\nOptions: \nA. Ligase\nB. Hydrolase\nC. Transferase\nD. Synthetase\nE. Phosphatase\nF. Lyase\nG. Oxidoreductase\nH. Decarboxylase\nI. Kinase\nJ. Isomerase\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 813, "output_tokens": 236, "total_tokens": 1049}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5180", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 57-year-old man receives radiation therapy for a squamous cell carcinoma of the lung. Despite therapy, the tumor progressively increases in size, and he dies 6 months later. His tumor cells contain a point mutation in the p53 gene (TP53), leading to an inactive gene product. Based on this finding, the progressive tumor growth despite irradiation therapy is most likely to be related to a defect in cell cycle arrest in which of the following phases of the cell cycle?\n\nOptions: \nA. Metaphase\nB. G1\nC. Prophase\nD. G0\nE. Prometaphase\nF. S phase\nG. Anaphase\nH. M\nI. Telophase\nJ. G2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 896, "output_tokens": 411, "total_tokens": 1307}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5143", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sauna use, sometimes referred to as \"sauna bathing,\" is characterized by short-term passive exposure to extreme heat. This exposure elicits mild hyperthermia \u2013 an increase in the body's core temperature \u2013 that induces a thermoregulatory response involving neuroendocrine, cardiovascular, and cytoprotective mechanisms that work together to restore homeostasis and condition the body for future heat stressors\u2026 In recent decades, sauna bathing has emerged as a means to increase lifespan and improve overall health, based on compelling data from observational, interventional, and mechanistic studies. Of particular interest are the findings from studies of participants in the Kuopio Ischemic Heart Disease Risk Factor (KIHD) Study, an ongoing prospective population-based cohort study of health outcomes in more than 2,300 middle-aged men from eastern Finland, which identified strong links between sauna use and reduced death and disease\u2026 The KIHD findings showed that men who used the sauna two to three times per week were 27 percent less likely to die from cardiovascular-related causes than men who didn't use the sauna.[2] Furthermore, the benefits they experienced were found to be dose-dependent: Men who used the sauna roughly twice as often, about four to seven times per week, experienced roughly twice the benefits \u2013 and were 50 percent less likely to die from cardiovascular-related causes.[2] In addition, frequent sauna users were found to be 40 percent less likely to die from all causes of premature death. These findings held true even when considering age, activity levels, and lifestyle factors that might have influenced the men's health.[2]... The KIHD also revealed that frequent sauna use reduced the risk of developing dementia and Alzheimer's disease in a dose-dependent manner. Men who used the sauna two to three times per week had a 66 percent lower risk of developing dementia and a 65 percent lower risk of developing Alzheimer's disease, compared to men who used the sauna only one time per week\u2026 The health benefits associated with sauna use extended to other aspects of mental health, as well. Men participating in the KIHD study who used the sauna four to seven times per week were 77 percent less likely to develop psychotic disorders, regardless of the men's dietary habits, socioeconomic status, physical activity, and inflammatory status (as measured by C-reactive protein)\u2026Exposure to high temperature stresses the body, eliciting a rapid, robust response. The skin and core body temperatures increase markedly, and sweating ensues. The skin heats first, rising to 40\u00b0C (104\u00b0F), and then changes in core body temperature occur, rising slowly from 37\u00b0C (98.6\u00b0F, or normal) to 38\u00b0C (100.4\u00b0F) and then rapidly increasing to 39\u00b0C (102.2\u00b0F)\u2026  Cardiac output, a measure of the amount of work the heart performs in response to the body's need for oxygen, increases by 60 to 70 percent, while the heart rate (the number of beats per minute) increases and the stroke volume (the amount of blood pumped) remains unchanged.[5] During this time, approximately 50 to 70 percent of the body's blood flow is redistributed from the core to the skin to facilitate sweating. The average person loses approximately 0.5 kg of sweat while sauna bathing.[11] Acute heat exposure also induces a transient increase in overall plasma volume to mitigate the decrease in core blood volume. This increase in plasma volume not only provides a reserve source of fluid for sweating, but it also acts like the water in a car's radiator, cooling the body to prevent rapid increases in core body temperature and promoting heat tolerance\u2026 Repeated sauna use acclimates the body to heat and optimizes the body's response to future exposures, likely due to a biological phenomenon known as hormesis, a compensatory defense response following exposure to a mild stressor that is disproportionate to the magnitude of the stressor. Hormesis triggers a vast array of protective mechanisms that not only repair cell damage but also provide protection from subsequent exposures to more devastating stressors\u2026 The physiological responses to sauna use are remarkably similar to those experienced during moderate- to vigorous-intensity exercise. In fact, sauna use has been proposed as an alternative to exercise for people who are unable to engage in physical activity due to chronic disease or physical limitations.[13]\n\nThe review article sources a lot of data from Finland population studies, where the incidence of sauna use is substantially higher than most countries. Using the data, which of the following is something that is more plausible in Finland than elsewhere?\n\nOptions: \nA. Lower rates of cardiovascular-related deaths among frequent sauna users.\nB. More gold medals in adolescent skiing.\nC. A higher percentage of the population with optimized body's response to heat.\nD. Higher incidence of sauna-related injuries.\nE. Increased prevalence of heat tolerance in the population.\nF. Decreased rates of psychotic disorders among frequent sauna users.\nG. Improved marriage satisfaction rates.\nH. An 86-year old male mayor who is revered in the community.\nI. Decreased risk of dementia and Alzheimer's disease due to frequent sauna use.\nJ. Increased rate of pets in the household.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "The text highlights that sauna use leads to an optimized physiological response to heat through hormesis and acclimation. Since Finland has a much higher incidence of sauna bathing, the population there would be more likely to develop this adaptation. Therefore, the most plausible outcome in Finland is a higher percentage of the population with an optimized body's response to heat.\n\n\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 6760, "output_tokens": 672, "total_tokens": 7432}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5483", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sauna use, sometimes referred to as \"sauna bathing,\" is characterized by short-term passive exposure to extreme heat. This exposure elicits mild hyperthermia \u2013 an increase in the body's core temperature \u2013 that induces a thermoregulatory response involving neuroendocrine, cardiovascular, and cytoprotective mechanisms that work together to restore homeostasis and condition the body for future heat stressors\u2026 In recent decades, sauna bathing has emerged as a means to increase lifespan and improve overall health, based on compelling data from observational, interventional, and mechanistic studies. Of particular interest are the findings from studies of participants in the Kuopio Ischemic Heart Disease Risk Factor (KIHD) Study, an ongoing prospective population-based cohort study of health outcomes in more than 2,300 middle-aged men from eastern Finland, which identified strong links between sauna use and reduced death and disease\u2026 The KIHD findings showed that men who used the sauna two to three times per week were 27 percent less likely to die from cardiovascular-related causes than men who didn't use the sauna.[2] Furthermore, the benefits they experienced were found to be dose-dependent: Men who used the sauna roughly twice as often, about four to seven times per week, experienced roughly twice the benefits \u2013 and were 50 percent less likely to die from cardiovascular-related causes.[2] In addition, frequent sauna users were found to be 40 percent less likely to die from all causes of premature death. These findings held true even when considering age, activity levels, and lifestyle factors that might have influenced the men's health.[2]... The KIHD also revealed that frequent sauna use reduced the risk of developing dementia and Alzheimer's disease in a dose-dependent manner. Men who used the sauna two to three times per week had a 66 percent lower risk of developing dementia and a 65 percent lower risk of developing Alzheimer's disease, compared to men who used the sauna only one time per week\u2026 The health benefits associated with sauna use extended to other aspects of mental health, as well. Men participating in the KIHD study who used the sauna four to seven times per week were 77 percent less likely to develop psychotic disorders, regardless of the men's dietary habits, socioeconomic status, physical activity, and inflammatory status (as measured by C-reactive protein)\u2026Exposure to high temperature stresses the body, eliciting a rapid, robust response. The skin and core body temperatures increase markedly, and sweating ensues. The skin heats first, rising to 40\u00b0C (104\u00b0F), and then changes in core body temperature occur, rising slowly from 37\u00b0C (98.6\u00b0F, or normal) to 38\u00b0C (100.4\u00b0F) and then rapidly increasing to 39\u00b0C (102.2\u00b0F)\u2026  Cardiac output, a measure of the amount of work the heart performs in response to the body's need for oxygen, increases by 60 to 70 percent, while the heart rate (the number of beats per minute) increases and the stroke volume (the amount of blood pumped) remains unchanged.[5] During this time, approximately 50 to 70 percent of the body's blood flow is redistributed from the core to the skin to facilitate sweating. The average person loses approximately 0.5 kg of sweat while sauna bathing.[11] Acute heat exposure also induces a transient increase in overall plasma volume to mitigate the decrease in core blood volume. This increase in plasma volume not only provides a reserve source of fluid for sweating, but it also acts like the water in a car's radiator, cooling the body to prevent rapid increases in core body temperature and promoting heat tolerance\u2026 Repeated sauna use acclimates the body to heat and optimizes the body's response to future exposures, likely due to a biological phenomenon known as hormesis, a compensatory defense response following exposure to a mild stressor that is disproportionate to the magnitude of the stressor. Hormesis triggers a vast array of protective mechanisms that not only repair cell damage but also provide protection from subsequent exposures to more devastating stressors\u2026 The physiological responses to sauna use are remarkably similar to those experienced during moderate- to vigorous-intensity exercise. In fact, sauna use has been proposed as an alternative to exercise for people who are unable to engage in physical activity due to chronic disease or physical limitations.[13]\n\nBased on the article, which of the following statements is the author likely to agree with?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sauna use can prevent the onset of dementia in all cases.\nB. Sauna use is beneficial for mental health regardless of other lifestyle factors.\nC. Patients on a diet would benefit from sauna use.\nD. Patients with skin conditions may be cured with sauna use.\nE. Sauna use may increase the risk of heart disease.\nF. Salt restriction would be equal to sauna use for hypertensive patients.\nG. Heart surgery patients who cannot run on treadmills may benefit from sauna use.\nH. Frequent sauna use causes a significant loss of body weight.\nI. Sauna use can be a potential treatment for Alzheimer's disease.\nJ. Sauna use can completely replace the need for exercise.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 5283, "output_tokens": 485, "total_tokens": 5768}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5507", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Laryngoscopic examination of the vocal folds after suspected recurrent laryngeal nerve damage usually shows that the vocal fold on the injured side is tensed and in an intermediate position between adduction and abduction. This is because\n\nOptions: \nA. Both cricothyroid and interarytenoid muscles are fully active.\nB. Cricothyroid muscle is weak but the interarytenoids are paralyzed.\nC. cricothyroid muscle is paralyzed but the interarytenoids are fully active.\nD. cricothyroid muscle is paralyzed but the interarytenoids are weak.\nE. Cricothyroid muscle is weak but the interarytenoids are fully active.\nF. cricothyroid muscle is still functional but the interarytenoid muscles are fully active.\nG. Interarytenoid muscles are still functional but the cricothyroid is weak.\nH. Both cricothyroid and interarytenoid muscles are paralyzed.\nI. cricothyroid muscle is still functional but the interarytenoids are weak.\nJ. Interarytenoid muscles are still functional but the cricothyroid is fully active.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1312, "output_tokens": 525, "total_tokens": 1837}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5408", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which statement about intestinal \"brakes\" and \"accelerators\" is FALSE?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Short-chain fatty acids which move from colon to caecum (reflux) promote ileo-caecal motility\nB. The arrival of fiber in the colon causes an increase in motility and a switch from the \"fasting\" to the \"feeding\" pattern.\nC. The arrival of lipid in the duodenum causes an immediate reduction in motility and a switch from the \"fasting\" to the \"feeding\" pattern.\nD. Food in the stomach causes gastrin release, which stimulates acid secretion\nE. Protein ingestion leads to immediate increase in intestinal motility\nF. Gastric acid secretion inhibits small intestinal motility\nG. The presence of bile in the intestine slows down motility\nH. The presence of undigested food in the colon stimulates intestinal motility\nI. Dietary starch is a potent stimulator of small intestinal motility because it causes insulin release from the pancreas\nJ. The presence of glucose in the duodenum accelerates intestinal motility\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1267, "output_tokens": 428, "total_tokens": 1695}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5179", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A study is designed to evaluate the feasibility of acupuncture in children with chronic headaches. Sixty children with chronic headaches are recruited for the study. In addition to their usual therapy, all children are treated with acupuncture three times a week for 2 months. Which of the following best describes this study design?\n\nOptions: \nA. Randomized control trial\nB. Case-control\nC. Case series\nD. Crossover\nE. Longitudinal\nF. Meta-analysis\nG. Cohort\nH. Cross-sectional\nI. Qualitative study\nJ. Systematic review\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 832, "output_tokens": 459, "total_tokens": 1291}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5422", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A psychologist conducts an experiment in which subjects are asked to learn a series of \u201cfacts\u201d which are actually statements that have been fabricated by the research team. The subjects consist of undergraduate students at the university where the experiment is being conducted. The subjects are randomly assigned to groups that are compensated either $10 or $20 for their participation, are given either 15 minutes or 30 minutes to learn the facts, and are asked to recall the facts either in the same room in which they learned the facts or in a very different, unfamiliar setting. Which of the following are dependent variables in this experiment?\nI. The amount the subjects were compensated.\nII. The room in which the subjects were asked to recall facts.\nIII. The number of facts the subjects can recall.\nIV. The time the subjects were given to learn the facts.\n\nOptions: \nA. I and II only\nB. III only\nC. I, II, and III only\nD. II, III, and IV only\nE. I and IV only\nF. I and III and IV only\nG. I, III, and IV only\nH. II and IV only\nI. II only\nJ. I, II, and IV only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1361, "output_tokens": 306, "total_tokens": 1667}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5313", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A teacher sets up a reward system for her elementary school students. At the end of each day, she gives a sticker to each student who showed up on time that morning. At the end of each week, she gives a sticker to any student who got above a 90% on three quizzes in a row. After months of this regimen, she finds that performance on the quizzes has increased significantly but that tardiness has only decreased slightly. Which of the following best explains the teacher\u2019s observation?\n\nOptions: \nA. The students had more intrinsic motivation to do well on quizzes than to show up on time.\nB. The students' behavior change was stronger in response to a variable-ratio schedule than it was to a continuous reinforcement schedule.\nC. The students were more excited about the quizzes than about the reward system.\nD. The students' behavior change was stronger in response to a variable-interval schedule than it was to a fixed-ratio schedule.\nE. Variable ratio schedules create the strongest responses and behavior that is the least susceptible to extinction.\nF. The students\u2019 behavior change was stronger in response to a fixed-ratio schedule than it was to a continuous reinforcement schedule.\nG. The students' behavior change was weaker in response to a fixed-ratio schedule than it was to a continuous reinforcement schedule.\nH. The students' behavior change was stronger in response to a fixed-interval schedule than it was to a continuous reinforcement schedule.\nI. The students' behavior change was stronger in response to a continuous reinforcement schedule than it was to a variable-ratio schedule.\nJ. The students\u2019 behavior change was stronger in response to a fixed-ratio schedule than it was to a variable-interval schedule.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{F}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1944, "output_tokens": 419, "total_tokens": 2363}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5316", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A scientist using mouse models to determine the response of blood hormones to large levels of glucose in the body discovers a new hormone not previously described. According to his data, this hormone is found both inside and out of cells when carrying out its function, increase the amount of nucleic acid in the cell while functioning, and are derived from a structure containing four hydroxycarbon rings. This will likely be categorized as which type of hormone?\n\nOptions: \nA. Lipid-based\nB. Eicosanoid\nC. Glycoprotein\nD. Enzymatic\nE. Protein-based\nF. Carbohydrate-based\nG. Nucleic acid-based\nH. Steroid\nI. Amino acid\nJ. Peptide\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 922, "output_tokens": 342, "total_tokens": 1264}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5107", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: All other things being equal, which of the following persons is likely to live the longest?\n\nOptions: \nA. A black woman\nB. A Hispanic man\nC. A white woman\nD. An Asian man\nE. A white man\nF. A Native American man\nG. A Hispanic woman\nH. A Native American woman\nI. A black man\nJ. An Asian woman\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 604, "output_tokens": 345, "total_tokens": 949}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5294", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a cohort study of elderly women, the relative risk ratio for hip fractures among those who exercise regularly is 1.2 (95% confidence interval of 1.1 to 1.8). Which of the following is the most appropriate conclusion about the effect of regular exercise on the risk for hip fracture?\n\nOptions: \nA. Statistically significant overall increase in risk\nB. Statistically insignificant change in risk for those who exercise regularly\nC. Statistically significant overall decrease in risk\nD. Statistically nonsignificant decrease in risk\nE. Statistically significant decrease in risk only for those over 80\nF. Statistically significant overall decrease in risk for those who exercise regularly\nG. Statistically nonsignificant overall decrease in risk\nH. Statistically significant increase in risk only for those under 70\nI. No statistically significant change in risk\nJ. Statistically nonsignificant increase in risk\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1224, "output_tokens": 362, "total_tokens": 1586}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5402", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements is incorrect regarding fatty acid \u00df-oxidation?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. The rate of \u00df-oxidation is regulated by the availability of carbohydrates and the rate of utilisation of \u00df-oxidation products\nB. Peroxisomes are the site for the degradation of xenobiotics and eicosanoids\nC. Within the liver peroxisomes serve to oxidise very long chain fatty acids to medium chain products\nD. The rate of b-oxidation is regulated by the availability of fatty acids and the rate of utilisation of b-oxidation products\nE. The major site of fatty acid \u00df-oxidation is the peroxisomes, the mitochondria also contain enzymes for this pathway\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 937, "output_tokens": 290, "total_tokens": 1227}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4952", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During a study of renal glomeruli, a healthy animal kidney is kept in a vascular bath preparation at a constant afferent arterial pressure of 100 mm Hg. If the efferent arteriole is constricted with a vascular clamp, which of the following Starling forces is most likely to change in the glomeruli?\n\nOptions: \nA. Increased filtration coefficient (Kf)\nB. Increased hydrostatic pressure\nC. Increased blood flow\nD. Increased oncotic pressure\nE. Decreased hydrostatic pressure\nF. No change in Starling forces\nG. Decreased oncotic pressure\nH. Decreased filtration coefficient (Kf)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 884, "output_tokens": 325, "total_tokens": 1209}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5411", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The function of the gastrointestinal tract can be classified in several ways. Which of the following functions is most important for survival immediately after a meal?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Elimination of toxins\nB. Stimulation of appetite\nC. Maintenance of barrier function\nD. Extraction of maximum value from nutrients\nE. Control of blood sugar levels\nF. Production of hormones for growth and repair\nG. Regulation of body temperature\nH. Processing of food into a liquid form\nI. Absorption and retention of water and electrolytes\nJ. Production of digestive enzymes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 868, "output_tokens": 372, "total_tokens": 1240}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5524", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A new severe respiratory illness caused by a newly identified virus is discovered. Which of the following properties of a killed vaccine relative to a live vaccine is the most appropriate rationale for developing a killed vaccine for this illness?\n\nOptions: \nA. Is more likely to provide sterilizing immunity\nB. Can be administered in higher doses\nC. Develops more rapid protective immunity\nD. Is less likely to require subsequent boosters for lifelong immunity\nE. Is less likely to cause an allergic reaction\nF. Is more effective for immunocompromised individuals\nG. Is most likely to generate mucosal immunity\nH. Is less likely to cause local adverse reactions at the site of injection\nI. Avoids the concern for reversion to virulence\nJ. Is less likely to be affected by preexisting antibodies\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1058, "output_tokens": 383, "total_tokens": 1441}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5164", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A patient suffers a broken neck with damage to the spinal cord at the level of the sixth cervical vertebra.\n\nOptions: \nA. It is impossible to predict an effect on breathing.\nB. Their breathing rate will significantly increase.\nC. They will only be able to breathe quietly.\nD. Their breathing will be erratic and unpredictable.\nE. They will be unable to breathe without life support.\nF. Breathing will be unaffected.\nG. They will be able to breathe only with the help of a ventilator.\nH. They will be able to breathe only in short, shallow breaths.\nI. They will have to breathe through a tracheostomy tube.\nJ. They will not be able to breathe out, only in.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}  \n\nDamage at the sixth cervical vertebra spares the phrenic nerve (C3\u2013C5), which innervates the diaphragm, so the patient can still breathe but with impaired intercostal and abdominal muscles. This typically requires mechanical ventilation support for adequate breathing, especially during sleep or exertion. Therefore, they will need a ventilator to assist breathing.", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1110, "output_tokens": 486, "total_tokens": 1596}, "model_used": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_4996", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Assuming that the level of glucose is low, a mutation in the repressor associated with the lac operon of E. coli which prevents binding of the repressor to lactose should result in: \n\nOptions: \nA. expression of the genes only when glucose is present\nB. lack of expression or reduced expression of the lac operon genes under all circumstances\nC. no change in the expression of the lac operon genes\nD. expression of the genes only when lactose is absent\nE. constitutive expression of the lac operon genes\nF. expression of the genes only when lactose is present\nG. increased expression of the lac operon genes under all circumstances\nH. expression of the genes only when glucose is absent\nI. constitutive repression of the lac operon genes\nJ. reduced expression of the lac operon genes only when lactose is present\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1086, "output_tokens": 398, "total_tokens": 1484}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5397", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A study is conducted to assess the effectiveness of a new drug for the treatment of type 2 diabetes mellitus. A total of 1000 patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus are enrolled. Patients are randomly assigned to receive the new drug or standard treatment. The alpha and beta values for calculating probability are 0.05 and 0.20, respectively. Results show that the new drug is significantly better than standard treatment. If this study had been performed in a population of only 500 patients, which of the following would have been most likely to increase?\n\nOptions: \nA. Chance of a type II error\nB. Chance of a false positive result\nC. Size of the study population\nD. Power of the study\nE. Sensitivity of the study\nF. Specificity of the study\nG. Chance of a false negative result\nH. Probability of the alpha value\nI. Chance of a type I error\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1152, "output_tokens": 387, "total_tokens": 1539}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5214", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following factors has NOT received as much support as the others in research investigating why social support is related to better health?\n\nOptions: \nA. Physiological\nB. Behavioral\nC. Biological\nD. Anthropological\nE. Environmental\nF. Psychological\nG. Gerontological\nH. Neurological\nI. Social\nJ. Sociological\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "generated_result": {"generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}", "success": true, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 552, "output_tokens": 328, "total_tokens": 880}, "model_used": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507", "provider": "openrouter", "error": null}, "cost": null, "accuracy": null, "for_optimality": false}, {"global index": "MMLUPro_health_5269", "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the mos